1abe54842dc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062884 - Remove static from cast in widget/gtk/GfxInfoUtils.h to fix -Wunused-template with clang 23 r=gtk-reviewers,emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318321\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/GfxInfoUtils.h"], "git_node": "1f8ec3c5fdb6ad3655a3ca400936448053e73884", "git_parents": ["b7a1d63587b79add395ef543097bd9b139ccb121"], "node": "79b41d7180d135e54c49973eda94d31845a1b740", "parents": ["b311eb543fb65d326f6e9d0121d1efe092417a47"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062884 - Fix unused function templates in ipc to fix -Wunused-template with clang 23 r=ipc-reviewers,mccr8\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318315\n", "files": ["ipc/glue/Endpoint.h", "ipc/glue/IPCMessageUtils.h"], "git_node": "aeeb29ecd5e57a83f71e2153a68127b95e895fa7", "git_parents": ["1f8ec3c5fdb6ad3655a3ca400936448053e73884"], "node": "0856e3ba8a2af575cba5829e7df6b454460bc8a8", "parents": ["79b41d7180d135e54c49973eda94d31845a1b740"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062884 - Fix unused function templates in dom to fix -Wunused-template with clang 23 r=dom-core-reviewers,dom-storage-reviewers,gfx-reviewers,smaug,lsalzman,jesup\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318316\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsContentUtils.cpp", "dom/bindings/BindingUtils.h", "dom/canvas/WebGLContextDraw.cpp", "dom/canvas/WebGLShader.cpp", "dom/indexedDB/ActorsParent.cpp", "dom/indexedDB/IDBObjectStore.cpp", "dom/promise/Promise-inl.h", "dom/promise/gtest/NativeThenHandler.cpp", "dom/streams/StreamUtils.h"], "git_node": "81a308e15df2a4f01640b35e0be3e7c940394377", "git_parents": ["aeeb29ecd5e57a83f71e2153a68127b95e895fa7"], "node": "ba12c6c3704bbb585d2b5755d26734bf23933bb7", "parents": ["0856e3ba8a2af575cba5829e7df6b454460bc8a8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "serge-sans-paille \u003csguelton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062993 - Properly reference dav1d in toolkit/content/license.html r=sylvestre\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318132\n", "files": ["toolkit/content/license.html"], "git_node": "352431f2be38a0006f76ee104257c1d94cbfb052", "git_parents": ["81a308e15df2a4f01640b35e0be3e7c940394377"], "node": "9bcee471b6213977f7a7594c7a3eddb31456a6d7", "parents": ["ba12c6c3704bbb585d2b5755d26734bf23933bb7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Henri Sivonen \u003chsivonen@hsivonen.fi\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2042751 - Make `maybe_gather_combining()` in the collator fetch the CCC for non-starters in `upcoming`. r=iain\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318082\n", "files": ["js/src/tests/non262/Intl/Collator/ccc.js", "third_party/rust/icu_collator/src/elements.rs"], "git_node": "3496bae17f4b8df7d866e24dd46a10ee536e1ac8", "git_parents": ["352431f2be38a0006f76ee104257c1d94cbfb052"], "node": "38c701ff0cdd7b273f937e665202ce17c82c6d4c", "parents": ["9bcee471b6213977f7a7594c7a3eddb31456a6d7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Simon Chopin \u003cschopin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1933057 - mozcrash: print both stackwalk stdout and stderr r=gsvelto\n\n`minidump-stackwalk` might print spurious warnings or errors that aren't\nfatal, it shouldn't suppress the entire output of mozcrash. In\nparticular, the next patch will have it emit warning when crashes involve\nsystem libraries that don't have symbols.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312745\n", "files": ["testing/mozbase/mozcrash/mozcrash/mozcrash.py"], "git_node": "6e195b7fe78f716de4b47773c61d32cfbcbdc0e0", "git_parents": ["3496bae17f4b8df7d866e24dd46a10ee536e1ac8"], "node": "30f93cd82865c60f6858248078eae1a5f6a53a55", "parents": ["38c701ff0cdd7b273f937e665202ce17c82c6d4c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Simon Chopin \u003cschopin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1933057 - mozcrash: use symbols in binaries for local builds r=gsvelto\n\nIf the data is already available locally, we might as well use it, as\nthe .sym files might not have all data, e.g. system libraries, or not be\nthere at all if the user hasn't run ./mach buildsymbols.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312734\n", "files": ["testing/mozbase/mozcrash/mozcrash/mozcrash.py"], "git_node": "5e9ec8cac2e60260c70f26e24635d6845e5a8cfa", "git_parents": ["6e195b7fe78f716de4b47773c61d32cfbcbdc0e0"], "node": "9f7313ce5780c03b89f2c74fa6f20660e5579591", "parents": ["30f93cd82865c60f6858248078eae1a5f6a53a55"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061668 - Don't let the mouseup that follows a contextmenu event dismiss the panel-list it opened. r=mstriemer\n\nA contextmenu event is dispatched during the button press on Linux and macOS, so a\npanel-list opened from one is already an auto popover when the button is released,\nand that release light-dismisses it. At the pointerdown no auto popover was open\nyet, so the document's popover pointerdown target was never recorded; at the\npointerup the release target has no popover ancestor either, so the two match and\nHidePopoverStackUntil hides the whole auto popover stack. Since that happens\nnatively, hide() never runs and the open attribute stays set, so the element state\ndesyncs from the popover state.\n\nOpening as a manual popover keeps the panel in the top layer but out of the auto\npopover stack, so light dismiss leaves it alone. What's worth checking is that the\nlisteners addHideListeners() already installs cover everything light dismiss did:\noutside mousedown, Escape, focus changes, scroll, resize and window blur.\n\nOne limitation of the test: only the popover attribute assertion actually\ndiscriminates the fix. The assertions that the panel survives the mouseup pass with\nand without it, because a synthesized release under mochitest-chrome does not\nreproduce the dismissal; the end-to-end behavior was verified by hand and against\nthe urlbar result context menu.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317046\n", "files": ["toolkit/content/tests/widgets/chrome-nova.toml", "toolkit/content/tests/widgets/chrome.toml", "toolkit/content/tests/widgets/test_panel_list_contextmenu.html", "toolkit/content/widgets/panel-list/panel-list.mjs"], "git_node": "cf16cafd0e8c22859363ac84dae1f3e219b7abc4", "git_parents": ["5e9ec8cac2e60260c70f26e24635d6845e5a8cfa"], "node": "3b594cd513aabf6b39a3e082ca62ab0b3dab1e5b", "parents": ["9f7313ce5780c03b89f2c74fa6f20660e5579591"], "tags": []}, {"author": "serge-sans-paille \u003csguelton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062945 - Properly credit graphite2 in toolkit/content/license.html r=sylvestre DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318089\n", "files": ["toolkit/content/license.html"], "git_node": "c0c9da695555db54582861da10a6ba0584818d1b", "git_parents": ["cf16cafd0e8c22859363ac84dae1f3e219b7abc4"], "node": "8ed10d9e53d9f22eb11ed72c32a3ca769035a4e4", "parents": ["3b594cd513aabf6b39a3e082ca62ab0b3dab1e5b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "AndiAJ \u003candiaj@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060415 - Fix httpsOnlyModeEnabledInNormalBrowsingTest UI test r=jajohnson\n\nThe UI test was flaky because it clicked the \u201cContinue to HTTP Site\u201d a split second before loading the HTTPS-Only error page, so the button wasn\u2019t there yet and the click failed.\n\nThe fix makes continueToHttpSite() wait for the button to actually appear before tapping it (the same wait the \u201cGo Back\u201d path already had).\n\nThe UI test successfully passed 50x on Firebase \u2705\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318084\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/BrowserPage.kt"], "git_node": "651ad2ef8393eb12b5910e08140d56a7b287a5f3", "git_parents": ["c0c9da695555db54582861da10a6ba0584818d1b"], "node": "f1d635717374630e69f09ef5d340aabc43594af4", "parents": ["8ed10d9e53d9f22eb11ed72c32a3ca769035a4e4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061788 - Make `HTMLEditor::InsertFromDataTransfer` use the almost same order as `HTMLTransferablePreparer::AddDataFlavorsInBestOrder` r=edgar\n\nWhen we create a `DataTransfer` from `nsITransferable`,\n`HTMLTransferablePreparer::AddDataFlavorsInBestOrder` adds the data\nwith preferred order of `HTMLEditor`. However,\n`HTMLEditor::InsertFromDataTransfer` is called with `DataTransfer`\ncreated outside `HTMLEditor`. Therefore, the order can be any.\nHowever, `HTMLEditor` should use the same order as far as possible.\n\nHowever, the coming `DataTransfer`'s data order may be meaningful\nespecially when it's an image because converting image format may be\nlossy conversion. Therefore, this patch does not reorder the images\nwith `clipboard.paste_image_type` pref to keep current behavior.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318030\n", "files": ["editor/libeditor/HTMLEditorDataTransfer.cpp", "editor/libeditor/tests/mochitest.toml", "editor/libeditor/tests/test_dragdrop_img_with_data_url.html"], "git_node": "e643932019293569aac21f83ca1c77d2e08003e8", "git_parents": ["651ad2ef8393eb12b5910e08140d56a7b287a5f3"], "node": "313a6f32f3871585dce39288d2d2d678f94085a8", "parents": ["f1d635717374630e69f09ef5d340aabc43594af4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandra Borovova \u003caborovova@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062863 - Update metadata for clipboard-apis/permissions-policy/clipboard-read/clipboard-read-enabled-by-permissions-policy.tentative.https.sub.html on Android.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318386\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/clipboard-apis/permissions-policy/clipboard-read/clipboard-read-enabled-by-permissions-policy.tentative.https.sub.html.ini"], "git_node": "edb95d86224928f75131572aeeba304e47acaf29", "git_parents": ["e643932019293569aac21f83ca1c77d2e08003e8"], "node": "1d523ac974e77d89b2e30086ec00858922cc0c8a", "parents": ["313a6f32f3871585dce39288d2d2d678f94085a8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jon Coppeard \u003cjcoppeard@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062958 - Clear mark bits in stolen chunks immediately outside concurrent marking builds r=sfink\n\nAs per the comments we only need to defer clearing the mark bits in stolen\nchunks if concurrent marking can be happening. It's best to avoid this if\npossible because it means we need to iterate all the chunks.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318100\n", "files": ["js/src/gc/BufferAllocator.cpp", "js/src/gc/BufferAllocator.h"], "git_node": "ffe404accb90f8ae750f611324b7bb913680309b", "git_parents": ["edb95d86224928f75131572aeeba304e47acaf29"], "node": "d576a10c3c1120924cea39b1920c524f9b56ca89", "parents": ["1d523ac974e77d89b2e30086ec00858922cc0c8a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jon Coppeard \u003cjcoppeard@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062891 - Make string flag changes only affect concurrent marking builds r=spidermonkey-reviewers,sfink\n\nI wasn't able to detect any change from the patches in the regressing bug when\nrunning sunspider locally.\n\nNevertheless we can make these changes only affect concurrent marking builds\nwhich should fix the problem.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318071\n", "files": ["js/src/gc/Cell.h", "js/src/gc/Marking.cpp", "js/src/vm/StringType.cpp", "js/src/vm/StringType.h"], "git_node": "0e95034e487d2f2b3801f4d13bc204e5c1cd6369", "git_parents": ["ffe404accb90f8ae750f611324b7bb913680309b"], "node": "b06aa863bb1baa240f559ebd020478183d8b8b73", "parents": ["d576a10c3c1120924cea39b1920c524f9b56ca89"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Keith Cirkel \u003ckeithamus@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2018913 - Part 2: Implement scoped document set for cross-document upgrade ordering r=edgar\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313456\n", "files": ["dom/base/CustomElementRegistry.cpp", "dom/base/CustomElementRegistry.h", "dom/base/Element.cpp", "dom/base/ShadowRoot.cpp", "dom/base/nsRange.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/custom-elements/registries/CustomElementRegistry-upgrade.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/custom-elements/registries/Element-innerHTML.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/custom-elements/registries/scoped-registry-define-upgrade-criteria.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/custom-elements/registries/scoped-registry-define-upgrade-order.html.ini"], "git_node": "31ce26b30abe1e3569cae80cb8e61654e106113a", "git_parents": ["0e95034e487d2f2b3801f4d13bc204e5c1cd6369"], "node": "b694e438ff11a566777d9cb0c72470972c1f0a07", "parents": ["b06aa863bb1baa240f559ebd020478183d8b8b73"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062884 - Remove static from mozilla::detail::MaybeGetHash/EnsureHash to fix -Wunused-template with clang 23 r=sergesanspaille\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318309\n", "files": ["mfbt/HashTable.h"], "git_node": "7a176282f8b349285ad91d6d872d14c2d0570a6b", "git_parents": ["31ce26b30abe1e3569cae80cb8e61654e106113a"], "node": "f850c35cb817fd9bee58fba99de977024792e8fa", "parents": ["b694e438ff11a566777d9cb0c72470972c1f0a07"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandre Poirot \u003cpoirot.alex@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057352 - Use a dedicated logic for each nested resource update. r=devtools-reviewers,nchevobbe\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313895\n", "files": ["devtools/shared/commands/resource/moz.build", "devtools/shared/commands/resource/nested-update-processors/moz.build", "devtools/shared/commands/resource/nested-update-processors/stylesheet.js", "devtools/shared/commands/resource/resource-command.js"], "git_node": "722b7ac749c5a10212e3b9afd09e0f54fc5146d9", "git_parents": ["7a176282f8b349285ad91d6d872d14c2d0570a6b"], "node": "9a445ad133bbf0faef45705038c0488547831629", "parents": ["f850c35cb817fd9bee58fba99de977024792e8fa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan Grulich \u003cjgrulich@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054619 - WebRTC backport: Video capture: validate SPA pod values to prevent OOB reads r=pehrsons\n\nAdd bounds checks when reading SPA pod choice values in OnNodeParam\nand ParseFormat. Validate that the pod value size matches the expected\ntype using spa_pod_type_size() and that the number of choice items\nis sufficient before accessing the underlying arrays.\n\nThis is a simple backport of an WebRTC upstream change.\n\nUpstream commit: a0253ec15b3d3072fb35d6be29ba9224c36f9dd7\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318394\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_capture/linux/pipewire_session.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/a0253ec15b.no-op-cherry-pick-msg"], "git_node": "6ae767c411c38fea206ede5ba23e6405c725d705", "git_parents": ["722b7ac749c5a10212e3b9afd09e0f54fc5146d9"], "node": "9c1a83656bac07beeebcb47958c0c27ab467e5c8", "parents": ["9a445ad133bbf0faef45705038c0488547831629"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Derek Schuff \u003cdschuff@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2037722 [wpt PR 59714] - Add CI script for syncing selected WebAssembly proposal tests, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd CI script for syncing selected WebAssembly proposal tests (#59714)\n\n* Prototype script for adding WebAssembly proposal tests\n\nThe current update-wasm-tests workflow updates the wasm core tests by checking\nout the spec repo and regenerating them. This PR also adds support for\nupdating proposals that have not yet been merged into the main spec. It does\nthis by checking out the proposal repo, determining which tests are updated\ncompared to the main spec, building the tests (with the fork's interpreter),\nand copying just the updated tests into WPT as tentative tests.\n\n* add stack switching\n\n* filter out non-wast files\n\n* fix trailing whitespace\n\n* address some of the review feedback\n\n* Record udpated and merged proposals for PR body\n\n* Simplify Wasm test update workflow and improve PR body details\n\n- Update `update-proposals.py` to include repository URLs and commit hashes in the proposals summary.\n- Refactor `update-wasm-tests.yml` workflow to:\n    - Dynamically determine if core spec tests, proposal tests, or both have changed.\n    - Simplify the commit message to \"Update Wasm tests\" with a suffix indicating the changes (core, proposals, or both).\n    - Combine the PR body generation and PR creation steps.\n    - Use `gh pr create --body-file` to pass the PR body, eliminating the complex multi-line output block.\n    - Include detailed repository and revision information for both core spec and proposals in the PR body.\n\n* remove trailing whitespace\n--\n\nwpt-commits: d3f45e122beb48035bc1eecda21f253d71f6d236\nwpt-pr: 59714\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/.github/workflows/update-wasm-tests.yml", "testing/web-platform/tests/CODEOWNERS", "testing/web-platform/tests/wasm/proposals.json", "testing/web-platform/tests/wasm/tools/update-proposals.py"], "git_node": "8c35607fffd93a5d3da4ed4e3cf76d74c01f0f05", "git_parents": ["6ae767c411c38fea206ede5ba23e6405c725d705"], "node": "bea6ef83ee10ca099db4f5294f6f07c0d09df7d2", "parents": ["9c1a83656bac07beeebcb47958c0c27ab467e5c8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hoch Hochkeppel (HE/HIM) \u003cmhochk@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062340 [wpt PR 61832] - [Grid] Fix fragmentation edge case, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[Grid] Fix fragmentation edge case\n\nPrior to this change, the code assumed that a grid item whose row is\npositioned above the current fragmentainer had been laid out in a\nprevious fragment, so long as we were already fragmenting. This missed\nthe case where there is no previous fragment because we are in the first\nfragment (and the row was positioned above the current fragmentainer for\nreasons other than belonging to a previous fragment).\n\nThis change adds a check to confirm we are actually *mid*-fragmentation\nbefore skipping, and a WPT that exercises this scenario.\n\nThis in turn avoids some DCHECK and related failures that can happen\nfrom having a node that doesn't get laid out.\n\nBug: 435228826\nChange-Id: I32ce619af218981aca77a3da532800b95219696e\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8203945\nReviewed-by: Kurt Catti-Schmidt \u003ckschmi@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Hoch Hochkeppel \u003cmhochk@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Morten Stenshorne \u003cmstensho@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1676533}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 26bc0012354f88631114be2f8b3db0b475ac64e8\nwpt-pr: 61832\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-container-fragmentation-013.html"], "git_node": "a155bd7efcfaf6cd0777dc3e51c0960cbd66a54a", "git_parents": ["8c35607fffd93a5d3da4ed4e3cf76d74c01f0f05"], "node": "8e3493bacd9b7bf0b92a7182336e3feccb4ddf77", "parents": ["bea6ef83ee10ca099db4f5294f6f07c0d09df7d2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062340 [wpt PR 61832] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61832\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-container-fragmentation-013.html.ini"], "git_node": "9f409eb17dd6e357d802502ff36a2c06bd56d396", "git_parents": ["a155bd7efcfaf6cd0777dc3e51c0960cbd66a54a"], "node": "87a5654e11c5063aa9d8441059b0d6fbf478bf67", "parents": ["8e3493bacd9b7bf0b92a7182336e3feccb4ddf77"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Eldar Pulatov \u003cepulatov.dev@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062370 [wpt PR 61834] - [web-tests] Add keyDown editing regression test, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[web-tests] Add keyDown editing regression test\n\nAdd a WPT for a character-producing WebDriver keyDown action. Assert\nthat keydown, beforeinput, and input are dispatched in order and that\nthe focused text input contains the character when the action completes.\n\nAlso assert that canceling keydown prevents beforeinput and input and\nleaves the value unchanged. Keeping keyDown and keyUp in separate action\nsequences detects character insertion incorrectly deferred to keyUp.\n\nThis adds regression coverage for the EventSender fix in\nhttps://crrev.com/c/8171743.\n\nBug: 397870172\nChange-Id: If2012870ab621728635b33bb24eab32756a060a5\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8216791\nCommit-Queue: Dan Clark \u003cdaniec@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Dave Tapuska \u003cdtapuska@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Dan Clark \u003cdaniec@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1676660}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 6fcf788c8992faa04b9b9d85b8717da466bf5ce1\nwpt-pr: 61834\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/uievents/keyboard/keydown-input-events.html"], "git_node": "954fc58c47f607d4061daaef446767dc725b38b4", "git_parents": ["9f409eb17dd6e357d802502ff36a2c06bd56d396"], "node": "60214e19ce2a15abac52744e923912dd4926e8d6", "parents": ["87a5654e11c5063aa9d8441059b0d6fbf478bf67"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daniel Clark \u003cdaniec@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062386 [wpt PR 61836] - Bail out of paste command if frame is removed during paste event handler, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nBail out of paste command if frame is removed during paste event handler\n\nWhen a paste into an iframe triggers a paste event handler the\nhandler can disconnect the iframe. If this happens we crash in\nEditor.CanPaste() because the FrameSelection it relies on doesn't\nexpect to be working in a disconnected frame.\n\nFix the crash by bailing out after the paste event if we find the\nframe has gone away.\n\nFixed: 542666937\nChange-Id: I1bdabc17ec8005cc1f41dee1ed071ab4919ba426\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8226608\nReviewed-by: Jack Miller \u003cjackmil@google.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Dan Clark \u003cdaniec@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1676681}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 6496278acfbd6c12db85d2cbc7b1f822fb2d81ba\nwpt-pr: 61836\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/clipboard-apis/detached-iframe/paste-on-detaching-iframe.https.html"], "git_node": "79c894c22e0bccd2486d02fb6bede6d1e84886aa", "git_parents": ["954fc58c47f607d4061daaef446767dc725b38b4"], "node": "d0ec66827e9f72b6e25aab2f0a1d58372aaba620", "parents": ["60214e19ce2a15abac52744e923912dd4926e8d6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ahmad Saleem \u003c52317531+Ahmad-S792@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062433 [wpt PR 61837] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=321424, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=321424 (#61837)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: fd1c532b80aebd9daf729cf5e74b2c3e3e899cc3\nwpt-pr: 61837\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-masking/clip-path/clip-path-shape-svg-rotated-container-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-masking/clip-path/clip-path-shape-svg-rotated-container.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-masking/clip-path/clip-path-shape-svg-rotated-shape-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-masking/clip-path/clip-path-shape-svg-rotated-shape.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-masking/clip-path/clip-path-shape-svg-scaled-shape-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-masking/clip-path/clip-path-shape-svg-scaled-shape.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-masking/clip-path/clip-path-shape-svg-view-box-rotated-shape-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-masking/clip-path/clip-path-shape-svg-view-box-rotated-shape.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-masking/clip-path/clip-path-shape-svg-view-box-scaled-shape-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-masking/clip-path/clip-path-shape-svg-view-box-scaled-shape.html"], "git_node": "ea4205d4cbcd7edb10029ca998596248eb8012ac", "git_parents": ["79c894c22e0bccd2486d02fb6bede6d1e84886aa"], "node": "371e2da8ad312cdc0116f1957241abc5a8c90d87", "parents": ["d0ec66827e9f72b6e25aab2f0a1d58372aaba620"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ahmad Saleem \u003c52317531+Ahmad-S792@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062435 [wpt PR 61838] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=321386, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=321386 (#61838)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: baa638a2e4ae9e09413f4cfbeefdb9adf2016b24\nwpt-pr: 61838\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webaudio/the-audio-api/the-audiobuffersourcenode-interface/audiobuffersource-reverse-long-buffer.html"], "git_node": "d311a5b1e2ef8f214926267f09ce3cf453ce1c90", "git_parents": ["ea4205d4cbcd7edb10029ca998596248eb8012ac"], "node": "45479d0c05022876ae0f87e66bcf34f419caf54e", "parents": ["371e2da8ad312cdc0116f1957241abc5a8c90d87"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062435 [wpt PR 61838] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61838\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webaudio/the-audio-api/the-audiobuffersourcenode-interface/audiobuffersource-reverse-long-buffer.html.ini"], "git_node": "70a8b591a324d32cd843b54dcf8796c0ea2f216f", "git_parents": ["d311a5b1e2ef8f214926267f09ce3cf453ce1c90"], "node": "d72a29a747a0e2c4999043d0647e0fc9f63f185a", "parents": ["45479d0c05022876ae0f87e66bcf34f419caf54e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Liu \u003clcdavid@google.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062381 [wpt PR 61835] - Add a runtime feature for scroll-snap-type: pair, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd a runtime feature for scroll-snap-type: pair\n\nChange-Id: I618b05cf7ae8ff6ab4db18c590bb568a7b185591\nBug: 542706103\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8197524\nCommit-Queue: David Liu \u003clcdavid@google.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Robert Flack \u003cflackr@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Vladimir Levin \u003cvmpstr@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1676696}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: cbf4c230d7e6f2df24dde01b5d6942f17abed639\nwpt-pr: 61835\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-scroll-snap/pair/scroll-snap-type-pair.tentative.html"], "git_node": "8d2bc1cc70de692d461de49008359ada9d7792a5", "git_parents": ["70a8b591a324d32cd843b54dcf8796c0ea2f216f"], "node": "832d1324d1df80411d40d4a03fd29b77bdcf73f0", "parents": ["d72a29a747a0e2c4999043d0647e0fc9f63f185a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062381 [wpt PR 61835] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61835\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-scroll-snap/pair/scroll-snap-type-pair.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "e0562b8177a94617f3bfd409f34014fcf68f5ff4", "git_parents": ["8d2bc1cc70de692d461de49008359ada9d7792a5"], "node": "e34dd7a8c21a04d5fed79188fc0499796262ffc8", "parents": ["832d1324d1df80411d40d4a03fd29b77bdcf73f0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sam Sneddon \u003cgsnedders@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056800 [wpt PR 61471] - Report worker errors in OffscreenCanvas reftests, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd failOnError/reftestStep/reftestPromise to common/reftest-wait.js\n\nReftests that wait on an event or promise that may never fire (e.g. an\nunimplemented API) currently hang until the harness timeout instead of\nfailing fast. These helpers let a reftest report a synchronous throw\nor promise rejection as an immediate, visible failure and stop waiting\nfor a screenshot, mirroring how testharness.js converts exceptions\nraised in step_func/promise_test into test failures. failOnError skips\nrel=mismatch-only reftests, since an error page, which necessarily\ndiffers from the reference, would cause a spurious pass.\n\n--\nReport worker errors in OffscreenCanvas reftests\n\nUncaught exceptions, mostly unimplemented APIs, in the worker left\nreftest-wait set forever, causing timeouts and adding more than 20\nminutes of runtime to both Firefox and Safari.\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 192938a148ff4d05f381a9cdb6845bf61085f350, 2517845b612a4290cfef50ec259efcf9a2806011\nwpt-pr: 61471\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/common/reftest-wait.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/compositing/2d.composite.grid.filter.no_shadow.drawImage.w.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/compositing/2d.composite.grid.filter.no_shadow.fillRect.w.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/compositing/2d.composite.grid.filter.no_shadow.pattern.w.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/compositing/2d.composite.grid.filter.shadow.drawImage.w.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/compositing/2d.composite.grid.filter.shadow.fillRect.w.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/compositing/2d.composite.grid.filter.shadow.pattern.w.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/compositing/2d.composite.grid.no_filter.no_shadow.drawImage.w.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/compositing/2d.composite.grid.no_filter.no_shadow.fillRect.w.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/compositing/2d.composite.grid.no_filter.no_shadow.pattern.w.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/compositing/2d.composite.grid.no_filter.shadow.drawImage.w.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/compositing/2d.composite.grid.no_filter.shadow.fillRect.w.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/compositing/2d.composite.grid.no_filter.shadow.pattern.w.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/fill-and-stroke-styles/2d.gradient.colorInterpolationMethod.w.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/fill-and-stroke-styles/2d.gradient.hueInterpolationMethod.w.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/filters/2d.filter.canvasFilterObject.componentTransfer.discrete.tentative.w.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/filters/2d.filter.canvasFilterObject.componentTransfer.gamma.tentative.w.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/filters/2d.filter.canvasFilterObject.componentTransfer.identity.tentative.w.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/filters/2d.filter.canvasFilterObject.componentTransfer.linear.tentative.w.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/filters/2d.filter.canvasFilterObject.componentTransfer.table.tentative.w.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/filters/2d.filter.canvasFilterObject.dropShadow.tentative.w.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/filters/2d.filter.canvasFilterObject.gaussianBlur.tentative.w.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/filters/2d.filter.drop-shadow-globalAlpha.w.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/filters/2d.filter.layers.componentTransfer.discrete.tentative.w.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/filters/2d.filter.layers.componentTransfer.gamma.tentative.w.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/filters/2d.filter.layers.componentTransfer.identity.tentative.w.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/filters/2d.filter.layers.componentTransfer.linear.tentative.w.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/filters/2d.filter.layers.componentTransfer.table.tentative.w.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/filters/2d.filter.layers.dropShadow.tentative.w.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/filters/2d.filter.layers.gaussianBlur.tentative.w.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/layers/2d.layer.anisotropic-blur.isotropic.tentative.w.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/layers/2d.layer.anisotropic-blur.mostly-x.tentative.w.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/layers/2d.layer.anisotropic-blur.mostly-y.tentative.w.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/layers/2d.layer.anisotropic-blur.x-only.tentative.w.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/layers/2d.layer.anisotropic-blur.y-only.tentative.w.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/layers/2d.layer.blur-from-outside-canvas.no-clipping.ctx-filter.w.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/layers/2d.layer.blur-from-outside-canvas.no-clipping.layer-filter.tentative.w.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/layers/2d.layer.blur-from-outside-canvas.with-clipping.ctx-filter.w.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/layers/2d.layer.blur-from-outside-canvas.with-clipping.layer-filter.tentative.w.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/layers/2d.layer.clearRect.full.w.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/layers/2d.layer.clearRect.partial.w.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/layers/2d.layer.clip-inside-and-outside.ctx-filter.w.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/layers/2d.layer.clip-inside-and-outside.laye