android-reviewers,alastun\" for causing fenix.ui.efficiency.test failures. IGNORE BAD COMMIT MESSAGES\n\nThis reverts commit c087e7d78e5db684cb2afd8745f739882f144443.\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/onboarding/DefaultBrowserPromptManager.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/onboarding/OnboardingFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/onboarding/DefaultBrowserPromptManagerTest.kt"], "git_node": "e7558542c85c50fe746dadcba70d193ce07029c1", "git_parents": ["7b6fee2b1d209681d45243c113c523b7af7bc0e9"], "node": "afec2ca7f1ae8a5504e6eaf5e16a4499f0c14c72", "parents": ["c82917c08ae9bff59d171176dc270b5a0a852faf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055599 - Use align-content in the UA sheet to implement input / button centering. r=Oriol,layout-reviewers,firefox-style-system-reviewers,dholbert\n\nThis implements the proposal in\nhttps://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/14190, and allows authors to\noverride this if they need to.\n\n`\u003cinput\u003e` might want an `!important` if it causes compatibility issues?\nBut hopefully not.\n\nWill wait to land this until there's a resolution, of course.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312564\n", "files": ["layout/generic/nsBlockFrame.h", "layout/reftests/forms/button/button-display-grid-fullsize-1.html", "layout/style/res/forms.css", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/rendering/non-replaced-elements/form-controls/resets.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/rendering/widgets/baseline-alignment-and-overflow.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/rendering/widgets/button-layout/anonymous-button-content-box-ref.html", "xpcom/ds/StaticAtoms.py"], "git_node": "c1385efce5601b64ea84b7259d12f816fd942575", "git_parents": ["e7558542c85c50fe746dadcba70d193ce07029c1"], "node": "7179f008c861883b6d94fc1f74594c2ea181bebf", "parents": ["afec2ca7f1ae8a5504e6eaf5e16a4499f0c14c72"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jeremy Swinarton \u003cjswinarton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2052608: Restore the collapsed tab group label hover highlight in Nova and match corner rounding to the label r=sthompson,tabbrowser-reviewers,desktop-theme-reviewers,mstriemer\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315332\n", "files": ["browser/themes/osx/browser.css", "browser/themes/shared/tabbrowser/tabs.css"], "git_node": "184240f6f327d2eb160f6158f38d3c20757f74db", "git_parents": ["c1385efce5601b64ea84b7259d12f816fd942575"], "node": "dc9315e3c50ad1abf45f73c0eae45d1999ebd38b", "parents": ["7179f008c861883b6d94fc1f74594c2ea181bebf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "AndiAJ \u003candiaj@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063195 - Migrate pauseResumeCancelDownloadTest UI test to the efficiency framework r=jajohnson\n\nThe UI test successfully passed 25x on Firebase \u2705\nAll UI tests successfully passed 1x on Firebase \u2705\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318447\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/DownloadTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/BrowserPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/NotificationPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/DownloadsSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/NotificationSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/CustomTabsTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/DownloadTest.kt"], "git_node": "6f5b0ab1a85291c8b429be0a231547639f92e012", "git_parents": ["184240f6f327d2eb160f6158f38d3c20757f74db"], "node": "ef7c88edc89c26ba9b2229b80e14205bdae10d78", "parents": ["dc9315e3c50ad1abf45f73c0eae45d1999ebd38b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "AndiAJ \u003candiaj@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063242 - Migrate media notification related UI tests to the efficiency framework r=jajohnson\n\nBoth UI tests successfully passed 25x on Firebase \u2705\nAll UI tests successfully passed 1x on Firebase \u2705\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318448\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/MediaNotificationTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/BrowserPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/NotificationPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/BrowserPageSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/NotificationSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/MediaNotificationTest.kt"], "git_node": "966f97f5d21e7a2a3c2f18b49550e9ded7e8337c", "git_parents": ["6f5b0ab1a85291c8b429be0a231547639f92e012"], "node": "f50c089ebc06dd33e62182095fa9b04569071864", "parents": ["ef7c88edc89c26ba9b2229b80e14205bdae10d78"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Chevobbe \u003cnchevobbe@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062153 - [devtools] Fix RDM Device Settings modal. r=jdescottes,desktop-theme-reviewers,tabbrowser-reviewers,sclements,hjones,devtools-reviewers.\n\nWhen the dialog is displayed, span the RDM iframe to the bottom row so it overlaps the browser stack,\nas well as a potential bottom-docked DevTools toolbox.\nWe also need to adjust the z-index so it's displayed on top of the browser stack.\nFinally, we set the `accomodate-ua` class on the .browserContainer element, and\nuse it to udpate the `--rdm-toolbar-height` variable, that we then use to set\nthe grid row's height; this way the row is always the same height, even when\nwe open the dialog (if we wouldn't do that, the row would grow, and we wouldn't\nhave the same space between the RDM toolbar and the content page).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317419\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/browser-shared.css", "browser/themes/shared/tabbrowser/content-area.css", "devtools/client/responsive/responsive-browser.css", "devtools/client/responsive/ui.js"], "git_node": "07c342e3e5d546fecc3ae2fde9032ef4996abca7", "git_parents": ["966f97f5d21e7a2a3c2f18b49550e9ded7e8337c"], "node": "ce4b1454d6120352476b99ea9c82222fecc57c16", "parents": ["f50c089ebc06dd33e62182095fa9b04569071864"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Maryam \u003cmomar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2007804 - Add `lid` to the global Copy Clean Link strip list r=emz\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318412\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/antitracking/StripOnShareLists/MPL2/StripOnShare.json"], "git_node": "78dd39231cb1bf49233fa6ce6243fc6db65af0bc", "git_parents": ["07c342e3e5d546fecc3ae2fde9032ef4996abca7"], "node": "b45e8cf5e8d63fd073cd91d95ea7c08bf723d7e2", "parents": ["ce4b1454d6120352476b99ea9c82222fecc57c16"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lars Eggert \u003clars@eggert.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062857 - Hand TLS token certificate DER to about:networking as typed arrays r=valentin,necko-reviewers\n\nWhich should be much faster.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318451\n", "files": ["dom/chrome-webidl/NetDashboard.webidl", "netwerk/base/Dashboard.cpp"], "git_node": "59a76485b90aec06af46da1ae0dca90eb8d0a8d4", "git_parents": ["78dd39231cb1bf49233fa6ce6243fc6db65af0bc"], "node": "57013a7b5dfa28f12d8f84268bd4a88f4b200c63", "parents": ["b45e8cf5e8d63fd073cd91d95ea7c08bf723d7e2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061752 - Re-enable platform decoding for H264 on Windows ARM64. r=webrtc-reviewers,bwc\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318395\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "d5ccd921a39a9bb86264e3bd4a60a5e8b676cf63", "git_parents": ["59a76485b90aec06af46da1ae0dca90eb8d0a8d4"], "node": "92af323345a9b4800d695a7e1cc1c88035ff79d3", "parents": ["57013a7b5dfa28f12d8f84268bd4a88f4b200c63"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Marcin Kozi\u0144ski \u003cmkozinski@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059021 - Ensure duplicated handles are always owned by the crash helper r=afranchuk\n\nThis moves the task of duplicating handles that need to be passed to the\ncrash helper from a push model to a pull model, it has a few benefits:\n- Received handles are guaranteed to be valid (or duplication will fail)\n- We don't need to wait for the crash helper process to start on Windows\n  before we're able to register child processes with it. This might\n  speedup first process startup.\n- We deliberately avoid duplicating pseudo-handles as we don't want\n  those to be duplicated across processes since they might cause some\n  nasty surprises.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317540\n", "files": ["toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_client/src/lib.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_client/src/platform/android.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_client/src/platform/unix.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_client/src/platform/windows.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_common/build.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_common/src/breakpad/windows_strings.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_common/src/ipc_connector/windows.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_common/src/platform/windows.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_server/src/ipc_server.rs"], "git_node": "6479dff71825d54520abd39342817eaecaa7db7d", "git_parents": ["d5ccd921a39a9bb86264e3bd4a60a5e8b676cf63"], "node": "dd8b4460e7c4a52334d4bfdc833bbbc3d81e7b7d", "parents": ["92af323345a9b4800d695a7e1cc1c88035ff79d3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jon Coppeard \u003cjonco@pobox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061686 - Part 1: Simplify mutex implementation a little r=jandem\n\nThis changes Mutex to use public inheritance from MutexImpl. Despite the\ncomment saying we didn't want to do this I couldn't see a good reason not too\n(and OffTheBooksMutex also does this elsewhere in the codebase).\n\nThis adds a method to add checks around condition variable wait operations to\navoid having to do the checks in that class.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317067\n", "files": ["js/src/threading/ConditionVariable.h", "js/src/threading/Mutex.cpp", "js/src/threading/Mutex.h"], "git_node": "414ed7661cd33aaea7321fe45a9c7632fbeaa050", "git_parents": ["6479dff71825d54520abd39342817eaecaa7db7d"], "node": "163cdf4f02cae038ad9a0d601a017e17e6795a0b", "parents": ["dd8b4460e7c4a52334d4bfdc833bbbc3d81e7b7d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jon Coppeard \u003cjonco@pobox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061686 - Part 2: Split out mutex order checks into base class r=jandem\n\nThis splits the mutex checks out into a base class so they can also be used for\nLightLock.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317068\n", "files": ["js/src/threading/Mutex.cpp", "js/src/threading/Mutex.h", "js/src/vm/Initialization.cpp"], "git_node": "8bc0408963e2adf579b64ff890c9d3198100d22c", "git_parents": ["414ed7661cd33aaea7321fe45a9c7632fbeaa050"], "node": "3276072e69d3ca28db0ddcabdfe8fb52de052a00", "parents": ["163cdf4f02cae038ad9a0d601a017e17e6795a0b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jon Coppeard \u003cjonco@pobox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061686 - Part 3: Decrease the scope we hold the marking lock for when synchronizing JIT data r=jandem\n\nPreviously the marking lock was held at fairly high level, which lead to compliation\nand memory allocation happening with the lock held. This meant we could in fact\ntake other (Mutex) locks while holding a LightLock, which wasn't intended.\n\nThis patch reduces the scope of this lock by only taking it when necessary. It\nmoves disacarding existing stubs into AttachBaselineCacheIRStub as an optional\nstep so it can happen after taking the lock. The lock is passed as a Maybe so\nit can return with it still held. I also had to\n\nIt also splits out CompileBaselineCacheIRStub from AttachBaselineCacheIRStub.\n\nSimilarly the patch makes it so we only takes the lock when necessary during\ntrial inlining. This does mean we will take the lock more often during\nconcurrent marking. I don't think this will be a big problem but we can address\nit later if it becomes one.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317069\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/BaselineCacheIRCompiler.cpp", "js/src/jit/BaselineCacheIRCompiler.h", "js/src/jit/StubFolding.cpp", "js/src/jit/StubFolding.h", "js/src/jit/TrialInlining.cpp", "js/src/jit/TrialInlining.h"], "git_node": "fd13f2cc8fdeaa2c0652031c6024d670ac101f7a", "git_parents": ["8bc0408963e2adf579b64ff890c9d3198100d22c"], "node": "3f0439a2aec89feeb07922bda04c630e6a1c4b75", "parents": ["3276072e69d3ca28db0ddcabdfe8fb52de052a00"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jon Coppeard \u003cjonco@pobox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061686 - Part 4: Give LightLock a mutex order and allow interop with normal Mutexes r=jandem\n\nThis uses the existing mutex order checks for LightLock too.\n\nThis also allows a single thread to hold more than one at a time which was\npreviously disallowd. This is not wrong but probably shouldn't be encouraged.\nUse from more than two thread is still disallowed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317070\n", "files": ["js/src/gc/Cell.h", "js/src/gc/LightLock.cpp", "js/src/gc/LightLock.h", "js/src/jsapi-tests/testLightLock.cpp", "js/src/vm/MutexIDs.h"], "git_node": "39e51f6da13fbb81cdb9f09cb47d9f819c6c6d68", "git_parents": ["fd13f2cc8fdeaa2c0652031c6024d670ac101f7a"], "node": "16c1975fe25086f90e86c79a277892cb7b64d4e0", "parents": ["3f0439a2aec89feeb07922bda04c630e6a1c4b75"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Manuel Bucher \u003cmanuel@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058537 - Remove overlapping addTestTrackers call to fix intermittent browser_permissionPropagation.js timeout r=timhuang\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314691\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/antitracking/test/browser/browser.toml", "toolkit/components/antitracking/test/browser/browser_permissionPropagation.js"], "git_node": "b4788302cf070ca74e46074301cfc0a35fa71b4c", "git_parents": ["39e51f6da13fbb81cdb9f09cb47d9f819c6c6d68"], "node": "a5692a8d7fbffa8285ed5c19a67926cf80c5b884", "parents": ["16c1975fe25086f90e86c79a277892cb7b64d4e0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lando \u003clando@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Merge autoland to mozilla-central\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-and-ignore-on-img-itself.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-and-ignore-on-text-itself.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-body-with-child-img.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-img-already-loaded.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-img-itself.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-observe-after-paint-with-buffering.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-observe-after-paint-without-buffering.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/contain