, "desc": "Bug 2063307 - Declare bypassProxy before usage r=leplatrem\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318485\n", "files": ["services/settings/Utils.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "d472398a6611b1796a502fd7620ae174c2b8d5b1", "git_parents": ["d266b50cb2c90a7a8171872a05a63f856e2ff6df"], "node": "6c11ad2715b81827b6e6d8f0dab9e59c7c812897", "parents": ["c7f53f82f22e3514f6c246328375ed1ce71897c7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anna Weine \u003canna.weine@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055978 - upgrade NSS to NSS_3_127_RTM. r=nss-reviewers,jschanck UPGRADE_NSS_RELEASE\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318505\n", "files": ["security/nss/TAG-INFO", "security/nss/cmd/selfserv/selfserv.c", "security/nss/doc/src/releases/index.md", "security/nss/doc/src/releases/nss_3_127.md", "security/nss/gtests/pk11_gtest/pk11_der_private_key_import_unittest.cc", "security/nss/gtests/ssl_gtest/tls_ech_unittest.cc", "security/nss/lib/nss/nss.h", "security/nss/lib/softoken/pkcs11.c", "security/nss/lib/softoken/softkver.h", "security/nss/lib/ssl/tls13ech.c", "security/nss/lib/util/nssutil.h", "security/nss/moz.yaml", "security/nss/tests/smime/smime.sh"], "git_node": "6513b5e74000c9f6cd105b6bd3a2a8fc4bd92cce", "git_parents": ["d472398a6611b1796a502fd7620ae174c2b8d5b1"], "node": "236f5fc94e62656a01a2f7242c8f060e7e1492b5", "parents": ["6c11ad2715b81827b6e6d8f0dab9e59c7c812897"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chris Peterson \u003ccpeterson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2051730 - replace-malloc is only enabled in Nightly. r=glandium\n\nBug 2052050 removed the distinction between \"early Beta\" and Nightly (in\npreparation to remove \"early Beta\" entirely in bug 2052054). Update\nreplace_malloc_default() to reflect that replace-malloc is now only\nenabled in Nightly builds.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317382\n", "files": ["build/moz.configure/memory.configure"], "git_node": "6b9b8b2f03bb662babda403eea249c883df16697", "git_parents": ["6513b5e74000c9f6cd105b6bd3a2a8fc4bd92cce"], "node": "395d210d0a1112dc20ff175735c5d8c7a8cea47b", "parents": ["236f5fc94e62656a01a2f7242c8f060e7e1492b5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chris Peterson \u003ccpeterson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2051730 - PHC is only enabled in Android's Beta builds. r=pbone\n\nBug 2052050 removed the distinction between \"early Beta\" and Nightly (in\npreparation to remove \"early Beta\" entirely in bug 2052054). Update\nphc_default() to reflect that PHC is now only enabled in Android's\nNightly builds.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317383\n", "files": ["build/moz.configure/memory.configure"], "git_node": "482938ea0e2b44e11dd86a574ab0889ba8022e25", "git_parents": ["6b9b8b2f03bb662babda403eea249c883df16697"], "node": "3444d070fd66d48c403fe851c0c818a94470089b", "parents": ["395d210d0a1112dc20ff175735c5d8c7a8cea47b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chris Peterson \u003ccpeterson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2051730 - Enable GECKO_TRACE_ENABLE in Dev Edition builds. r=mvanstraten,firefox-build-system-reviewers,sylvestre\n\nBug 2052050 removed the distinction between \"early Beta\" and Nightly (in\npreparation to remove \"early Beta\" entirely in bug 2052054). Instead of\nfalling back to Nightly-only, enable Gecko trace in Dev Edition builds\nfor more test coverage.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317384\n", "files": ["toolkit/moz.configure"], "git_node": "f400f9de13b600b28a0205017826db982408d299", "git_parents": ["482938ea0e2b44e11dd86a574ab0889ba8022e25"], "node": "6580a7ab90ea4bba5617928ad33e862ecf3456a4", "parents": ["3444d070fd66d48c403fe851c0c818a94470089b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Watt \u003cjwatt@jwatt.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061539. Avoid clobbering sentinel values of sticky limits. r=layout-reviewers,emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317007\n", "files": ["layout/generic/StickyScrollContainer.cpp"], "git_node": "9e6b8472bef21df35a72f4624df71f2df6ba7217", "git_parents": ["f400f9de13b600b28a0205017826db982408d299"], "node": "d476f0c411e59ed74de9c22d8acc464ddb37febb", "parents": ["6580a7ab90ea4bba5617928ad33e862ecf3456a4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "no bug - update to ruff 0.16.3 r=linter-reviewers,ahal DONTBUILD\n\nno python change\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318503\n", "files": ["python/sites/lint.txt", "python/sites/python-test.txt"], "git_node": "c403f99fd961a956aad7f6b05688d4a233478dfe", "git_parents": ["9e6b8472bef21df35a72f4624df71f2df6ba7217"], "node": "e127fcda51210fbbd906490f6548e044d70b86d5", "parents": ["d476f0c411e59ed74de9c22d8acc464ddb37febb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Giulia Cardieri \u003cgcardieri@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056551: Adjust smart window switcher outline focus and hover state r=emilio\n\n**Issue/Cause**: Previously, we used outline as part of the window switcher hover state for Nova. However, this caused a very wide circle on keyboard focus.\n**Solution**: For the hover state we need a purple-ish circle around the switcher button, but it already has a border so I opted to use a pseudo element for it. I also added a variable to the toolbar button icon sizing to make it more robust and reuse for this pseudo element.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314084\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/browser-shared.css", "browser/themes/shared/toolbarbuttons.css"], "git_node": "d7eb64a2df7aadd9cfee208f866f1b6bad45a6b5", "git_parents": ["c403f99fd961a956aad7f6b05688d4a233478dfe"], "node": "76b575be742c5e298fa0482122a1b1e293de5e8a", "parents": ["e127fcda51210fbbd906490f6548e044d70b86d5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057700 - Don't count a crash the harness logged quietly as an unexpected crash, r=ahal.\n\nmozharness fails a job when the number of crash actions exceeds the number of\nexpected CRASH statuses. A test that times out is force-killed to get a minidump\nof the hang, which emits a crash action, but the test ends as TIMEOUT, so nothing\nraises that limit: the job goes red with \"Got 1 unexpected crashes\" and no failing\ntest, even though the timeout was retried and passed.\n\nHarnesses already mark these: mozcrash's quiet flag is set for crashes they don't\nconsider worth reporting -- mochitest passes it when crashes are expected, xpcshell\nwhen they are expected or the test will be retried. Don't count those. The stacks\nare still logged and the dump still uploaded; a crash on a run that isn't retried\nis unaffected and still fails the job.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318256\n", "files": ["testing/mozbase/mozlog/mozlog/handlers/statushandler.py", "testing/mozbase/mozlog/tests/test_structured.py"], "git_node": "5213dab526cda7367a8700318388d9b7509e5559", "git_parents": ["d7eb64a2df7aadd9cfee208f866f1b6bad45a6b5"], "node": "7b0c5b5e0ecba8c2f50de94816e7256e396ada82", "parents": ["76b575be742c5e298fa0482122a1b1e293de5e8a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056929 - Simplify tab context line styling. r=baku,desktop-theme-reviewers,mstriemer\n\nUse border so that the height is the same with fractional scales.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316562\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/tabbrowser/tabs.css"], "git_node": "4c34e74c0ad0698207e80bc2ed76bda5609cf160", "git_parents": ["5213dab526cda7367a8700318388d9b7509e5559"], "node": "9d5a42b65127a8358805840a074353a09042daaa", "parents": ["7b0c5b5e0ecba8c2f50de94816e7256e396ada82"], "tags": []}, {"author": "John Oberhauser \u003cj.git@obez.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060384 - Creating automotive feature module r=android-reviewers,nalexander,sfamisa\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316880\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/.buildconfig.yml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/automotive/README.md", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/automotive/build.gradle", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/automotive/lint-baseline.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/automotive/proguard-rules.pro", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/automotive/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/automotive/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/automotive/AndroidAutomotiveFeatureFlag.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/.buildconfig.yml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/build.gradle", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/automotive/AndroidAutomotiveFeatureFlag.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/MenuDialogFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/search/SearchFragmentStore.kt", "taskcluster/config.yml"], "git_node": "01da0949f2ed6368d62b17da01c995a0c4fc9e1d", "git_parents": ["4c34e74c0ad0698207e80bc2ed76bda5609cf160"], "node": "55d4e0716bee74782bdbcfff5a56e18bddd1fd39", "parents": ["9d5a42b65127a8358805840a074353a09042daaa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nikki Sharpley \u003cnsharpley@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063028 - Increase account panel width for Nova r=sthompson,desktop-theme-reviewers,hjones\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318179\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/customizableui/panelUI-shared.css"], "git_node": "58455d56c0138aeac98f7ab64c4feaebd96e362b", "git_parents": ["01da0949f2ed6368d62b17da01c995a0c4fc9e1d"], "node": "6d833d7697a5306599f3e8a601de6c46f392805f", "parents": ["55d4e0716bee74782bdbcfff5a56e18bddd1fd39"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicholas Poon \u003cnpoon@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057329 - Make send to devices bottom sheet in native share sheet scrollable r=android-reviewers,devota\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317953\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/share/SendToDevicesScreen.kt"], "git_node": "a3cb7cdccde4ec8c9881798d5d0066028d044f53", "git_parents": ["58455d56c0138aeac98f7ab64c4feaebd96e362b"], "node": "1689b88feaa88b4de9926eed2e1cd4ae5dd6e1fc", "parents": ["6d833d7697a5306599f3e8a601de6c46f392805f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "canalun \u003ci.am.kanaru.sato@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057067 - Adopt a flag to manage scroll-linked effective properties. r=hiro,firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nThis is a behavior-preserving refactor, replacing the hardcoded switch\nwith a `SCROLL_LINKED_EFFECTIVE` property flag. The flagged properties\nare exactly the ones the switch listed.\n\nNote that the original behavior covers neither aliases nor custom\nproperties, while the flag table used by `nsCSSProps::PropFlags()` has\nentries for aliases, which seems to inherit the flags of the property they\nalias. This patch therefore restricts the lookup to ids below\n`eCSSProperty_COUNT`, in order to preserve the original behavior.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316967\n", "files": ["layout/style/CSSPropFlags.h", "layout/style/GenerateCSSProperties.py", "layout/style/nsDOMCSSAttrDeclaration.cpp", "servo/components/style/properties/longhands.toml", "servo/components/style/properties/mod.rs", "servo/components/style/properties/shorthands.toml"], "git_node": "7f6aa8631156a5d9e1d04d227810cfcab13602aa", "git_parents": ["a3cb7cdccde4ec8c9881798d5d0066028d044f53"], "node": "0844b66d8db1ad666cc18b5c1582f27bb4e6c2a1", "parents": ["1689b88feaa88b4de9926eed2e1cd4ae5dd6e1fc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicholas Poon \u003cnpoon@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061755 - Enable the native share sheet by default for all channels r=android-reviewers,gl\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317859\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/nimbus.fml.yaml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/SecretSettingsFragment.kt"], "git_node": "dca712fc03cad43bd4a7395697196389fa5a6f14", "git_parents": ["7f6aa8631156a5d9e1d04d227810cfcab13602aa"], "node": "3184acd32748bcef801da29d9b97a9f1df71328f", "parents": ["0844b66d8db1ad666cc18b5c1582f27bb4e6c2a1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dale Harvey \u003cdale@arandomurl.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057605 - Keep urlbar row highlighted while resultmenu open. r=dao,desktop-theme-reviewers,urlbar-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316761\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarView.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-results/browser_result_menu.js", "browser/themes/shared/urlbar/view-nova.css", "browser/themes/shared/urlbar/view-proton.css"], "git_node": "f9d58d3d6d04f3c9f9f8896cf4dced12c92794dd", "git_parents": ["dca712fc03cad43bd4a7395697196389fa5a6f14"], "node": "e6a8d3d81c2df6cc934c9fff70d7aadb2ffd26e7", "parents": ["3184acd32748bcef801da29d9b97a9f1df71328f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Roger Yang \u003croyang@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063332 - Enable media session notification improvements in Release. r=android-reviewers,twhite\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318491\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/nimbus.fml.yaml"], "git_node": "e66edc4788e179353b4cf9e38437f9dcdfbf8a2d", "git_parents": ["f9d58d3d6d04f3c9f9f8896cf4dced12c92794dd"], "node": "ea24a833f870d6880e52014f73369a22daa8ba93", "parents": ["e6a8d3d81c2df6cc934c9fff70d7aadb2ffd26e7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jon Coppeard \u003cjcoppeard@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2042768 - Remove incorrect weak map marking checks r=sfink\n\nThis removes the incorrect check (that actually wasn't running until recently\nbecause of another bug) and adds more checks that are hopefuly correct this time.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D303321\n", "files": ["js/src/gc/Verifier.cpp", "js/src/gc/WeakMap-inl.h", "js/src/gc/WeakMap.h", "js/src/jit-test/tests/gc/bug-2042768.js"], "git_node": "312c85e601dc9e578082dcd0b09c9849ba51f3c1", "git_parents": ["e66edc4788e179353b4cf9e38437f9dcdfbf8a2d"], "node": "c10ef3050a7976caeaa81570b248be23c06d233c", "parents": ["ea24a833f870d6880e52014f73369a22daa8ba93"], "tags": []}, {"author": "fatadel \u003cafatkhutdinov@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059026 - Improve session handling and evidence rigor in the profiler-analysis skill. r=canova,ai4dev-reviewers,padenot\n\nUse named sessions consistently in SKILL.md and all ten walkthroughs, point at the\nnewer entry commands the walkthroughs predate, and fix the guide-reading,\nprofile-source and daemon-cleanup guidance.\n\nIn the font initialization pair, source the sample counts from commands whose\noutput is shown, and stop asserting mutex ownership that sampled stacks cannot\nestablish.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316239\n", "files": [".agents/skills/profiler-analysis/SKILL.md", ".agents/skills/profiler-analysis/references/firefox-macos-startup-font-initialization-cli.md", ".agents/skills/profiler-analysis/references/firefox-macos-startup-font-initialization.md", ".agents/skills/profiler-analysis/references/macos-extensions-hang-infinite-recursion-cli.md", ".agents/skills/profiler-analysis/references/macos-ipc-blob-url-accumulation-cli.md", ".agents/skills/profiler-analysis/references/resource-usage-linux-fat-aar-build-cli.md", ".agents/skills/profiler-analysis/references/simpleperf-non-rooted-fenix-sync-history-fetch-cli.md", ".agents/skills/profiler-analysis/references/simpleperf-non-rooted-firefox-startup-cli.md", ".agents/skills/profiler-analysis/references/windows-broken-stackwalk-jpeg-avx2-cli.md", ".agents/skills/profiler-analysis/references/windows-test-timeout-cross-process-race-cli.md", ".claude/skills/profiler-analysis/SKILL.md", ".claude/skills/profiler-analysis/references/firefox-macos-startup-font-initialization-cli.md", ".claude/skills/profiler-analysis/references/firefox-macos-startup-font-initialization.md", ".claude/skills/profiler-analysis/references/macos-extensions-hang-infinite-recursion-cli.md", ".claude/skills/profiler-analysis/references/macos-ipc-blob-url-accumulation-cli.md", ".claude/skills/profiler-analysis/references/resource-usage-linux-fat-aar-build-cli.md", ".claude/skills/profiler-analysis/references/simpleperf-non-rooted-fenix-sync-history-fetch-cli.md", ".claude/skills/profiler-analysis/references/simpleperf-non-rooted-firefox-startup-cli.md", ".claude/skills/profiler-analysis/references/windows-broken-stackwalk-jpeg-avx2-cli.md", ".claude/skills/profiler-analysis/references/windows-test-timeout-cross-process-race-cli.md"], "git_node": "9140934113e680465baaf152a551c072d36540ca", "git_parents": ["312c85e601dc9e578082dcd0b09c9849ba51f3c1"], "node": "2b895d82450482eddc93e3401f70837b2e5ef11b", "parents": ["c10ef3050a7976caeaa81570b248be23c06d233c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jon Coppeard \u003cjcoppeard@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061775 - Ensure GC marker knows which zone we're in when marking weakmaps r=sfink\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318433\n", "files": ["js/src/gc/GCMarker.h", "js/src/gc/Marking.cpp", "js/src/gc/WeakMap-inl.h", "js/src/jit-test/tests/gc/bug-2061775.js"], "git_node": "e475305dbfbb2765cc206ca40fa2d309cfb7c004", "git_parents": ["9140934113e680465baaf152a551c072d36540ca"], "node": "f9db7682c311738bb16c49dedf0bd459d163d2a4", "parents": ["2b895d82450482eddc93e3401f70837b2e5ef11b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Justin Link \u003cjlink@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1915251: Unlock rather than force-discard images when a pres shell is destroyed r=tnikkel,layout-reviewers,emilio\n\nPresShell::Destroy force-discarded all of the document's visible images'\ndecoded surfaces (via ClearApproximatelyVisibleFramesList with\nOnNonvisible::DiscardImages). Because images survive in the shared imgLoader\ncache keyed by URL, tearing down a pres shell and quickly re-using the same\nimages (reload, back/forward, same-site navigation, iframe churn) forced a\nfull re-decode and re-downscale of surfaces that were just thrown away.\n\nUntrack (and thus unlock) the visible images instead, leaving reclamation to\nthe SurfaceCache expiration timer. Quick re-navigations can then reuse the\ndecoded surfaces, while surfaces that are not reused expire or are dropped\nunder memory pressure on their own. Non-visible tracked images are still\ndiscarded in Document::DeletePresShell.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313143\n", "files": ["layout/base/PresShell.cpp"], "git_node": "210c13a3cc30a142b9e4a0f399dbfb3d75c7e457", "git_parents": ["e475305dbfbb2765cc206ca40fa2d309cfb7c004"], "node": "bf9fa6dfdb7601da78eadb531844db4864a7390f", "parents": ["f9db7682c311738bb16c49dedf0bd459d163d2a4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjfkthame@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063133 - Update harfbuzz to version 14.3.1. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318449\n", "files": ["gfx/harfbuzz/NEWS", "gfx/harfbuzz/moz.yaml", "gfx/harfbuzz/src/OT/Var/VARC/VARC.cc", "gfx/harfbuzz/src/OT/Var/VARC/VARC.hh", "gfx/harfbuzz/src/OT/glyf/glyf.hh", "gfx/harfbuzz/src/gen-tag-table.py", "gfx/harfbuzz/src/graph/graph.hh", "gfx/harfbuzz/src/hb-aat-layout-common.hh", "gfx/harfbuzz/src/hb-cff-interp-cs-common.hh", "gfx/harfbuzz/src/hb-depend.cc", "gfx/harfbuzz/src/hb-gpu-draw.cc", "gfx/harfbuzz/src/hb-gpu-fragment-glsl.hh", "gfx/harfbuzz/src/hb-gpu-fragment-hlsl.hh", "gfx/harfbuzz/src/hb-gpu-fragment-msl.hh", "gfx/harfbuzz/src/hb-gpu-fragment-wgsl.hh", "gfx/harfbuzz/src/hb-gpu-fragment.glsl", "gfx/harfbuzz/src/hb-gpu-fragment.hlsl", "gfx/harfbuzz/src/hb-gpu-fragment.msl", "gfx/harfbuzz/src/hb-gpu-fragment.wgsl", "gfx/harfbuzz/src/hb-gpu-paint.hh", "gfx/harfbuzz/src/hb-kern.hh", "gfx/harfbuzz/src/hb-limits.hh", "gfx/harfbuzz/src/hb-ot-cff1-table.cc", "gfx/harfbuzz/src/hb-ot-cff1-table.hh", "gfx/harfbuzz/src/hb-ot-cff2-table.cc", "gfx/harfbuzz/src/hb-ot-cff2-table.hh", "gfx/harfbuzz/src/hb-ot-tag-table.hh", "gfx/harfbuzz/src/hb-ot-var-avar-table.hh", "gfx/harfbuzz/src/hb-paint-extents.hh", "gfx/harfbuzz/src/hb-raster-paint.hh", "gfx/harfbuzz/src/hb-raster.hh", "gfx/harfbuzz/src/hb-subset-plan-var.cc", "gfx/harfbuzz/src/hb-vector-paint.hh", "gfx/harfbuzz/src/hb-version.h", "gfx/harfbuzz/src/hb-wasm-api-list.hh", "gfx/harfbuzz/src/hb-wasm-api-shape.hh", "gfx/harfbuzz/src/hb-wasm-api.h", "gfx/harfbuzz/src/wasm/rust/harfbuzz-wasm/src/lib.rs"], "git_node": "54054bb3bf1a5d3b4fd070d209c188169111ca34", "git_parents": ["210c13a3cc30a142b9e4a0f399dbfb3d75c7e457"], "node": "480637258b16af9192430fdc4729795c690f48c4", "parents": ["bf9fa6dfdb7601da78eadb531844db4864a7390f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nika Layzell \u003cnika@thelayzells.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056357 - Part 1: Unify IPDL actor devirutalization logic, and require types to be fully qualified, r=ipc-reviewers,necko-reviewers,dom-storage-reviewers,jesup,mccr8\n\nThe devirtualization logic which was previously used was imprecise, and\npreviously didn't require the type name to be fully qualified. This\npatch updates the logic to require full qualification of the type from\nIPDL, which will be necessary for later parts.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316602\n", "files": ["dom/filesystem/PFileSystemRequest.ipdl", "dom/indexedDB/PBackgroundIDBCursor.ipdl", "dom/indexedDB/PBackgroundIDBDatabase.ipdl", "dom/indexedDB/PBackgroundIDBFactory.ipdl", "dom/indexedDB/PBackgroundIDBFactoryRequest.ipdl", "dom/indexedDB/PBackgroundIDBRequest.ipdl", "dom/indexedDB/PBackgroundIDBTransaction.ipdl", "dom/indexedDB/PBackgroundIDBVersionChangeTransaction.ipdl", "dom/indexedDB/PBackgroundIndexedDBUtils.ipdl", "dom/ipc/PURLClassifierLocal.ipdl", "dom/ipc/PURLClassifierLocalByName.ipdl", "dom/media/gmp/PChromiumCDM.ipdl", "dom/media/gmp/PGMP.ipdl", "dom/media/gmp/PGMPContent.ipdl", "dom/media/gmp/PGMPStorage.ipdl", "dom/media/gmp/PGMPTimer.ipdl", "dom/media/gmp/PGMPVideoDecoder.ipdl", "dom/media/gmp/PGMPVideoEncoder.ipdl", "dom/media/ipc/PRemoteEncoder.ipdl", "dom/media/systemservices/PMedia.ipdl", "dom/media/webrtc/PMediaTransport.ipdl", "dom/storage/PBackgroundSessionStorageService.ipdl", "extensions/spellcheck/ipc/PRemoteSpellcheckEngine.ipdl", "gfx/layers/ipc/PAPZ.ipdl", "gfx/layers/ipc/PCanvas.ipdl", "gfx/layers/ipc/PCompositorBridge.ipdl", "gfx/vr/ipc/PVR.ipdl", "gfx/vr/ipc/PVRGPU.ipdl", "gfx/vr/ipc/PVRLayer.ipdl", "gfx/vr/ipc/PVRManager.ipdl", "ipc/ipdl/ipdl/lower.py", "ipc/testshell/PTestShellCommand.ipdl", "js/xpconnect/loader/PScriptCache.ipdl", "netwerk/protocol/websocket/PWebSocket.ipdl"], "git_node": "858573a9f98f5475fde595aa1ed096cad9384c1a", "git_parents": ["54054bb3bf1a5d3b4fd070d209c188169111ca34"], "node": "72618fb8522f2befe7f99f534a037d486e7f375b", "parents": ["480637258b16af9192430fdc4729795c690f48c4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nika Layzell \u003cnika@thelayzells.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056357 - Part 2: Add a helper method for IProtocol -\u003e actor downcasts, r=ipc-reviewers,mccr8\n\nThis new approach adds a type trait (ActorTraits), and a helper method\n(IProtocol::ActorCast) to perform the downcast. Thanks to the new downcast\nhelper, we can also move the ParamTraits implementation for protocol types into\nC++, reducing the amount of generated code slightly.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316603\n", "files": ["ipc/glue/ProtocolMessageUtils.h", "ipc/glue/ProtocolUtils.h", "ipc/ipdl/ipdl/lower.py"], "git_node": "921967b63237c1092357040c75d69cdbb3c552f4", "git_parents": ["858573a9f98f5475fde595aa1ed096cad9384c1a"], "node": "d36479289c2714004c86c485b1eec280521c34a6", "parents": ["72618fb8522f2befe7f99f534a037d486e7f375b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nika Layzell \u003cnika@thelayzells.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056357 - Part 3: Use ActorDynCast instead of manual downcasting, r=ipc-reviewers,media-playback-reviewers,padenot,mccr8\n\nThere are a few places where we have previously manually checked the\nProtocolId and/or side to do manual downcasting, which can now use\nActorDynCast instead.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316604\n", "files": ["docshell/base/BrowsingContextGroup.cpp", "docshell/base/nsDocShellLoadState.cpp", "dom/media/ipc/RemoteImageHolder.cpp", "gfx/ipc/CanvasManagerParent.cpp", "gfx/layers/composite/TextureHost.cpp", "gfx/layers/ipc/CanvasTranslator.cpp"], "git_node": "0e8f5138c64e500405ff68ddef74de15f66f5a51", "git_parents": ["921967b63237c1092357040c75d69cdbb3c552f4"], "node": "f32b2e411f98f2a3fbfdff2fb1e57cdbb0f8c02c", "parents": ["d36479289c2714004c86c485b1eec280521c34a6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nika Layzell \u003cnika@thelayzells.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056357 - Part 4: Use ActorCast in more places, r=ipc-reviewers,media-playback-reviewers,cookie-reviewers,dom-worker-reviewers,padenot,baku,edenchuang,mccr8\n\nThere are a number of places which were doing manual static_casts to\nconvert from actor types to their concrete types. Change a number of\nthese callers to use the new safe ActorCast helper instead.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316605\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsContentPermissionHelper.cpp", "dom/credentialmanagement/identity/WebIdentityParent.cpp", "dom/credentialmanagement/identity/WebIdentityParent.h", "dom/ipc/BrowserBridgeChild.h", "dom/ipc/BrowserBridgeParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/BrowserParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/ContentParent.cpp", "dom/locks/LockManagerParent.cpp", "dom/locks/LockRequestChild.cpp", "dom/locks/LockRequestParent.cpp", "dom/media/ipc/RemoteDecoderChild.cpp", "dom/media/ipc/RemoteMediaDataEncoder.cpp", "dom/serviceworkers/FetchEventOpChild.cpp", "dom/serviceworkers/FetchEventOpProxyChild.cpp", "dom/webauthn/WebAuthnTransactionParent.cpp", "dom/webserial/SerialManagerParent.cpp", "dom/workers/remoteworkers/RemoteWorkerChild.cpp", "dom/workers/remoteworkers/RemoteWorkerControllerParent.cpp", "dom/workers/remoteworkers/RemoteWorkerServiceChild.cpp", "gfx/layers/ipc/CanvasChild.cpp", "gfx/layers/wr/WebRenderBridgeChild.cpp", "ipc/glue/BackgroundChildImpl.cpp", "ipc/glue/BackgroundParentImpl.cpp", "ipc/testshell/TestShellParent.cpp", "netwerk/base/SimpleChannel.cpp", "netwerk/cookie/CookieServiceChild.cpp", "netwerk/dns/DNSRequestChild.cpp", "netwerk/ipc/DocumentChannelParent.cpp", "netwerk/ipc/NeckoChild.cpp", "netwerk/ipc/NeckoParent.cpp", "netwerk/ipc/SocketProcessChild.cpp", "netwerk/ipc/SocketProcessParent.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/data/nsDataChannel.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/HttpChannelChild.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/HttpChannelParent.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/websocket/WebSocketChannelChild.cpp"], "git_node": "c044e5943d66c077b4ddd31a9870d0a5363574d8", "git_parents": ["0e8f5138c64e500405ff68ddef74de15f66f5a51"], "node": "66da57562b74ea879909936534cdec0f764b9bce", "parents": ["f32b2e411f98f2a3fbfdff2fb1e57cdbb0f8c02c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Christian Grossegger \u003cchr.grossegger@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1698140 - Don't claim PDF channels that have no browsing context in PdfStreamConverter. r=Gijs,calixte\n\nWhen a consumer opens a PDF channel that is not a docshell/document load (e.g.\nopening a PDF attachment from the Thunderbird compose window via nsIURILoader),\nthe channel has no targetBrowsingContext. getConvertedType currently still\nrewrites the channel's type to text/html so PDF.js can take over - but PDF.js\ncannot render without a DOM window, and the rewritten text/html type then breaks\nthe external-helper-app fallback. Bail out early so the load is handled normally\nas application/pdf and routed to the user's PDF handler.\n\nThis implements the targetBrowsingContext check suggested in comment 29.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D304451\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/PdfStreamConverter.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/test/browser.toml", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/test/browser_pdfjs_no_browsing_context.js"], "git_node": "9e8e6f61959b5a990d6ee8d7a44100c9e90d69d7", "git_parents": ["c044e5943d66c077b4ddd31a9870d0a5363574d8"], "node": "bfb93fd71bb6582d4eddef55737c39c6ab923b56", "parents": ["66da57562b74ea879909936534cdec0f764b9bce"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Christopher DiPersio \u003ccdipersio@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063340 - MemoriesSchedulers should wait the full cooldown if not enough evidence accumulated r=cmurray\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318493\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/models/memories/MemoriesSchedulers.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_MemoriesSchedulers.js"], "git_node": "3bae267f925c21405e6ea0642839e2f60572eb19", "git_parents": ["9e8e6f61959b5a990d6ee8d7a44100c9e90d69d7"], "node": "5b35d483dfb84097f01b2a67c33b9ce8fb7b399d", "parents": ["bfb93fd71bb6582d4eddef55737c39c6ab923b56"], "tags": []}, {"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2059026 - Improve session handling and evidence rigor in the profiler-analysis skill. r=canova,ai4dev-reviewers,padenot\" for causing lint failures @profiler-analysis/SKILL.md. IGNORE B