void rounding in nsGlobalWindowOuter::GetInnerSize when this is a system call.\n\nSince the ViewportSize highlighter calls Window#inner(Width|Height) as a system\ncall, we're getting non rounded values.\nWe then display the size with a single decimal, as it should be precise enough.\n\nAlso remove unused nsPIDOMWindowOuter nsresult GetInnerWidth|Height and their\nnsGlobalWindowOuter overrides.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318182\n", "files": ["devtools/client/inspector/test/highlighter/browser_inspector_highlighter-rulers_03.js", "devtools/client/inspector/test/highlighter/browser_inspector_highlighter-viewport-size.js", "devtools/server/actors/highlighters/viewport-size.js", "dom/base/nsGlobalWindowInner.cpp", "dom/base/nsGlobalWindowInner.h", "dom/base/nsGlobalWindowOuter.cpp", "dom/base/nsGlobalWindowOuter.h", "dom/base/nsPIDOMWindow.h", "dom/documentpip/DocumentPictureInPicture.cpp", "dom/webidl/Window.webidl"], "git_node": "8d40e71077335d0a955971133d122fba0a3cf12f", "git_parents": ["1b8d8d6f61fe2f467de26be3036d2d9161248abf"], "node": "02080d28b020a147bb36aa30bc775f046464c1b8", "parents": ["08e9ab8a17800b4afe0fb0ae4ccc69257a6c1ca7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Chevobbe \u003cnchevobbe@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2041622 - Handle substitution functions in InspectorUtils.getComputationSteps. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,layout-reviewers,emilio.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318056\n", "files": ["layout/inspector/tests/mochitest.toml", "layout/inspector/tests/test_getComputationSteps.html", "servo/ports/geckolib/glue.rs"], "git_node": "055aad1198fb836f201039e40cfe2a8ca5c5184d", "git_parents": ["8d40e71077335d0a955971133d122fba0a3cf12f"], "node": "6813ab8e057d998ae6b8243d30d94f46101c2538", "parents": ["02080d28b020a147bb36aa30bc775f046464c1b8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kelly Cochrane \u003ckcochrane@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062351 - Remove outer window gaps of floating chrome for nova r=desktop-theme-reviewers,emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317821\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/browser-shared.css", "browser/themes/shared/sidebar.css", "browser/themes/shared/tabbrowser/content-area.css", "gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/helper_zoom_out_clamped_scrollpos.html"], "git_node": "dfea1bfeb5532fb35faf33da917a8044da0077f9", "git_parents": ["055aad1198fb836f201039e40cfe2a8ca5c5184d"], "node": "68c700a973f2f59d333ac353b964f45d6fc9ecd3", "parents": ["6813ab8e057d998ae6b8243d30d94f46101c2538"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Artur Iunusov \u003caiunusov@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058001 - validate quota object size r=dom-storage-reviewers,jari\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314688\n", "files": ["dom/quota/RemoteQuotaObjectParent.cpp"], "git_node": "0863c9ac9305e1fed901e79192e819685a8fb8d1", "git_parents": ["dfea1bfeb5532fb35faf33da917a8044da0077f9"], "node": "14cd9579274d2541f865b0be74cc4b7454ac26a4", "parents": ["68c700a973f2f59d333ac353b964f45d6fc9ecd3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "pollymce \u003cpmceldowney@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063251: fix build failure with misleading message if you manually move your checked out dir. `topsrcdir` is used in a relative path for `MOZ_OBJDIR`, so cache should be invalidated if it changes. r=geckoview-reviewers,ahochheiden,nalexander\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318504\n", "files": ["mobile/android/gradle/mozconfig.gradle"], "git_node": "4f3ccf788b2dad893c0919dc6cb4d770e61e24f1", "git_parents": ["0863c9ac9305e1fed901e79192e819685a8fb8d1"], "node": "9105fc1da3ce89c47db14d8a12d20f5363b24420", "parents": ["14cd9579274d2541f865b0be74cc4b7454ac26a4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Sudiaman \u003cjsudiaman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053921 - Fix [Windows HCM] Sidebar tab buttons do not use correct or consistent styles for selection r=desktop-theme-reviewers,kcochrane\n\n`moz-button.css` sets the background color of selected buttons to `--button-background-color-selected`. However, this gets overwritten by a rule in `sidebar-main.css`, which sets the background color of any non-ghost button to `--toolbarbutton-background-color-active`.\n\nFix: Remove this rule, so that `moz-button` can apply its logic, which natively handles the high contrast case (both in and out of Nova).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318208\n", "files": ["browser/components/sidebar/sidebar-main.css"], "git_node": "2e85e48e7adab5fd02f4df98d231919f70954830", "git_parents": ["4f3ccf788b2dad893c0919dc6cb4d770e61e24f1"], "node": "1bed1f8ec8c64d41f5844585d393b2cc87cffd8f", "parents": ["9105fc1da3ce89c47db14d8a12d20f5363b24420"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Boris Chiou \u003cboris.chiou@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2047019 - Use intrinsic iteration duration for auto duration. r=layout-scroll-driven-animation-reviewers,dshin\n\nPer spec, if we have a resolved timeline duration and the specified\niteration duration is auto, we set start delay and end delay to 0, and\nwe should just use the intrinsic iteration duration [1], which is the\ntimeline duration (i.e. 100%) divided by the iteration count.\n\n[1] https://drafts.csswg.org/web-animations-2/#intrinsic-iteration-duration\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317960\n", "files": ["dom/animation/TimingParams.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/scroll-animations/scroll-timelines/effect-updateTiming.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/scroll-animations/scroll-timelines/intrinsic-iteration-duration.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "933c8d828aa07af42ebdb64171b797f9adb90078", "git_parents": ["2e85e48e7adab5fd02f4df98d231919f70954830"], "node": "aaa33664e61339ef0e701ae482d07d367d2ccb83", "parents": ["1bed1f8ec8c64d41f5844585d393b2cc87cffd8f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yubin Jamora \u003cyjamora@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063308 - Gate /command palette display r=ngrato,urlbar-reviewers,Standard8\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318482\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_smartbar_command_palette.js", "browser/components/urlbar/content/SmartbarInputUtils.mjs"], "git_node": "84897673353233e3188733570813e1aceb9cfa87", "git_parents": ["933c8d828aa07af42ebdb64171b797f9adb90078"], "node": "83db1b01394c1a77b5e523b935adbe5952b48a67", "parents": ["aaa33664e61339ef0e701ae482d07d367d2ccb83"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063392 - Update AndroidX Compose BOM to 2026.08.00. r=android-reviewers,007\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318533\n", "files": ["gradle/libs.versions.toml"], "git_node": "05c582404dc7be9f1dee37b7bd0d07fad0db4317", "git_parents": ["84897673353233e3188733570813e1aceb9cfa87"], "node": "a0cd05e92acaa0086e1779dbed4f8bfc2ddf341d", "parents": ["83db1b01394c1a77b5e523b935adbe5952b48a67"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Steve Fink \u003csfink@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057458 - Remove assertion that depends on marking only a single object for testing r=spidermonkey-reviewers,jonco\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316392\n", "files": ["js/src/gc/GC.cpp", "js/src/jit-test/tests/gc/bug2057458.js"], "git_node": "d9c12776afaf0492ebcae83f5106642730d3dd35", "git_parents": ["05c582404dc7be9f1dee37b7bd0d07fad0db4317"], "node": "a0b0004d0c47fd173e1ae4b27df39fe4911fca1d", "parents": ["a0cd05e92acaa0086e1779dbed4f8bfc2ddf341d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Swarup Ukil \u003csukil@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057006 - Avoid terminating animation on the display:none root element. r=boris,firefox-style-system-reviewers,hiro,emilio\n\nIn addition to keeping the animation alive, we avoid throttling it while the\ntarget is frameless due to display:none. Otherwise animations that bring the\nframe back, i.e. `display: block -\u003e none -\u003e block`, are never restyled or\nrebuilt and the element stays hidden until the animation ends.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317622\n", "files": ["dom/animation/Animation.h", "dom/animation/KeyframeEffect.cpp", "dom/animation/KeyframeEffect.h", "layout/style/RestyleManager.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-animations/display-interpolation.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-animations/display-none-dont-cancel-pseudo.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-animations/display-none-dont-cancel.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-animations/display-none-prevents-starting-in-subtree.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-animations/display-none-to-display-block-dont-cancel.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-animations/display-none-to-display-block-while-running.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-transitions/display-none-no-animations.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-animations/display-none-to-display-block-while-running.tentative.html"], "git_node": "1ec07df035007fecbf1b12ec0266fe4207546b7d", "git_parents": ["d9c12776afaf0492ebcae83f5106642730d3dd35"], "node": "59705e84703d370540cec9e23399b703327f5325", "parents": ["a0b0004d0c47fd173e1ae4b27df39fe4911fca1d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "canalun \u003ci.am.kanaru.sato@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062805 - Add a diagram of the architecture around APZCTreeManager. r=botond,hiro\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317962\n", "files": ["gfx/docs/APZCTreeManagerArchitecture.excalidraw", "gfx/docs/APZCTreeManagerArchitecture.svg", "gfx/docs/AsyncPanZoom.md"], "git_node": "e96991110303ed2490d5840de3864e1bbdf7a485", "git_parents": ["1ec07df035007fecbf1b12ec0266fe4207546b7d"], "node": "aab413a7816a3a75750d6de29270fd36f50c9298", "parents": ["59705e84703d370540cec9e23399b703327f5325"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kyle Jones \u003ckjones@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060664 - Use MAC for callbacks in HNT TelemetryFeed r=mconley\n\nWhen MAC is enabled route impressions, click, and report\ncallbacks through the MAC singleton instead of directly\nusing HTTP calls. The callback URLs are still checked against\nconfigured allowed endpoints.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316381\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/lib/AdsClient.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/TelemetryFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/xpcshell/test_TelemetryFeed.js"], "git_node": "d91d4aa10b2f95c1656e338c3a6ec4d3b4b13189", "git_parents": ["e96991110303ed2490d5840de3864e1bbdf7a485"], "node": "3c4e8f9f47112b021ce5e1cbe824bd01ca003988", "parents": ["aab413a7816a3a75750d6de29270fd36f50c9298"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lando \u003clando@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Merge mozilla-central to autoland\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "5bc5b565a920f10706d6d75d19dfc6feea3acb0c", "git_parents": ["d91d4aa10b2f95c1656e338c3a6ec4d3b4b13189", "ee8e457ae20efb27313476fed0bed50571c1199f"], "node": "dd8a6a26f9bd8b66e13138be8024f0ef092158f0", "parents": ["3c4e8f9f47112b021ce5e1cbe824bd01ca003988", "70b193e0c1e115fa42422ab1d6afe617f4621919"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Seunghyun An \u003csan55@wisc.edu\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063033 - Do not delete borrowed MozFramebuffer color backings. r=gfx-reviewers,stransky,lsalzman\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318191\n", "files": ["gfx/gl/MozFramebuffer.cpp", "gfx/gl/MozFramebuffer.h", "gfx/gl/gtest/TestMozFramebuffer.cpp", "gfx/gl/gtest/moz.build", "gfx/layers/SurfacePoolWayland.cpp"], "git_node": "d9a1b493c4f318244eb03080f87fcceca739e966", "git_parents": ["5bc5b565a920f10706d6d75d19dfc6feea3acb0c"], "node": "e2019fb7a49891a30fdb5445f44c2634202b0f1f", "parents": ["dd8a6a26f9bd8b66e13138be8024f0ef092158f0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan Varga \u003cjvarga@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057579 - Complete the CSSRotate implementation; r=emilio,firefox-style-system-reviewers\n\nComplete the remaining `CSSRotate` functionality by implementing the missing\nattribute setters and `ToMatrix()`, adding constructor and setter argument\nvalidation, and enabling the corresponding WPT coverage.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314876\n", "files": ["layout/style/typedom/CSSRotate.cpp", "layout/style/typedom/CSSRotate.h", "layout/style/typedom/CSSTransformComponent.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-typed-om/stylevalue-subclasses/cssRotate.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-typed-om/stylevalue-subclasses/cssTransformComponent-2d-flattening.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-typed-om/stylevalue-subclasses/cssTransformComponent-toMatrix.html.ini"], "git_node": "5ae42765670e1c00a9167327c3226ea9fc05bdb5", "git_parents": ["d9a1b493c4f318244eb03080f87fcceca739e966"], "node": "8cab93a7491c77e82f41aaadb79fd59b102e8195", "parents": ["e2019fb7a49891a30fdb5445f44c2634202b0f1f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan Varga \u003cjvarga@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057579 - Complete the CSSScale implementation; r=emilio,firefox-style-system-reviewers\n\nComplete the remaining `CSSScale` functionality by implementing the missing\nattribute setters and `ToMatrix()`, adding constructor and setter argument\nvalidation, and enabling the corresponding WPT coverage.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314877\n", "files": ["layout/style/typedom/CSSScale.cpp", "layout/style/typedom/CSSScale.h", "layout/style/typedom/CSSTransformComponent.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-typed-om/stylevalue-subclasses/cssScale.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-typed-om/stylevalue-subclasses/cssTransformComponent-2d-flattening.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-typed-om/stylevalue-subclasses/cssTransformComponent-toMatrix.html.ini"], "git_node": "453b7d2e1fc1422a53bbf86d8e7896371ebe339b", "git_parents": ["5ae42765670e1c00a9167327c3226ea9fc05bdb5"], "node": "7860c5944acad3d7782675efd1b1ff63bcc12624", "parents": ["8cab93a7491c77e82f41aaadb79fd59b102e8195"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jed Davis \u003cjld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054631 - Modernize principal IPC in WebBrowserPersist. r=ipc-reviewers,nika\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315147\n", "files": ["dom/webbrowserpersist/PWebBrowserPersistDocument.ipdl", "dom/webbrowserpersist/WebBrowserPersistDocumentChild.cpp", "dom/webbrowserpersist/WebBrowserPersistDocumentParent.cpp", "dom/webbrowserpersist/WebBrowserPersistDocumentParent.h", "dom/webbrowserpersist/WebBrowserPersistRemoteDocument.cpp", "dom/webbrowserpersist/WebBrowserPersistRemoteDocument.h"], "git_node": "e5c8c32141953ca406598c26db3696f6ca847538", "git_parents": ["453b7d2e1fc1422a53bbf86d8e7896371ebe339b"], "node": "b66e39095863fc076d5fe74d3f0da3f1f20ce3f7", "parents": ["7860c5944acad3d7782675efd1b1ff63bcc12624"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephen Thompson \u003csthompson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057832 - remove Nova-specific skip for browser_fullscreen_tab_preview.js r=tabbrowser-reviewers,dao\n\nIn 6 test runs, this test only failed 1 time, and only when Nova was disabled. There is some intermittent behavior in this test that is already skipped in Linux 22.04 Wayland opt from bug 1949995.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318333\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/test/fullscreen/browser.toml"], "git_node": "4f76230810e5061e7e70079936a41c119cad6565", "git_parents": ["e5c8c32141953ca406598c26db3696f6ca847538"], "node": "759c89b24508d53c675d9eaec158592cc8bfd5b1", "parents": ["b66e39095863fc076d5fe74d3f0da3f1f20ce3f7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ben Hearsum \u003cben@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063404: adjust watersheds in update integrity tests to sidestep missing mar channel id overrides r=releng-reviewers,Eijebong\n\nThis is a quick fix for the root problem: don't use a last-watershed that would have an incompatible `update-settings.ini` file. Let's land this in short order so we can fix this prior to the next Beta.\n\nIn a follow-up, we can override mar channel IDs to fix the root problem.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318553\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/test-update-integrity/kind.yml"], "git_node": "98c447b7e08afaef9dcc6d19fc09cde00b86ff91", "git_parents": ["4f76230810e5061e7e70079936a41c119cad6565"], "node": "1a7b839bf5c5606fd01bc98a3e7dd98361313306", "parents": ["759c89b24508d53c675d9eaec158592cc8bfd5b1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "hannajones \u003chjones@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056950 - ensure theme-picker responds to external data changes r=mstriemer,niklas\n\nThere's a lot going on here that impacts a few different teams so I'll try to summarize the changes:\n\n* Send theme-picker events to the window rather than directly to the instance to handle cases where we have multiple theme pickers on the same page and want them to stay in sync (i.e. new tab)\n* Add an integration test to ensure the new tab theme pickers stay in sync. This has the side effect of adding some (additional?) test coverage for the theme picker in new tab more generally.\n* Add pref listeners so that theme-pickers will respond to external changes (i.e. directly changing a pref in about:config or enabling a theme via about:addons)\n* Add an integration test to ensure this is working as expected in about:editprofile.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314685\n", "files": ["browser/actors/ThemePickerChild.sys.mjs", "browser/actors/ThemePickerParent.sys.mjs", "browser/components/profiles/content/edit-profile-card.mjs", "browser/components/profiles/tests/browser/browser_edit_profile_theme_picker_nova_test.js", "toolkit/content/widgets/theme-picker/theme-picker-remote-controller.mjs"], "git_node": "6e4002bb2d060f1228f173d9885ca5b4830c38d0", "git_parents": ["98c447b7e08afaef9dcc6d19fc09cde00b86ff91"], "node": "ae2090954a4f1cbce596e53c367b69d8af575f54", "parents": ["1a7b839bf5c5606fd01bc98a3e7dd98361313306"], "tags": []}, {"author": "hannajones \u003chjones@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060950 - ensure new theme picker is shown on the create profile page r=niklas\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316632\n", "files": ["browser/components/profiles/ProfilesParent.sys.mjs", "browser/components/profiles/content/edit-profile-card.mjs", "browser/components/profiles/content/new-profile-card.mjs", "browser/components/profiles/content/new-profile.html", "browser/components/profiles/moz.build", "browser/components/profiles/tests/browser/browser-legacy.toml", "browser/components/profiles/tests/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/profiles/tests/browser/browser_create_profile_page_test.js", "browser/components/profiles/tests/browser/browser_edit_profile_test.js", "browser/components/profiles/tests/browser/browser_edit_profile_theme_picker_nova_test.js", "browser/components/profiles/tests/browser/browser_edit_profile_theme_picker_test.js", "toolkit/modules/RemotePageAccessManager.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "7307b5bf15a71cb3977fd03acfe3f931abb7ac75", "git_parents": ["6e4002bb2d060f1228f173d9885ca5b4830c38d0"], "node": "3cd0e63a161bcb6c2fbd808fadf7b3bd188ddecc", "parents": ["ae2090954a4f1cbce596e53c367b69d8af575f54"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lando \u003clando@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056950, 2060950: apply code formatting via Lando\n\n# ignore-this-changeset\n", "files": ["browser/components/profiles/moz.build"], "git_node": "1c621a7397ee6ce3ee4149700cec58b9b936b7dd", "git_parents": ["7307b5bf15a71cb3977fd03acfe3f931abb7ac75"], "node": "3834d5cb53e1da330ac0898e6e94d031937599d8", "parents": ["3cd0e63a161bcb6c2fbd808fadf7b3bd188ddecc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "longsonr \u003clongsonr@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063211 Part 1 - Make GetNonScalingStrokeTransform return a Maybe r=emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318510\n", "files": ["layout/svg/SVGGeometryFrame.cpp", "layout/svg/SVGGradientFrame.cpp", "layout/svg/SVGPatternFrame.cpp", "layout/svg/SVGTextFrame.cpp", "layout/svg/SVGUtils.cpp", "layout/svg/SVGUtils.h"], "git_node": "3034e694fefb4812c3db8bcc19ef7d56699d1e24", "git_parents": ["1c621a7397ee6ce3ee4149700cec58b9b936b7dd"], "node": "03b804d5f0631bf05c627d7b7a65b110d5d1c563", "parents": ["3834d5cb53e1da330ac0898e6e94d031937599d8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "longsonr \u003clongsonr@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063211 Part 2 - Make GetGeometryBounds return a Maybe r=emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318511\n", "files": ["dom/svg/SVGCircleElement.cpp", "dom/svg/SVGCircleElement.h", "dom/svg/SVGContentUtils.cpp", "dom/svg/SVGContentUtils.h", "dom/svg/SVGEllipseElement.cpp", "dom/svg/SVGEllipseElement.h", "dom/svg/SVGGeometryElement.h", "dom/svg/SVGLineElement.cpp", "dom/svg/SVGLineElement.h", "dom/svg/SVGPolyElement.cpp", "dom/svg/SVGPolyElement.h", "dom/svg/SVGRectElement.cpp", "dom/svg/SVGRectElement.h", "layout/svg/SVGGeometryFrame.cpp"], "git_node": "497fc2b0ad316a051a1c844e1d8c7facc7da26d3", "git_parents": ["3034e694fefb4812c3db8bcc19ef7d56699d1e24"], "node": "79930f2b5f1ff564fdc78d1011d628e32917df88", "parents": ["03b804d5f0631bf05c627d7b7a65b110d5d1c563"], "tags": []}, {"author": "longsonr \u003clongsonr@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063211 Part 3 - Create bounds calculation methods on SVGGeometryElement and use them r=emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318512\n", "files": ["dom/svg/SVGGeometryElement.cpp", "dom/svg/SVGGeometryElement.h", "layout/svg/SVGGeometryFrame.cpp"], "git_node": "25f26e51384528c22df22b86aeb618bc049b6972", "git_parents": ["497fc2b0ad316a051a1c844e1d8c7facc7da26d3"], "node": "449bc712e8dd504009934d536a276f9489821541", "parents": ["79930f2b5f1ff564fdc78d1011d628e32917df88"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kagami Sascha Rosylight \u003ckrosylight@proton.me\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059144 - Part 1: Validate principal and scope for push r=asuth,tschuster,nika\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315347\n", "files": ["dom/base/MessageManagerCallback.h", "dom/base/ProcessMessageManager.cpp", "dom/base/ProcessMessageManager.h", "dom/chrome-webidl/MessageManager.webidl", "dom/ipc/ContentParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/ContentParent.h", "dom/ipc/InProcessImpl.cpp", "dom/ipc/nsIDOMProcessParent.idl", "dom/push/PushComponents.sys.mjs", "dom/push/test/xpcshell/test_service.js", "dom/push/test/xpcshell/test_service_child.js", "dom/push/test/xpcshell/test_service_parent.js", "dom/push/test/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/push-api/principal.https.window.js"], "git_node": "118ce57a07224f1e2ff7583dee8031c6e821c72e", "git_parents": ["25f26e51384528c22df22b86aeb618bc049b6972"], "node": "840b4542151f5abc79f18676dd90df6ac9bbe413", "parents": ["449bc712e8dd504009934d536a276f9489821541"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kagami Sascha Rosylight \u003ckrosylight@proton.me\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059144 - Part 2: Add ChromeUtils.validateServiceWorkerScope r=asuth,dom-worker-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316038\n", "files": ["dom/base/ChromeUtils.cpp", "dom/base/ChromeUtils.h", "dom/chrome-webidl/ChromeUtils.webidl", "dom/push/PushComponents.sys.mjs", "dom/serviceworkers/ServiceWorkerUtils.cpp", "dom/serviceworkers/ServiceWorkerUtils.h", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/push-api/principal.https.window.js"], "git_node": "17d521a2160bda75f18d6f4fe06ff0726d146ddb", "git_parents": ["118ce57a07224f1e2ff7583dee8031c6e821c72e"], "node": "db7b5fe2ed80e6bb766855421cc7b6d3701a71da", "parents": ["840b4542151f5abc79f18676dd90df6ac9bbe413"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kagami Sascha Rosylight \u003ckrosylight@proton.me\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059144 - Part 3: Add nsIPrincipal::IsAddonPrincipal r=robwu,asuth,dom-worker-reviewers,ckerschb\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317509\n", "files": ["caps/BasePrincipal.cpp", "caps/BasePrincipal.h", "caps/nsIPrincipal.idl", "dom/serviceworkers/ServiceWorkerUtils.cpp"], "git_node": "a30c3249cd39f4f44d3707d3861aa4a01212d0ab", "git_parents": ["17d521a2160bda75f18d6f4fe06ff0726d146ddb"], "node": "2e57c5f83d05a5502675457413e045682b522e12", "parents": ["db7b5fe2ed80e6bb766855421cc7b6d3701a71da"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lando \u003clando@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059144: apply code formatting via Lando\n\n# ignore-this-changeset\n", "files": ["dom/push/PushComponents.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "3fb049de28cea67a1b6338629fef12e67a0b9442", "git_parents": ["a30c3249cd39f4f44d3707d3861aa4a01212d0ab"], "node": "0cd4c3788bf771d081b98accc7dce6198216eb88", "parents": ["2e57c5f83d05a5502675457413e045682b522e12"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Cosmin Sabou \u003ccsabou@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2057458 - Remove assertion that depends on marking only a single object for testing r=spidermonkey-reviewers,jonco\" for causing failures on bug2057458.js IGNORE BAD COMMIT MESSAGES\n\nThis reverts commit d9c12776afaf0492ebcae83f5106642730d3dd35.\n", "files": ["js/src/gc/GC.cpp", "js/src/jit-test/tests/gc/bug2057458.js"], "git_node": "d640577f2f27f11192a9d8d53f3ee44121a265e4", "git_parents": ["3fb049de28cea67a1b6338629fef12e67a0b9442"], "node": "c9071d5ebeabbfee57664079a82d837ede3b6a2d", "parents": ["0cd4c3788bf771d081b98accc7dce6198216eb88"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Markus Stange \u003cmstange.moz@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063149 - Update samply toolchain and use jslb for the intermediate native profiling artifacts. r=perftest-reviewers,kshampur\n\nThis reduces the time spent post-processing profiles from almost 3 minutes to just under 1 minute.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318541\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/fetch/toolchains.yml", "testing/raptor/raptor/etw_profile.py", "testing/raptor/raptor/perf_profile.py", "testing/raptor/raptor/samply_profile.py"], "git_node": "59440346a13922e9de91153ff6b1142a9cb92bc6", "git_parents": ["d640577f2f27f11192a9d8d53f3ee44121a265e4"], "node": "0fd253da4e6932e3485514389c63012a9b38cf3f", "parents": ["c9071d5ebeabbfee57664079a82d837ede3b6a2d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Markus Stange \u003cmstange.moz@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063155 - Tell perf to use the monotonic clock. r=perftest-reviewers,kshampur\n\nWithout this, we were getting random offsets between perf sample timestamps\nand the corresponding marker file and jitdump timestamps.\n\nThere are various ways to set this, from `-k 1` to `-k mono` to `-k CLOCK_MONOTONIC`;\nyou have to do it anytime you use perf record with jitdump, as documented\non various pieces of jitdump documentation. Examples:\n\nhttps://firefox-source-docs.mozilla.org/performance/jit_profiling_with_perf.html\nhttps://support.arm.com/documentation/101816/9-8/JIT-profiling-support/JIT-profiling-using-perf\nhttps://theunixzoo.co.uk/blog/2025-09-14-linux-perf-jit.html\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318545\n", "files": ["testing/raptor/raptor/perf_profile.py"], "git_node": "e125b252f5863cfc0a888c8a44735e80959cbaeb", "git_parents": ["59440346a13922e9de91153ff6b1142a9cb92bc6"], "node": "8d5fc8ab5785f3194ca9ec48e23c835e407e4483", "parents": ["0fd253da4e6932e3485514389c63012a9b38cf3f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061411 - Apply a scale transform to embedded-bitmap glyphs r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nBitmap fonts rasterize with an identity glyph shape, so a transform's scale\nsurvives only as the scalar RasterizedGlyph::scale. The device glyph path from\nbug 2044211 multiplies that into the atlas footprint, so a scaled emoji paints\nat its untransformed size: too small scaling up, too big and clipped scaling\ndown (bug 2062234).\n\nWiden the bug 2055177 bitmap-strike gate from \"not an axis-aligned scale\" to\n\"not a pure translation\", so a scale joins rotation and skew on the local-raster\npath.\n\n2056856-bitmap-clip becomes scale(1.0)-only: wrench fakes a device pixel scale\nwith a root scale transform, so at other scales its glyphs are no longer\ndevice-grid-placed and it asserts nothing.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318258\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/text_run.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/text/2061411-bitmap-scale-ref.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/text/2061411-bitmap-scale.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/text/reftest.list"], "git_node": "4e48f9ab6f40f42de1ad3d9b5dd3179b93f03c1b", "git_parents": ["e125b252f5863cfc0a888c8a44735e80959cbaeb"], "node": "a3bde9d0055b325c9abd9b5df623aa7f524ca6b5", "parents": ["8d5fc8ab5785f3194ca9ec48e23c835e407e4483"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063214 - Move instead of copy the CrashEventID string in CrashReporterHost::FinalizeCrashReport r=gsvelto,afranchuk,ipc-reviewers,mccr8\n\nuuidString is dead after the assignment, so move it instead of copying.\nFixes Coverity CID 1700061 (COPY_INSTEAD_OF_MOVE).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318403\n", "files": ["ipc/glue/CrashReporterHost.cpp"], "git_node": "b1b54b0a14ad9fc3f236ae5220c259759cfe9463", "git_parents": ["4e48f9ab6f40f42de1ad3d9b5dd3179b93f03c1b"], "node": "9e639d72dd3ff814b210ab75cc310cdca7ec0b7f", "parents": ["a3bde9d0055b325c9abd9b5df623aa7f524ca6b5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063238 - doc: fix the dead DevTools contribution workflow links r=devtools-reviewers,nchevobbe\n\ndevtools/docs/contributor/contributing.md described getting code into\nthe repository as three links: find-bugs.md, fixing-bugs.md and\nmaking-prs.md, under a ./contributing/ directory that does not exist.\nThey built to href=\"#./contributing/find-bugs.md\", so the whole \"Help\nwith code\" path silently went nowhere. Sphinx does not warn about it\nbecause a \"#\" fragment looks like a local anchor.\n\nPoint the three steps at the general documentation instead, which is\nwhat contributor/index.md already tells readers to do: it says this\nsection \"only contains technical information specific to Firefox\nDevTools\". Note that DevTools patches go to #devtools-reviewers.\n\nbugs-issues.md still split bugs across mozilla-central and the\ndevtools-html GitHub organisation. All DevTools code lives in\nmozilla-central now, so drop the dead organisation search links and\npoint at filing-good-bugs for how to write an actionable report.\n\nFor bugs to work on, point at the DevTools project on Codetribute\nrather than firefox-dev.tools, which no longer lists bugs itself.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318454\n", "files": ["devtools/docs/contributor/bugs-issues.md", "devtools/docs/contributor/contributing.md"], "git_node": "f37ae94413728a0f5d606e116113f4de20c33b9c", "git_parents": ["b1b54b0a14ad9fc3f236ae5220c259759cfe9463"], "node": "b2810f77448a091bd674d2a7da992f55c802322f", "parents": ["9e639d72dd3ff814b210ab75cc310cdca7ec0b7f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063238 - doc: fix the commit message link in the frontend review docs r=firefox-source-docs-reviewers,ahal DONTBUILD\n\nThe link to the commit message guidance was written as a document path\nwith a fragment, \"/contributing/contribution_quickref.md#commit-message\",\nwhich Sphinx reported as a missing myst cross-reference and rendered as\na dead link.\n\ncontribution_quickref.md defines a commit-message target, so use a\n{ref} to it instead.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318456\n", "files": ["browser/docs/FrontendCodeReviewBestPractices.md"], "git_node": "51fa32a6f18058e132f212a681e07d22554bb557", "git_parents": ["f37ae94413728a0f5d606e116113f4de20c33b9c"], "node": "ba31f84d72e35417b6eb3250025fcafe2701c8cb", "parents": ["b2810f77448a091bd674d2a7da992f55c802322f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jack Brown \u003cjbrown@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055619 - Add URLKeywordAnalyzer query-derivation module for the search CTA r=mconley\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313113\n", "files": ["toolkit/modules/URLKeywordAnalyzer.sys.mjs", "toolkit/modules/moz.build", "toolkit/modules/tests/xpcshell/test_URLKeywordAnalyzer.js", "toolkit/modules/tests/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "0ac28bf1cbb6ab595821959e09a8e2fd485b36e2", "git_parents": ["51fa32a6f18058e132f212a681e07d22554bb557"], "node": "3f817da1c03024ba08d75b53c0b515442abbb346", "parents": ["ba31f84d72e35417b6eb3250025fcafe2701c8cb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jack Brown \u003cjbrown@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055637 - Render the gated Search CTA on the online dnsNotFound error page r=fluent-reviewers,desktop-theme-reviewers,bolsson,hjones,mconley\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313114\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/test/about/browser.toml"