planar buffers. r=jolin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D293636\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webcodecs/audio-data-copyto-oversized.any.js"], "git_node": "ce97a78b9dd993a33205495bcd058ddc179db1c4", "git_parents": ["cf68db9f1859dd93d425cf32da92b6724238fd1e"], "node": "f7f8fae922448333dbdd6e8ce233ae04ad8de643", "parents": ["5ace8fc6d4548fe0c42111988e0495c75e02cf72"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chun-Min Chang \u003cchun.m.chang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2025883 - Add tests for AudioData interleaved-to-interleaved frame offset. r=media-playback-reviewers,padenot\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D290713\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webcodecs/audio-data-copyto-offset.any.js"], "git_node": "43d50db6f225428afcf08f0c5986f2291ec4eeeb", "git_parents": ["ce97a78b9dd993a33205495bcd058ddc179db1c4"], "node": "c9623a21623ee8a18b84e6bb63c88a9133a88f2b", "parents": ["f7f8fae922448333dbdd6e8ce233ae04ad8de643"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chun-Min Chang \u003cchun.m.chang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2025883 - Add tests for AudioData planar-to-interleaved frame offset. r=media-playback-reviewers,padenot\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D290714\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webcodecs/audio-data-copyto-offset.any.js"], "git_node": "ae8ba69544997405a80ab4ef9053cc02f330dabc", "git_parents": ["43d50db6f225428afcf08f0c5986f2291ec4eeeb"], "node": "81c164badd59f2b168e95b1528fd68f1eba7b108", "parents": ["c9623a21623ee8a18b84e6bb63c88a9133a88f2b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chun-Min Chang \u003cchun.m.chang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2022604 - Add WPT for VideoFrame.copyTo() canvas-backed RGB stride handling. r=media-playback-reviewers,padenot\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D291010\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webcodecs/videoFrame-copyTo-canvas.window.js"], "git_node": "6a4eff5ff8525d02c0fe292a1dd51962fed3ded7", "git_parents": ["ae8ba69544997405a80ab4ef9053cc02f330dabc"], "node": "7b6a5db6121c9428f60e9463e6525818678d690d", "parents": ["81c164badd59f2b168e95b1528fd68f1eba7b108"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lando \u003clando@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2022604, 2025883: apply code formatting via Lando\n\n# ignore-this-changeset\n", "files": ["dom/media/webcodecs/gtest/TestVideoFrame.cpp"], "git_node": "f83305d74dd629c9c71407bf355e087f946fad14", "git_parents": ["6a4eff5ff8525d02c0fe292a1dd51962fed3ded7"], "node": "a05b8023578662cb17010843d595e55f56388368", "parents": ["7b6a5db6121c9428f60e9463e6525818678d690d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ting-Yu Lin \u003ctlin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063136 Part 1 - Convert anonymous enum flag for transform matrix to enum class. r=firefox-svg-reviewers,longsonr\n\nThis doesn't change behavior.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318367\n", "files": ["dom/base/Element.cpp", "dom/svg/SVGContentUtils.cpp", "dom/view-transitions/ViewTransition.cpp", "layout/base/LayoutConstants.h", "layout/base/nsLayoutUtils.cpp", "layout/base/nsLayoutUtils.h", "layout/generic/nsIFrame.cpp", "layout/generic/nsIFrame.h"], "git_node": "1f6768dfc648b6fa24cdd2344bfcdccb0d1ae4ce", "git_parents": ["f83305d74dd629c9c71407bf355e087f946fad14"], "node": "a91a9c0a057f6c750114690a3821f9e8bc5047ee", "parents": ["a05b8023578662cb17010843d595e55f56388368"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ting-Yu Lin \u003ctlin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063136 Part 2 - Use TransformMatrixFlags to replace bool params. r=layout-reviewers,emilio\n\nNote the param `aStopAtStackingContextAndDisplayPortAndOOFFrame` has an\n\"AndOOFFrame\" suffix. We removed the support in bug 1636071. The flag name\nalready reflects the reality.\n\nAlso, improve the implementation of `TransformGfxRectToAncestor()` by using\n`LayoutDeviceRect::FromAppUnits()`. This doesn't change behavior.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318368\n", "files": ["layout/base/nsLayoutUtils.cpp", "layout/base/nsLayoutUtils.h", "layout/inspector/InspectorUtils.cpp", "layout/painting/RetainedDisplayListBuilder.cpp"], "git_node": "593897eff0e23d9948ee4dbcd4b5bf28afe44136", "git_parents": ["1f6768dfc648b6fa24cdd2344bfcdccb0d1ae4ce"], "node": "43f414ef48f057934831b20499f0d592b037842b", "parents": ["a91a9c0a057f6c750114690a3821f9e8bc5047ee"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan Varga \u003cjvarga@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057579 - Relax the tolerance for the CSSSkew.toMatrix() WPT; r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,dshin\n\nUse a slightly larger tolerance for the `CSSSkew.toMatrix()` test to account\nfor precision loss when converting angle values through the style system.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314878\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-typed-om/stylevalue-subclasses/cssTransformComponent-toMatrix.html"], "git_node": "3e01d0ca6548a1c7c04453eab28c368f98756ea2", "git_parents": ["593897eff0e23d9948ee4dbcd4b5bf28afe44136"], "node": "e2d6eaac526a4d8ef939c16eccd4ae80eb87cf8b", "parents": ["43f414ef48f057934831b20499f0d592b037842b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062145 - Close the downloads panel the tests that trigger a download leave open, r=Gijs,devtools-reviewers.\n\nDownloadsPanel.hidePanel() early-returns while _waitingDataForOpen is set and\nnever clears it, so a pending _openPopupIfDataReady reopens the panel. Waiting\nfor popupshown before hiding is the only order that works.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317403\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/test/general/browser_unknownContentType_title.js", "devtools/client/webconsole/test/browser/browser_jsterm_screenshot_command_warnings.js", "dom/security/test/https-first/browser_mixed_content_download.js", "dom/security/test/mixedcontentblocker/browser_test_mixed_content_download.js", "dom/url/tests/browser_download_after_revoke.js", "toolkit/components/contentanalysis/tests/browser/browser_download_content_analysis.js", "uriloader/exthandler/tests/mochitest/browser_save_filenames.js"], "git_node": "cf506d44bfde9cef61fdf03cc5f0c5248b4c0206", "git_parents": ["3e01d0ca6548a1c7c04453eab28c368f98756ea2"], "node": "98ee82f33c0facfcc05386303c2f4904e59e48f3", "parents": ["e2d6eaac526a4d8ef939c16eccd4ae80eb87cf8b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062145 - Close the account panel browser_avatar_menu_signin_cta_variants.js leaves open, r=omc-reviewers,hanna_a.\n\nThe panel is deliberately held open across tasks here, so this closes it from a\ncleanup function rather than where it is opened.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317410\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/test/sync/browser_avatar_menu_signin_cta_variants.js"], "git_node": "00bdd371baeb6497e1412e4dd1e05cda69ea9b66", "git_parents": ["cf506d44bfde9cef61fdf03cc5f0c5248b4c0206"], "node": "73ec02433e7126c818ecf1403db222be76b49e7d", "parents": ["98ee82f33c0facfcc05386303c2f4904e59e48f3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062189 - Wait for the parent process to register the menu item before opening a context menu in the browserAction, pageAction and sidebarAction contextMenu tests, r=extension-reviewers,rpl.\n\ncontextMenus.create() is fire-and-forget in the child, and nothing in extension\nstartup waits for the parent to finish registering the item - which includes\nopening a kvstore. So these tests can open their context menu before the item\nexists, and find it missing.\n\nAwait create()'s completion callback, the handshake browser_ext_contextMenus.js\nalready uses. It is the only one that observes the parent-side registration;\nsending a message after create() would race it just as startup() does.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317523\n", "files": ["browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_ext_browserAction_contextMenu.js", "browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_ext_pageAction_contextMenu.js", "browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_ext_sidebarAction_contextMenu.js"], "git_node": "e3f81fcb94c16422e2643009af485d88647fdfd8", "git_parents": ["00bdd371baeb6497e1412e4dd1e05cda69ea9b66"], "node": "238b056c52da4faa640be4e5a26fcad273060bb7", "parents": ["73ec02433e7126c818ecf1403db222be76b49e7d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062186 - Fix the intermittent stale about:preferences tab in browser_ext_url_overrides_newtab.js, r=extension-reviewers,rpl.\n\nThe test clicked the doorhanger's Manage button while its New Tab page was still\nloading. openPreferences() does not reuse a loading tab, so about:preferences\nopened in a new one that the test never closed. Wait for the load, and assert\nwhich tab the preferences page lands in.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317525\n", "files": ["browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser-search-and-settings.toml", "browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_ext_url_overrides_newtab.js"], "git_node": "c02ebe1d487482c3ddfdffde9be1c46be1ce4f6d", "git_parents": ["e3f81fcb94c16422e2643009af485d88647fdfd8"], "node": "4d89ec493bd556dfd8ee306c3ec15e2956127f02", "parents": ["238b056c52da4faa640be4e5a26fcad273060bb7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062191 - Use fake media streams in browser_ext_webrtc.js and re-enable it on mac, r=extension-reviewers,rpl.\n\nThe test set media.navigator.permission.fake but not\nmedia.navigator.streams.fake, so its one getUserMedia() call expected to succeed\nwent through the real device path. Only streams.fake bypasses the OS camera and\nmicrophone check, and only macOS implements that check, so the call fails there\nand nowhere else.\n\nRemoving all three mac conditions: this is the macOS permission check, not\nanything version specific.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317526\n", "files": ["browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_ext_webrtc.js"], "git_node": "f22844d2d7c424875ac74b56d88590f8d489e9f6", "git_parents": ["c02ebe1d487482c3ddfdffde9be1c46be1ce4f6d"], "node": "1c346518c67545e5ad04d7a5c5738476f89eb8ff", "parents": ["4d89ec493bd556dfd8ee306c3ec15e2956127f02"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062193 - Expect windows.update() to clamp an off-screen position to the screen's available area in browser_ext_windows_size.js, and re-enable the test on mac, r=extension-reviewers,rpl.\n\nThe test expected an off-screen position to be clamped to exactly (0, 0), which\nonly holds where the available rect starts at the screen origin. It does not on\nmacOS, where that rect excludes the menu bar. Compare against the screen's\navailable origin, read at runtime, instead.\n\nRemoving all three mac conditions: the expectation is no longer written down, so\nit is not version specific.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317527\n", "files": ["browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser-windows.toml", "browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_ext_windows_size.js"], "git_node": "36ffcad0ba0cb10d8348d99fbe0095359e03fcf4", "git_parents": ["f22844d2d7c424875ac74b56d88590f8d489e9f6"], "node": "9121687e582786646983784ba119efa2baf58667", "parents": ["1c346518c67545e5ad04d7a5c5738476f89eb8ff"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2030542 - Wait for the favicon to reach the top sites list in browser_ext_topSites.js, and re-enable the test on linux x11 opt, r=extension-reviewers,rpl.\n\nupdateTopSites() can be satisfied by a list computed before the favicon was\nadded, since toggling the feed pref does not clear the previous one. The two\ntasks that assert favicons then read that list and see favicon: null. Wait for\nthe favicon too.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317530\n", "files": ["browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_ext_topSites.js"], "git_node": "ba2c3a5b0735e67b4fd904a6fd324a9f79c44cf1", "git_parents": ["36ffcad0ba0cb10d8348d99fbe0095359e03fcf4"], "node": "d4422bdf027dfc1d0987e2a25f22591912395811", "parents": ["9121687e582786646983784ba119efa2baf58667"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rolf Rando \u003crrando@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058723 - AITab generation code r=Mardak,ai-platform-reviewers,fluent-reviewers,flod,thasan\n\nFirst patch to enable tool call and template system behind a config.\n\nUnblocks ML Evals and UI/UX template iteration\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314785\n", "files": ["browser/app/profile/firefox.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/Chat.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/PromptLoader.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/Tools.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/Utils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/aitab/AITab.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/aitab/component_schema.json", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/aitab/jar.mn", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/aitab/moz.build", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/moz.build", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/aitab_viewer_stub.html", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_aitab_generation.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_aitab_schema_override.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_aitab_validation.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/xpcshell/test_aitab_parse.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/xpcshell/test_aitab_viewer.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml", "browser/locales-preview/aiWindow.ftl", "toolkit/components/ml/content/EngineProcess.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "18b914c1818605f4136c8ab372a9ea1b07bb7344", "git_parents": ["ba2c3a5b0735e67b4fd904a6fd324a9f79c44cf1"], "node": "542090414df797fc79d39f441a4b669ad0f8d359", "parents": ["d4422bdf027dfc1d0987e2a25f22591912395811"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julian Descottes \u003cjdescottes@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056332 - [devtools-a11y] Update about:debugging Message component to support role=alert r=nchevobbe,devtools-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315128\n", "files": ["devtools/client/aboutdebugging/src/components/shared/Message.css", "devtools/client/aboutdebugging/src/components/shared/Message.js", "devtools/client/aboutdebugging/test/node/components/__snapshots__/shared-message.test.js.snap"], "git_node": "ada8083382d40f809684f1dad556034f6ea24f4e", "git_parents": ["18b914c1818605f4136c8ab372a9ea1b07bb7344"], "node": "d5c3c2219c5d91793b1db399f7c1058ffa42f662", "parents": ["542090414df797fc79d39f441a4b669ad0f8d359"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julian Descottes \u003cjdescottes@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056332 - [devtools-a11y] announce error message for about:debugging network location input r=Jamie,nchevobbe\n\nFollowing the suggestion from @Jamie , adding aria described by and refocusing the input.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314642\n", "files": ["devtools/client/aboutdebugging/src/components/connect/NetworkLocationsForm.js", "devtools/client/aboutdebugging/test/browser/browser_aboutdebugging_connect_networklocations.js"], "git_node": "2ae5cde5a0c9e870f827246e6c0c3ea3125b7dcd", "git_parents": ["ada8083382d40f809684f1dad556034f6ea24f4e"], "node": "f9d1ffed9b329c1f7c7b72138e216f38f91c3afe", "parents": ["d5c3c2219c5d91793b1db399f7c1058ffa42f662"], "tags": []}, {"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2059144: apply code formatting via Lando\" for causing wpt failures @principal.https.window.html. IGNORE BAD COMMIT MESSAGES\n\nThis reverts commit 3fb049de28cea67a1b6338629fef12e67a0b9442.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2059144 - Part 3: Add nsIPrincipal::IsAddonPrincipal r=robwu,asuth,dom-worker-reviewers,ckerschb\"\n\nThis reverts commit a30c3249cd39f4f44d3707d3861aa4a01212d0ab.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2059144 - Part 2: Add ChromeUtils.validateServiceWorkerScope r=asuth,dom-worker-reviewers\"\n\nThis reverts commit 17d521a2160bda75f18d6f4fe06ff0726d146ddb.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2059144 - Part 1: Validate principal and scope for push r=asuth,tschuster,nika\"\n\nThis reverts commit 118ce57a07224f1e2ff7583dee8031c6e821c72e.\n", "files": ["caps/BasePrincipal.cpp", "caps/BasePrincipal.h", "caps/nsIPrincipal.idl", "dom/base/ChromeUtils.cpp", "dom/base/ChromeUtils.h", "dom/base/MessageManagerCallback.h", "dom/base/ProcessMessageManager.cpp", "dom/base/ProcessMessageManager.h", "dom/chrome-webidl/ChromeUtils.webidl", "dom/chrome-webidl/MessageManager.webidl", "dom/ipc/ContentParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/ContentParent.h", "dom/ipc/InProcessImpl.cpp", "dom/ipc/nsIDOMProcessParent.idl", "dom/push/PushComponents.sys.mjs", "dom/push/test/xpcshell/test_service.js", "dom/push/test/xpcshell/test_service_child.js", "dom/push/test/xpcshell/test_service_parent.js", "dom/push/test/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml", "dom/serviceworkers/ServiceWorkerUtils.cpp", "dom/serviceworkers/ServiceWorkerUtils.h", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/push-api/principal.https.window.js"], "git_