 ["be3497e0d0aa464028b7f04f34bfacff3e1186b3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "DrSeed Lu \u003cdr.seed.lu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2039602 - Add a setting for the open tabs hover preview to Customize Sidebar r=fluent-reviewers,kcochrane,bolsson\n\nCustomize Sidebar now shows a \"Show preview on hover\" option nested under\nthe Open Tabs tool. It is checked by default and controls the\nsidebar.openTabsPanel.hoverPreview.enabled pref that was added in Bug 2039601.\n\nThe option only renders while Open Tabs is enabled, following how expand on\nhover and hide tabs and sidebar are nested under vertical tabs.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318262\n", "files": ["browser/components/sidebar/sidebar-customize.mjs", "browser/components/sidebar/tests/browser/browser_customize_sidebar.js", "browser/components/sidebar/tests/browser/head.js", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/sidebar.ftl"], "git_node": "1118cb51cd3c48957c6bfa48652a7ca536d795b9", "git_parents": ["70e75212c48df32fa70b07235746afb79ea5fe86"], "node": "61aa458dd84d9fa5bc4be8a5034f6607a83422ea", "parents": ["103a880c99d9be69b3be6be53daafdcd26e23ad1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Swarup Ukil \u003csukil@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059655 - Update tainted range to be relative to substituted value. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318245\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/custom_properties.rs", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-values/attr-security.html"], "git_node": "5e480f6e4b7c465781622bbf4dbf0e604f2cfae7", "git_parents": ["1118cb51cd3c48957c6bfa48652a7ca536d795b9"], "node": "ead18ec7e299ace85216fc5773be1851aa276df7", "parents": ["61aa458dd84d9fa5bc4be8a5034f6607a83422ea"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060153 - Add the guard to `BrowserParent::RecvSynthesizeNativeMouseMove` r=edgar\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316452\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/BrowserParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/BrowserParent.h"], "git_node": "e423fd5de85f5943696a28ac698fdcb79d9a5f37", "git_parents": ["5e480f6e4b7c465781622bbf4dbf0e604f2cfae7"], "node": "757ad53c305bfb371e7261044d567c743a29e755", "parents": ["ead18ec7e299ace85216fc5773be1851aa276df7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060599 - Make `IMContextWrapper::OnKeyEvent` forget the previous commit string first r=m_kato\n\nIf the input context is set to not editable, the last committed grapheme\ncluster is never cleared. Therefore, the following `eKeyDown` and\n`eKeyPress` events after an editable element blurred will be initialized\nwith the committed grapheme cluster. The value is required only\nimmediately after the call of `OnKeyEvent`. Therefore, it should forget\nthe old value first. Then, the value becomes a void string and\n`nsGtkKeyUtils::DispatchKeyDownOrKeyUpEvent` will compute the typed\ncharacter from the `GdkEventKey` values.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318325\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/IMContextWrapper.cpp", "widget/gtk/nsGtkKeyUtils.cpp"], "git_node": "17d2c129e57b8953ec4d531fbfec5a4a6ff3130a", "git_parents": ["e423fd5de85f5943696a28ac698fdcb79d9a5f37"], "node": "f9e58e025ced46c209d32c6709c58f72a3422913", "parents": ["757ad53c305bfb371e7261044d567c743a29e755"], "tags": []}, {"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2039602 - Add a setting for the open tabs hover preview to Customize Sidebar r=fluent-reviewers,kcochrane,bolsson\" for causing bc failures @browser_customize_sidebar.js.\n\nThis reverts commit 1118cb51cd3c48957c6bfa48652a7ca536d795b9.\n", "files": ["browser/components/sidebar/sidebar-customize.mjs", "browser/components/sidebar/tests/browser/browser_customize_sidebar.js", "browser/components/sidebar/tests/browser/head.js", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/sidebar.ftl"], "git_node": "7dc9a4c9a53f5a65efc3b24d1e91cc93811cbc4f", "git_parents": ["17d2c129e57b8953ec4d531fbfec5a4a6ff3130a"], "node": "9f6a3cee7ce3b435c6dafb0c304f70c10a02edd8", "parents": ["f9e58e025ced46c209d32c6709c58f72a3422913"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Olivier Mehani \u003comehani@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063497 - workflows: pin actions/create-github-app-token to hash for v3.2.0 DOT_GITHUB_OVERRIDE DONTBUILD r=sheehan\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318378\n", "files": [".github/workflows/pr-handler.yml"], "git_node": "3c14eb676e91310d62b1ae58ac66c3c94f08c0cf", "git_parents": ["7dc9a4c9a53f5a65efc3b24d1e91cc93811cbc4f"], "node": "cf137d90e1a7c51fed43a0fc4a12e90744e40be7", "parents": ["9f6a3cee7ce3b435c6dafb0c304f70c10a02edd8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "canalun \u003ci.am.kanaru.sato@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1975760 - Part 9: Refactor EncryptedRandomAccessBlock. r=jari,dom-storage-reviewers\n\nThis is a behavior-preserving refactor. Firstly, this removes\n`AssignFromBytes`, which is used only in a test and actually not\nnecessary. Secondly, this replaces `memcpy` into `mozilla::LittleEndian::*`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310186\n", "files": ["dom/quota/EncryptedRandomAccessBlock.h", "dom/quota/test/gtest/TestEncryptedRandomAccessBlock.cpp"], "git_node": "cedd9d8032f969bb89d79fbf572f5f299dc55a7b", "git_parents": ["3c14eb676e91310d62b1ae58ac66c3c94f08c0cf"], "node": "854ee0ec3e0ec2b806f2d6971d7dc664ec77329f", "parents": ["cf137d90e1a7c51fed43a0fc4a12e90744e40be7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "canalun \u003ci.am.kanaru.sato@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1975760 - Part 10: Refactor ZeroExtendTo to avoid unnecessary block saves. r=jari,dom-storage-reviewers\n\nThis is a behavior-preserving refactor. \"Behavior-preserving\" here is from\nthe perspective of the whole codebase: the stream's observable behavior and\nthe resulting on-disk data are unchanged. Internally it removes one redundant\nwrite to the base stream, as described below.\n\n|ZeroExtendTo| already has a branch that saves the dirty current block, yet\nthe caller still had to save it beforehand. This was because the last block\nindex was computed as |mTotalBlockCount - 1|, and a not-yet-persisted\nappended block is not counted in |mTotalBlockCount|; without the caller's\nsave, that index would point at the wrong block.\n\nSo stop relying on |mTotalBlockCount| here and derive the last block index\nfrom |mLogicalSize|, which reflects the appended block whether or not it has\nbeen saved.\n\nThis lets the current block be saved only when it is actually needed. In\nparticular, when the last block was already the loaded current block it was\nsaved once during setup and then again after the fill; now it is extended in\nplace and written only once.\n\nThis patch also adds a comment and an assertion mentioning that the last block\nis not saved at the end of the method.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310187\n", "files": ["dom/quota/EncryptedRandomAccessStream.cpp"], "git_node": "49eb43b997d97fc23af7ef75f196554f6d6c703e", "git_parents": ["cedd9d8032f969bb89d79fbf572f5f299dc55a7b"], "node": "131004265fb376655d22b2ce7588c227dea9b74d", "parents": ["854ee0ec3e0ec2b806f2d6971d7dc664ec77329f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "canalun \u003ci.am.kanaru.sato@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1975760 - Part 11: Implement the EncryptedRandomAccessStream SetEOF. r=jari,dom-storage-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310188\n", "files": ["dom/quota/EncryptedRandomAccessStream.cpp", "dom/quota/test/gtest/TestEncryptedRandomAccessStream.cpp"], "git_node": "68c18264bfe43b004c6cf883d659f454e5b212d3", "git_parents": ["49eb43b997d97fc23af7ef75f196554f6d6c703e"], "node": "ae7fa612dda2ca923bd56769835c23819018d0a6", "parents": ["131004265fb376655d22b2ce7588c227dea9b74d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "canalun \u003ci.am.kanaru.sato@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1975760 - Part 12: Implement the EncryptedRandomAccessStream serialization. r=jari,dom-storage-reviewers,ipc-reviewers,nika\n\nThis wires EncryptedRandomAccessStream into the IPC serialization path. It adds\nEncryptedRandomAccessStreamParams to the RandomAccessStreamParams union and adds\nthe corresponding serialization and deserialization handling.\n\nSerialization is performed by an override of the instance Serialize() method,\nso that the stream can be used as a drop-in replacement for the cleartext random\naccess stream. The method saves the current block, serializes the base stream and\nthe master key, and then closes itself. Serialization cannot fail, so a failure\nto save the current block is expressed as parameters that the receiving side rejects.\nNote that the logical position is not part of the parameters, so a deserialized\nstream starts at zero.\n\nDeserialization similarly goes through the static CreateFromParams() factory instead\nof the usual instance Deserialize() method.\nDeserializeRandomAccessStream normally default-constructs an empty stream and then\nrestores its members from the serialized parameters by calling Deserialize().\nEncryptedRandomAccessStream does not fit that pattern.\nThe stream is intentionally constructed through Create() because construction validates\nthe backing data. In particular, it reads and validates the final block to determine\nthe logical size. As a result, a valid base stream and master key must already be\navailable when the object is constructed.\nDefault-constructing an empty object and restoring those members afterward would\nviolate these invariants and lead to an awkward design.\nInstead, CreateFromParams() deserializes the base stream and master key, then passes\nthem to Create(). DeserializeRandomAccessStream calls this factory directly. The\ninstance Deserialize() method remains unreachable.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310747\n", "files": ["dom/quota/EncryptedRandomAccessStream.cpp", "dom/quota/EncryptedRandomAccessStream.h", "dom/quota/EncryptedRandomAccessStream_impl.h", "dom/quota/moz.build", "ipc/glue/RandomAccessStreamParams.ipdlh", "ipc/glue/RandomAccessStreamUtils.cpp", "ipc/gtest/TestRandomAccessStreamUtils.cpp"], "git_node": "2370ffcbe260a707a64e67abd181dd064fb215b2", "git_parents": ["68c18264bfe43b004c6cf883d659f454e5b212d3"], "node": "6307e1a0dd52370d28a0629ba4dded0c16c50465", "parents": ["ae7fa612dda2ca923bd56769835c23819018d0a6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lando \u003clando@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1975760: apply code formatting via Lando\n\n# ignore-this-changeset\n", "files": ["ipc/glue/RandomAccessStreamUtils.cpp"], "git_node": "a6f03e6e5e1a57d34860c229a430572f63579f47", "git_parents": ["2370ffcbe260a707a64e67abd181dd064fb215b2"], "node": "ac829d692e6edd1239ea4c3e53150a0d60ddfa22", "parents": ["6307e1a0dd52370d28a0629ba4dded0c16c50465"], "tags": []}, {"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 1975760: apply code formatting via Lando\" for causing build bustages @EncryptedRandomAccessStream_impl.h.\n\nThis reverts commit a6f03e6e5e1a57d34860c229a430572f63579f47.\n\nRevert \"Bug 1975760 - Part 12: Implement the EncryptedRandomAccessStream serialization. r=jari,dom-storage-reviewers,ipc-reviewers,nika\"\n\nThis reverts commit 2370ffcbe260a707a64e67abd181dd064fb215b2.\n\nRevert \"Bug 1975760 - Part 11: Implement the EncryptedRandomAccessStream SetEOF. r=jari,dom-storage-reviewers\"\n\nThis reverts commit 68c18264bfe43b004c6cf883d659f454e5b212d3.\n\nRevert \"Bug 1975760 - Part 10: Refactor ZeroExtendTo to avoid unnecessary block saves. r=jari,dom-storage-reviewers\"\n\nThis reverts commit 49eb43b997d97fc23af7ef75f196554f6d6c703e.\n\nRevert \"Bug 1975760 - Part 9: Refactor EncryptedRandomAccessBlock. r=jari,dom-storage-reviewers\"\n\nThis reverts commit cedd9d8032f969bb89d79fbf572f5f299dc55a7b.\n", "files": ["dom/quota/EncryptedRandomAccessBlock.h", "dom/quota/EncryptedRandomAccessStream.cpp", "dom/quota/EncryptedRandomAccessStream.h", "dom/quota/EncryptedRandomAccessStream_impl.h", "dom/quota/moz.build", "dom/quota/test/gtest/TestEncryptedRandomAccessBlock.cpp", "dom/quota/test/gtest/TestEncryptedRandomAccessStream.cpp", "ipc/glue/RandomAccessStreamParams.ipdlh", "ipc/glue/RandomAccessStreamUtils.cpp", "ipc/gtest/TestRandomAccessStreamUtils.cpp"], "git_node": "5bf08f75b11a53613b6b3770fc0461f5a0ae9dd0", "git_parents": ["a6f03e6e5e1a57d34860c229a430572f63579f47"], "node": "b2d097bb4cdc4bcf55e161942233401220b525a4", "parents": ["ac829d692e6edd1239ea4c3e53150a0d60ddfa22"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Timothy Nikkel \u003ctnikkel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062926. Make modules/freetype2 vendor with its local changes. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nThe revision in moz.yaml still said VER-2-14-2 although bug 2025203 updated the\nsources to 2.14.3, because a mach vendor bug kept the revision field from being\nupdated (bug 2056510, since fixed). Re-vendoring therefore downgraded 470 files. Point\nrelease and revision at VER-2-14-3, which is what the tree contains.\n\nThe three cherry-picks made since then were applied straight to the vendored sources\nwith no patch files, so re-vendoring dropped them: bug 2032039 (fix\ntt_face_colr_blend_layer for a FT_PIXEL_MODE_MONO source), bug 2032043 (upstream\n1803559c) and bug 2038537 (truetype interpreter fixes). Add a patch for each, numbered\nin the order they landed because two of them touch ttinterp.c.\n\nThese are cherry-picks, so a future upstream release should contain them, at which\npoint patch will refuse to apply them and they can be dropped. That is the failure we\nwant: without the patch files, vendoring a release that does not have them yet loses\nthe fixes silently instead.\n\nWith this, `./mach vendor modules/freetype2/moz.yaml -r VER-2-14-3 --patch-mode check\n--force` reproduces the committed tree exactly.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318077\n", "files": ["modules/freetype2/moz.yaml", "modules/freetype2/patches/0001-Bug-2032039-colr-blend-layer-mono-source.patch", "modules/freetype2/patches/0002-Bug-2032043-cherry-pick-upstream-1803559c.patch", "modules/freetype2/patches/0003-Bug-2038537-truetype-interpreter-fixes.patch"], "git_node": "a1986a7396bd3e92103d17e0c6d03e10916dbf99", "git_parents": ["5bf08f75b11a53613b6b3770fc0461f5a0ae9dd0"], "node": "db9e6215859ccd70765d0e5a7772f643c553eec4", "parents": ["b2d097bb4cdc4bcf55e161942233401220b525a4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Timothy Nikkel \u003ctnikkel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062919. Add a patch file for the ots ParseVariationDataSubtable overflow check. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nThe size_t range check added to ParseVariationDataSubtable in bug 2053326 was\napplied directly to our copy of variations.cc without adding a patch file for it,\nso re-vendoring ots did not reapply it and could not reproduce the committed tree.\nThe next update of ots would have quietly dropped the check.\n\nCapture it as ots-variation-overflow.patch and add it to the patches list. With\nthis, `./mach vendor gfx/ots/moz.yaml -r 57df65763716060895afafb1d8a1905aa84c7133\n--patch-mode check --force` reproduces the committed tree exactly.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318072\n", "files": ["gfx/ots/moz.yaml", "gfx/ots/ots-variation-overflow.patch"], "git_node": "55383f3c8cfcaf40484f980e62724b4995b617f3", "git_parents": ["a1986a7396bd3e92103d17e0c6d03e10916dbf99"], "node": "0bcec8743e7d95bab316b5c24742faeeec229233", "parents": ["db9e6215859ccd70765d0e5a7772f643c553eec4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062253 part 1 - Give yield and await ops a contiguous range of resume indices. r=iain\n\nBefore this patch, resume indices for yield/await ops were interleaved with resume\nindices for `JSOp::TableSwitch` cases. This patch changes that so the yield/await resume\nindices come first. The table switch resume indices are collected in a separate list\nand appended to the end of the resume-offsets list after bytecode emission.\n\nThe interleaving made it a bit harder to Ion-compile generators. Before I made this\nchange, the `MTableSwitch` we create for generator resume indices could have 'holes'\nfor unrelated `JSOp::TableSwitch` resume indices. It also required a mapping from\n`AfterYield`-index to resume index. With this patch, the i-th suspend op in the script\nhas resume index `i`. This is asserted in `JSScript::assertValidJumpTargets`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317499\n", "files": ["js/src/frontend/BytecodeEmitter.cpp", "js/src/frontend/BytecodeEmitter.h", "js/src/frontend/BytecodeSection.cpp", "js/src/frontend/BytecodeSection.h", "js/src/frontend/SwitchEmitter.cpp", "js/src/jit-test/tests/generators/tableswitch-resume-indices.js", "js/src/jit/BaselineCodeGen.cpp", "js/src/vm/JSScript.cpp", "js/src/vm/Opcodes.h"], "git_node": "ae7fc3961367ec5e26843fa85bd8d16197317072", "git_parents": ["55383f3c8cfcaf40484f980e62724b4995b617f3"], "node": "b7f89d0b63ab209442dab2459b080782025155f4", "parents": ["0bcec8743e7d95bab316b5c24742faeeec229233"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062253 part 2 - Let Ion's overrecursion check skip the interrupt check for generator resume. r=iain\n\nWhen resuming a generator we want to check for overrecursion but not arbitrary\ninterrupts. This is the equivalent of the Baseline change in bug 2060131 part 4.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317500\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/CodeGenerator.cpp", "js/src/jit/MIROps.yaml", "js/src/jit/VMFunctionList-inl.h", "js/src/jit/VMFunctions.cpp", "js/src/jit/VMFunctions.h", "js/src/jit/WarpBuilder.cpp"], "git_node": "a862c3c9fe0dedfafff08ed0236132fb14b2fb3b", "git_parents": ["ae7fc3961367ec5e26843fa85bd8d16197317072"], "node": "696d1d1781512fcbaf48bb56b9f4e9d6dc8f178d", "parents": ["b7f89d0b63ab209442dab2459b080782025155f4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062253 part 3 - Support JSOp::IsGenClosing in WarpBuilder. r=iain\n\nThis op is used for for-of loops that can yield, and for explicit resource\nmanagement bytecode.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317501\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/CodeGenerator.cpp", "js/src/jit/Lowering.cpp", "js/src/jit/MIROps.yaml", "js/src/jit/WarpBuilder.cpp", "js/src/jit/WarpBuilder.h", "js/src/jit/WarpOracle.cpp"], "git_node": "1adea5810cb30d4f95ad661417e5df084a3e929c", "git_parents": ["a862c3c9fe0dedfafff08ed0236132fb14b2fb3b"], "node": "f95a857d7cf7edf5f992efa8c33fe31f5de66f91", "parents": ["696d1d1781512fcbaf48bb56b9f4e9d6dc8f178d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062253 part 4 - Add new MIR instructions used for resuming a generator in Ion. r=iain\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317502\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/CodeGenerator.cpp", "js/src/jit/GenerateMIRFiles.py", "js/src/jit/LIROps.yaml", "js/src/jit/Lowering.cpp", "js/src/jit/MIR.h", "js/src/jit/MIROps.yaml"], "git_node": "c1384beabbff02b990605da0874915f5dd7ee142", "git_parents": ["1adea5810cb30d4f95ad661417e5df084a3e929c"], "node": "710eb127a4ae2c7aff1e6ecf064880d471e8faa6", "parents": ["f95a857d7cf7edf5f992efa8c33fe31f5de66f91"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062253 part 5 - Redo mid-generator-resume bailouts in Baseline. r=iain\n\nIf an Ion frame bails out while the `IsResumingGenerator` flag is set, we always\nredo the resume in Baseline. The only effectful instruction on that path is the\n`MSetInitializedLength` to clear the generator stack storage array right before we\nclear the frame descriptor flag, and nothing between these instructions can bail out.\n\n`HandleExceptionIon` pops a mid-resume frame and keeps propagating, like\n`HandleExceptionBaseline` already does, because `JSOp::AfterYield` hasn't restored\nthe expression stack slots and the environment chain is still the suspended generator's.\nOnly resource errors can get there: the overrecursion check in the resume prologue\nand OOM from instructions LICM hoisted into a loop's resume merge block.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317503\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/generators/resume-bailout.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/generators/resume-oom.js", "js/src/jit/BaselineBailouts.cpp", "js/src/jit/BaselineCodeGen.cpp", "js/src/jit/BaselineCodeGen.h", "js/src/jit/BaselineJIT.cpp", "js/src/jit/BaselineJIT.h", "js/src/jit/InstructionReordering.cpp", "js/src/jit/JitFrames.cpp"], "git_node": "868cfe120c2658a29858cf194e677b2e3d6f08f5", "git_parents": ["c1384beabbff02b990605da0874915f5dd7ee142"], "node": "1ac66ee7ee35fcde5594d5628aab2509465023ec", "parents": ["710eb127a4ae2c7aff1e6ecf064880d471e8faa6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062253 part 6 - Add a bytecode analysis pass to determine the resume dispatch structure. r=iain\n\nThis adds a stand-alone analysis pass that WarpBuilder will use before MIR building.\nIt builds the dispatch structure for the prologue and for each loop with `AfterYield`\nops. This lets WarpBuilder build MIR in a single pass without having to figure\nout the dispatch structure.\n\nFor a generator like this:\n```js\nfunction* gen() {\n  for (var i = 0; i \u003c 1000; i++) {\n    yield 1;\n    yield 2;\n    for (var j = 0; j \u003c 10; j++) {\n      yield 3;\n    }\n    for (var k = 0; k \u003c 10; k++) {} // no yield =\u003e no dispatch\n  }\n  yield 4;\n}\n```\nthe analysis produces the following data (annotated JIT spew):\n```\nprologue:\n  resumeIndex 0 =\u003e AfterYield @ 11   // after InitialYield\n  resumeIndex 1-3 =\u003e LoopHead @ 24\n  resumeIndex 4 =\u003e AfterYield @ 301\nLoopHead @ 123:                      // inner loop dispatch\n  resumeIndex 3 =\u003e AfterYield @ 174\nLoopHead @ 24:                       // outer loop dispatch\n  resumeIndex 1 =\u003e AfterYield @ 75\n  resumeIndex 2 =\u003e AfterYield @ 110\n  resumeIndex 3-3 =\u003e LoopHead @ 123\n```\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317504\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/GeneratorResumeAnalysis.cpp", "js/src/jit/GeneratorResumeAnalysis.h", "js/src/jit/JitSpewChannelList.h", "js/src/jit/moz.build"], "git_node": "4f10a6002a9aa0aeb91bef2671b938ee23d0db81", "git_parents": ["868cfe120c2658a29858cf194e677b2e3d6f08f5"], "node": "be7d908f5176eb61314eafda2b6c2d54ae4d7eab", "parents": ["1ac66ee7ee35fcde5594d5628aab2509465023ec"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062253 part 7 - Build MIR for the generator/async resume path in WarpBuilder. r=iain\n\nThis uses the analysis added in the previous patch to generate MIR for resuming\na generator or async function directly in Ion. Nothing enters this graph yet\nbecause the resumers still send every resume to Baseline.\n\nA resume dispatch is generated for the prologue and for each loop that contains\nan `AfterYield` op. To resume in the middle of a loop, the resume is routed through\nthe outer loop headers to avoid irreducible control flow. This requires a merge block\nbefore the loop header and then a resume dispatch in the loop header.\n\nThe prologue restores all state except for the expression stack slots. These stack\nslots are restored at the `AfterYield` op when we know the actual stack depth.\n\nThe resume path from the prologue to the `AfterYield` op does not have any effectful\noperations. Like Baseline, the prologue has an overrecursion check but this does not\ninclude the interrupt check on the resume path. Loop interrupt checks are also not\nadded on the resume path because we don't actually loop in this case.\n\nFor an `AfterYield` op with no suspend built, we generate an `UncompiledGeneratorResume`\nbailout to redo the generator resume in Baseline. This is used for example for\na yield or await inside a catch-block.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317505\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/BaselineBailouts.cpp", "js/src/jit/CodeGenerator.cpp", "js/src/jit/Ion.cpp", "js/src/jit/IonTypes.h", "js/src/jit/WarpBuilder.cpp", "js/src/jit/WarpBuilder.h"], "git_node": "c89868e80bec63a5a311643fab50a4ea4b267daf", "git_parents": ["4f10a6002a9aa0aeb91bef2671b938ee23d0db81"], "node": "421d6d5e7647aa1e4cd3eb21c3a39ca963c3916e", "parents": ["be7d908f5176eb61314eafda2b6c2d54ae4d7eab"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062253 part 8 - Resume suspended generators and async functions in Ion. r=iain\n\nThis changes the resumers to let `Next` resumes enter Ion through `jitCodeRaw`.\nThe `YieldAnalyzer` code is no longer needed.\n\n`Throw` and `Return` still resume in Baseline via `loadJitCodeRawNoIon` because\nIon doesn't really help there and might actually be slower.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317506\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/BaselineCodeGen.cpp", "js/src/jit/BytecodeAnalysis.cpp", "js/src/jit/BytecodeAnalysis.h", "js/src/jit/CodeGenerator.cpp", "js/src/jit/Ion.cpp", "js/src/jit/Jit.cpp", "js/src/jit/MacroAssembler.cpp", "js/src/jit/TrialInlining.cpp"], "git_node": "5e81b625437dfc2e21a83c46ad2b83b6cbbc4ee7", "git_parents": ["c89868e80bec63a5a311643fab50a4ea4b267daf"], "node": "74f101306cb27ceed946caef9dca7dd01b0f18b3", "parents": ["421d6d5e7647aa1e4cd3eb21c3a39ca963c3916e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062253 part 9 - Remove MGeneratorReturn. r=iain\n\n`MGeneratorReturn` was a return in the middle of a block. Suspends now terminate\nthe block so we can use a plain `MReturn`.\n\nThis also de-duplicates `LReturn` code.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317507\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/CodeGenerator.cpp", "js/src/jit/LIROps.yaml", "js/src/jit/Lowering.cpp", "js/src/jit/Lowering.h", "js/src/jit/MIROps.yaml", "js/src/jit/WarpBuilder.cpp", "js/src/jit/arm/Lowering-arm.cpp", "js/src/jit/arm64/Lowering-arm64.cpp", "js/src/jit/loong64/Lowering-loong64.cpp", "js/src/jit/mips64/Lowering-mips64.cpp", "js/src/jit/riscv64/Lowering-riscv64.cpp", "js/src/jit/shared/LIR-shared.h", "js/src/jit/shared/Lowering-shared-inl.h", "js/src/jit/shared/Lowering-shared.h", "js/src/jit/x64/Lowering-x64.cpp", "js/src/jit/x86/Lowering-x86.cpp"], "git_node": "02588fd152a913a2c7c0e7fba16a2b71bfb3a41b", "git_parents": ["5e81b625437dfc2e21a83c46ad2b83b6cbbc4ee7"], "node": "be8a36e4d0a7b566059148107f5dc60110d17643", "parents": ["74f101306cb27ceed946caef9dca7dd01b0f18b3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062253 part 10 - Add tests. r=iain\n\nThis adds a collection of jit-tests with `--fast-warmup --no-threads` to make sure\na default jit-test run has decent coverage of Ion-generator-resume edge cases.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317508\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/generators/resume-arguments.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/generators/resume-basic.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/generators/resume-debugger.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/generators/resume-dispatch.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/generators/resume-finally.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/generators/resume-iterators.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/generators/resume-loops.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/generators/resume-prebarrier.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/generators/resume-tdz.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/generators/resume-this-super.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/generators/resume-using.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/generators/resume-yield-star.js"], "git_node": "06f7ee29c6c7880bf3b952c2d7e399e4026ee1bc", "git_parents": ["02588fd152a913a2c7c0e7fba16a2b71bfb3a41b"], "node": "ae7d905c697d127ffbbf93fb055ff682e6c4a9a5", "parents": ["be8a36e4d0a7b566059148107f5dc60110d17643"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tim Elliott \u003ctle@holymonkey.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2033250 - Use libjpeg-turbo IDCT scaling to reduce JPEG decode cost when downscaling. r=gfx-reviewers,tnikkel\n\nWhen a JPEG is being decoded to a significantly smaller output size, ask\nlibjpeg-turbo to produce a 1/2, 1/4, or 1/8 scaled intermediate via its IDCT\nscaling rather than decoding at full resolution and discarding most of the\ndata in the downscaling filter. The SurfacePipe is fed the scaled dimensions\nand Lanczos3 finishes the job.\n\nRestricted to images whose dimensions are a whole number of MCUs; otherwise\npadding in the trailing MCU row/column can smear into visible pixels at\nreduced scales (crbug.com/890745, libjpeg-turbo issue 297).\n\nGated by image.jpeg.dct-scaling.enabled (default off) with\nimage.jpeg.dct-scaling.min-factor controlling how much downscaling to leave\nfor Lanczos (default 2.5x).\n\nAdds DownscaleDctOn/DownscaleDctOff gtest benchmarks.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D295157\n", "files": ["image/decoders/nsJPEGDecoder.cpp", "image/test/gtest/Common.cpp", "image/test/gtest/Common.h", "image/test/gtest/TestDecoders.cpp", "image/test/gtest/TestDecodersPerf.cpp", "image/test/gtest/green-exif-orient6.jpg", "image/test/gtest/moz.build", "image/test/reftest/downscaling/downscale-dct-ref.html", "image/test/reftest/downscaling/downscale-dct.html", "image/test/reftest/downscaling/lime-red-16px.png", "image/test/reftest/downscaling/lime-red-8px.png", "image/test/reftest/downscaling/reftest.list", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "4b22885afbab433a257974c3a9569f9257bb24d6", "git_parents": ["06f7ee29c6c7880bf3b952c2d7e399e4026ee1bc"], "node": "58b73c16f4eb70fd0e92b9c4fc6617709e6fb743", "parents": ["ae7d905c697d127ffbbf93fb055ff682e6c4a9a5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Bone \u003cpbone@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2004862 - Remove randomised arena IDs r=glandium\n\nThis has been running on release for 6 months, we can remove the old\ncode paths now.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316694\n", "files": ["memory/build/moz.build", "memory/build/mozjemalloc.cpp"], "git_node": "41d3739808278ad9ed0d50f61f3e848cb61eb7bc", "git_parents": ["4b22885afbab433a257974c3a9569f9257bb24d6"], "node": "edf899bd9b005f0737be2063dcdc7edf8a32be2b", "parents": ["58b73c16f4eb70fd0e92b9c4fc6617709e6fb743"], "tags": []}, {"author": "canalun \u003ci.am.kanaru.sato@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1975760 - Part 9: Refactor EncryptedRandomAccessBlock. r=jari,dom-storage-reviewers\n\nThis is a behavior-preserving refactor. Firstly, this removes\n`AssignFromBytes`, which is used only in a test and actually not\nnecessary. Secondly, this replaces `memcpy` into `mozilla::LittleEndian::*`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310186\n", "files": ["dom/quota/EncryptedRandomAccessBlock.h", "dom/quota/test/gtest/TestEncryptedRandomAccessBlock.cpp"], "git_node": "df15655e269eb0b992efedcf4a5ad293f48dafbe", "git_parents": ["41d3739808278ad9ed0d50f61f3e848cb61eb7bc"], "node": "38371725cc14659fcb08cab6b076760ac338e2c2", "parents": ["edf899bd9b005f0737be2063dcdc7edf8a32be2b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "canalun \u003ci.am.kanaru.sato@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1975760 - Part 10: Refactor ZeroExtendTo to avoid unnecessary block saves. r=jari,dom-storage-reviewers\n\nThis is a behavior-preserving refactor. \"Behavior-preserving\" here is from\nthe perspective of the whole codebase: the stream's observable behavior and\nthe resulting on-disk data are unchanged. Internally it removes one redundant\nwrite to the base stream, as described below.\n\n|ZeroExtendTo| already has a branch that saves the dirty current block, yet\nthe caller still had to save it beforehand. This was because the last block\nindex was computed as |mTotalBlockCount - 1|, and a not-yet-persisted\nappended block is not counted in |mTotalBlockCount|; without the caller's\nsave, that index would point at the wrong block.\n\nSo stop relying on |mTotalBlockCount| here and derive the last block index\nfrom |mLogicalSize|, which reflects the appended block whether or not it has\nbeen saved.\n\nThis lets the current block be saved only when it is actually needed. In\nparticular, when the last block was already the loaded current block it was\nsaved once during setup and then again after the fill; now it is extended in\nplace and written only once.\n\nThis patch also adds a comment and an assertion mentioning that the last block\nis not saved at the end of the method.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310187\n", "files": ["dom/quota/EncryptedRandomAccessStream.cpp"], "git_node": "8d196821d1f4b80c3d9f7b1c7a2994a85e9f16b9", "git_parents": ["df15655e269eb0b992efedcf4a5ad293f48dafbe"], "node": "58601b81ff5e52a5808c054f1b8648f2504fb43f", "parents": ["38371725cc14659fcb08cab6b076760ac338e2c2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "canalun \u003ci.am.kanaru.sato@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1975760 - Part 11: Implement the EncryptedRandomAccessStream SetEOF. r=jari,dom-storage-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310188\n", "files": ["dom/quota/EncryptedRandomAccessStream.cpp", "dom/quota/test/gtest/TestEncryptedRandomAccessStream.cpp"], "git_node": "9ff845594e28dbbe677f6c867cc19d3a00ebf323", "git_parents": ["8d196821d1f4b80c3d9f7b1c7a2994a85e9f16b9"], "node": "4817385ee892eecf778a2ca01e2bd522c3b2cf80", "parents": ["58601b81ff5e52a5808c054f1b8648f2504fb43f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "canalun \u003ci.am.kanaru.sato@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1975760 - Part 12: Implement the EncryptedRandomAccessStream serialization. r=jari,dom-storage-reviewers,ipc-reviewers,nika\n\nThis wires EncryptedRandomAccessStream into the IPC serialization path. It adds\nEncryptedRandomAccessStreamParams to the RandomAccessStreamParams union and adds\nthe corresponding serialization and deserialization handling.\n\nSerialization is performed by an override of the instance Serialize() method,\nso that the stream can be used as a drop-in replacement for the cleartext random\naccess stream. The method saves the current block, serializes the base stream and\nthe master key, and then closes itself. Serialization cannot fail, so a failure\nto save the current block is expressed as parameters that the receiving side rejects.\nNote that the logical position is not part of the parameters, so a deserialized\nstream starts at zero.\n\nDeserialization similarly goes through the static CreateFromParams() factory instead\nof the usual instance Deserialize() method.\nDeserializeRandomAccessStream normally default-constructs an empty stream and then\nrestores its members from the serialized parameters by calling Deserialize().\nEncryptedRandomAccessStream does not fit that pattern.\nThe stream is intentionally constructed through Create() because construction validates\nthe backing data. In particular, it reads and validates the final block to determine\nthe logical size. As a result, a valid base stream and master key must already be\navailable when the object is constructed.\nDefault-constructing an empty object and restoring those members afterward would\nviolate these invariants and lead to an awkward design.\nInstead, CreateFromParams() deserializes the base stream and master key, then passes\nthem to Create(). DeserializeRandomAccessStream calls this factory directly. The\ninstance Deserialize() method remains unreachable.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310747\n", "files": ["dom/quota/EncryptedRandomAccessStream.cpp", "dom/quota/EncryptedRandomAccessStream.h", "dom/quota/EncryptedRandomAccessStream_impl.h", "dom/quota/moz.build", "ipc/glue/RandomAccessStreamParams.ipdlh", "ipc/glue/RandomAccessStreamUtils.cpp", "ipc/gtest/TestRandomAccessStreamUtils.cpp"], "git_node": "f360de8050f0678b4a31f9b1fe3fafd14c3280e5", "git_parents": ["9ff845594e28dbbe677f6c867cc19d3a00ebf323"], "node": "91c101f2ed498716603662fc7e8d9f889a0fee38", "parents": ["4817385ee892eecf778a2ca01e2bd522c3b2cf80"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lando \u003clando@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1975760: apply code formatting via Lando\n\n# ignore-this-changeset\n", "files": ["ipc/glue/RandomAccessStreamUtils.cpp"], "git_node": "8e42adb00f0d301d1b74f71d5f7d49228eb712c9", "git_parents": ["f360de8050f0678b4a31f9b1fe3fafd14c3280e5"], "node": "477c0df9965c2460b1582048e8ff9cb333dd2556", "parents": ["91c101f2ed498716603662fc7e8d9f889a0fee38"], "tags": []}], "date": 1786698151, "git_changesets": ["bfa4adcb4fc1c12e0338f43c1837371b373dfde4", "70e75212c48df32fa70b07235746afb79ea5fe86", "1118cb51cd3c48957c6bfa48652a7ca536d795b9", "5e480f6e4b7c465781622bbf4dbf0e604f2cfae7", "e423fd5de85f5943696a28ac698fdcb79d9a5f37", "17d2c129e57b8953ec4d531fbfec5a4a6ff3130a", "7dc9a4c9a53f5a65efc3b24d1e91cc93811cbc4f", "3c14eb676e91310d62b1ae58ac66c3c94f08c0cf", "cedd9d8032f969bb89d79fbf572f5f299dc55a7b", "49eb43b997d97fc23af7ef75f196554f6d6c703e", "68c18264bfe43b004c6cf883d659f454e5b212d3", "2370ffcbe260a707a64e67abd181dd064fb215b2", "a6f03e6e5e1a57d34860c229a430572f63579f47", "5bf08f75b11a53613b6b3770fc0461f5a0ae9dd0", "a1986a7396bd3e92103d17e0c6d03e10916dbf99", "55383f3c8cfcaf40484f980e62724b4995b617f3", "ae7fc3961367ec5e26843fa85bd8d16197317072", "a862c3c9fe0dedfafff08ed0236132fb14b2fb3b", "1adea5810cb30d4f95ad661417e5df084a3e929c", "c1384beabbff02b990605da0874915f5dd7ee142", "868cfe120c2658a29858cf194e677b2e3d6f08f5", "4f10a6002a9aa0aeb91bef2671b938ee23d0db81", "c89868e80bec63a5a311643fab50a4ea4b267daf", "5e81b625437dfc2e21a83c46ad2b83b6cbbc4ee7", "02588fd152a913a2c7c0e7fba16a2b71bfb3a41b", "06f7ee29c6c7880bf3b952c2d7e399e4026ee1bc", "4b22885afbab433a257974c3a9569f9257bb24d6", "41d3739808278ad9ed0d50f61f3e848cb61eb7bc", "df15655e269eb0b992efedcf4a5ad293f48dafbe", "8d196821d1f4b80c3d9f7b1c7a2994a85e9f16b9", "9ff845594e28dbbe677f6c867cc19d3a00ebf323", "f360de8050f0678b4a31f9b1fe3fafd14c3280e5", "8e42adb00f0d301d1b74f71d5f7d49228eb712c9"], "user": "sstanca@mozilla.com"}, "45098": {"changesets": [{"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062189 - Wait for the parent process to register the menu item before opening a context menu in the browserAction, pageAction and sidebarAction contextMenu tests, r=extension-reviewers,rpl.\n\ncontextMenus.create() is fire-and-forget in the child, and nothing in extension\nstartup waits for the parent to finish registering the item - which includes\nopening a kvstore. So these tests can open their context menu before the item\nexists, and find it missing.\n\nAwait create()'s completion callback, the handshake browser_ext_contextMenus.js\nalready uses. It is the only one that observes the parent-side registration;\nsending a message after create() would race it just as startup() does.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317523\n", "files": ["browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_ext_browserAction_contextMenu.js", "browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_ext_pageAction_contextMenu.js", "browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_ext_sidebarAction_contextMenu.js"], "git_node": "ed9b06b03ccc861c376b2fcaaf78b65a75bc6048", "git_parents": ["8e42adb00f0d301d1b74f71d5f7d49228eb712c9"], "node": "64608ae1358718234c1312ce5629c14eb175272e", "parents": ["477c0df9965c2460b1582048e8ff9cb333dd2556"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062191 - Use fake media streams in browser_ext_webrtc.js and re-enable it on mac, r=extension-reviewers,rpl.\n\nThe test set media.navigator.permission.fake but not\nmedia.navigator.streams.fake, so its one getUserMedia() call expected to succeed\nwent through the real device path. Only streams.fake bypasses the OS camera and\nmicrophone check, and only macOS implements that check, so the call fails there\nand nowhere else.\n\nRemoving all three mac conditions: this is the macOS permission check, not\nanything version specific.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317526\n", "files": ["browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_ext_webrtc.js"], "git_node": "34deaa65f4f10f1f5d49e8dd6f3b20234c5706f1", "git_parents": ["ed9b06b03ccc861c376b2fcaaf78b65a75bc6048"], "node": "7b82bb96779488c1312afad3393b44baa30898ce", "parents": ["64608ae1358718234c1312ce5629c14eb175272e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062193 - Expect windows.update() to clamp an off-screen position to the screen's available area in browser_ext_windows_size.js, and re-enable the test on mac, r=extension-reviewers,rpl.\n\nThe test expected an off-screen position to be clamped to exactly (0, 0), which\nonly holds where the available rect starts at the screen origin. It does not on\nmacOS, where that rect excludes the menu bar. Compare against the screen's\navailable origin, read at runtime, instead.\n\nRemoving all three mac conditions: the expectation is no longer written down, so\nit is not version specific.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317527\n", "files": ["browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser-windows.toml", "browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_ext_windows_size.js"], "git_node": "10e4e7321bea742dcb66b0ba80016f3c1f6f9c8c", "git_parents": ["34deaa65f4f10f1f5d49e8dd6f3b20234c5706f1"], "node": "f6343b76a0ea67034f7ec92deb69ebf31e8b835b", "parents": ["7b82bb96779488c1312afad3393b44baa30898ce"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2030542 - Wait for the favicon to reach the top sites list in browser_ext_topSites.js, and re-enable the test on linux x11 opt, r=extension-reviewers,rpl.\n\nupdateTopSites() can be satisfied by a list computed before the favicon was\nadded, since toggling the feed pref does not clear the previous one. The two\ntasks that assert favicons then read that list and see favicon: null. Wait for\nthe favicon too.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317530\n", "files": ["browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_ext_topSites.js"], "git_node": "3bf6ea5cdc4d39ebaf222c42553fba5f85747080", "git_parents": ["10e4e7321bea742dcb66b0ba80016f3c1f6f9c8c"], "node": "1e939c43d704edefab5cd8716782e4ad9da4b3f6", "parents": ["f6343b76a0ea67034f7ec92deb69ebf31e8b835b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Release Engineering Landoscript \u003crelease+landoscript@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug - Bumping Firefox l10n changesets r=release a=l10n-bump DONTBUILD CLOSED TREE\n\nach -\u003e 8ddea90b283e727853c3c1bb2632179c56f59a01\naf -\u003e 8ddea90b283e727853c3c1bb2632179c56f59a01\nan -\u003e 8ddea90b283e727853c3c1bb2632179c56f59a01\nar -\u003e 8ddea90b283e727853c3c1bb2632179c56f59a01\nast -\u003e 8ddea90b283e727853c3c1bb2632179c56f59a01\naz -\u003e 8ddea90b283e727853c3c1bb2632179c56f59a01\nbe -\u003e 8ddea90b283e727853c3c1bb263217