95f35192bd7f8c0e7e82be5a272da19b57"], "tags": []}, {"author": "iain holmes \u003ciholmes@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053447: Part 5 - Update for enterprise policies.r=mkaply\n\nUpdate to support the DisableLaunchOnLogin enterprise policy\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316049\n", "files": ["browser/components/enterprisepolicies/Policies.sys.mjs", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/browser/browser_policy_disable_launch_on_login.js", "toolkit/modules/launchonlogin/LaunchOnLogin.sys.mjs", "toolkit/modules/launchonlogin/UnsupportedLaunchOnLogin.sys.mjs", "toolkit/modules/launchonlogin/WindowsLaunchOnLogin.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "f7b5903422837ea876645d1e574f49b8e3a6003b", "git_parents": ["6ec82897da0e79cfcdb5bf348c0f7f6b0768c3f5"], "node": "525b3a315a76b5f95ec7116097c82a044e4d3429", "parents": ["bff88be5fd0b576e23f6cc0c5b156cd8bb1774c0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "longsonr \u003clongsonr@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063531 - Use matrix.Inverse rather than matrix.Invert when it is simpler r=firefox-svg-reviewers,dholbert\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318694\n", "files": ["layout/svg/FilterInstance.cpp", "layout/svg/SVGClipPathFrame.cpp", "layout/svg/SVGGeometryFrame.cpp", "layout/svg/SVGIntegrationUtils.cpp", "layout/svg/SVGTextFrame.cpp", "layout/svg/SVGUtils.cpp"], "git_node": "62e02c60f21e2ac405f24dc407c691867055f2e6", "git_parents": ["f7b5903422837ea876645d1e574f49b8e3a6003b"], "node": "b52af339bf0c3136850fbd8fc90bab6695a50fb6", "parents": ["525b3a315a76b5f95ec7116097c82a044e4d3429"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Kaply \u003cmozilla@kaply.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2041238 - Hide unified extensions panel \"Discover extensions\" button when discopane is disabled. r=extension-reviewers,robwu\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318247\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser-addons.js", "browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_unified_extensions_empty_panel.js"], "git_node": "2d9ed3886eeb4016786b9d18d0295b2b73a05667", "git_parents": ["62e02c60f21e2ac405f24dc407c691867055f2e6"], "node": "9c4832c131adb8e78b99aa0ea130d92a2b1c8c6f", "parents": ["b52af339bf0c3136850fbd8fc90bab6695a50fb6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "t-p-white \u003ctowhite@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062950 - Move default browser prompt gating into DefaultBrowserPromptManager. r=android-reviewers,alastun,aaronmt\n\n**Fix**\n* Folded the Nimbus enabled check into `canShowPrompt()` alongside the existing device-capable, not-already-default, and not-yet-shown checks, instead of gating on it separately in `OnboardingFragment`.\n* Add tests covering the enabled-flag case and the `maybePromptToSetAsDefaultBrowser` integration path.\n\n**Expected behaviour**\nThe set to default system prompt should be shown during onboarding when:\n  - the device is capable\n  - the onboarding card is the set to default card\n  - Firefox (current build) is not already default browser\n  - the set to default prompt is enabled\n  - the prompt has not already been shown during onboarding\n\n{F77595754}\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318095\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/OverlayRegistry.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/onboarding/DefaultBrowserPromptManager.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/onboarding/OnboardingFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/onboarding/DefaultBrowserPromptManagerTest.kt"], "git_node": "266b2dc3530aa7ec1705745e705b34d76199310d", "git_parents": ["2d9ed3886eeb4016786b9d18d0295b2b73a05667"], "node": "18e8ecfa857f6b0ace77e74237551ae3f1380f2a", "parents": ["9c4832c131adb8e78b99aa0ea130d92a2b1c8c6f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephen Thompson \u003csthompson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057856 - skip browser_sizemodeBeforeMinimized.js on Linux 22.04 r=sclements\n\nConfirmed that this test times out when minimizing a maximized window in all tested configurations of Linux 22.04 Wayland:\n\n- opt or debug\n- Nova enabled or Nova disabled\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318328\n", "files": ["browser/components/sessionstore/test/browser.toml"], "git_node": "b38552c4a58e13a7da62aac8472edf95fabcdde0", "git_parents": ["266b2dc3530aa7ec1705745e705b34d76199310d"], "node": "515d85b617cee4036e00e8d60865905e30906737", "parents": ["18e8ecfa857f6b0ace77e74237551ae3f1380f2a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062792 - Make gfxFontUtils::ReadCanonicalName treat empty name strings as missing. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nSome of its callers check for an empty result, and reject it,\nbut this isn't done consistently. Instead of making callers check,\ntreat empty strings as missing in ReadCanonicalName and have it\nreturn failure.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318729\n", "files": ["gfx/thebes/gfxFontUtils.cpp"], "git_node": "7bed5eeb52810c6d62aa80f20c4d47e9bd7c33d1", "git_parents": ["b38552c4a58e13a7da62aac8472edf95fabcdde0"], "node": "0f65d05cdbe4c5fabfc3c10c55a2d03dec4bc171", "parents": ["515d85b617cee4036e00e8d60865905e30906737"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mark Striemer \u003cmstriemer@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058216 - Part 1: Sync Nova button design tokens from Figma r=desktop-theme-reviewers,jules,ini\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318362\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/styles/nova/_tokens.scss", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/nova/tokens-figma-primitives.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/nova/tokens-figma-theme.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-figma-primitives.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-figma-theme.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-shared.css", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/src/nova-export-clean-variables.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/src/tokens/base/color.nova.tokens.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/src/tokens/components/button.nova.tokens.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/src/tokens/components/button.tokens.json"], "git_node": "946d06a003706e730f916cf8d427c3842a35a0ff", "git_parents": ["7bed5eeb52810c6d62aa80f20c4d47e9bd7c33d1"], "node": "4ae3eb1b91c2bb91e42a5e05a0d6b3cd2b6f2bc9", "parents": ["0f65d05cdbe4c5fabfc3c10c55a2d03dec4bc171"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Maxx Crawford \u003cmcrawford@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063604 - Keep the per-widget size menu when side-by-side is active r=thecount\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318740\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Widgets.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Widgets/Widgets.test.jsx"], "git_node": "2e1364689126e9b7796e609e1d9e869e881e32f5", "git_parents": ["946d06a003706e730f916cf8d427c3842a35a0ff"], "node": "ea21ca58a60bb9001a992589edcc470b4d5f6cad", "parents": ["4ae3eb1b91c2bb91e42a5e05a0d6b3cd2b6f2bc9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Beth Rennie \u003cbeth@brennie.ca\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063432 - Document SECURE_FEATURE_IDS r=nimbus-reviewers,aminomancer\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318568\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/nimbus/lib/RemoteSettingsExperimentLoader.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "d893dc7744d3452a07e080ba21fcef5af5c65029", "git_parents": ["2e1364689126e9b7796e609e1d9e869e881e32f5"], "node": "b0714e3af502496f47e03c814156d29cae76b667", "parents": ["ea21ca58a60bb9001a992589edcc470b4d5f6cad"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054044 - Vendor static-dumps for doh-config and doh-providers r=necko-reviewers,jesup\n\nPreviously the doh providers would only be used after the first\nremote settings update.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316769\n", "files": ["services/settings/static-dumps/main/doh-config.json", "services/settings/static-dumps/main/doh-providers.json", "testing/profiles/common/user.js", "toolkit/components/doh/test/browser/head.js"], "git_node": "e80c05750e76126daba95fd02b7938dc9a038968", "git_parents": ["d893dc7744d3452a07e080ba21fcef5af5c65029"], "node": "1e557c94c930e1d30a30da7125740b6c4211c1e8", "parents": ["b0714e3af502496f47e03c814156d29cae76b667"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Zoya \u003czfatima@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053949 - Changed tokens to surfaceBright r=android-reviewers,jdelorenzo\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316277\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabgroups/EditTabGroup.kt"], "git_node": "934f7deaa1ee5cb9ac1157250b935ce7b7c3e104", "git_parents": ["e80c05750e76126daba95fd02b7938dc9a038968"], "node": "dd3e9b414761a9c24c58ae2ea9132db92f0ee549", "parents": ["1e557c94c930e1d30a30da7125740b6c4211c1e8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057865 - Guard browser_lastSeenActive.js's minimize coverage instead of skipping the file. r=sthompson,tabbrowser-reviewers\n\nWayland offers no way to observe that a window was minimized (bug 2063202), so\nthe minimize half of the switchingWindows task can never pass there. The rest of\nthe file is platform-neutral, so guard that half and let the remaining coverage\nkeep running on Wayland.\n\nBrowserTestUtils.canMinimize holds the platform check, since other tests that\ncall window.minimize() face the same question.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318401\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser.toml", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser_lastSeenActive.js", "testing/mochitest/BrowserTestUtils/BrowserTestUtils.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "e4c93d05c96040312bd5ced935a3479fe8431980", "git_parents": ["934f7deaa1ee5cb9ac1157250b935ce7b7c3e104"], "node": "53fdb7a27796f0c63332dfdd62cc4c2ada121dce", "parents": ["dd3e9b414761a9c24c58ae2ea9132db92f0ee549"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061443 - Show the network status again when switching back to a still-loading tab. r=tabbrowser-reviewers,jsudiaman\n\nStatusPanel.update() only takes XULBrowserWindow.status into account while\nbusyUI is true, but nothing updated the panel when busyUI itself changed. On a\ntab switch the switched-to tab's cached status is applied first and busyUI is\nset afterwards, so the status was stored and never shown -- and on a stalled\nload no further status notification arrives to correct that.\n\nFor a load starting in the foreground there is usually no status to show at\nthat point, but a status notification can arrive ahead of the top-level\nSTATE_START, and that status becomes visible too.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316891\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/statuspanel/browser.toml", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/statuspanel/browser_statuspanel_tabswitch.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/statuspanel/slow_page.sjs"], "git_node": "3069ffa87390ab070a45f33a85e8ec571ee6c0ba", "git_parents": ["e4c93d05c96040312bd5ced935a3479fe8431980"], "node": "e41a7bad55a8bfc0ee34b10a837996a842cff741", "parents": ["53fdb7a27796f0c63332dfdd62cc4c2ada121dce"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandre Lissy \u003clissyx@lissyx.dyndns.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063194 - Force eslint prefer-const on Policies.sys.mjs r=mkaply,jneuberger\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318380\n", "files": ["browser/components/enterprisepolicies/Policies.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "a6b87ed4de61cedbe473347b6bdd8208d77e24c0", "git_parents": ["3069ffa87390ab070a45f33a85e8ec571ee6c0ba"], "node": "16b6353ef56b9aeb6c04de40f3d019686b304d11", "parents": ["e41a7bad55a8bfc0ee34b10a837996a842cff741"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Janika \u003cjneuberger@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059713 - P2. Support DisableAppUpdate, AppAutoUpdate, ManualAppUpdateOnly in firefox_enterprise r=mkaply DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318741\n", "files": ["browser/components/enterprisepolicies/schemas/policies-schema.json"], "git_node": "b0a8b5d5bf7a213c37d666863e0bc0b888247635", "git_parents": ["a6b87ed4de61cedbe473347b6bdd8208d77e24c0"], "node": "5ec442cf0f3b06711c31045864ffb063a5e7445c", "parents": ["16b6353ef56b9aeb6c04de40f3d019686b304d11"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063498 - Update Sentry to version 8.53.0. r=android-reviewers,adhingra\n\nPicks up a consumer ProGuard rule that stops R8 from horizontally merging distinct\nThrowable subclasses, which previously collapsed unrelated custom exceptions into a\nsingle runtime type and produced incorrect issue titles and grouping in Sentry.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318645\n", "files": ["gradle/libs.versions.toml"], "git_node": "57a0001bce3dcc00d8b13695350066588f634fbd", "git_parents": ["b0a8b5d5bf7a213c37d666863e0bc0b888247635"], "node": "737ad9bf16aa26b977d3667a5a9145a155c0495a", "parents": ["5ec442cf0f3b06711c31045864ffb063a5e7445c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1699341 - Re-enable browser_ext_popup_select_in_oopif.js on TSan, r=extension-reviewers,robwu.\n\nRemove obsolete skip-if. The test passes now, and the\ncondition was removed before in bug 1732829 before it\nwas restored for unknown reasons in bug 1750839.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318271\n", "files": ["browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser-action.toml"], "git_node": "13ee18a947eaeac2504ccd842594cda6a316e074", "git_parents": ["57a0001bce3dcc00d8b13695350066588f634fbd"], "node": "3eb11fdeb091aae60aabb10e24a000b08ae1fb4c", "parents": ["737ad9bf16aa26b977d3667a5a9145a155c0495a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "rperta \u003crperta@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2063194 - Force eslint prefer-const on Policies.sys.mjs r=mkaply,jneuberger\" for causing lint failrues\n\nThis reverts commit a6b87ed4de61cedbe473347b6bdd8208d77e24c0.\n", "files": ["browser/components/enterprisepolicies/Policies.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "6fa02c73f2bad2398dfb4691c6680315b3b14f60", "git_parents": ["13ee18a947eaeac2504ccd842594cda6a316e074"], "node": "f31f223a8c9579452e9ca9237f68a178f4407157", "parents": ["3eb11fdeb091aae60aabb10e24a000b08ae1fb4c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "rperta \u003crperta@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2054044 - Vendor static-dumps for doh-config and doh-providers r=necko-reviewers,jesup\" for causing bc failures at browser_aboutNetError_telemetry.js\n\nThis reverts commit e80c05750e76126daba95fd02b7938dc9a038968.\n", "files": ["services/settings/static-dumps/main/doh-config.json", "services/settings/static-dumps/main/doh-providers.json", "testing/profiles/common/user.js", "toolkit/components/doh/test/browser/head.js"], "git_node": "e4cdb382b6029457b492fdc13c8e38f616b1f1b7", "git_parents": ["6fa02c73f2bad2398dfb4691c6680315b3b14f60"], "node": "665006d089ae5a6ad467249a684dc6013e7bb44f", "parents": ["f31f223a8c9579452e9ca9237f68a178f4407157"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kui-Feng Lee \u003cthinker.li@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058661 - Clear the drag source window's GdkDragContext pointer synchronously. r=stransky\n\ngtk_drag_begin_with_coordinates() returns a borrowed context: GtkDragSourceInfo\nholds the only reference, and gtk_drag_source_info_destroy() drops it as soon as\nthe drag-end handler returns. nsWindow::mSourceDragContext was cleared only from\nan async runnable (EndDragSessionMainThread -\u003e EndDragSessionImpl), so between\nGTK's unref and that runnable the pointer dangled, and nsWindow::OnUnmap() calls\ngtk_drag_cancel() on it. Content can land an unmap in that window with a\nwindow.close() task queued before the drag ended.\n\nEndDragSessionImpl keeps its own clear for drags torn down without a drag-end.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315509\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/nsDragSessionSource.cpp"], "git_node": "39b3d67e87f8061fe04f97007e0ef23f50ffc06e", "git_parents": ["e4cdb382b6029457b492fdc13c8e38f616b1f1b7"], "node": "9e0f139d76f5e7ab9c605ff6332d9ccf07849b18", "parents": ["665006d089ae5a6ad467249a684dc6013e7bb44f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandre Lissy \u003clissyx@lissyx.dyndns.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063194 - Force eslint prefer-const on Policies.sys.mjs r=mkaply,jneuberger\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318380\n", "files": ["browser/components/enterprisepolicies/Policies.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "768edafec6cdceee6cf870e2a5c9b70f159ffad2", "git_parents": ["39b3d67e87f8061fe04f97007e0ef23f50ffc06e"], "node": "706e619269c86e5ebdae290bbb902607741dd12f", "parents": ["9e0f139d76f5e7ab9c605ff6332d9ccf07849b18"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063115 - Fetch the full Gradle dependency cache for the geckoview-lite builds. r=nalexander\n\nOn the release channel the geckoview-lite fat AAR build binds to GeckoView's api variant, which hides\nGeckoView's implementation dependencies, so the examples compile against the older androidx versions that\nappcompat asks for. The lite dependency cache never holds those: in the toolchain build the same project\ndependency binds to a runtime variant instead, GeckoView's own androidx.core wins the conflict, and nothing\never resolves the older ones. Which variant is chosen comes down to the capability GeckoView derives from\nits artifact id, and that only matches what a project dependency asks for on release, lite and fat AAR\ntogether, which is why nothing else sees this.\n\nThe full artifact does hold those versions, incidentally, because fenix and android-components resolve them\nin passes of their own. It is a superset of the lite artifact, so the lite builds lose nothing by fetching\nit, at the cost of roughly half a gigabyte more per fetch.\n\nThe lite toolchain keeps its definition, now unused, while we work out whether a second dependency cache\nearns its keep.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318725\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/build-fat-aar/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/build/android.yml"], "git_node": "8248585832bcde2ba7e35fc00c058b9c300af7cb", "git_parents": ["768edafec6cdceee6cf870e2a5c9b70f159ffad2"], "node": "32dc40c84c4e5761910ca2b534c6dea1ed258f21", "parents": ["706e619269c86e5ebdae290bbb902607741dd12f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Henri Sivonen \u003chsivonen@hsivonen.fi\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056118 - Step back in numeric mode if identical prefix ends with digit but only one of left or right starts with digit. r=dminor\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318712\n", "files": ["js/src/tests/non262/Intl/Collator/numeric.js", "third_party/rust/icu_collator/src/comparison.rs"], "git_node": "b3b09e0841b3ca04d004a600b800b64674c75501", "git_parents": ["8248585832bcde2ba7e35fc00c058b9c300af7cb"], "node": "5dd84dc0b0a5063bc9d026fbf5edd3266797c367", "parents": ["32dc40c84c4e5761910ca2b534c6dea1ed258f21"], "tags": []}, {"author": "He