oBlack() to correctly support YUV/I420 black\n\n    Currently, SetFrameDataToBlack() assumes the frame format is always\n    ARGB/BGRA (4 bytes per pixel packed) and uses a flat memset to 0x00,\n    which correctly represents transparent black for RGB.\n\n    However, for YUV/I420 formats, zero-initializing the buffer results\n    in Y=0, U=0, V=0, which maps to a distinct medium-dark green in RGB.\n    When I420 desktop frames are cleared (e.g. inside Chromium's scaling and\n    pillarbox/letterbox margin rendering pipeline), the margins render\n    as bright green sidebars instead of black.\n\n    This refactors SetFrameDataToBlack() to inspect the pixel_format()\n    and correctly fill the Y plane to 0x00, and U/V planes to 0x80 (128)\n    for standard YUV formats (FOURCC_I420, FOURCC_YV12, FOURCC_YU12,\n    FOURCC_IYUV), yielding grayscale black.\n\n    Also adds a new test to desktop_frame_unittest to verify that YUV\n    black is set correctly.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:518064225\n    Change-Id: Iec72c02084e60dea938b25cf8c2f8301e481526d\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/476903\n    Reviewed-by: Alexander Cooper \u003calcooper@chromium.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Jordan Bayles \u003cjophba@google.com\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Mark Foltz \u003cmfoltz@chromium.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48140}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/desktop_capture/desktop_frame.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/desktop_capture/desktop_frame_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "7200dd7f9079e9c0bb665e5eec358f414192d845", "git_parents": ["1b4722a2ba8f3dc6e44a296ada46e2e8f9e21f9c"], "node": "831a1f717e4d584ccd1cf1d50f4a3f836bf15394", "parents": ["ddd8b1f1e7c173e58acf7c7f7cc16624b3452204"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Froman \u003cmfroman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058693 - Vendor libwebrtc from c2de539f9f\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.