omium_revision 0684228bad..d2e77a4444 (1655859:1656016)\n\n    Change log: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+log/0684228bad..d2e77a4444\n    Full diff: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/0684228bad..d2e77a4444\n\n    Changed dependencies\n    * src/build: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/build/+log/e6c068b762..ba1add1a18\n    * src/ios: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/ios/+log/eecc66a9f1..94ceb0ca99\n    * src/testing: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/testing/+log/013809b6f8..fd965820a5\n    * src/third_party: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/third_party/+log/e10c039c8f..20b3520603\n    * src/third_party/android_deps/autorolled/cipd: cO11U_8GS4ddi9IxmYqAQqbRzOqPIQDzD58W9gLJBEQC..TZ04S8u-PzFgQNUf3mSRDJzhTfhtFvJziImfJhVo0vMC\n    * src/third_party/boringssl/src: https://boringssl.googlesource.com/boringssl.git/+log/e802ea0dc4..6f9594a4d4\n    * src/third_party/fuzztest/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/google/fuzztest.git/+log/4329d19d94..03fccf58b4\n    * src/third_party/grpc/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/grpc/grpc.git/+log/8df3af2df7..9b95dd51a5\n    * src/third_party/libyuv: https://chromium.googlesource.com/libyuv/libyuv.git/+log/8e8139a504..8aeb3a9ca3\n    * src/third_party/llvm-libc/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/llvm/llvm-project/libc.git/+log/5a572b071a..5261bd3476\n    * src/third_party/perfetto: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/google/perfetto.git/+log/72997b8161..16833ad2c4\n    * src/tools: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/tools/+log/0f274185b0..5416cace53\n    DEPS diff: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/0684228bad..d2e77a4444/DEPS\n\n    BUG=None\n\n    Change-Id: Ie3e64a34c9006bace0cc5da1c7087919d0801cbd\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/487400\n    Bot-Commit: chromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cchromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: chromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cchromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48144}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/DEPS", "third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor"], "git_node": "41507a6ae2dc777da856c328d1ac8bed1a857b61", "git_parents": ["dbaecf14e66cf78e3981e53c4b0b9073533d8335"], "node": "308d7a03573603f77f116ca3408e6236b3f86b20", "parents": ["7e53904bf0e2d98550669668e5df0141659e4ec4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Froman \u003cmfroman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058693 - Vendor libwebrtc from 56185999e0\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/56185999e082241058db6a8749106c5167ea8c42\n    Propagate transport overhead via BitrateAllocationUpdate\n\n    Refactor transport overhead delivery so that RtpTransportControllerSend\n    notifies TargetTransferRateObserver on network route changes. Call\n    forwards the updated transport overhead to BitrateAllocator, which\n    includes packet_overhead in BitrateAllocationUpdate and notifies all\n    active observers when overhead increases. Individual audio and video\n    send streams inspect BitrateAllocationUpdate to update their packet\n    sizes and payload bitrates. This ensures that transport overhead is\n    properly set even if audio and video streams are created after the\n    network route has changed.\n\n    Removes legacy OnTransportOverheadChanged from\n    RtpTransportControllerSendInterface and OnAudioTransportOverheadChanged\n    from Call.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:461532446\n    Change-Id: I53b7e3f34f6f45b343540c79e55dadaaa58ca8dc\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/485580\n    Reviewed-by: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Per Kjellander \u003cperkj@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Jakob Ivarsson\u200e \u003cjakobi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48145}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/call/bitrate_allocation.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/transport/network_control.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/audio/audio_send_stream.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/audio/audio_send_stream.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/audio/audio_send_stream_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/bitrate_allocator.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/bitrate_allocator.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/bitrate_allocator_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/call.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/call.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/rtp_transport_controller_send.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/rtp_transport_controller_send.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/rtp_transport_controller_send_interface.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/rtp_video_sender.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/rtp_video_sender.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/rtp_video_sender_interface.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/rtp_video_sender_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/test/mock_rtp_transport_controller_send.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/engine/fake_webrtc_call.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/engine/fake_webrtc_call.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/engine/webrtc_video_engine.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/engine/webrtc_voice_engine.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0001.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0029.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0080.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0095.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0109.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0123.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0134.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/scenario/audio_stream.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_send_stream_impl_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_send_stream_tests.cc"], "git_node": "7dcaa8c61d725a54a3ee0a523b3d3998520effd1", "git_parents": ["41507a6ae2dc777da856c328d1ac8bed1a857b61"], "node": "5c1ccd3a84e1c9ed07516a3000380df7513b919f", "parents": ["308d7a03573603f77f116ca3408e6236b3f86b20"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Froman \u003cmfroman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058693 (MOZ) - upstream removed OnAudioTransportOverheadChanged\n", "files": ["media/webrtc/signaling/gtest/MockCall.h"], "git_node": "01baa168aa62ffade9d7cfcb1509ed37142fd34f", "git_parents": ["7dcaa8c61d725a54a3ee0a523b3d3998520effd1"], "node": "32b5dd53092cc0c08e1f2df3be23cf33d3462516", "parents": ["5c1ccd3a84e1c9ed07516a3000380df7513b919f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Froman \u003cmfroman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058693 - Vendor libwebrtc from c125d002da\n\nWe already cherry-picked this when we vendored 8acefd4f50.\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/c125d002da4a05b4c00d665f589b078b30b74618\n    Revert \"Use GetTimestamp in encoded frame clone functions.\"\n\n    This reverts commit 8acefd4f5076e0c371f9b891e4bfcf477af13929.\n\n    Reason for revert: Upstream fixed.\n\n    Original change's description:\n    \u003e Use GetTimestamp in encoded frame clone functions.\n    \u003e\n    \u003e Mock frames in Chromium tests do not overload the new\n    \u003e GetRtpTimestampInfo() and fail.\n    \u003e\n    \u003e Bug: chromium:524901718\n    \u003e Change-Id: I67ce2478b1b096ed82e22d72c88d0bdd41848c5a\n    \u003e Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/486860\n    \u003e Commit-Queue: Guido Urdaneta \u003cguidou@webrtc.org\u003e\n    \u003e Commit-Queue: Leonardo Evi \u003cevil@chromium.org\u003e\n    \u003e Reviewed-by: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    \u003e Reviewed-by: Guido Urdaneta \u003cguidou@webrtc.org\u003e\n    \u003e Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48122