sting: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/testing/+log/e6ecb69170..bff47f84f9\n    * src/third_party: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/third_party/+log/773cf3db24..b111c6e8d0\n    * src/third_party/boringssl/src: https://boringssl.googlesource.com/boringssl.git/+log/27c62ff54d..191d9aa000\n    * src/third_party/compiler-rt/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/llvm/llvm-project/compiler-rt.git/+log/7c0d0b6903..65b1f193f3\n    * src/third_party/depot_tools: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/tools/depot_tools.git/+log/23ed94f584..e1d474d53f\n    * src/third_party/eigen3/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/gitlab.com/libeigen/eigen.git/+log/bc5f5f685a..70034bc005\n    * src/third_party/grpc/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/grpc/grpc.git/+log/3a1fabb34b..6d0b58e009\n    * src/third_party/harfbuzz/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/harfbuzz/harfbuzz.git/+log/511df88b82..28f4dc622f\n    * src/third_party/kotlinc/current: g-CsXZkERrHwwfFpXucgwbdyB-4827ciPlnFG-JircsC..CNW8t-Mi3vb2lw4BgSM89qgSiuY8XNJLp2eR6K8aLZ0C\n    * src/third_party/libaom/source/libaom: https://aomedia.googlesource.com/aom.git/+log/b973895c4c..43f2b6a990\n    * src/third_party/libvpx/source/libvpx: https://chromium.googlesource.com/webm/libvpx.git/+log/fcdfe1c297..8592391cdb\n    * src/third_party/llvm-libc/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/llvm/llvm-project/libc.git/+log/5d7e05dc6e..7b7132872a\n    * src/third_party/perfetto: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/google/perfetto.git/+log/eaba73d454..a4ff4fb849\n    * src/third_party/r8/cipd: DVH4goXudQ_5x7Anis0boVW2UGuqrsVsIp8Y2qhOTfIC..YZ8NmCeYkjS2-KZCRLM1T-Fndg4-DDY9Mo7XrVIMgOwC\n    * src/tools: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/tools/+log/9dea47bc6b..c18b216b52\n    * src/tools/luci-go: git_revision:288f56893bcbd07c840fc47f8dce8b551d4f37ee..git_revision:2a7debf61d7c6904fec529caf5b0da3222ad7a1f\n    * src/tools/luci-go: git_revision:288f56893bcbd07c840fc47f8dce8b551d4f37ee..git_revision:2a7debf61d7c6904fec529caf5b0da3222ad7a1f\n    * src/tools/luci-go: git_revision:288f56893bcbd07c840fc47f8dce8b551d4f37ee..git_revision:2a7debf61d7c6904fec529caf5b0da3222ad7a1f\n    DEPS diff: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/0a587d5886..fd4007362e/DEPS\n\n    BUG=None\n\n    Change-Id: I80a82974e1be6fec90f8ed9465dd0ab941984a85\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/488060\n    Bot-Commit: chromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cchromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: chromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cchromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48169}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/DEPS", "third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor"], "git_node": "eec6ab87d34dfc79ec924ffd6f917d57a2c71de0", "git_parents": ["8adca5c6e2c0465bfac5a7e9886108a675a8a10e"], "node": "ed7706debb97f00dd9b5b529fc9665f71f5d68b2", "parents": ["2bdbbd1faf5224b2d8e34fb82b4c695622254e80"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Froman \u003cmfroman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058693 - Vendor libwebrtc from d5c7b6da89\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/d5c7b6da897d69e7bbcc2440696f65ecbd007abe\n    Reland \"Sframe encryptor implementation\"\n\n    This reverts commit 3590bc3fc94418ecddf2a2cf392e19f8a1a17a05.\n\n    Reason for revert: Dependency added downstream\n\n    Original change's description:\n    \u003e Revert \"Sframe encryptor implementation\"\n    \u003e\n    \u003e This reverts commit 4820cf11c56af592ea4ed02cbce7c0b1a7656fbe.\n    \u003e\n    \u003e Reason for revert: Breaks downstream projects due to new third party dependency.\n    \u003e\n    \u003e Original change's description:\n    \u003e \u003e Sframe encryptor implementation\n    \u003e \u003e\n    \u003e \u003e This CL introduces the concrete Sframe encryptor that sits between the\n    \u003e \u003e public key-management API and the media pipeline, implementing the\n    \u003e \u003e sender-side wiring for Sframe end-to-end encryption.\n    \u003e \u003e\n    \u003e \u003e # High-level design\n    \u003e \u003e The implementation follows a three-layer split that matches the existing\n    \u003e \u003e WebRTC layering and respects the api/ visibility rules: 1. Public API\n    \u003e \u003e layer (api/sframe/) - A narrow, stable interface that exposes only key\n    \u003e \u003e management to applications: setting an encryption key on the sender\n    \u003e \u003e side.\n    \u003e \u003e\n    \u003e \u003e 2. Internal media interface layer (modules/sframe/) - Extends the public\n    \u003e \u003e key-management interface with the Encrypt and \"max ciphertext size\"\n    \u003e \u003e entry points used by the media pipeline. This is the surface the media\n    \u003e \u003e channel speaks to; application code never sees it.\n    \u003e \u003e\n    \u003e \u003e 3. Concrete impl layer (modules/sframe/) - Implements the media\n    \u003e \u003e interface on top of the cisco/sframe library.\n    \u003e \u003e\n    \u003e \u003e Splitting key management from frame protection lets the public handle\n    \u003e \u003e expose only the small surface applications need, while the media\n    \u003e \u003e pipeline talks to a richer interface internally.\n    \u003e \u003e\n    \u003e \u003e Bug: webrtc:479862368\n    \u003e \u003e Change-Id: Id93dba5874b6f5b1f32723755dd404af202f6ecf\n    \u003e \u003e Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/481301\n    \u003e \u003e Reviewed-by: Harald Alvestrand \u003chta@webrtc.org\u003e\n    \u003e \u003e Reviewed-by: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    \u003e \u003e Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    \u003e \u003e Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48065}\n    \u003e\n    \u003e Bug: webrtc:479862368\n    \u003e Change-Id: Icef4fe1ce6e391b045f7b94087ee419b7899a96c\n    \u003e Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/485200\n    \u003e Commit-Queue: Johannes Kron \u003ckron@webrtc.org\u003e\n    \u003e Bot-Commit: rubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com \u003crubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    \u003e Reviewed-by: Harald Alvestrand \u003chta@webrtc.org\u003e\n    \u003e Reviewed-by: Bj\u00f6rn Terelius \u003cterelius@webrtc.org\u003e\n    \u003e Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48077}\n\n    Bug: webrtc:479862368\n    Change-Id: Ie9dae7c1e52f459b5b5b762937febadab9a33588\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/488000\n    Commit-Queue: Bj\u00f6rn Terelius \u003cterelius@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Bot-Commit: rubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com \u003crubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48170}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/sframe/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/sframe/DEPS", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/sframe/sframe_encryptor.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/sframe/sframe_encryptor.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/sframe/sframe_encryptor_decryptor_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/sframe/sframe_media_encryptor_interface.h"], "git_node": "059ea9976d9fbae1b6393e2bf874a9be6d559f37", "git_parents": ["eec6ab87d34dfc79ec924ffd6f917d57a2c71de0"], "node": "a3bf6e74fc8acf2719342d4f435932e62c2b7731", "parents": ["ed7706debb97f00dd9b5b529fc9665f71f5d68b2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Froman \u003cmfroman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058693 - Vendor libwebrtc from 6f7a8dc98f\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/6f7a8dc98f1e340b8da7e4bafc831881dd9f6053\n    Cleanup unused and expired RtcpLossNotification field trial\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42220379, b/493520221\n    Change-Id: Id6bdd6bc8d225603a193100bff1822f2f607da60\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/488100\n    Auto-Submit: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48171}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/experiments/field_trials.py", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/base/codec.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/engine/webrtc_video_engine_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "973d28e2a939752f5e20b41cd7b0e6a484cad9e3", "git_parents": ["059ea9976d9fbae1b6393e2bf874a9be6d559f37"], "node": "b7c8cc69d97c1b16290642a39f160bcc014c07a6", "parents": ["a3bf6e74fc8acf2719342d4f435932e62c2b7731"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Froman \u003cmfroman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058693 - Vendor libwebrtc from bcd9ca2788\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/bcd9ca27884944c7c916b0dba0996627b57fb905\n    Fix -Wpointer-bool-conversion warning in FunctionView\n\n    LLVM PR 204944 updated Clang's -Wpointer-bool-conversion and\n    -Wtautological-pointer-compare to look through lvalue references to\n    functions and warn when they are evaluated in a boolean context or\n    compared against null.\n    When passing a function designator/name without '&' to\n    webrtc::FunctionView, template argument deduction infers the type as an\n    lvalue reference to a function. Previously, FunctionView used a single\n    constructor for both function pointers and function references, which\n    checked 'f ? ... : nullptr'. Evaluating a function reference in this\n    ternary check triggered -Wpointer-bool-conversion.\n    This change splits the constructor into two mutually exclusive\n    constructors:\n    1. One for function pointers (using std::is_pointer), retaining the\n       null check.\n    2. One for function references (using std::is_function), initializing\n       call_ directly without the null check since function references can\n       never be null.\n\n    Bug: chromium:531796076\n    Change-Id: Ibb798adddb47c5a110232e4caf956eba2a0743fe\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/488020\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Zequan Wu \u003czequanwu@google.com\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Denise Tell \u003cdct@google.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48172}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/function_view.h"], "git_node": "cc6ac38b6f330de72baab6231ffcbb05e474ef98", "git_parents": ["973d28e2a939752f5e20b41cd7b0e6a484cad9e3"], "node": "95d27c07e79bafdac4b0ef1d01a71ec9e8e9e54d", "parents": ["b7c8cc69d97c1b16290642a39f160bcc014c07a6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Froman \u003cmfroman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058693 - Vendor libwebrtc from 2699cddd8b\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/2699cddd8b4da8684861da2c8a74742115523735\n    Roll chromium_revision fd4007362e..b3ad71d6b5 (1658512:1658920)\n\n    Change log: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+log/fd4007362e..b3ad71d6b5\n    Full diff: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/fd4007362e..b3ad71d6b5\n\n    Changed dependencies\n    * src/build: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/build/+log/40ba59e91a..3e1e94361a\n    * src/ios: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/ios/+log/f5aa0adbc5..3d106a7340\n    * src/testing: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/testing/+log/bff47f84f9..6b9129a147\n    * src/third_party: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/third_party/+log/b111c6e8d0..6282fd7d3e\n    * src/third_party/android_deps/autorolled/cipd: WegBnkWMZvTMgPfTunCMDof8RO5Y7MirhLTGBVpHwGoC..LpeK30X42ew5Q-AKB5TCEST0ZUydJ-EVqds0qAt1Db8C\n    * src/third_party/boringssl/src: https://boringssl.googlesource.com/boringssl.git/+log/191d9aa000..8daf854545\n    * src/third_party/depot_tools: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/tools/depot_tools.git/+log/e1d474d53f..020e532ce1\n    * src/third_party/eigen3/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/gitlab.com/libeigen/eigen.git/+log/70034bc005..4035ffe2c9\n    * src/third_party/grpc/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/grpc/grpc.git/+log/6d0b58e009..821431bfcd\n    * src/third_party/libunwind/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/llvm/llvm-project/libunwind.git/+log/557780c9ee..7ccfbebd65\n    * src/third_party/llvm-libc/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/llvm/llvm-project/libc.git/+log/7b7132872a..6acdd35440\n    * src/third_party/tflite/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/tensorflow/tensorflow.git/+log/66fe77c308..a12cd7d36b\n    * src/third_party/xnnpack/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/google/XNNPACK.git/+log/4b7c368f5e..d9ff5bf369\n    * src/tools: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/tools/+log/c18b216b52..81bf183239\n    DEPS diff: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/fd4007362e..b3ad71d6b5/DEPS\n\n    BUG=None\n\n    Change-Id: I97a4391fe9620bd6dbbabc28af3999d3b26248b3\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/488120\n    Bot-Commit: chromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cchromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: chromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cchromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48173}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/DEPS", "third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor"], "git_node": "5aa3cab8b11000fdcb54f713bb10200e98b96c38", "git_parents": ["cc6ac38b6f330de72baab6231ffcbb05e474ef98"], "node": "293c5f1aa1d7874a90673484d05b9bc148aa1a83", "parents": ["95d27c07e79bafdac4b0ef1d01a71ec9e8e9e54d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Froman \u003cmfroman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058693 - Vendor libwebrtc from 9e99574549\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/9e99574549687f5bd19e53fbd9c899fbbecc3512\n    Update WebRTC code version (2026-07-09T04:09:28).\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: I955274a5c8daad0ad20cae9126fb150ff3c07214\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/488180\n    Commit-Queue: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Bot-Commit: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48174}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/version.cc"], "git_node": "4921167d7be11171f0b1db2a46cb19c95cc76c9f", "git_parents": ["5aa3cab8b11000fdcb54f713bb10200e98b96c38"], "node": "d67bcb792e3fb85dcebbb31b1b1ee681fb29afcb", "parents": ["293c5f1aa1d7874a90673484d05b9bc148aa1a83"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Froman \u003cmfroman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058693 - Vendor libwebrtc from 564c815f62\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/564c815f624b7ecad2cb12e686e6a977de707417\n    Guard RtpFrameRefernceFinder from large temporal layer values\n\n    Large number of temporal layers is unssupported by WebRTC.\n\n    Bug: chromium:530708503\n    Change-Id: I64ad284d7c7b5c1064bf766b469f300615e3ecb7\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/488084\n    Reviewed-by: \u00c5sa Persson \u003casapersson@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48175}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/rtp_generic_ref_finder.cc"], "git_node": "b9efdbf9c2ae26c2a241fadf0fba71a1b0f88440", "git_parents": ["4921167d7be11171f0b1db2a46cb19c95cc76c9f"], "node": "f3d97b401103392f952040fd5b5a575e9a8a98c8", "parents": ["d67bcb792e3fb85dcebbb31b1b1ee681fb29afcb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Froman \u003cmfroman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058693 - Vendor libwebrtc from 0cad8a3d02\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/0cad8a3d02e14db929e7ceafeec186203ef56c5e\n    Cleanup expired field trial WebRTC-DefaultBitrateLimitsKillSwitch\n\n    Bug: b/493520221\n    Change-Id: I63124a629cfc377103a1564434cc914b209a5d36\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/488101\n    Reviewed-by: \u00c5sa Persson \u003casapersson@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48176}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/experiments/field_trials.py", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0068.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0102.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0131.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/quality_scaling_tests.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_stream_encoder.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_stream_encoder.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_stream_encoder_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "851c2c0c962ca8f5b73d513314bdf1e65776b97b", "git_parents": ["b9efdbf9c2ae26c2a241fadf0fba71a1b0f88440"], "node": "9b31ada1b25b19c9d2c695eecc932cbe33deb1fd", "parents": ["f3d97b401103392f952040fd5b5a575e9a8a98c8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Froman \u003cmfroman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058693 - Vendor libwebrtc from 99de2d0903\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/99de2d09036e61b72e4e6bba3ab09fedc40d18fe\n    Keyframe request on any stream forces keyframes on all streams in VP9\n\n    Before this change VP9 encoder wrapper issued KF only if it was\n    requested on the first stream (frame_types[0]) and ignored KF requests\n    for higher stream(s). Now it force a KF if it is requested for any\n    stream.\n\n    TAG=agy\n\n    Bug: webrtc:527515375, b/527798266\n    Change-Id: Id3618bda802ca8d98cb4c5c0629ae0857537891b\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/488082\n    Commit-Queue: Sergey Silkin \u003cssilkin@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48177}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/vp8/libvpx_vp8_encoder.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/vp9/libvpx_vp9_encoder.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/vp9/test/vp9_impl_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0001.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0018.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0097.patch"], "git_node": "71e0ee5760c0c08a6ba13d6c65a6b5b3b3559296", "git_parents": ["851c2c0c962ca8f5b73d513314bdf1e65776b97b"], "node": "2e787203e42245c342d6e4989fb2b7234780b692", "parents": ["9b31ada1b25b19c9d2c695eecc932cbe33deb1fd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Froman \u003cmfroman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058693 - Vendor libwebrtc from 7e5eefa1a6\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/7e5eefa1a6283833702b96521fa7c871e16810fd\n    Update WebRTC code version (2026-07-10T04:09:28).\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: I2e1278c9f86db7f7313fcff1b0bac039edaae0e0\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/488300\n    Bot-Commit: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48178}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/version.cc"], "git_node": "7aabcea6353586a1613f137db4ad0dfdfa960360", "git_parents": ["71e0ee5760c0c08a6ba13d6c65a6b5b3b3559296"], "node": "9467e6bff193e5a5c3f86bfb8e36e7c9b2d1aa2d", "parents": ["2e787203e42245c342d6e4989fb2b7234780b692"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Froman \u003cmfroman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058693 - Vendor libwebrtc from 8627513862\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/8627513862e9f69ae8e21a75065b0adb8cbcbe46\n    Allow repeat frames a first frame in EncoderSpeedController.\n\n    The purpose of special casing repeat-frame is that since they will be\n    very similar to the last frame, they will be artificially \"easy\" to\n    encode.\n\n    However, if an encoder is reconfigured mid stream it might start with a\n    repeat-frame, in which case it will be in effect a brand new frame. In\n    the same way, keyframes should also treat repeat-frames as regular ones.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:443906251\n    Change-Id: Ida738d498e0c2b374a271cb84fc7a4dbb2433e4a\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/488381\n    Commit-Queue: Sergey Silkin \u003cssilkin@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Auto-Submit: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Sergey Silkin \u003cssilkin@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48179}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/utility/encoder_speed_controller_impl.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/utility/encoder_speed_controller_impl_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "77833b1c2824a56f547a010f23b830341f77e52b", "git_parents": ["7aabcea6353586a1613f137db4ad0dfdfa960360"], "node": "3daa72b581a84aed76b1a9e5fd27df83da380e43", "parents": ["9467e6bff193e5a5c3f86bfb8e36e7c9b2d1aa2d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Froman \u003cmfroman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058693 - Vendor libwebrtc from 2e38b6834d\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/2e38b6834d4118fd327565cf9b22c8ce902672fe\n    Refactor FrameInstrumentationGenerator to handle missing VideoFrames.\n\n    If a raw `VideoFrame` is not available to when trying to generate frame\n    instrumentation data, still update the state with a sync messages.\n\n    This is especially important on keyframe where we've state that frame\n    instrumentation data must be available. Otherwise we may end up in a\n    state where we're unable to produce instrumentation at all for a layer.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:358039777\n    Change-Id: Id64e139ddcfa2bf4211aa624ec701fe6dcdcda7f\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/488400\n    Commit-Queue: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Sergey Silkin \u003cssilkin@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48180}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/corruption_detection/frame_instrumentation_generator_impl.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/corruption_detection/frame_instrumentation_generator_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/corruption_detection/frame_selector.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/corruption_detection/frame_selector.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/corruption_detection/halton_frame_sampler.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/corruption_detection/halton_frame_sampler.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/rtp_video_stream_receiver2_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "023fa21e8fe5e3f873b7b0abdd71b5169b65171d", "git_parents": ["77833b1c2824a56f547a010f23b830341f77e52b"], "node": "65d7f69fe13c6afd70e03e8b04c9f1caab36ac0d", "parents": ["3daa72b581a84aed76b1a9e5fd27df83da380e43"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Froman \u003cmfroman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058693 - Vendor libwebrtc from 4d75e27626\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/4d75e276262927deb4ebf0df5bd1da03b57e6dcb\n    Fix incorrect spatial id handling wrt frame metadata handler.\n\n    In some cases when simulcast is used, the spatial id is explicitly set\n    to 0. In VideoStreamEncoder, this lead to a problem the `stream_idx`\n    was set to 0 for all simulcast streams - prevent proper handling in the\n    frame encoder metadata writer.\n\n    This can be solved by simply taking the maximum of simulcast and spatial\n    id (or zero).\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42225300\n    Change-Id: If2b65ad0fdf9a44fb9e1bfb28adf87402b864a20\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/488380\n    Reviewed-by: Sergey Silkin \u003cssilkin@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48181}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0068.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0102.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0131.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_stream_encoder.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_stream_encoder_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "50eb353b9eec371231b19781298b21dc972ea640", "git_parents": ["023fa21e8fe5e3f873b7b0abdd71b5169b65171d"], "node": "0d6430b18babe6f1e7ae0a562bd988ebe74b8cbe", "parents": ["65d7f69fe13c6afd70e03e8b04c9f1caab36ac0d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Froman \u003cmfroman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058693 - Vendor libwebrtc from 74d5f02907\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/74d5f02907b5231a56fdfe9915b6401eb1bf44eb\n    dcsctp: Limit the effect of state cookie tampering\n\n    This commit enhances the security and robustness of the state cookie by\n    limiting what an attacker can achieve even if they manage to forge or\n    tamper with the cookie.\n\n    By storing the raw peer capabilities in the state cookie, we prevent an\n    attacker from enabling extensions that the local socket didn't signal\n    support for, limit the stream limits (incoming and outgoing) from what\n    was originally announced, and also eliminate some duplication in\n    capability parsing in the different methods to do connection handshakes.\n\n    This ensures that the state instantiated from a COOKIE ECHO strictly\n    matches the parameters of the original INIT, and if an attacker tampers\n    with it, the effects are very limited.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:522976080\n    Change-Id: Ia038ce183cbc28301d26be4a5657c6867dbff306\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/488460\n    Commit-Queue: Victor Boivie \u003cboivie@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48182}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/net/dcsctp/socket/capabilities.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/net/dcsctp/socket/dcsctp_socket.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/net/dcsctp/socket/state_cookie.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/net/dcsctp/socket/state_cookie.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/net/dcsctp/socket/state_cookie_test.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/net/dcsctp/socket/transmission_control_block.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/net/dcsctp/socket/transmission_control_block.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/net/dcsctp/socket/transmission_control_block_test.cc"], "git_node": "fa68c4df05b5fb72bea46eaa4a62dbd7ad0fffdb", "git_parents": ["50eb353b9eec371231b19781298b21dc972ea640"], "node": "c203f68b4b0ce6a7f23ae1c788ae82c054d6cc99", "parents": ["0d6430b18babe6f1e7ae0a562bd988ebe74b8cbe"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Froman \u003cmfroman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058693 - Vendor libwebrtc from 06ae2e94a5\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/06ae2e94a5bd1e23d1100ee1e214c62a9d0d069d\n    Update WebRTC code version (2026-07-11T04:08:48).\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: If485cb5cd4cfe0f4081595f9fe7800faeec7dfb4\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/488620\n    Bot-Commit: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48183}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/version.cc"], "git_node": "d1146c4133b829a631254928c9c16296c1bec71f", "git_parents": ["fa68c4df05b5fb72bea46eaa4a62dbd7ad0fffdb"], "node": "7844796694960e49bc4c3be0d9cddd05acc30a01", "parents": ["c203f68b4b0ce6a7f23ae1c788ae82c054d6cc99"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Froman \u003cmfroman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058693 - Vendor libwebrtc from 3fa9476304\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/3fa947630451197bca6fc57fc0c89d87bb299d01\n    Update WebRTC code version (2026-07-12T04:06:46).\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: Id31d29d12c5a06c46149ad5daf2c961b1c5cd928\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/488820\n    Commit-Queue: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Bot-Commit: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48184}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/version.cc"], "git_node": "0f739d9afd53255408e0c05a859b9d3a66c9f3e9", "git_parents": ["