@{#48219}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/source/rtcp_transceiver_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/call_stats2_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/frame_cadence_adapter_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "dd044662a0edd596292a373ee68b423cb7f7bf98", "git_parents": ["e5e2d69736369cc52b02c4c068b7936a1e65e4c3"], "node": "718f7bc4e8e30837eb9224867cf57b974051d797", "parents": ["a2eb8f4c2c72eed47fd7af1d6efa037fc9f5564f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Froman \u003cmfroman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058693 - Vendor libwebrtc from b19730570f\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/b19730570ff1c686fd34a9d74a18e7ba6083ec20\n    LogScreamSimulation: Log state periodically on packet sent\n\n    Refactor LogState to take a Timestamp parameter so it can be called\n    from both feedback handlers and packet sent handlers.\n    Extract UpdateFeedbackHistory to manage feedback events.\n    Log state on packet sent if more than 25ms has elapsed since the last LogState.\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: If9c770ea45a27859cd5fd45321c093a2f8f8ca07\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/490760\n    Reviewed-by: Bj\u00f6rn Terelius \u003cterelius@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Per Kjellander \u003cperkj@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48220}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_tools/rtc_event_log_visualizer/log_scream_simulation.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_tools/rtc_event_log_visualizer/log_scream_simulation.h"], "git_node": "3c3344c3068fd18b0cb0c4b85136a718dd425c10", "git_parents": ["dd044662a0edd596292a373ee68b423cb7f7bf98"], "node": "fc4cb9aa4602366ddbcbfb56c7b158b5851d349b", "parents": ["718f7bc4e8e30837eb9224867cf57b974051d797"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Froman \u003cmfroman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058693 - Vendor libwebrtc from a8180685cf\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/a8180685cf4da2c3cdb67980588a31ec8b9d4d19\n    Tune rtp_frame_reference_finder_fuzzer to create valid VP8 headers\n\n    To avoid testing with values that is not possible to receive over the\n    wire.\n\n    Bug: chromium:533920878\n    Change-Id: Ia26960c21d9962b0a498d258effadec0bc335239\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/490861\n    Commit-Queue: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: \u00c5sa Persson \u003casapersson@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48221}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/fuzzers/rtp_frame_reference_finder_fuzzer.cc"], "git_node": "f0305e80ae2abcc1df68dea90826a800da45ca1d", "git_parents": ["3c3344c3068fd18b0cb0c4b85136a718dd425c10"], "node": "f0c93619f419e5b07cdc033113c51fe6395da3dd", "parents": ["fc4cb9aa4602366ddbcbfb56c7b158b5851d349b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Froman \u003cmfroman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058693 - Vendor libwebrtc from bf6f744d19\n\nWe cherry-picked this in bug 2053579\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/bf6f744d19a84a7d0c3f5acbc844123a8197165a\n    Check RTP sequence number order when assembling H264 frame in PacketBuffer\n\n    PacketBuffer::buffer_ slots can be re-used by packets with with\n    different sequence numbers when their difference is multiple of\n    buffer_.size()\n\n    Non-H264 code path validates RTP sequence numbers continuity in\n    `PotentialNewFrame` helper, H264 code path missed such check as the new\n    test demonstrate.\n\n    Bug: chromium:537233963\n    Change-Id: I6af0f52bfcb3a4437450dffcece85bee7ce172cd\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/490840\n    Reviewed-by: \u00c5sa Persson \u003casapersson@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48222}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/bf6f744d19.no-op-cherry-pick-msg", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/p0001.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/p0002.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/p0003.patch"], "git_node": "ef3157eb779335f16d44b98bdd895ac6100bc499", "git_parents": ["f0305e80ae2abcc1df68dea90826a800da45ca1d"], "node": "6aeec15003c1c97064165a76d8c2b4f33480bb74", "parents": ["f0c93619f419e5b07cdc033113c51fe6395da3dd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Froman \u003cmfroman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058693 - Vendor libwebrtc from 0b52bb5022\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/0b52bb5022e8060f59e39b0c358a964150eaa4d0\n    Don't have test library depending on audio_processing_unittests.\n\n    Extract a echo_canceller_test_tools build target instead of depending on\n    audio_processing_unittests.\n\n    Change-Id: I4fa133ed3d90d0a2a62205814c543897ddb3f8e5\n    Bug: webrtc:498394143\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/491040\n    Commit-Queue: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Mirko Bonadei \u003cmbonadei@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48223}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/aec3/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/aec3/neural_residual_echo_estimator/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/ns/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0034.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0095.patch"], "git_node": "734048d16889d37435fdfef4e140baa5f881fd6d", "git_parents": ["ef3157eb779335f16d44b98bdd895ac6100bc499"], "node": "9e9e964ca444e518d1a7d341c37a917e651e8d01", "parents": ["6aeec15003c1c97064165a76d8c2b4f33480bb74"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Froman \u003cmfroman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058693 - Vendor libwebrtc from 9b7ac9cb13\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/9b7ac9cb13fb088948e6164673338626d0006b7a\n    ScreamV2: Add pacing_rate_received_factor parameter and floor pacing rate\n\n    Add field trial parameter pacing_rate_received_factor (PacingRateReceivedFactor, default = 0.8) to ScreamV2Parameters.\n    Floor SCReAM v2 pacing_rate() using params_.pacing_rate_received_factor.Get() * received_rate_ when received_rate_ is finite.\n\n    Add PacerDelayIsAcceptableAfterSingleDelaySpike and average pacing delay tracking helpers to SCReAM integration tests.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:447037083\n    Change-Id: I34f1abf92a6129176931ba1e5548fd9c0bd15d76\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/490820\n    Reviewed-by: Bj\u00f6rn Terelius \u003cterelius@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Per Kjellander \u003cperkj@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48224}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_v2.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_v2_parameters.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_v2_parameters.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/peer_scenario/bwe_integration_tests/scream_test.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/peer_scenario/bwe_integration_tests/stats_utilities.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/peer_scenario/bwe_integration_tests/stats_utilities.h"], "git_node": "35280bce062d5554eb9d16e9c931332a162c7b35", "git_parents": ["734048d16889d37435fdfef4e140baa5f881fd6d"], "node": "c88c6c3a1a06b11a58170833a1683acb362b011c", "parents": ["9e9e964ca444e518d1a7d341c37a917e651e8d01"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Froman \u003cmfroman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058693 - Vendor libwebrtc from 3af4fd72dc\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/3af4fd72dcfb4de63ae2f33ef8d1cff9029e1167\n    SCReAM: Add cwnd pushback calculation to ScreamNetworkController\n\n    Calculate cwnd_reduce_ratio in ScreamNetworkController based on pacer queue size and data in flight exceeding max_data_in_flight.\n\n    - Add min_pacing_delay_for_pushback (default 100ms) and max_pacing_delay_for_pushback (default 500ms) field trial parameters to ScreamV2Parameters.\n    - Calculate cwnd_reduce_ratio using pacing_rate and pacer_queue_size_ or data_in_flight \u003e max_data_in_flight.\n    - Add unit tests verifying cwnd_reduce_ratio behavior when pacer queue grows/shrinks and when congestion window is full.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:447037083\n    Change-Id: Ic7983241d7d41fdecc0eabbcf9fc384558631575\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/490860\n    Reviewed-by: Bj\u00f6rn Terelius \u003cterelius@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Per Kjellander \u003cperkj@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48225}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_network_controller.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_network_controller.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_network_controller_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_v2_parameters.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_v2_parameters.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/peer_scenario/bwe_integration_tests/scream_test.cc"], "git_node": "f18ec7ba38cfc62b0a2fd19f628a435f4c674971", "git_parents": ["35280bce062d5554eb9d16e9c931332a162c7b35"], "node": "d964dba1fee33a9daa9f301049eeff8a96ca216a", "parents": ["c88c6c3a1a06b11a58170833a1683acb362b011c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Froman \u003cmfroman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058693 - Vendor libwebrtc from 1a6f530bb0\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/1a6f530bb0a75830a488ffbbe3ac170a9ca8bf8c\n    WebRTC: Finish setting up for the migration to JNI Zero's DEFINE_JNI()\n\n    JNI Zero is launching a new feature that requires all .cc files to\n    add a macro call DEFINE_JNI(JavaClassName). This CL does two things:\n    1. Add DEFINE_JNI() to two files in the examples directory.\n    I missed these two files in my previous CL\n    https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/489720\n\n    2. Stop using @JniType in NativeTestWebrtc.java. This is the only\n    usage of @JniType in WebRTC, and stop using @JniType in WebRTC\n    would make the migration a lot easier.\n\n    To be clear, the @JniType syntax is still fully supported, and you\n    can feel free to use it once we finish the migration.\n    But for the purpose of this migration, getting rid of the only usage\n    of it would make the migration a lot easier, hence we converted it\n    to an equivalent, but more verbose, syntax.\n\n    Bug: chromium:481689330\n    Change-Id: Ia2a67c12580f449ab05289216ff09fabbda0c7e5\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/490900\n    Commit-Queue: Martin Kong \u003cmartinkong@google.com\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48226}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/examples/androidnativeapi/jni/android_call_client.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/examples/androidvoip/jni/android_voip_client.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/android/native_test_launcher.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/android/org/webrtc/native_test/NativeTestWebrtc.java"], "git_node": "6b1d0b1421ae33d93f42eabe23214be9f532555a", "git_parents": ["f18ec7ba38cfc62b0a2fd19f628a435f4c674971"], "node": "ddae379e08ba34e33cdab83dddb7b6183e88302d", "parents": ["d964dba1fee33a9daa9f301049eeff8a96ca216a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Froman \u003cmfroman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058693 - Vendor libwebrtc from 596524b5bf\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/596524b5bfe6879f2a3f6331bb8980bf1248f61a\n    Split unittest rtc_libraries under modules\n\n    Bug: webrtc:498394143\n    Change-Id: Ib25677ddd4fbf5bcc47437b009fa857e5c77fbc3\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/490780\n    Reviewed-by: Mirko Bonadei \u003cmbonadei@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48227}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_coding/codecs/opus/test/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_device/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_mixer/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/aec3/neural_residual_echo_estimator/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/agc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/agc2/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/agc2/rnn_vad/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/capture_levels_adjuster/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/capture_mixer/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/vad/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/goog_cc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/pcc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/rtp/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/pacing/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/re