inputs through AppleVT planar path r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nUse the existing planar CoreVideo buffer path for NVImage input and retain the exact Image until CoreVideo releases it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318168\n", "files": ["dom/media/platforms/apple/AppleVTEncoder.cpp"], "git_node": "5f035b20087ed26acb696f90fcda6f1461ed8326", "git_parents": ["b840b9e6584fa00f18b2f36cf9220835947e1580"], "node": "d9d910b1d573aa84a28a414caf330a0b779373a4", "parents": ["e6d9835169e0d403594eaa3c229745a7a42515de"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chun-Min Chang \u003cchun.m.chang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049474 - Add NVImage AppleVT encode test r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nEncode and drain an NV12 NVImage through AppleVT, validating the emitted AVCC bitstream.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318169\n", "files": ["dom/media/gtest/TestMediaDataEncoder.cpp"], "git_node": "006fc6b5beb2a5254ae4e6b43d8e73ea01cd9019", "git_parents": ["5f035b20087ed26acb696f90fcda6f1461ed8326"], "node": "aba88688abaab120417a8e36c932a9b81cf5e841", "parents": ["d9d910b1d573aa84a28a414caf330a0b779373a4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chun-Min Chang \u003cchun.m.chang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2028330 - Add gtest r=gfx-reviewers,bradwerth\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D292643\n", "files": ["image/test/gtest/TestDecoders.cpp", "image/test/gtest/avif_420_film_grain.avif", "image/test/gtest/avif_444_film_grain.avif", "image/test/gtest/moz.build"], "git_node": "5ca1407858d8cf34230d2d22e9dcb50c667869c6", "git_parents": ["006fc6b5beb2a5254ae4e6b43d8e73ea01cd9019"], "node": "a78ff5819100a38e3f040be96cf2934e1a618714", "parents": ["aba88688abaab120417a8e36c932a9b81cf5e841"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chun-Min Chang \u003cchun.m.chang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2029070 - Add crashtest r=media-playback-reviewers,kinetik\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D294330\n", "files": ["dom/media/webcodecs/crashtests/2029070.html", "dom/media/webcodecs/crashtests/crashtests.list"], "git_node": "1cb7c8ca7e7a3563fa7ee2a612056e0e32d104d2", "git_parents": ["5ca1407858d8cf34230d2d22e9dcb50c667869c6"], "node": "3640390c551aae1488ce76d249176e5aa0b7c462", "parents": ["a78ff5819100a38e3f040be96cf2934e1a618714"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daniel Holbert \u003cdholbert@cs.stanford.edu\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063700: Make about:compat column-of-buttons be content-sized, to avoid useless scrollbar from overflowing an arbitrary width. r=webcompat-reviewers,twisniewski\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318812\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/webcompat/about-compat/aboutCompat.css"], "git_node": "9c2c948d541230132f32c3006b53f852e050910e", "git_parents": ["1cb7c8ca7e7a3563fa7ee2a612056e0e32d104d2"], "node": "b28ca79b6759bdad5e6b3d46479ed7175148a95b", "parents": ["3640390c551aae1488ce76d249176e5aa0b7c462"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Botond Ballo \u003cbotond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063312 - Fix WebRenderUserData key computation in nsDisplayStickyPosition::UpdateScrollData. r=mstange\n\nThe WebRenderUserData key computed here needs to match the one\ncomputed in ClipManager which actually creates the WebRenderUserData,\nand that keys on the first continuation of the frame (since a sticky\nframe with multiple continuations creates a single sticky ASR with\na single WrAnimationProperty).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318860\n", "files": ["layout/painting/crashtests/2063312.html", "layout/painting/crashtests/crashtests.list", "layout/painting/nsDisplayList.cpp"], "git_node": "8b723d15b61935c73ef562ae287d17ef121d4451", "git_parents": ["9c2c948d541230132f32c3006b53f852e050910e"], "node": "38ad6e9e25752163346239e436486cf2b257b8fc", "parents": ["b28ca79b6759bdad5e6b3d46479ed7175148a95b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lando \u003clando@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Merge autoland to mozilla-central\n", "files": [], "git_node": "98f1235b79c19a808e3101160efb7810b71a75d7", "git_parents": ["dd2579cb6e7f1761a27ce64fb84d92c61d85c27f", "8b723d15b61935c73ef562ae287d17ef121d4451"], "node": "808fcc0ee37e67dcaa23da3de4c0569b3372d35d", "parents": ["23e1f148280c992651d7a6b5c9db9c4aa7ccb620", "38ad6e9e25752163346239e436486cf2b257b8fc"], "tags": []}], "date": 1786784191, "git_changesets": ["f0a35a5588781c5a88a6f7166ff4411bf492a8b9", "9606294ac903ac9bc848c0d7ba1df20ea5b88653", "fc80e4d55a5affbbfbc8aff5eee90a2c1a911a25", "f3697c71e56a0bba4dbdabbe2f790554256cffca", "fcb868bd2f421d892d296372d21b0ec094051289", "66314471ff8cafcd1d54067afbad852a93b8c234", "74a31edb7a1dce9562aeba7a83a8316984d50fbe", "ea2476a435bb09293212f7f12c7c3c056534c69b", "0975a43ff802db461965764ee98c1e50135e1fad", "b0771fe11f2ec6df912605fb959eb33521ea14b6", "a3c49e00c157b77276c742b1adbe55062b2ea791", "f1250b60331a4c5ae3fae81c16b05a5a4e4872e8", "262b1fc06e93c4884165e551083bcb809348764a", "07b509ec29268b4419261ee7a1e62429733b9221", "3b186a53121ab0bdbfb767a241010977c0abd7fb", "05422fac93bbfd0b5860dddc280a273a0cdd4958", "eeb9ff0218fbdb5aaec35cf8efd568fee605d2e9", "5f9786a664a7b017cc892edb60890955a239eab5", "936ee9782c6ff012b0eba0d224e850547d47c582", "914c5a4d038f423be79c54d019f4798ab2357b5c", "3898012b603e92b4651c6baab4ae3dc8b66d408f", "2fdd7a1279999b944b95f227da5e650dbc276c22", "59f2578b9b32fe769b1c0f3f4b46f6644cd19466", "f706a0b311b611584f1cf9b7d7d2bb7107d3b3a0", "485441bd2653a374b54da757d51a02df1d103993", "0f5deba013d8fbf9a94ef128a571b282bc321e81", "6707bff8efb68fb515232b555770d07cdeb3dd02", "a7b7c9c19b8535e213c08cb0562165efcf9b9831", "c89eda214d99f271e7d66b69e7a0b3b424ae7741", "c6e6c92023a4981aa26cbc1c2cc021d402945b13", "61ea736802d206acf46e03a861b62d00a4151155", "735d0dd6369cfb90a698df184625ae836309a22a", "8aa06bd4a33e771b3411ad335810862703955a99", "d13b3b92d9ed214aab0e7991470939087f0bdaef", "642422fe1188b52440e378498165916ecd21f53a", "598cb493acae75e73adca2198513f9bd9ebd92b1", "9a4d9875f991336107018a0d467ba24e44d5dd35", "2c8c4343b49d44c4ab38ef5a2a044df3afc2ba07", "158b465c7335a5b0c18132f85b014322f250a13a", "71ed217cbf1eac277dded9f500d8e93e56c9e5dd", "9958560b97ec2f36f6048d0abd011d8f58311852", "b94caf74ad63d40a15a6c7127a5d963ea1b5c13c", "9e6d6e3e9777dbe33635712a21a9251042a15800", "98ee5c9ec55c4e7f52e38f11b970add11865460a", "3db2798b0c9672946b70901687201e572c62aeaa", "e6be2fb60dedf9d2cf83ca7e22fe7f5fffc5d16c", "ec336a698012d10955dfa053e61ecf8161d7644f", "0c1ffdf0bf47c14bba9174ab2436dc2cbe9ce465", "09ed896db1875bebcd2608776f4aee495ffc1c4c", "c37f623bfb50b87d9343ceb1a72fa69ddf2ff8f9", "6015e4413bf26ff5420faa6ffca3a9dcbb50431c", "8d53b503b6b03c0cd9e7322e283cc446e380df9d", "e29e646b0a376be4b1277e38237fcb0f21374a0f", "02956042f9b2a81aeb43984970a2f382a20558b2", "a5e0f6d0c6dffdf61ac6cfc36bec69d8b5a1a70d", "224b6fa990eddf89537dcaa53983910ebdd2d160", "90a4917fb3999850608f8592c1b2bf1f6df69176", "fcc91e615297110ea80aae7904ac00580cb50188", "7a75cd40ddb718d3de004446b9b4bde390d0598c", "3461857bb012e9f4cb2f9e306df32184a3238435", "00fef1cb6705b521d5e2e14455bf3a037ddb5709", "a2bb76054d16b3cd3ec3fe5e1d6509050333956a", "bc8990ecaba1d83b92a2a79ed38d1cc11260434c", "b840b9e6584fa00f18b2f36cf9220835947e1580", "5f035b20087ed26acb696f90fcda6f1461ed8326", "006fc6b5beb2a5254ae4e6b43d8e73ea01cd9019", "5ca1407858d8cf34230d2d22e9dcb50c667869c6", "1cb7c8ca7e7a3563fa7ee2a612056e0e32d104d2", "9c2c948d541230132f32c3006b53f852e050910e", "8b723d15b61935c73ef562ae287d17ef121d4451", "98f1235b79c19a808e3101160efb7810b71a75d7"], "user": "imoraru@mozilla.com"}, "45102": {"changesets": [{"author": "Ting-Yu Lin \u003ctlin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055352 Part 1 - Move GetCombinedFragmentRects to AnchorPositioningUtils. r=layout-reviewers,emilio\n\nAll callers are in `AnchorPositioningUtils`, so keep the helper next to them.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318625\n", "files": ["layout/base/AnchorPositioningUtils.cpp", "layout/base/AnchorPositioningUtils.h", "layout/base/nsLayoutUtils.cpp", "layout/base/nsLayoutUtils.h"], "git_node": "7b86195861d0dadb4ab95c7e0fa252320e8b45b1", "git_parents": ["8b723d15b61935c73ef562ae287d17ef121d4451"], "node": "7811e02a393ca7a9c6455a92c94467767e5895c8", "parents": ["38ad6e9e25752163346239e436486cf2b257b8fc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ting-Yu Lin \u003ctlin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055352 Part 2 - Move GetMatchingContainingBlock into AnchorPositioningUtils. r=layout-reviewers,emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318626\n", "files": ["layout/base/AnchorPositioningUtils.cpp", "layout/base/AnchorPositioningUtils.h"], "git_node": "f242986e96efc4c81a651cf07bbe79c1472c1815", "git_parents": ["7b86195861d0dadb4ab95c7e0fa252320e8b45b1"], "node": "2f5dcd6e3ed737efc32d153c23405588b83300dc", "parents": ["7811e02a393ca7a9c6455a92c94467767e5895c8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ting-Yu Lin \u003ctlin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055352 Part 3 - Improve nsLayoutUtils::IsTransformed(). r=layout-reviewers,emilio\n\nAdd assertions to prevent misuse. For example, if `aTopFrame` is not a proper\nancestor of `aForFrame`, the method will traverse all the way to the root frame,\nwhich may be surprising.\n\nAdd a null check for `f` in the loop condition. If `aTopFrame` is non-null but\nnot on `aForFrame`'s ancestor chain, the walk runs past the root frame and would\ndereference null\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318627\n", "files": ["layout/base/nsLayoutUtils.cpp", "layout/base/nsLayoutUtils.h"], "git_node": "3038fe22199be4a61fead5fbb110e59914ca6f32", "git_parents": ["f242986e96efc4c81a651cf07bbe79c1472c1815"], "node": "022545ef81b531038c98997e2ec8593ab2faee10", "parents": ["2f5dcd6e3ed737efc32d153c23405588b83300dc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ting-Yu Lin \u003ctlin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055352 Part 4 - Pass absolute containing block into ResolveAnchorPosSize(). r=layout-reviewers,firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nThis makes the interface similar to `ResolveAnchorPosRect()`, and the next patch\nneeds the containing block.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318628\n", "files": ["layout/base/AnchorPositioningUtils.cpp", "layout/base/AnchorPositioningUtils.h", "layout/style/GeckoBindings.cpp"], "git_node": "207a1809509a65ef8f503ff18d1981d6ecaf13e3", "git_parents": ["3038fe22199be4a61fead5fbb110e59914ca6f32"], "node": "304df27fac48f091185bbf77f0e10da65a0972fc", "parents": ["022545ef81b531038c98997e2ec8593ab2faee10"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ting-Yu Lin \u003ctlin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055352 Part 5 - Decouple the role of aContainingBlock in GetCombinedFragmentRects(). r=layout-reviewers,emilio\n\n`aContainingBlock` has two purposes. If provided, it is used to restrict the\nunion of `aFrame`'s fragments to those under it, and it serves as the coordinate\nspace reference of the returned result.\n\nThis patch decouples the two roles. Now `aContainingBlock` is required, and\nserves as the coordinate space reference. An enum is introduced so that the\ncallers which previously passed no containing block can keep unioning all the\ncontinuations.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318629\n", "files": ["layout/base/AnchorPositioningUtils.cpp", "layout/base/AnchorPositioningUtils.h"], "git_node": "a3142e89318e68a16d089d952451a4b0fd23692a", "git_parents": ["207a1809509a65ef8f503ff18d1981d6ecaf13e3"], "node": "461033a8738d976ec879ea8ee86c8c4fb08e0bf5", "parents": ["304df27fac48f091185bbf77f0e10da65a0972fc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ting-Yu Lin \u003ctlin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055352 Part 6 - Add a helper to get rect in containing block's coordinate space. r=layout-reviewers,emilio\n\nThe old code unions all the rects of aFrame's continuations, and then translates\nit to the containing block's coordinate space. Translating a frame's rect to be\nrelative to its continuation is slow, since we need to accumulate both frames'\noffsets to the root frame. See `OffsetCalculator` in nsIFrame.cpp.\n\nSince the previous part makes aContainingBlock a required parameter, we can\ntranslate each rect to the containing block's coordinate space, and then union\nthem.\n\nThis doesn't change behavior, and prepares for a later part to get the\ntransformed rect.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318630\n", "files": ["layout/base/AnchorPositioningUtils.cpp"], "git_node": "f46c66817a049cfc5bb9e13415b6012ba50cebcb", "git_parents": ["a3142e89318e68a16d089d952451a4b0fd23692a"], "node": "633b48482b73eb71d53da523b0dce76ba61eb302", "parents": ["461033a8738d976ec879ea8ee86c8c4fb08e0bf5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ting-Yu Lin \u003ctlin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055352 Part 7 - Take transforms into account for anchor elements. r=layout-reviewers,emilio\n\nThis patch implements the spec\nhttps://drafts.csswg.org/css-anchor-position-1/#determining\n\nA new flag `TransformMatrixFlag::IgnoreScrolling` is added to get the\nscroll-ignoring transformed rect of the anchor element.\n\n`GetCombinedFragmentRects()` now accepts a new parameter `ApplyTransform` to\nrequest that the returned rect takes into account the transforms between the\nanchor and the abspos containing block.\n\n`ReassembleAnchorRect()` applies transforms on its single-fragment path, but\nleaves the multi-fragment reassembly untransformed. This is deferred until we\nfigure out what to do with dynamic update at `NeedReflowForAnchorPos()` [1].\nTrack in Bug 2063761.\n\n`anchor-scroll-002.html` contains an identity transform: `transform: scale(1)`\non a scroll container (.nonpos-cb) that sits between anchor and abspos CB. This\ntest will fail if we don't use `TransformMatrixFlag::IgnoreScrolling` when\ngetting the transformed rect.\n\nThis patch makes `transform-001` to `009` pass (`005` passes already).\n`transform-012` is related to animated `scale`, which was passed by accident.\nThis patch makes it fail. Track in Bug 2063754.\n\n[1] https://searchfox.org/firefox-main/rev/25d7109bf565c299435dec3dd2b9e79a1ce7c15d/layout/base/PresShell.cpp#11737,11756-11758\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318631\n", "files": ["layout/base/AnchorPositioningUtils.cpp", "layout/base/AnchorPositioningUtils.h", "layout/base/LayoutConstants.h", "layout/generic/nsIFrame.cpp", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-anchor-position/__dir__.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-anchor-position/transform-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-anchor-position/transform-002.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-anchor-position/transform-003.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-anchor-position/transform-004.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-anchor-position/transform-006.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-anchor-position/transform-007.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-anchor-position/transform-008.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-anchor-position/transform-009.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-anchor-position/transform-012.html.ini"], "git_node": "d68f3455fcf635e332a59b3969f07d9000240d49", "git_parents": ["f46c66817a049cfc5bb9e13415b6012ba50cebcb"], "node": "da79ac063c1241245e6c627b48da805727167a5a", "parents": ["633b48482b73eb71d53da523b0dce76ba61eb302"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Keith Cirkel \u003ckeithamus@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2045043 - Part 66 - Fixup final classes using _FINAL cycle collecting isupports macro in dom/media r=dom-core-reviewers,media-playback-reviewers,smaug,chunmin\n\nDifferentia