a767b71cf18d7c0d03708a4f134a2a2c897e56df\n", "files": ["mobile/locales/l10n-changesets.json"], "git_node": "e2150ea5a27e4c5dfba163873cb3fda83a6e5f82", "git_parents": ["cf94e075325f2d25715b50d73d0b1e9eb5b234ea"], "node": "4734e2f5112099a5f3497ce0c855b43387cae82a", "parents": ["324c88b3ee41de807ac6e93a54d38ae2f69ec9a3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058618 - Remove some obsolete stuff from gfxFontEntry. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\n(Preliminary cleanup, no functional change.)\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318732\n", "files": ["gfx/thebes/CoreTextFontList.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxDWriteFontList.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxFT2FontList.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxFcPlatformFontList.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxFont.h", "gfx/thebes/gfxFontEntry.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxFontEntry.h", "gfx/thebes/gfxHarfBuzzShaper.cpp"], "git_node": "620a2e26813212497cb92ec609bd43dffa7aa281", "git_parents": ["e2150ea5a27e4c5dfba163873cb3fda83a6e5f82"], "node": "b75d0e2395f35884febb38ae19dc7e42fca177e8", "parents": ["4734e2f5112099a5f3497ce0c855b43387cae82a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058618 - Guard mCharacterMap with the gfxFontEntry's RWLock. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nIt's kept as an atomic ptr so that we can check for existence without needing to lock;\nwe only need to lock around mutations (write) or dereferencing (read).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318733\n", "files": ["gfx/thebes/CoreTextFontList.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxDWriteFontList.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxFT2FontList.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxFcPlatformFontList.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxFontEntry.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxFontEntry.h", "gfx/thebes/gfxHarfBuzzShaper.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxHarfBuzzShaper.h", "gfx/thebes/gfxUserFontSet.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxUserFontSet.h"], "git_node": "c95e46459845cb1cf5fd443db3cc3157b97298e0", "git_parents": ["620a2e26813212497cb92ec609bd43dffa7aa281"], "node": "72cbf3bdc9c70439669d1af5e63a30be52e2b0a8", "parents": ["b75d0e2395f35884febb38ae19dc7e42fca177e8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Benjamin Beurdouche \u003cbbeurdouche@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055642 - Route security-key PRF requests around ASAuthorization on macOS \u003c 26.4 r=jschanck\n\nASAuthorization only grew a `prf` property on\nASAuthorizationSecurityKeyPublicKeyCredentialRegistration in macOS 26.4;\nplatform passkeys got one in 15.0. Below that, a PRF request aimed at a\nsecurity key is accepted and the extension is silently dropped, so the\ncaller gets a credential it cannot derive a secret from -- which is worse\nthan a slower path. Send those requests to authenticator-rs instead.\n\nThis mirrors the AppID fallback immediately above it in GetAssertion, but\nis needed on MakeCredential as well, which had no fallback branch at all.\nThe heuristic is deliberately conservative: an explicit \"platform\"\nattachment request is never redirected, since authenticator-rs has no\nplatform authenticator to offer, and an assertion is only redirected when\nits allow list names no internal or hybrid credential.\n\nAlso export WebAuthnArgs.h, WebAuthnEnumStrings.h and\nWebAuthnTransportIdentifiers.h. The first carries the nsIWebAuthn*Args\nimplementations, the other two are macro-only; together they let a\nnon-content consumer in the parent process build a WebAuthn request\nwithout reimplementing the args interfaces. The first such consumer is the\nLockstore FIDO2 KEK tier in the next commit.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315859\n", "files": ["dom/webauthn/WebAuthnService.cpp", "dom/webauthn/moz.build"], "git_node": "4e81fcce1baf02d180c760e321fb8629571c1d85", "git_parents": ["c95e46459845cb1cf5fd443db3cc3157b97298e0"], "node": "2071e8eb639954de6f67bd1a99dd59b19aa5d1a1", "parents": ["72cbf3bdc9c70439669d1af5e63a30be52e2b0a8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063742 - Add a fontGroup cache for offscreen-canvas workers to fix pathological performance with frequent font changes. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nTo avoid bloating the size of CanvasRenderingContext2D, both this new FontGroupCache\nand the existing FontStyleCache (used by document-connected canvas contexts) are put\nbehind UniquePtrs, and only created when needed; any given context will only be using\none of them at a time.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318895\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/CanvasRenderingContext2D.cpp", "dom/canvas/CanvasRenderingContext2D.h"], "git_node": "a199202bebedf6159899568a1e55dd016ac8db8f", "git_parents": ["4e81fcce1baf02d180c760e321fb8629571c1d85"], "node": "90d0043f91a19a3e1a665752499c509a3c362530", "parents": ["2071e8eb639954de6f67bd1a99dd59b19aa5d1a1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063502 - Make stretched cross-size computation earlier so it affects percentages. r=TYLin,layout-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318722\n", "files": ["layout/generic/nsFlexContainerFrame.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-flexbox/flex-basis-013.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-flexbox/flex-item-percentage-height-img-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-sizing/intrinsic-percent-replaced-026.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-flexbox/flex-basis-014.html"], "git_node": "c3707a7d8ca54ace3503b810650383f39704f918", "git_parents": ["a199202bebedf6159899568a1e55dd016ac8db8f"], "node": "ecd392da146770cb4dfd66e652da7df96f244b42", "parents": ["90d0043f91a19a3e1a665752499c509a3c362530"], "tags": []}, {"author": "tannal \u003cmtan@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059312 - Part 3: Enable the mathml.a flag to fix the ci failures for Firefox beta r=emilio\n\nThis enable the `mathml.a.element.enabled` flag for all WPT in the mathml/ directory.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318942\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/mathml/__dir__.ini"], "git_node": "fa86453174841631c0b8d680b7083454a1af17f6", "git_parents": ["c3707a7d8ca54ace3503b810650383f39704f918"], "node": "e5a1ce9fd7bf81cffc1e998a08772e348fa1e425", "parents": ["ecd392da146770cb4dfd66e652da7df96f244b42"], "tags": []}, {"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2063502 - Make stretched cross-size computation earlier so it affects percentages. r=TYLin,layout-reviewers\" for causing wr failures.\n\nThis reverts commit c3707a7d8ca54ace3503b810650383f39704f918.\n", "files": ["layout/generic/nsFlexContainerFrame.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-flexbox/flex-basis-013.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-flexbox/flex-item-percentage-height-img-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-sizing/intrinsic-percent-replaced-026.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-flexbox/flex-basis-014.html"], "git_node": "b92ddb557a68cbe8b6af2c00f61410de7d55ee9d", "git_parents": ["fa86453174841631c0b8d680b7083454a1af17f6"], "node": "ead4f3d5cec81d6af2c9814423223f346de6350c", "parents": ["e5a1ce9fd7bf81cffc1e998a08772e348fa1e425"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063502 - Make stretched cross-size computation earlier so it affects percentages. r=TYLin,layout-reviewers\n\nAspectRatio fix is needed so that some crashtests don't hit negative\nsize asserts which now start triggering that codepath.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318722\n", "files": ["layout/generic/AspectRatio.cpp", "layout/generic/crashtests/crashtests.list", "layout/generic/nsFlexContainerFrame.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-flexbox/flex-basis-013.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-flexb