ozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Automatic version bump NO BUG a=release CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/manifest.json"], "git_node": "1aa79c6a258254051df1936340985e439918e096", "git_parents": ["7c611117298561f542198076e70e641d4dd080bc"], "node": "ccb266bc1852ba0d1ddceef1c7d66e9636d36f27", "parents": ["2872f5810f11e8e89f45f2589390fc6aa00b98e8"], "tags": []}], "date": 1786923929, "git_changesets": ["1aa79c6a258254051df1936340985e439918e096"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "45106": {"changesets": [{"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062273 - Skip the happy eyeballs 0-RTT xpcshell tests on Windows MSIX. r=necko-reviewers,valentin\n\ntest_happy_eyeballs_h1_0rtt.js and test_happy_eyeballs_h2_0rtt.js hang in their\nsetup under MSIX: asyncStartTLSTestServer launches ZeroRttAcceptServer, which has\nto connect back into the xpcshell process's own loopback listener, and that\ninbound callback never arrives. The setup stays blocked on the serverReady promise\nuntil the harness kills the process, so the tests time out without running a task.\n\nThese two tests started running on Windows MSIX when the xpcshell msix variant\nmoved to Windows 25H2, and have never passed there. Widen the existing\nThunderbird-only skip to all MSIX builds, matching the other tests that use\nasyncStartTLSTestServer.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318894\n", "files": ["netwerk/test/unit/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "e83826fbe08bb7fbd6b73c2951c89602ecf814de", "git_parents": ["7c611117298561f542198076e70e641d4dd080bc"], "node": "62073238ee9823ac0aeecc62b1733521704cab06", "parents": ["2872f5810f11e8e89f45f2589390fc6aa00b98e8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Benjamin Peterson \u003cbenjamin@engflow.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063920 - Remove stray layout/mathml/output.txt. r=emilio,layout-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator