ti@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062653 [wpt PR 61855] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=296995, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=296995 (#61855)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 4efd350b18e5fa6fec4fad64feabc57e3eb41e17\nwpt-pr: 61855\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-values/if-conditionals.html"], "git_node": "2de08c41a9e3ea051017d957f0bc3a0e2b3f203c", "git_parents": ["0ed42db23bc1e167d897a4d671845489ade1e307"], "node": "256cd72ebe4b20e60ca01f6a5587f8c8fb470e1b", "parents": ["853e08ab6cb20925dd12af655e4011f5c3ce763e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062653 [wpt PR 61855] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61855\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-values/if-conditionals.html.ini"], "git_node": "fa09b901caffe28512d5bc45364fafabe9b57cb1", "git_parents": ["2de08c41a9e3ea051017d957f0bc3a0e2b3f203c"], "node": "0652351db5da1e8e6e58cbae41b442daaf38e3de", "parents": ["256cd72ebe4b20e60ca01f6a5587f8c8fb470e1b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Rivoal \u003cgit@florian.rivoal.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062686 [wpt PR 61859] - Block ellipsis fitting next to a float, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nBlock ellipsis fitting next to a float (#61859)\n\nSee https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/14047\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 111fd17ef18bca6cdb88b47bdd932ae442d28140\nwpt-pr: 61859\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/block-ellipsis-041.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/reference/block-ellipsis-041-ref.html"], "git_node": "34d268494ef61c10c464e8d28df1a935e3a4fc5c", "git_parents": ["fa09b901caffe28512d5bc45364fafabe9b57cb1"], "node": "d9773f8a7fc62fba40205d9c5b060cee5268bcb4", "parents": ["0652351db5da1e8e6e58cbae41b442daaf38e3de"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062686 [wpt PR 61859] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61859\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/block-ellipsis-041.html.ini"], "git_node": "9a73c8c63e029eb32da3fafeebc873f9983446ac", "git_parents": ["34d268494ef61c10c464e8d28df1a935e3a4fc5c"], "node": "4834ca79b2a46c59112596f4aa13e96345b96f7c", "parents": ["d9773f8a7fc62fba40205d9c5b060cee5268bcb4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062681 [wpt PR 61858] - streamHTML: Aborting a stream should stop the parser rather than finish, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nstreamHTML: Aborting a stream should stop the parser rather than finish\n\nFinishing gracefully has some side effects such as completing script\nelements and running deferred scripts.\n\nUpdate existing tests to verify this.\n\nBug: 491743369\nChange-Id: Id0f3309f07bc14b6f79377874defbbdb6d9bb16c\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8224427\nReviewed-by: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@google.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1677245}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: ede129b303ad59f011b9eed3db95357f42a366d6\nwpt-pr: 61858\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/domparsing/tentative/stream-append-html-unsafe.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/domparsing/tentative/stream-append-html.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/domparsing/tentative/stream-html-defer-async-script.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/domparsing/tentative/stream-html-unsafe.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/domparsing/tentative/stream-html.html"], "git_node": "3867df8b3ac6193167b9f97056f4900ab766a13d", "git_parents": ["9a73c8c63e029eb32da3fafeebc873f9983446ac"], "node": "b7426645a2f8e125d721a6b44fce4a9eabadb452", "parents": ["4834ca79b2a46c59112596f4aa13e96345b96f7c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062681 [wpt PR 61858] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61858\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/domparsing/tentative/stream-append-html-unsafe.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/domparsing/tentative/stream-html-defer-async-script.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/domparsing/tentative/stream-html-unsafe.html.ini"], "git_node": "30814d3a3db72085024ab43ffefbf0896f4796e9", "git_parents": ["3867df8b3ac6193167b9f97056f4900ab766a13d"], "node": "a30843481e82cd710e68819ff0d94b23e02e0494", "parents": ["b7426645a2f8e125d721a6b44fce4a9eabadb452"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062624 [wpt PR 61852] - Fix stack overflow caused by revert-rule resolution cycles, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFix stack overflow caused by revert-rule resolution cycles\n\nWhen setting a property to revert which previously had a revert-rule\nvalue, it causes an infinite cycle. This patch fixes it by doing cycle\nchecking and returning CSSUnsetValue when there is a cycle.\n\nThis affected customizable select because it was using revert-rule in\nthe UA stylesheet.\n\nThis behavior is not standardized, and there is an ongoing spec\ndiscussion here: https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/13916\n\nFixed: 542646754\nChange-Id: Idf732dcfb681fc48ccbc895e0dcafef0dc33d679\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8201945\nReviewed-by: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Anders Hartvoll Ruud \u003candruud@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1677271}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 1156bb207a641a3790a83fa89ad5ad74926b9a1a\nwpt-pr: 61852\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-cascade/revert-rule-cycle.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/all-revert-crash.html"], "git_node": "c93ad286c9bd994048e320d2b8f267e334db085d", "git_parents": ["30814d3a3db72085024ab43ffefbf0896f4796e9"], "node": "ac7b862acbdf3ca810dd6e31d13d437a37887809", "parents": ["a30843481e82cd710e68819ff0d94b23e02e0494"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062624 [wpt PR 61852] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61852\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-cascade/revert-rule-cycle.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/appearance-base-and-base-select.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/picker-and-slotted.html.ini"], "git_node": "1c8e1fefabf1dcb16723d2d3b611b262115d80c7", "git_parents": ["c93ad286c9bd994048e320d2b8f267e334db085d"], "node": "dca2dde05687e79bc63e3dffca56178710c54ae9", "parents": ["ac7b862acbdf3ca810dd6e31d13d437a37887809"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daniel Vogelheim \u003cvogelheim@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062729 [wpt PR 61862] - XML parser sets \"already started\" flag for DOMParser::parseFromString., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nXML parser sets \"already started\" flag for DOMParser::parseFromString.\n\nDOMParser::parseFromString shouldn't execute scripts. The HTML parser\nwill set the \"already started\" flag for script elements. This changes\nthe XML parser to also do so.\n\nSpec justification:\n- https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-domparser-parsefromstring\n  - step 3, \"otherwise\" branch.\n- https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#parsing-xhtml-documents:already-started\n\nThis is guarded by DOMParserXmlScriptAlreadyStarted runtime enabled\nflag, which can act as a \"kill switch\" in case of web compat issues.\n\nBug: 542115030, 540021703\nChange-Id: I93859d7fe066a1d5ffe549a95c304a397f039945\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8215568\nReviewed-by: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Daniel Vogelheim \u003cvogelheim@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1677296}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 94f31c25000fbc5ae5d3273f43bc28ad2f67f28f\nwpt-pr: 61862\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/domparsing/DOMParser-parseFromString-xml-scripting-support-disabled.html"], "git_node": "939714aa650983247575b3d5984625d33ae450cc", "git_parents": ["1c8e1fefabf1dcb16723d2d3b611b262115d80c7"], "node": "2f01b0b946e33de1ccd637d8b796f209c8fc8789", "parents": ["dca2dde05687e79bc63e3dffca56178710c54ae9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Guohui Deng \u003cguohuideng@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062734 [wpt PR 61863] - Implement performance.measureConditional(...), a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nImplement performance.measureConditional(...)\n\nperformance.measureConditional(...) creates lightweight tracing points that\nonly occur in PerformanceLongAnimationFrameTiming.\n\nExplainer:\nhttps://github.com/MicrosoftEdge/MSEdgeExplainers/blob/main/ConditionalTracing/explainer-for-loaf.md\nI2P:\nhttps://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/g/blink-dev/c/Ur_FiEgzLvk/m/NOCKYJs1BwAJ\n\nChromestatus: https://chromestatus.com/feature/5693676597673984\nBug: 383157188\nChange-Id: Iec40a2c7b5529c7a5015c01914c677ba98dc1ff4\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8144480\nReviewed-by: Scott Haseley \u003cshaseley@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Guohui Deng \u003cguohuideng@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@google.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1677415}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: a4b55a68840baebdcfb225ff7bbe7fcb3fc0a228\nwpt-pr: 61863\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/long-animation-frame/conditional-measure-time-resolve.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/long-animation-frame/conditional-tracing-buffer-limit.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/long-animation-frame/conditional-tracing.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/long-animation-frame/conditional-user-timing-basic.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/long-animation-frame/conditional-user-timing-buffer-limit.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/long-animation-frame/resources/utils.js"], "git_node": "cd9fa095f03dfc3671f2565fe91b433dd280fec0", "git_parents": ["939714aa650983247575b3d5984625d33ae450cc"], "node": "45b3f28b33541fff854a9ed674403cdc3227cd71", "parents": ["2f01b0b946e33de1ccd637d8b796f209c8fc8789"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062734 [wpt PR 61863] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61863\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/long-animation-frame/conditional-tracing-buffer-limit.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/long-animation-frame/conditional-tracing.html.ini"], "git_node": "1db9eabb99a149ab9a6ccba6431ce097f0f89b2a", "git_parents": ["cd9fa095f03dfc3671f2565fe91b433dd280fec0"], "node": "1a9e3e6f998dfa93bd34aa1894602347b7053821", "parents": ["45b3f28b33541fff854a9ed674403cdc3227cd71"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062789 [wpt PR 61866] - Fix some streamHTML cases and refactor, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFix some streamHTML cases and refactor\n\n- Stream to template contents when calling templateElement.streamHTML\n- Use correct stringification to avoid asserts\n- Remove unused references to trusted-types\n- Move initialization to Create method instead of start algo,\n  to avoid superfluous members.\n\nBug: 491743369\nChange-Id: I868ae563d38954a2cca765b6650936d68e897f1d\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8222285\nReviewed-by: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@google.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1677441}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 05cc099b85c7f70853536bfcb35ae175bf4d6062\nwpt-pr: 61866\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/domparsing/tentative/stream-append-html.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/domparsing/tentative/stream-positional.html"], "git_node": "ae9e382f97428d1ea4060d0ed09b31ef45dce107", "git_parents": ["1db9eabb99a149ab9a6ccba6431ce097f0f89b2a"], "node": "20ec701238a96a95f0b21bd2db7b7d2460f2e34f", "parents": ["1a9e3e6f998dfa93bd34aa1894602347b7053821"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062789 [wpt PR 61866] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61866\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/domparsing/tentative/stream-append-html.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/domparsing/tentative/stream-positional.html.ini"], "git_node": "5420ad73a290865ecb804dbe23a5ad44895ea482", "git_parents": ["ae9e382f97428d1ea4060d0ed09b31ef45dce107"], "node": "0e7426169595073a10c36bd9201ed60ebb2ead2b", "parents": ["20ec701238a96a95f0b21bd2db7b7d2460f2e34f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Helmut Januschka \u003chelmut@januschka.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060786 [wpt PR 61746] - Apply text-decoration-thickness to SVG \u003ctext\u003e and zoom inheritance, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nApply text-decoration-thickness to SVG \u003ctext\u003e and zoom inheritance\n\nRemove the SVG Text NG-era StyleAdjuster override that forced the\nthickness to auto (crbug.com/40790224), mark the property\naffected_by_zoom so explicit inheritance respects the child's\neffective zoom, and update the affected tests.\n\nBug: 540446272, 420443621\nChange-Id: I604173989ae4b86a09178b3a1b6385a38264c974\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8179313\nReviewed-by: Kevin Babbitt \u003ckbabbitt@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Helmut Januschka \u003chelmut@januschka.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1677473}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 0e64d6885439d5a2eff75351133a46c88c572e5c\nwpt-pr: 61746\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-viewport/zoom/text-decoration-thickness.html"], "git_node": "83340667c3cbc3df5b81c9e4e841fc1055547b81", "git_parents": ["5420ad73a290865ecb804dbe23a5ad44895ea482"], "node": "54bc2d28962e37331ca8f91f32d760ed30303519", "parents": ["0e7426169595073a10c36bd9201ed60ebb2ead2b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060786 [wpt PR 61746] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61746\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-viewport/zoom/text-decoration-thickness.html.ini"], "git_node": "0f2173546986c500578100514231961eac365cf6", "git_parents": ["83340667c3cbc3df5b81c9e4e841fc1055547b81"], "node": "219d5d659ced8be7d4667e6b91c0b515337643b9", "parents": ["54bc2d28962e37331ca8f91f32d760ed30303519"], "tags": []}, {"author": "mark a. foltz \u003cmfoltz@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062804 [wpt PR 61868] - [WebMCP] Validate before registering AbortSignal algorithm., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[WebMCP] Validate before registering AbortSignal algorithm.\n\nPreviously, ModelContext::registerTool() installed the\nToolUnregisterAbortAlgorithm on the provided AbortSignal before\ncompleting exposedTo origin validation. If exposedTo contains an invalid\nor untrustworthy origin, the registration Promise was rejected with\nSecurityError, but the abort algorithm remained attached to the signal.\n\nBecause the abort algorithm unregisters by string name, aborting the\nsignal later would evict a subsequent, valid tool registered with the\nsame name.\n\nThis CL ensures that ToolUnregisterAbortAlgorithm is only registered\nonto the AbortSignal after all options and exposedTo validations have\nsucceeded.\n\nFixed: 543349473\nChange-Id: Id9fd3dc8cb63515299800da4f2485b8dfc3dd402\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8236351\nReviewed-by: Khushal Sagar \u003ckhushalsagar@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Mark Foltz \u003cmfoltz@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Dominic Farolino \u003cdom@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Mark Foltz \u003cmfoltz@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1677576}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 83b63594532f89d8949a2c7c3c9ff34408bfdef8\nwpt-pr: 61868\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/imperative/exposedTo-invalid-origins.https.html"], "git_node": "252ad2d79302739404c97a3dd7b8a9c60f9cec33", "git_parents": ["0f2173546986c500578100514231961eac365cf6"], "node": "6a0a4d95c07224916f6e98127102f8acca0dec60", "parents": ["219d5d659ced8be7d4667e6b91c0b515337643b9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062804 [wpt PR 61868] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61868\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webmcp/imperative/exposedTo-invalid-origins.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "37a79233f39aeb3810ffd73ac7f754ff8a7ed50a", "git_parents": ["252ad2d79302739404c97a3dd7b8a9c60f9cec33"], "node": "b898562f68194cbe433ce7a35f52c884931f08b0", "parents": ["6a0a4d95c07224916f6e98127102f8acca0dec60"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Syed AbuTalib \u003clowkey@google.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062833 [wpt PR 61869] - Add optional iamf canPlayType test, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd optional iamf canPlayType test\n\nWith the IamfAudioDecoding flag enabled, we see this line:\n`[PRECONDITION_FAILED] audio/mp4; codecs=\"iamf.001.001.Opus\" (optional)\naudio/mp4`. This line does not exist with the flag enabled.\n\nBug: 412395831\nChange-Id: I23fe649f48bc07fe0234649c67879e293c7e6e9e\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8244847\nReviewed-by: Thomas Guilbert \u003ctguilbert@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Syed AbuTalib \u003clowkey@google.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1677666}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: bd5d2dbf177589a27804fa7bed451847f18986b9\nwpt-pr: 61869\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/embedded-content/media-elements/mime-types/canPlayType.html"], "git_node": "77bfb773542ddedf2fce765d9d4f59051fc76c7d", "git_parents": ["37a79233f39aeb3810ffd73ac7f754ff8a7ed50a"], "node": "ed64e4819edb472b394d3b16b8e0540bb189dfa6", "parents": ["b898562f68194cbe433ce7a35f52c884931f08b0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062833 [wpt PR 61869] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61869\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/media-elements/mime-types/canPlayType.html.ini"], "git_node": "c138d36f5edcafafa770ee616f5ef31edea3046a", "git_parents": ["77bfb773542ddedf2fce765d9d4f59051fc76c7d"], "node": "0f06445d495d733d0ad3ad193c0024b91dd50391", "parents": ["ed64e4819edb472b394d3b16b8e0540bb189dfa6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Claire Chambers \u003cclchambers@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062697 [wpt PR 61860] - CC Clip paths: Temporarily fall back for empty inset paths, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nCC Clip paths: Temporarily fall back for empty inset paths\n\nIn the case of an inset with zero area and rounded corners, CC Clip\npaths would inappropriately use discrete interpolation, when CSS spec\nmandates smooth interpolation on each individual value. This is due to\nthe interpolation code's reliance on SKIA paths.\n\nDue to how broken the behavior is, a temporary fallback is being added,\nwhich will be resolved later by solving crbug.com/474206417 (directly\ninterpolating rounded rects)\n\n(Note for linked bug - this CL fixes a 2nd issue mentioned in the\nreddit thread in comment #12. The main issue has already been fiexed)\n\nBug: 536479735\nChange-Id: I1ae761662f151bb2b63bc6e1563d32bd81c25fb0\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8227846\nCommit-Queue: Claire Chambers \u003cclchambers@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Kevin Ellis \u003ckevers@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1677677}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: d1a5e9fc2c9a6c7d94077a48dd82afaaa7ac48b1\nwpt-pr: 61860\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-masking/clip-path/animations/clip-path-animation-inset-rounded-100-percent-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-masking/clip-path/animations/clip-path-animation-inset-rounded-100-percent.html"], "git_node": "9a7625b7ee08e665b51baa7462ed71048d3f176b", "git_parents": ["c138d36f5edcafafa770ee616f5ef31edea3046a"], "node": "aa50d6bc8a2bc79b51084b23c6bd33c5e9951a4f", "parents": ["0f06445d495d733d0ad3ad193c0024b91dd50391"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Celeste Pan \u003ccelestepan@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062840 [wpt PR 61871] - [Masonry] Compute static positions for OOF items in grid-lanes with fill-reverse and content alignment, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[Masonry] Compute static positions for OOF items in grid-lanes with fill-reverse and content alignment\n\nPer the resolution of this CSSWG issue [1] this CL computes correct\nstatic positions for out-of-flow (OOF) items in grid-lanes containers\nwhen fill-reverse is applied.\n\nPreviously, we applied fill-reverse before any OOF items had been\nplaced, meaning that the static positions of the OOF items were never\nupdated correctly. This change moves fill-reverse applications for OOF\nitems to occur after both in-flow and OOF items have been placed.\n\nWe are able to compute fill-reverse for both indefinite and definite\nsize containers during placement in `PlaceOutOfFlowItems` since the\nstacking axis sizes have already been resolved at the time the method is\ncalled.\n\nNote that we will not be changing the static positions of out-of-flow\nitems for content alignment per the CSSWG resolution [2].\n\n[1] https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/13931 [2]\nhttps://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/13931\n\nChange-Id: I7da92e44107185658766d830f6e4433a3d1068fd\nBug: 343257585\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/7808903\nReviewed-by: Kurt Catti-Schmidt \u003ckschmi@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Celeste Pan \u003ccelestepan@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1677681}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: baf78c4f5849582294a81ee4cb6c91c469a087d5\nwpt-pr: 61871\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/column-grid-lanes-oof-align-content-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/column-grid-lanes-oof-align-content-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/column-grid-lanes-oof-align-content-002-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/column-grid-lanes-oof-align-content-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/column-grid-lanes-oof-align-content-003-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/column-grid-lanes-oof-align-content-003.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/column-grid-lanes-oof-fill-reverse-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/column-grid-lanes-oof-fill-reverse-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/column-grid-lanes-oof-fill-reverse-002-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/column-grid-lanes-oof-fill-reverse-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/column-grid-lanes-oof-fill-reverse-003-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/column-grid-lanes-oof-fill-reverse-003.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/column-grid-lanes-oof-justify-content-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/column-grid-lanes-oof-justify-content-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/row-grid-lanes-oof-align-content-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/row-grid-lanes-oof-align-content-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/row-grid-lanes-oof-fill-reverse-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/row-grid-lanes-oof-fill-reverse-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/row-grid-lanes-oof-fill-reverse-002-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/row-grid-lanes-oof-fill-reverse-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/row-grid-lanes-oof-fill-reverse-003-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/row-grid-lanes-oof-fill-reverse-003.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/row-grid-lanes-oof-justify-content-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/row-grid-lanes-oof-justify-content-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/row-grid-lanes-oof-justify-content-002-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/row-grid-lanes-oof-justify-content-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/alignment/row-fill-reverse-align-items-indefinite-size-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/alignment/row-fill-reverse-align-items-indefinite-size-001.html"], "git_node": "7487bd8545a025b006a2203e7f25022674afa5fb", "git_parents": ["9a7625b7ee08e665b51baa7462ed71048d3f176b"], "node": "79e5f24b3a7c658169ea4d4c591e1dcba23d9514", "parents": ["aa50d6bc8a2bc79b51084b23c6bd33c5e9951a4f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062840 [wpt PR 61871] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61871\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/column-grid-lanes-oof-align-content-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/column-grid-lanes-oof-align-content-002.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/column-grid-lanes-oof-align-content-003.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/column-grid-lanes-oof-fill-reverse-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/column-grid-lanes-oof-fill-reverse-002.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/column-grid-lanes-oof-fill-reverse-003.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/column-grid-lanes-oof-justify-content-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/row-grid-lanes-oof-align-content-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/row-grid-lanes-oof-fill-reverse-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/row-grid-lanes-oof-fill-reverse-002.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/row-grid-lanes-oof-fill-reverse-003.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/row-grid-lanes-oof-justify-content-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/row-grid-lanes-oof-justify-content-002.html.ini"], "git_node": "3fa9e89544affe45a0557ff7055ad144f8666e4d", "git_parents": ["7487bd8545a025b006a2203e7f25022674afa5fb"], "node": "e67258a83137090b8f41d0bb6d0a5dda07ef1f3b", "parents": ["79e5f24b3a7c658169ea4d4c591e1dcba23d9514"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chris Thompson \u003ccthomp@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062865 [wpt PR 61874] - Implement WebSocket constructor option bag, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nImplement WebSocket constructor option bag\n\nThis CL adds support for passing an option bag (WebSocketInit\ndictionary) as the second argument to the WebSocket constructor. The\noption bag currently supports a protocols member, allowing developers to\nspecify subprotocols (mirroring the existing protocols argument).\n\nThis feature is guarded by the new WebSocketOptionBag runtime-enabled\nfeature flag. When disabled, attempting to use the option bag\nconstructor overload throws a TypeError. Web platform tests have been\nadded to verify the behavior.\n\nChromeStatus entry: https://chromestatus.com/feature/5080055102439424\n\nIntent-to-Prototype thread:\nhttps://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/g/blink-dev/c/YwkXWzPUJ7U/m/kSuHLvkpBwAJ\n\nTAG=agy\nCONV=d49fff98-9ad5-4ac6-8a3f-c6022b98b1f9\n\nBug: 542670554\nChange-Id: I062512c13e2a4a2ed76a101e9a524db55f797766\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8197225\nReviewed-by: Adam Rice \u003cricea@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Kentaro Hara \u003charaken@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Chris Thompson \u003ccthomp@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1677754}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 530ee022a1dac7d1b076ce06e159380ea457db22\nwpt-pr: 61874\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/websockets/constructor/option-bag.any.js"], "git_node": "9bce3d5077981ca65b5bbcdfb16c05a8c734a26f", "git_parents": ["3fa9e89544affe45a0557ff7055ad144f8666e4d"], "node": "6facf9cc2326fa1914594ecd832e43439278c7e8", "parents": ["e67258a83137090b8f41d0bb6d0a5dda07ef1f3b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062865 [wpt PR 61874] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61874\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/websockets/constructor/option-bag.any.js.ini"], "git_node": "7fbb85cfc2b31ee88e5af8fabf202c02470bb32a", "git_parents": ["9bce3d5077981ca65b5bbcdfb16c05a8c734a26f"], "node": "61a8128eae92ee3fe66b6bcab3e57ab1adc199cd", "parents": ["6facf9cc2326fa1914594ecd832e43439278c7e8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Antti Koivisto \u003cantti@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062872 [wpt PR 61877] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=284895, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=284895 (#61877)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 83e596f658653262f55a66f5bb78dd305aed39ec\nwpt-pr: 61877\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-values/ident-function-computed.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-values/ident-function-parsing.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-values/ident-function-substitution.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-variables/var-ident-function.html"], "git_node": "c696af0751c28b8609711b9694d28ff67ed34f0e", "git_parents": ["7fbb85cfc2b31ee88e5af8fabf202c02470bb32a"], "node": "eddd54f8468b9714b9274dd7622f882a5b218c94", "parents": ["61a8128eae92ee3fe66b6bcab3e57ab1adc199cd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062872 [wpt PR 61877] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61877\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-values/ident-function-computed.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-values/ident-function-parsing.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-values/ident-function-substitution.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-variables/var-ident-function.html.ini"], "git_node": "349a74225f3136e17e5a051e853fa15a88f710ce", "git_parents": ["c696af0751c28b8609711b9694d28ff67ed34f0e"], "node": "c4a2a41b96d3aa29adb266d42cb9b0fc7b69ad6c", "parents": ["eddd54f8468b9714b9274dd7622f882a5b218c94"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yoshisto Yanagisawa \u003cyyanagisawa@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062867 [wpt PR 61875] - ServiceWorker: Run Timing-Allow-Origin check for filtered subresource responses, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nServiceWorker: Run Timing-Allow-Origin check for filtered subresource responses\n\nCL 8182169 set timing_allow_passed to true only for kBasic and kDefault\nresponse types, and unconditionally false for filtered response types.\nHowever, filtered subresource responses (such as kCors or kOpaque)\nthat provide a valid Timing-Allow-Origin header matching the request\ninitiator should also pass the Timing Allow check.\n\nThis CL updates ServiceWorkerSubresourceLoader::StartResponse to run\nnetwork::TimingAllowOriginCheck on response_head_-\u003eparsed_headers\nagainst resource_request_.request_initiator for filtered responses,\nconsistent with ServiceWorkerMainResourceLoader.\n\nTAG=agy\nCONV=b2563ec8-2e72-4911-be75-51e4aa2cf6bd\n\nBug: 517092658\nChange-Id: Ib8cbc494b9aa0df12213e1eed6c1a97150607ac7\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8246358\nReviewed-by: Shunya Shishido \u003csisidovski@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Yoshisato Yanagisawa \u003cyyanagisawa@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1677769}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 9f03608812cb7bdc34874b8ead51fd50c824ea40\nwpt-pr: 61875\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/service-workers/service-worker/resource-timing-cross-origin-server-timing.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/service-workers/service-worker/resources/server-timing.py"], "git_node": "57fb2724a1f184f4344186e885a9e0cc45084184", "git_parents": ["349a74225f3136e17e5a051e853fa15a88f710ce"], "node": "2778275937a61206f4825740f3b8852ce8d6e145", "parents": ["c4a2a41b96d3aa29adb266d42cb9b0fc7b69ad6c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062867 [wpt PR 61875] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61875\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/service-workers/service-worker/resource-timing-cross-origin-server-timing.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "aa5fb886d043619b7a91029a56a2177303cd8e0f", "git_parents": ["57fb2724a1f184f4344186e885a9e0cc45084184"], "node": "ad73cd46fad24f4cfebb7d5e4b826d054ccc18c4", "parents": ["2778275937a61206f4825740f3b8852ce8d6e145"], "tags": []}, {"author": "mingmingtasd \u003cmingming1.xu@intel.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061131 [wpt PR 61774] - WebNN: Emit resample2d output sizes to ORT to avoid shape divergence, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebNN: Emit resample2d output sizes to ORT to avoid shape divergence\n\nThe ORT backend built the Resize node from resample2d.scales whenever\nscales were supplied, leaving the output sizes empty and letting ONNX\nRuntime and the execution provider re-derive the output shape. WebNN\nvalidates that shape in double precision (floor(input size * scale) per\nspec), but the re-derivation is done in single precision. For output\ndimensions above 2^24, float32 can no longer represent consecutive\nintegers, so the backend allocates the resample2d output one element\nsmaller than WebNN's validated shape.\n\nWebNN bakes its validated (larger) shape into the index clamp bounds of\ndownstream indexing operators (gather, gatherND, scatterND, ...). When\nthe backend under-allocates the resampled axis, the largest index those\nclamps admit is one element past the allocated tensor, so an\nattacker-supplied index can reach an out-of-bounds read or write on the\nbackend tensor.\n\nFix this by always emitting the resample2d output sizes (never scales)\nwhen building the Resize node, mirroring the existing sizes path used by\nBlockwiseExpand. This forces any execution provider used by the ORT\nbackend to use the exact, already-validated integer shape instead of\nrecomputing it in float32, eliminating the divergence at its source.\nThis was verified end to end against the ORT CPU, DirectML, and\nOpenVINO GPU execution providers.\n\nAlso drop the stale comment that claimed the spec does not define the\nresample2d output size formula; the spec now specifies\nfloor(input size * scale), which matches the existing validation.\n\nAdd a WebNN conformance test at the 2^24 + 1 boundary: it gathers the\nlast index of a resample2d output and checks it matches a direct read of\nthat index, which holds only when WebNN and the backend agree on the\nshape.\n\nBug: 541732324\nChange-Id: Icfcdb7c5f3852b298b6356b147993995e06fad0a\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8201644\nReviewed-by: Hu, Ningxin \u003cningxin.hu@intel.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Xu, Mingming1 \u003cmingming1.xu@intel.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1677773}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: cc56ec6f03522f4eeb89c3524d0593e4c9972b16\nwpt-pr: 61774\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webnn/conformance_tests/resample2d-gather-shape-divergence.https.any.js"], "git_node": "a0f1a6676c9394c96f9f5c633c45538ebe4cc0fc", "git_parents": ["aa5fb886d043619b7a91029a56a2177303cd8e0f"], "node": "f81a47d17584d535e14cc866c348e37efe9e85fd", "parents": ["ad73cd46fad24f4cfebb7d5e4b826d054ccc18c4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moonira \u003cmoonira@google.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062916 [wpt PR 61882] - Updated random() in if() test according to recent spec resolution, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nUpdated random() in if() test according to recent spec resolution\n\nIn [0] it was resolved that:\n\nIf a random() is evaluated within an arb-sub function as part of\nsubstitution (rather than as the substitution value itself),\nits random-ua-ident will have the form \"ua-early-PROPERTY-INDEX\",\nwhere PROPERTY is the name of the property it's used in,\nand INDEX is the nth usage of random() across all arb-subs\nin the property, in parse order.\n\n[0] https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/13662#issuecomment-4672428004\n\nBug: 522304655, 413385732\nChange-Id: I90b43222f6464056829eb4ad5ec82ac94bfa5548\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8206604\nReviewed-by: Philip J\u00e4genstedt \u003cfoolip@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Philip J\u00e4genstedt \u003cfoolip@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1677830}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: fd5aa72cff25eecb91b1838a018626391d4f1f6c\nwpt-pr: 61882\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-values/random-in-if.tentative.html"], "git_node": "208aad857c59ba78a4728f3025b2f655ccc861ea", "git_parents": ["a0f1a6676c9394c96f9f5c633c45538ebe4cc0fc"], "node": "85d0f9f0264e2dd52ee6f12b130fffbf0c5dee36", "parents": ["f81a47d17584d535e14cc866c348e37efe9e85fd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062916 [wpt PR 61882] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61882\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-values/random-in-if.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "b3001917b8b1d37a3d854a17d771d93fae2be9d7", "git_parents": ["208aad857c59ba78a4728f3025b2f655ccc861ea"], "node": "08ab28825072adae9d6601956240396d645d0c7c", "parents": ["85d0f9f0264e2dd52ee6f12b130fffbf0c5dee36"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sam Sneddon \u003cgsnedders@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062466 [wpt PR 61844] - Use the standard wpt_report.json filename for infrastructure tests, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nUse the standard wpt_report.json filename for infrastructure tests\n\nThe per-browser suffix dates from when a single task ran all three\nbrowsers, so each browser needed a distinct filename to avoid\noverwriting the others' report. 644c18e758 (TC: run infrastructure/\nseparately per browser) split each browser into its own task with its\nown artifact upload, removing that collision risk and making it safe\nto drop the suffix.\n\nBy using wpt_report.json, the same filename the regular test tasks\nalready pass, we now automatically gzip the report file.\n\nAdditionally, the non-standard filename meant that wpt.fyi did not\nfind the infrastructure results, and thus did not consume them.\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 4f9d122a3d6ab8de72e398cb72f2d4972abe96a7\nwpt-pr: 61844\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/tools/ci/ci_wptrunner_infrastructure.sh"], "git_node": "5e68aae7ad336a9774a71718bcba7670b43d4cca", "git_parents": ["b3001917b8b1d37a3d854a17d771d93fae2be9d7"], "node": "f04ec24bdd44605969cccceede6787e2ec1c3ca8", "parents": ["08ab28825072adae9d6601956240396d645d0c7c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Rivoal \u003cgit@florian.rivoal.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2047121 [wpt PR 60577] - Line clamp clips floats in at the block end, not elsewhere, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nLine clamp clips floats in at the block end, not elsewhere (#60577)\n\nSee https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/13668 and https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/14047\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 8e3d3261432a28800a28676d9b7617b3e7bc0f33\nwpt-pr: 60577\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-with-floats-012.html"], "git_node": "e788816f1fb35ce8a589e3ad242407e764b6c0aa", "git_parents": ["5e68aae7ad336a9774a71718bcba7670b43d4cca"], "node": "7e6858551fd3ee6a8b6e031d59779027005ae3d6", "parents": ["f04ec24bdd44605969cccceede6787e2ec1c3ca8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2047121 [wpt PR 60577] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 60577\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-with-floats-012.html.ini"], "git_node": "9f1d9d90240b731c03b37b0a90bd8cab626a8219", "git_parents": ["e788816f1fb35ce8a589e3ad242407e764b6c0aa"], "node": "644ee19f0821d43d7e232f8d739f1a83ba70965d", "parents": ["7e6858551fd3ee6a8b6e031d59779027005ae3d6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Karl Dubost \u003ckarlcow@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061713 [wpt PR 61810] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=318096, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=318096 (#61810)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 961c13f7f062c82dc3e6046cdd41af6b93e7519f\nwpt-pr: 61810\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/svg/struct/scripted/currentScale-outermost.html"], "git_node": "ec302b01953144a51218242b3e434c87e0e0d303", "git_parents": ["9f1d9d90240b731c03b37b0a90bd8cab626a8219"], "node": "ea7d195940ea3e5c37a5b49dfa78188a08fa2fb7", "parents": ["644ee19f0821d43d7e232f8d739f1a83ba70965d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061713 [wpt PR 61810] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61810\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/svg/struct/scripted/currentScale-outermost.html.ini"], "git_node": "4df2925652f3e29939dba62f9b6a5bcd543d4dba", "git_parents": ["ec302b01953144a51218242b3e434c87e0e0d303"], "node": "822f64a19c503263ebe814ec1d6ccd048c55f4ed", "parents": ["ea7d195940ea3e5c37a5b49dfa78188a08fa2fb7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Manuel Rego \u003crego@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062935 [wpt PR 61883] - aamtests: Fix _find_fully_loaded_tab, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\naamtests: Fix _find_fully_loaded_tab (#61883)\n\nInstead of returning, let's continue searching for other frames.\nThis fixes running aamtests on desktop environment.\n--\n\nwpt-commits: ae4fc09f4763664d6712fe5f70b14d5689542237\nwpt-pr: 61883\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/core-aam/aamtests/support/atspi_wrapper.py"], "git_node": "151ec88f89b3681ea7e6d320cef1140e790f75c1", "git_parents": ["4df2925652f3e29939dba62f9b6a5bcd543d4dba"], "node": "a157d887109bfd235025ed6307507f49f1c11cee", "parents": ["822f64a19c503263ebe814ec1d6ccd048c55f4ed"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hoch Hochkeppel (HE/HIM) \u003cmhochk@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062874 [wpt PR 61878] - Agnosticize cjk-kerning WPT, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAgnosticize cjk-kerning WPT\n\nThis does *not* make us pass this test, it improves the test and reduces\nthe test expectations noise.\n\nWhen this test was first added it referenced a subset font that did not\nget checked in with it, so was actually using (potentially OS-specific)\nfallback fonts. This change adds a newly generated font that satisfies\nthe test's intent (supports the 4 characters being used, and the\nkern/palt features).\n\nIt also adjusts the font size to avoid potential pixel rounding\ndifferences, and waits for the font to load to avoid a race.\n\nWith these changes, the test now behaves the same on all OSes, so we\ncan reduce to a single -expectations file.\n\nBug: 40876238\nChange-Id: Ie460ec2fa2865e5756fac74a492edaa5f7d9b3de\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8235618\nReviewed-by: Koji Ishii \u003ckojii@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Dominik R\u00f6ttsches \u003cdrott@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Kurt Catti-Schmidt \u003ckschmi@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Hoch Hochkeppel \u003cmhochk@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1678125}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 6d45c406c143d9838924c3c1e49cd0163e40e1ed\nwpt-pr: 61878\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-fonts/cjk-kerning.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-fonts/resources/NotoSansJP-cjk-kerning-test-subset.otf"], "git_node": "959957d8c63bce77d23511d26ab05cd3a22107b8", "git_parents": ["151ec88f89b3681ea7e6d320cef1140e790f75c1"], "node": "e446ee2d71224806fd5903b9a7c31c7da20782f7", "parents": ["a157d887109bfd235025ed6307507f49f1c11cee"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephen Chenney \u003cschenney@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063139 [wpt PR 61891] - [HiC] Add tests for SVG use of content outside the subtree, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[HiC] Add tests for SVG use of content outside the subtree\n\nVerify that, when SVG inside a canvas subtree uses content from\noutside the subtree, the content still respects visited link and\ncross-origin image privacy.\n\nIt works because the used content is cloned into the subtree so\npainted within it.\n\nFixed: 532190464\nChange-Id: I12f8de6de217b8189ed71d6b9aac9924c4902d3a\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8233404\nCommit-Queue: Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Stephen Chenney \u003cschenney@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1678224}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: ccb72cce0a850cd43122cfd00a680a78a2f34a7b\nwpt-pr: 61891\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/svg-use-outside-subtree-images-ignored.tentative.https.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/visited-link-svg-use-outside-subtree-ignored.tentative.html"], "git_node": "58c500d4f16fcdb6a6fc4693d802794cabfd70ea", "git_parents": ["959957d8c63bce77d23511d26ab05cd3a22107b8"], "node": "d94dcff738668db659e1aab0f7127a3c7037e584", "parents": ["e446ee2d71224806fd5903b9a7c31c7da20782f7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063139 [wpt PR 61891] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61891\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/svg-use-outside-subtree-images-ignored.tentative.https.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/visited-link-svg-use-outside-subtree-ignored.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "291992bd4f48978778723023e1ebe92d28c82f90", "git_parents": ["58c500d4f16fcdb6a6fc4693d802794cabfd70ea"], "node": "291dab8468f93a2ba36e8c36f3c593146fda4450", "parents": ["d94dcff738668db659e1aab0f7127a3c7037e584"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephen Chenney \u003cschenney@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063143 [wpt PR 61893] - [HiC] Disallow non-subtree SVG paint resources, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[HiC] Disallow non-subtree SVG paint resources\n\nSVG Paint Resources may use visited link colors, or the\n\u003cpattern\u003e element may contain arbitrary DOM content, including\nforms with autofill. When defined outside the canvas subtree\nthese elements are not marked as being inside the subtree, which\ndefeats various privacy preserving measures. So disallow the\nuse of resources from outside the canvas subtree when inside the\ncanvas subtree.\n\nAdd tests and start to re-organize the privacy tests to make it\neasier to see what areas we are testing.\n\nA bug has been filed to verify the behavior of SVG \u003cuse\u003e elements.\n\nFixed: 514489101\nChange-Id: Ife76a6c02aaa2c3eefdb604343b849a213657900\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8058744\nCommit-Queue: Stephen Chenney \u003cschenney@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1678269}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 0d824311fd03bbaf3bfb60f06e332beb42ecdea8\nwpt-pr: 61893\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/svg-linear-gradient-outside-subtree-ignored.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/svg-pattern-outside-subtree-ignored.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/svg-radial-gradient-outside-subtree-ignored.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/visited-link-color-ignored.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/visited-link-currentcolor-ignored.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/visited-link-decoration-color-ignored.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/visited-link-svg-fill-stroke-color-ignored.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/visited-link/visited-link-color-ignored.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/visited-link/visited-link-currentcolor-ignored.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/visited-link/visited-link-decoration-color-ignored.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/visited-link/visited-link-svg-fill-stroke-color-ignored.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/visited-link/visited-link-svg-linear-gradiant-ignored.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/visited-link/visited-link-svg-pattern-ignored.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/visited-link/visited-link-svg-radiant-gradiant-ignored.tentative.html"], "git_node": "c8a27db165e654e5bad68650a85382d813a94634", "git_parents": ["291992bd4f48978778723023e1ebe92d28c82f90"], "node": "76111718896469ab76e8aeda4c4a08eb5b6906d9", "parents": ["291dab8468f93a2ba36e8c36f3c593146fda4450"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063143 [wpt PR 61893] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61893\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/svg-linear-gradient-outside-subtree-ignored.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/svg-pattern-outside-subtree-ignored.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/svg-radial-gradient-outside-subtree-ignored.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/visited-link-color-ignored.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/visited-link-currentcolor-ignored.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/visited-link-decoration-color-ignored.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/visited-link-svg-fill-stroke-color-ignored.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/visited-link/visited-link-color-ignored.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/visited-link/visited-link-currentcolor-ignored.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/visited-link/visited-link-decoration-color-ignored.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/visited-link/visited-link-svg-fill-stroke-color-ignored.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/visited-link/visited-link-svg-linear-gradiant-ignored.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/visited-link/visited-link-svg-pattern-ignored.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/visited-link/visited-link-svg-radiant-gradiant-ignored.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "045dbce762b8fc03aa1b5420fa25243edca9024b", "git_parents": ["c8a27db165e654e5bad68650a85382d813a94634"], "node": "b662804f779c5d2c017c31f3b1e5295830189c40", "parents": ["76111718896469ab76e8aeda4c4a08eb5b6906d9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jean-Yves Avenard \u003cjean-yves.avenard@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053541 [wpt PR 61143] - TrackList and Tracks shouldn't be exposed in a DedicatedWorker., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nTrackList and Tracks shouldn't be exposed in a DedicatedWorker. (#61143)\n\nUpdate as per w3c/media-source#361\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 212d2016e281b0c99ca2844654c1a5c17aad9e6d\nwpt-pr: 61143\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/interfaces/media-source.idl", "testing/web-platform/tests/media-source/idlharness.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/media-source/idlharness.window.js"], "git_node": "4e7e038f8b9c896c6885ae6341af58bd1762b4a1", "git_parents": ["045dbce762b8fc03aa1b5420fa25243edca9024b"], "node": "c11c427b6c91f3e899e770aa35dc877545cebca0", "parents": ["b662804f779c5d2c017c31f3b1e5295830189c40"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053541 [wpt PR 61143] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61143\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/media-source/idlharness.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/media-source/idlharness.window.js.ini"], "git_node": "099beaa54d899fe248feb362e00308f3d2c2229b", "git_parents": ["4e7e038f8b9c896c6885ae6341af58bd1762b4a1"], "node": "5b73bf14083f14509de1bd680e922a9fc692ba77", "parents": ["c11c427b6c91f3e899e770aa35dc877545cebca0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Fran\u00e7ois Beaufort \u003cbeaufort.francois@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063148 [wpt PR 61896] - [WebMCP] Reject executeTool when tool result cannot be JSON serialized, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[WebMCP] Reject executeTool when tool result cannot be JSON serialized\n\nWhen an imperative or declarative WebMCP tool returns an object that\ncannot be JSON-serialized (e.g. a circular object), v8::JSON::Stringify\nthrows an exception in V8 without being caught. Previously, this caused\nan uncaught TypeError to be logged to the DevTools console, but the\ncode fell back to String conversion (e.g. \"[object Object]\") and\nresolved the executeTool promise successfully.\n\nThis CL wraps v8::JSON::Stringify in a v8::TryCatch scope for both\nimperative and declarative tool results, catches any serialization\nerrors, logs the failure message, and properly fails the tool invocation\nso that executeTool() rejects with an UnknownError DOMException.\n\nBug: 543815035\nChange-Id: I4424c4671076a4532a11e401d773f6c5c9715417\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8224523\nReviewed-by: Dominic Farolino \u003cdom@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Dominic Farolino \u003cdom@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1678357}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: ac742e381c4c8d8e13d142c25bddbd42d40617e3\nwpt-pr: 61896\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/declarative/executeTool-respondWith-circular-object.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/imperative/executeTool-error-window-onerror.https.html"], "git_node": "2f19eae6945b70d175c99a4460ecee2c7363c13d", "git_parents": ["099beaa54d899fe248feb362e00308f3d2c2229b"], "node": "4cdffe54d881c3750fc75a6e184939aa0be61a00", "parents": ["5b73bf14083f14509de1bd680e922a9fc692ba77"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063148 [wpt PR 61896] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61896\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webmcp/declarative/executeTool-respondWith-circular-object.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webmcp/imperative/executeTool-error-window-onerror.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "a407712e433104ad8757a37545cdcdb4a65c9b11", "git_parents": ["2f19eae6945b70d175c99a4460ecee2c7363c13d"], "node": "5f1ef63480e1ee476a27fb598b2c5f4d115b9b30", "parents": ["4cdffe54d881c3750fc75a6e184939aa0be61a00"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Marcos C\u00e1ceres \u003ccaceres_m@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062964 [wpt PR 61886] - [geolocation] fix the accuracyMode test's precise case and coordinate assertions, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[geolocation] fix the accuracyMode test's precise case and coordinate assertions (#61886)\n\nThe second test is named \"precise\" but requested \"approximate\" and then asserted that altitude,\naltitudeAccuracy, heading and speed come back populated, which w3c/geolocation#233 requires to be null\nfor an approximate position.\n\nThe first test asserted that the emulated latitude, longitude and accuracy come back unchanged, which an\nimplementation that actually coarsens cannot satisfy, and the pull request leaves the coarsened area to\nthe underlying system.\n\nAlso drops two assignments to an undeclared calledAsync global.\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 315976933870b34d6ea30e3f6643403edae678ba\nwpt-pr: 61886\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/geolocation/getCurrentPosition-accuracyMode.https.html"], "git_node": "6c6f73b244d537fa4216c7ba43a455a9d7292668", "git_parents": ["a407712e433104ad8757a37545cdcdb4a65c9b11"], "node": "61a9dcca7a62275f9eb56958a1a55cd070330243", "parents": ["5f1ef63480e1ee476a27fb598b2c5f4d115b9b30"], "tags": []}, {"author": "lilly \u003c173393835+cupidsity@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056394 [wpt PR 61426] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=319426, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=319426 (#61426)\n\n* WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=319426\n\n* Update fuzzy value for corner-shape superellipse concave test\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: lilly \u003c173393835+codedbycupidity@users.noreply.github.com\u003e\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 28c5298658d4dad055db5e3356895c5a6b1f03a7\nwpt-pr: 61426\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-superellipse-c