Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D301275\n", "files": ["dom/media/MediaTrackGraph.cpp", "dom/media/MediaTrackGraphImpl.h", "dom/media/gtest/TestAudioTrackGraph.cpp"], "git_node": "186f4c8a3c90dc7b398203b0d87cd67ba459c783", "git_parents": ["5c0ae53343b58726f66960a18bef96d13486f742"], "node": "bb4b18c692e6250223136dd76c5aac401ca4466c", "parents": ["b7413f2349f75ea6c3873645ec8b988b05672ded"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1993981 - Implement AbstractThread for MediaTrackGraphImpl. r=karlt\n\nThis patch makes MediaTrackGraphImpl implement AbstractThread and its base\ninterface nsISerialEventTarget.\n\nThis allows running nsIRunnables natively on the graph.\n\nTo facilitate runnables that need to run during graph shutdown, the graph will\ncall OnDiscard() on those runnables that QI to nsIDiscardableRunnable and they\nmay run then. Note that runnables dispatched through the nsISerialEventTarget\nand AbstractThread APIs (i.e. Dispatch()) will wrap runnables that don't\nimplement nsIDiscardableRunnable so they run on shutdown by default. This should\navoid silently dropping async tasks from e.g. MozPromise that require settling\nbefore being released.\nDuring shutdown, nsIRunnable's Run() will not be called directly by the graph,\nand all runnables will be processed (OnDiscard() and release) on the main\nthread to guarantee event order consistency.\n\nMessageBlocks are removed, as the graph no longer will manage the batching of\ntasks dispatched from main thread. The main thread's tail dispatcher will manage\nbatching instead, and dispatched per-thread group runnables will enter\nmBackMessageQueue regularly. The same mechanism now works from any thread. Only\nmain thread dispatches affect the graph's lifecycle, however.\n\nFor a non-main thread to dispatch tasks to the graph, it will have to be sure to\nkeep the graph alive. The only guarantee for this is still to hold onto a live\ntrack.\n\nAny thread that is used to dispatch a task to the graph must support tail\ndispatch. While not strictly required for the function of the graph, this\nenforces the old mechanism of running messages from main thread atomically, and\nspreads that behavior to any other thread. It also reduces contention on the\ngraph's Monitor.\n\nDispatching from the graph to any other thread should also use tail dispatch for\nperformance reasons -- e.g dispatching to the busy main thread may suffer from\nlock contention which is not ideal on the real-time audio thread. However,\nenforcing tail dispatch when dispatching *from* the graph thread is not possible\nwithout going through a proxy function. This is by convention for now.\n\nTail dispatch from the graph to the main thread means that the main thread state\nis updated before graph thread to main thread runnables run.\n\nThis requires some child revisions or it may render issues:\n- D277177: to allow non-tail dispatched messages to the graph from the\n           IPC I/O Child for AudioWorklet MessagePorts.\n- D277181: to maintain atomicity between all messages dispatched from a single\n           task on a given thread, as AbstractThread normally closes a target\n           group runnable for new tasks upon tail dispatch to another target.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D277176\n", "files": ["dom/media/MediaTrackGraph.cpp", "dom/media/MediaTrackGraph.h", "dom/media/MediaTrackGraphImpl.h", "dom/media/gtest/TestAudioCallbackDriver.cpp", "dom/media/gtest/TestAudioDecoderInputTrack.cpp", "dom/media/gtest/TestAudioTrackGraph.cpp", "dom/media/gtest/TestDecodedStream.cpp", "dom/media/gtest/TestDeviceInputTrack.cpp", "xpcom/threads/AbstractThread.h"], "git_node": "7cdca42e6da4c77b167be8832d0a82cd54a2df7d", "git_parents": ["186f4c8a3c90dc7b398203b0d87cd67ba459c783"], "node": "36a2e5538e1bbd6783917d98485a12e1916936d7", "parents": ["bb4b18c692e6250223136dd76c5aac401ca4466c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1993981 - In MediaTrackGraphImpl natively support AudioWorklet's message passing. r=karlt\n\nThis patch does two things to support AudioWorklet:\n- Supports target shutdown tasks.\n- Exempts the IPC I/O Child thread from the tail dispatch requirement.\n\nThe IPC I/O Child thread does not support tail dispatch, and there are no\nordering requirements between those messages and any from other threads.\n\nPrior to D277176, these messages went through GraphRunner::mThread. It was\ngiven to the MessageChannel opened in the AudioWorklet through\nGetCurrentSerialEventTarget().\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D277177\n", "files": ["dom/media/MediaTrackGraph.cpp", "dom/media/MediaTrackGraphImpl.h"], "git_node": "7365f2d5bb2841a8e3f03eea7480d97e09bf8625", "git_parents": ["7cdca42e6da4c77b167be8832d0a82cd54a2df7d"], "node": "f3fce358e2ba64cd854182e48f7a20be6c341575", "parents": ["36a2e5538e1bbd6783917d98485a12e1916936d7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1993981 - To MockProcessedMediaTrack add mocks for {Add|Remove}ListenerImpl. r=karlt\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D277178\n", "files": ["dom/media/gtest/TestAudioTrackGraph.cpp"], "git_node": "165e177d7aebc46ca0b28f33a76dd4854384fb0a", "git_parents": ["7365f2d5bb2841a8e3f03eea7480d97e09bf8625"], "node": "6707668d3facd4bac2c0b2ea881318d9a6966827", "parents": ["f3fce358e2ba64cd854182e48f7a20be6c341575"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1993981 - Unit test event ordering between the graph and main thread. r=karlt\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D277179\n", "files": ["dom/media/gtest/TestAudioTrackGraph.cpp"], "git_node": "864197925fafa3999eb2f91909b1db651aa6d1ba", "git_parents": ["165e177d7aebc46ca0b28f33a76dd4854384fb0a"], "node": "694f5770d97379ef743c517f5d3da2035bb2bc4d", "parents": ["6707668d3facd4bac2c0b2ea881318d9a6966827"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1993981 - Unit test message atomicity. r=karlt\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D277180\n", "files": ["dom/media/gtest/TestAudioTrackGraph.cpp"], "git_node": "edde7ff9c21903decc50b4db1ffd545a96e65540", "git_parents": ["864197925fafa3999eb2f91909b1db651aa6d1ba"], "node": "0a7814a68ff38c26bfa8248f0269313f319d56f8", "parents": ["694f5770d97379ef743c517f5d3da2035bb2bc4d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1993981 - Introduce an atomicity policy for tail dispatch. r=karlt,xpcom-reviewers,nika,webrtc-reviewers,bwc,media-playback-reviewers\n\nFor MediaTrackGraph to be able to switch its manual batching of control\nmessages to tail dispatch, the message atomicity guarantee it provides needs to\nbe retained. This patch introduces an atomicity mode for tail dispatch to\nsupport the graph.\n\nTo tidy up the AbstractThread API, the old boolean aSupportsTailDispatch flag\npassed at construction is changed to a new TailDispatchPolicy enum. Converting\ncallers which passed that flag is the bulk of the change.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D277181\n", "files": ["dom/media/MediaDecoderStateMachineBase.cpp", "dom/media/MediaFormatReader.cpp", "dom/media/MediaManager.cpp", "dom/media/MediaTrackGraph.cpp", "dom/media/gtest/TestAudioTrackGraph.cpp", "dom/media/gtest/TestWebrtcTaskQueueWrapper.cpp", "dom/media/hls/HLSDemuxer.cpp", "dom/media/webcodecs/WebCodecsUtils.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/PeerConnectionCtx.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/libwebrtcglue/VideoConduit.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/libwebrtcglue/WebrtcTaskQueueWrapper.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/libwebrtcglue/WebrtcTaskQueueWrapper.h", "media/webrtc/signaling/gtest/mediapipeline_unittest.cpp", "xpcom/tests/gtest/TestAutoOwningEventTarget.cpp", "xpcom/tests/gtest/TestDelayedRunnable.cpp", "xpcom/tests/gtest/TestStateMirroring.cpp", "xpcom/tests/gtest/TestTargetShutdownTask.cpp", "xpcom/tests/gtest/TestTaskQueue.cpp", "xpcom/threads/AbstractThread.cpp", "xpcom/threads/AbstractThread.h", "xpcom/threads/TaskDispatcher.h", "xpcom/threads/TaskQueue.cpp", "xpcom/threads/TaskQueue.h"], "git_node": "3eba0a27139e6f2276913191923b13f3f64f05c9", "git_parents": ["edde7ff9c21903decc50b4db1ffd545a96e65540"], "node": "48574c9879809cf4e6525023ca578e75bb926c5d", "parents": ["0a7814a68ff38c26bfa8248f0269313f319d56f8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1993981 - Unit test graph shutdown message ordering. r=karlt\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D288112\n", "files": ["dom/media/gtest/TestAudioTrackGraph.cpp"], "git_node": "1a7e168f54f6af492380b66bc240728fa5d1b3dd", "git_parents": ["3eba0a27139e6f2276913191923b13f3f64f05c9"], "node": "d7ba75a4c1ef86f1b8684b198f6bd60e59893a54", "parents": ["48574c9879809cf4e6525023ca578e75bb926c5d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1993981 - Rename MediaTrackGraphImpl::LifecycleStateRef() -\u003e LifecycleState() and return state by value. r=karlt\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D305600\n", "files": ["dom/media/MediaTrackGraph.cpp", "dom/media/MediaTrackGraphImpl.h", "dom/media/gtest/TestDecodedStream.cpp"], "git_node": "86b579e21cdd88bf1d53ce7ad399fa44bdb4661f", "git_parents": ["1a7e168f54f6af492380b66bc240728fa5d1b3dd"], "node": "6d2e13f1a3392383e06cde2b76356f9fe29f3c6d", "parents": ["d7ba75a4c1ef86f1b8684b198f6bd60e59893a54"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Chevobbe \u003cnchevobbe@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055445 - [devtools] Display higher precision width and height in ViewportSize highlighter. r=emilio,devtools-reviewers,layout-reviewers,webidl,ochameau,jdescottes\n\nWe add a NeedsCallerType annotation on Window#inner(Width|Height) and use it\nto avoid rounding in nsGlobalWindowOuter::GetInnerSize when this is a system call.\n\nSince the ViewportSize highlighter calls Window#inner(Width|Height) as a system\ncall, we're getting non rounded values.\nWe then display the size with a single decimal, as it should be precise enough.\n\nAlso remove unused nsPIDOMWindowOuter nsresult GetInnerWidth|Height and their\nnsGlobalWindowOuter overrides.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318182\n", "files": ["devtools/client/inspector/test/highlighter/browser_inspector_highlighter-rulers_03.js", "devtools/client/inspector/test/highlighter/browser_inspector_highlighter-viewport-size.js", "devtools/server/actors/highlighters/viewport-size.js", "dom/base/nsGlobalWindowInner.cpp", "dom/base/nsGlobalWindowInner.h", "dom/base/nsGlobalWindowOuter.cpp", "dom/base/nsGlobalWindowOuter.h", "dom/base/nsPIDOMWindow.h", "dom/documentpip/DocumentPictureInPicture.cpp", "dom/html/test/browser_ImageDocument_svg_zoom.js", "dom/webidl/Window.webidl", "remote/marionette/actors/MarionetteCommandsChild.sys.mjs", "remote/webdriver-bidi/modules/windowglobal/browsingContext.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "c7974295848da3ca402184d309f0e33a2300e131", "git_parents": ["86b579e21cdd88bf1d53ce7ad399fa44bdb4661f"], "node": "8eef8800d2c71e8cae1f99c1ca685a00db565456", "parents": ["6d2e13f1a3392383e06cde2b76356f9fe29f3c6d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Timothy Nikkel \u003ctnikkel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063876. Update third_party/js/prosemirror/LICENSE to the revision it is vendored from. r=sylvestre\n\nThe root moz.yaml here vendors a single file, LICENSE, from the ProseMirror meta\nrepository at 0126a40c14d4, and the copy in the tree is an older revision of that file,\nso vendoring does not reproduce it:\n\n  -Copyright (C) 2015-2016 by Marijn Haverbeke \u003cmarijnh@gmail.com\u003e and others\n  +Copyright (C) 2015-2017 by Marijn Haverbeke \u003cmarijn@haverbeke.berlin\u003e and others\n\nOnly the copyright line differs, in the year range and the address. The MIT terms are\nbyte for byte identical, and the nine prosemirror-* packages vendored next to it already\ncarry the newer line, so this also brings the ten license files into agreement.\n\nNothing checked that vendoring reproduced the tree until now, so a one line difference in\na license file had nothing to surface it.\n\ntoolkit/content/license.html already carries this exact line for the ProseMirror packages, so the vendored copy was the only place still showing the older one.\n\nWith this, `./mach vendor third_party/js/prosemirror/moz.yaml -r\n0126a40c14d408a275743058d8cd04d3fc64834c --patch-mode check --force` reproduces the\ncommitted tree exactly.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318922\n", "files": ["third_party/js/prosemirror/LICENSE"], "git_node": "7e22765c313322946765be63ae98e4b467b355be", "git_parents": ["c7974295848da3ca402184d309f0e33a2300e131"], "node": "0d6c6b9c10e88c3b19db1bb355b137133b2576a7", "parents": ["8eef8800d2c71e8cae1f99c1ca685a00db565456"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julian Descottes \u003cjdescottes@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062544 - [devtools] Add preference to use a mock for MDN compat data r=devtools-reviewers,nchevobbe\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318843\n", "files": ["devtools/server/actors/compatibility/compatibility.js", "devtools/shared/compatibility/compatibility-dataset.js", "devtools/shared/compatibility/dataset/mock-css-properties.json", "devtools/shared/compatibility/dataset/moz.build", "devtools/shared/compatibility/moz.build"], "git_node": "6a3bab56331b8747399f8823c8c71b0be1386c0c", "git_parents": ["7e22765c313322946765be63ae98e4b467b355be"], "node": "3e94bd0a21a89ba9da10b7ffe63e15f33f1c27ad", "parents": ["0d6c6b9c10e88c3b19db1bb355b137133b2576a7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julian Descottes \u003cjdescottes@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062544 - [devtools] Update mdn compat tests to use mock compat data r=devtools-reviewers,nchevobbe\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318879\n", "files": ["devtools/client/inspector/compatibility/test/browser/browser.toml", "devtools/client/inspector/compatibility/test/browser/browser_compatibility_css-property_issue.js", "devtools/client/inspector/compatibility/test/browser/head.js", "devtools/client/inspector/rules/test/browser_part2.toml", "devtools/client/inspector/rules/test/browser_rules_css-compatibility-add-rename-rule.js", "devtools/client/inspector/rules/test/browser_rules_css-compatibility-check-add-fix.js", "devtools/client/inspector/rules/test/browser_rules_css-compatibility-learn-more-link.js", "devtools/client/inspector/rules/test/browser_rules_css-compatibility-toggle-rules.js", "devtools/client/inspector/rules/test/browser_rules_css-compatibility-tooltip-telemetry.js", "devtools/client/shared/test/shared-head.js", "devtools/server/actors/compatibility/lib/test/xpcshell/test_mdn-compatibility.js", "devtools/server/actors/compatibility/lib/test/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml", "devtools/server/tests/browser/browser.toml", "devtools/server/tests/browser/browser_compatibility_cssIssues.js", "devtools/shared/compatibility/README.md", "devtools/shared/compatibility/dataset/mock-css-properties.json"], "git_node": "a48c558ddad5ce55c5d619d98f5651b3180dfbef", "git_parents": ["6a3bab56331b8747399f8823c8c71b0be1386c0c"], "node": "4fd132b4e4e253635a22116ac7467cf1036264e9", "parents": ["3e94bd0a21a89ba9da10b7ffe63e15f33f1c27ad"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julian Descottes \u003cjdescottes@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062544 - [devtools] Add smoke tests for MDN compat live data r=devtools-reviewers,nchevobbe\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318880\n", "files": ["devtools/client/inspector/compatibility/test/browser/browser.toml", "devtools/client/inspector/compatibility/test/browser/browser_compatibility_live-data.js", "devtools/server/actors/compatibility/lib/test/xpcshell/test_mdn-compatibility-live-data.js", "devtools/server/actors/compatibility/lib/test/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "70a64ca123773ea50d1778fa375cdd3c61f8c994", "git_parents": ["a48c558ddad5ce55c5d619d98f5651b3180dfbef"], "node": "59691a4d6da2727e9ae744e65de9375b99a7bfe2", "parents": ["4fd132b4e4e253635a22116ac7467cf1036264e9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062823 - Let Tab land on the search input rather than the search button, behind a Nightly-only pref. r=daleharvey,Jamie,urlbar-reviewers\n\nThe search button declines to be the target of the toolbar tab stop in front\nof the address bar and the search bar, so that Tab lands on the input and the\nbutton is reached with Shift+Tab from there. In the address bar, forward\ntabbing consequently stops on the first site information button, so the number\nof stops before the input is unchanged.\n\nThe resulting tab order is asymmetric, which a11y review accepted while noting\nthat we may need to reconsider if users push back, so this is behind\nbrowser.urlbar.searchModeSwitcher.skipTabStop, enabled on Nightly only.\n\nThe button's markup carries tabindex=\"-1\", but the toolbar tab stop and the\nview-open Tab cycle both treated it as an ordinary toolbar button, setting a\ntabindex and removing it again on blur. Removing it from the moz-button host\nis what left the button permanently tabbable. Both now leave the button's own\ntabindex alone, which is a fix under either pref value and so isn't gated.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317259\n", "files": ["browser/app/profile/firefox.js", "browser/base/content/browser-toolbarKeyNav.js", "browser/base/content/test/keyboard/browser_toolbarKeyNav.js", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarPrefs.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/SearchModeSwitcher.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarChildController.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/searchbar/browser_searchbar_keyboard_navigation.js"], "git_node": "75869655dee0e9d4be6a791f25f5e815fe6d04f7", "git_parents": ["70a64ca123773ea50d1778fa375cdd3c61f8c994"], "node": "4b569f3431964135efb2415487896ab6146405b4", "parents": ["59691a4d6da2727e9ae744e65de9375b99a7bfe2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "iulian moraru \u003cimoraru@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2043211, Bug 2051282: apply code formatting via Lando\" for causing build bustages on jsep_track_unittest.cpp.\n\nThis reverts commit 05698d67c38a9dc80bd9b4ab8a891266c2c98825.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2051282 - Add back peer connection H264 telemetry on PCImpl Init. r=dbaker\"\n\nThis reverts commit 20f51a70af2b358b0a597f9fdf18dff70443af85.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2043211 - Add PeerConnectionImpl unittests for transport-cc pref behavior. r=dbaker\"\n\nThis reverts commit 082d27fc3a5e730af6192201c3b6f15e13f44a59.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2043211 - In jsep, move rtp header extensions to nsCString. r=webrtc-reviewers,bwc\"\n\nThis reverts commit 9f95b1ba567a7ded8b46794f83028d40e17faf60.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2043211 - In jsep, move rtp header extensions to nsTArray. r=webrtc-reviewers,dbaker\"\n\nThis reverts commit ba9a9cd9cfbff92246b098d15f4a51e3c05e8f95.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2043211 - Remove redundant CodecOverrides setters. r=webrtc-reviewers,bwc\"\n\nThis reverts commit 5a4194d5abbdc5da0a9eac40e2be6096ff8d3dd5.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2043211 - In PeerConnectionImpl clean up codec and rtp header extension getters. r=webrtc-reviewers,bwc,dbaker\"\n\nThis reverts commit ddb5a3f9b978b25603646831839a3bed91b3038e.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2043211 - Refactor EnumerateDefaultCodecs to take prefs by ref and output param by pointer. r=webrtc-reviewers,bwc\"\n\nThis reverts commit 3fb35b2bb7014fe4b1d3c77a784f78dbfe20f4ef.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2043211 - In jsep, move codecs to nsTArray. r=webrtc-reviewers,bwc\"\n\nThis reverts commit 1a527a01daed8d15662c25eca32eec1df25b47e2.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2043211 - Rename members and args in jsep_track_unittest to match Mozilla style. r=webrtc-reviewers,bwc\"\n\nThis reverts commit 41b31a0cc9af33692f650206846836c225b3232e.\n", "files": ["dom/media/webrtc/CodecInfo.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/DefaultCodecPreferences.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/DefaultCodecPreferences.h", "dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/PeerConnectionImpl.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/PeerConnectionImpl.h", "dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/RTCRtpReceiver.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/RTCRtpSender.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/RTCRtpTransceiver.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/RTCRtpTransceiver.h", "dom/media/webrtc/jsep/JsepCodecDescription.h", "dom/media/webrtc/jsep/JsepSession.h", "dom/media/webrtc/jsep/JsepSessionImpl.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/jsep/JsepSessionImpl.h", "dom/media/webrtc/jsep/JsepTrack.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/jsep/JsepTrack.h", "dom/media/webrtc/sdp/RsdparsaSdpAttributeList.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/sdp/SdpAttribute.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/sdp/SdpAttribute.h", "dom/media/webrtc/sdp/SipccSdpAttributeList.cpp", "media/webrtc/signaling/gtest/MockJsepCodecPreferences.h", "media/webrtc/signaling/gtest/jsep_session_unittest.cpp", "media/webrtc/signaling/gtest/jsep_track_unittest.cpp", "media/webrtc/signaling/gtest/moz.build", "media/webrtc/signaling/gtest/peer_connection_unittest.cpp", "media/webrtc/signaling/gtest/sdp_unittests.cpp"], "git_node": "b9b93c7817a5c2b5e3d85ace4d83487df4f57446", "git_parents": ["75869655dee0e9d4be6a791f25f5e815fe6d04f7"], "node": "16605c92854d3916e1a0bd2f028dbec3439b7168", "parents": ["4b569f3431964135efb2415487896ab6146405b4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Norisz Fay \u003cnfay@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 1993981 - Rename MediaTrackGraphImpl::LifecycleStateRef() -\u003e LifecycleState() and return state by value. r=karlt\" for causing bustage @ AbstractThread.h and Gtest failures @ StateWatching.h\n\nThis reverts commit 86b579e21cdd88bf1d53ce7ad399fa44bdb4661f.\n\nRevert \"Bug 1993981 - Unit test graph shutdown message ordering. r=karlt\"\n\nThis reverts commit 1a7e168f54f6af492380b66bc240728fa5d1b3dd.\n\nRevert \"Bug 1993981 - Introduce an atomicity policy for tail dispatch. r=karlt,xpcom-reviewers,nika,webrtc-reviewers,bwc,media-playback-reviewers\"\n\nThis reverts commit 3eba0a27139e6f2276913191923b13f3f64f05c9.\n\nRevert \"Bug 1993981 - Unit test message atomicity. r=karlt\"\n\nThis reverts commit edde7ff9c21903decc50b4db1ffd545a96e65540.\n\nRevert \"Bug 1993981 - Unit test event ordering between the graph and main thread. r=karlt\"\n\nThis reverts commit 864197925fafa3999eb2f91909b1db651aa6d1ba.\n\nRevert \"Bug 1993981 - To MockProcessedMediaTrack add mocks for {Add|Remove}ListenerImpl. r=karlt\"\n\nThis reverts commit 165e177d7aebc46ca0b28f33a76dd4854384fb0a.\n\nRevert \"Bug 1993981 - In MediaTrackGraphImpl natively support AudioWorklet's message passing. r=karlt\"\n\nThis reverts commit 7365f2d5bb2841a8e3f03eea7480d97e09bf8625.\n\nRevert \"Bug 1993981 - Implement AbstractThread for MediaTrackGraphImpl. r=karlt\"\n\nThis reverts commit 7cdca42e6da4c77b167be8832d0a82cd54a2df7d.\n\nRevert \"Bug 1993981 - Rename MediaTrackGraphImpl::Dispatch to DispatchToMainThread to avoid naming conflicts with nsISerialEventTarget. r=karlt\"\n\nThis reverts commit 186f4c8a3c90dc7b398203b0d87cd67ba459c783.\n\nRevert \"Bug 1993981 - Allow canceling cancelable and discardable tail-dispatched runnables. r=xpcom-reviewers,nika\"\n\nThis reverts commit 5c0ae53343b58726f66960a18bef96d13486f742.\n\nRevert \"Bug 1993981 - Implement nsIDirectTaskDispatcher for MediaTrackGraphImpl. r=karlt\"\n\nThis reverts commit 05da49140e79c5edf24bfa224e656585fc0f4b81.\n\nRevert \"Bug 1993981 - Store ControlMessages as runnables. r=karlt\"\n\nThis reverts commit 68a2b11b5fc85bb15d3e824e716306a55e094285.\n", "files": ["dom/media/MediaDecoderStateMachineBase.cpp", "dom/media/MediaFormatReader.cpp", "dom/media/MediaManager.cpp", "dom/media/MediaTrackGraph.cpp", "dom/media/MediaTrackGraph.h", "dom/media/MediaTrackGraphImpl.h", "dom/media/gtest/TestAudioCallbackDriver.cpp", "dom/media/gtest/TestAudioDecoderInputTrack.cpp", "dom/media/gtest/TestAudioTrackGraph.cpp", "dom/media/gtest/TestDecodedStream.cpp", "dom/media/gtest/TestDeviceInputTrack.cpp", "dom/media/gtest/TestWebrtcTaskQueueWrapper.cpp", "dom/media/hls/HLSDemuxer.cpp", "dom/media/webcodecs/WebCodecsUtils.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/PeerConnectionCtx.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/libwebrtcglue/VideoConduit.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/libwebrtcglue/WebrtcTaskQueueWrapper.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/libwebrtcglue/WebrtcTaskQueueWrapper.h", "media/webrtc/signaling/gtest/mediapipeline_unittest.cpp", "xpcom/tests/gtest/TestAutoOwningEventTarget.cpp", "xpcom/tests/gtest/TestDelayedRunnable.cpp", "xpcom/tests/gtest/TestStateMirroring.cpp", "xpcom/tests/gtest/TestTargetShutdownTask.cpp", "xpcom/tests/gtest/TestTaskQueue.cpp", "xpcom/threads/AbstractThread.cpp", "xpcom/threads/AbstractThread.h", "xpcom/threads/TaskDispatcher.h", "xpcom/threads/TaskQueue.cpp", "xpcom/threads/TaskQueue.h"], "git_node": "78d889f1dc3660d76f89d0941d121e3ed5a6ae11", "git_parents": ["b9b93c7817a5c2b5e3d85ace4d83487df4f57446"], "node": "2d0da34c9aba3abc45464023ac2b7c8ae1704a2a", "parents": ["16605c92854d3916e1a0bd2f028dbec3439b7168"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Norisz Fay \u003cnfay@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2062642 - Enable hw support for AV1 in WebRTC with a pref, when available on the platform. r=webrtc-reviewers,bwc\" for causing wpt failures @ decodingInfo-webrtc-power-efficient.any.html\n\nThis reverts commit 498711e128fedb7f40800f98a368a23f17348a91.\n", "files": ["dom/media/webrtc/libwebrtcglue/WebrtcMediaDataDecoderCodec.cpp", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "afed8deed47b0ce9c379aff8fd07dc9b99783956", "git_parents": ["78d889f1dc3660d76f89d0941d121e3ed5a6ae11"], "node": "b76de53f26082f50786ecb9f1294b64ade00c456", "parents": ["2d0da34c9aba3abc45464023ac2b7c8ae1704a2a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063271 - Remove dead Wayland minification workaround. r=stransky,gtk-reviewers\n\nWayland windows will never get the iconified state, so there's no way\nthey end up with nsSizeMode_Minimized.\n\nThis comes from bug 1572455 which predates the mSizeMode / mSizeState\nunification in bug 1773665. So when this landed, it was possible for a\nwayland window to have mSizeMode = Minimized, but that's no longer the\ncase.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318452\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/nsWindow.cpp"], "git_node": "9bd4b1639fa80b62bcbf0af85b86367d2974b13a", "git_parents": ["afed8deed47b0ce9c379aff8fd07dc9b99783956"], "node": "64f51e3a387caf0a90dd26d0e63ebd9e76b8ecab", "parents": ["b76de53f26082f50786ecb9f1294b64ade00c456"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Manuel Bucher \u003cmanuel@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058463 - Fix net-error-card tests using stale state to check exception button visibility r=crypto-reviewers,keeler\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314614\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/test/about/browser_aboutCertError_notYetValid.js", "browser/base/content/test/about/browser_aboutCertError_revoked.js", "browser/base/content/test/about/browser_aboutCertError_untrustedIssuer.js", "browser/base/content/test/about/browser_aboutNetError_invalid_cert_noUserFix.js"], "git_node": "647003e9dc4e5cbff4e63eff2194f1d89c551dbb", "git_parents": ["9bd4b1639fa80b62bcbf0af85b86367d2974b13a"], "node": "8af6fdc1503342544e5cd5bc30815d7f4c097b0d", "parents": ["64f51e3a387caf0a90dd26d0e63ebd9e76b8ecab"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Timothy Nikkel \u003ctnikkel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063948. Make third_party/llama.cpp vendor again. r=padenot\n\nTwo things stop `./mach vendor` from reproducing the tree, both from the patch rebase in\nbug 2043658.\n\nexceptions.patch has a hunk for src/models/models.h that removes\n`#include \"moz-overrides.h\"`, where its other fourteen hunks add that include. The patch is\nthe first one applied, so its base is pristine upstream, which has no such line and cannot\nhave it removed. patch reports\n\n  1 out of 1 hunks ignored--saving rejects to 'src/models/models.h.rej'\n\nand vendoring stops there, before the other twelve patches are applied at all. The tree has\nthe include, so only the patch file is wrong; regenerate the hunk to add it.\n\nThe include reordering in fifteen files is not in any patch. \"Rebase patch 1 (exceptions)\"\nmoved the system headers ahead of models.h in src/llama-model.cpp and fourteen\nsrc/models/*.cpp, directly in the sources, so re-vendoring puts back upstream's order. That\nordering matters now that models.h pulls in moz-overrides.h, which redefines the catch\nmacros: the reorder keeps those out of the system headers. Capture it as include-order.patch,\nlisted last so it applies on top of the other thirteen.\n\nAlso point the moz.yaml at Core :: Machine Learning: General rather than Core :: xul, which\nis what moz.build says for this directory. Updatebot files from the moz.yaml block, so its\nupdate bugs were going to xul.\n\nWith both, `./mach vendor third_party/llama.cpp/moz.yaml -r\n74ade52741203e5c8f81eaf06a96cb1cfe15f2a3 --patch-mode check --force` reproduces the\ncommitted tree exactly.\n\nNeither was visible without running the vendoring: the sources in the tree are correct, and\nnothing checked that they could be regenerated from the manifest until now.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318988\n", "files": ["third_party/llama.cpp/exceptions.patch", "third_party/llama.cpp/include-order.patch", "third_party/llama.cpp/moz.yaml"], "git_node": "e3bfebe1ae03efc05b4f8f4528d59cb9526445f4", "git_parents": ["647003e9dc4e5cbff4e63eff2194f1d89c551dbb"], "node": "c84cdcca86e2f1cb878c1ec7c8ad04db8b8a087a", "parents": ["8af6fdc1503342544e5cd5bc30815d7f4c097b0d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julian Seward \u003cjseward@acm.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055525 - part 1: handle variable-length trap insns in IsPlausibleStackMapKey.  r=bvisness.\n\nThis is the first of five final infrastructure patches needed to support the\ngoal of adding missing stackmaps for traps.\n\nThis patch updates IsPlausibleStackMapKey().  Currently it can only identify\ncall instructions and official-UD instructions, because no stackmap has any\nother kind of key.  Going forward it will need to handle stackmaps whose key is\nany faulting instruction.  The patch modifies IsPlausibleStackMapKey so that it\nno longer tries to identify trapping instructions itself.  Instead it delegates\nthat to the pre-existing routine SummarizeTrapInstruction.\n\nThis also has do deal with the problem that a stackmap key (which we are\nprovided with) points to the instruction after the call/trap with which it is\nassociated.  To find the relevant trap-insn key, we need to back up one\ninstruction.  But we don't know its length (in general), nor can we parse\ninstructions backwards (in general); so we are forced to iterate through all\npossible start positions of the previous instruction to find one that\nSummarizeTrapInstruction tells us is correct.\n\nIn practice this is not a big cost (~2.5 tries/call for x86_64, 1 try/call for\nall other targets) and also, this is only needed in ifdef-DEBUG code.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316783\n", "files": ["js/src/wasm/WasmGC.cpp", "js/src/wasm/WasmGC.h"], "git_node": "9914fa2d31a514d90c305603b2ba511dd90ed4a2", "git_parents": ["e3bfebe1ae03efc05b4f8f4528d59cb9526445f4"], "node": "6187c07db1d6b06dabd6ac8d161d523ea27f5c58", "parents": ["c84cdcca86e2f1cb878c1ec7c8ad04db8b8a087a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julian Seward \u003cjseward@acm.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055525 - part 2: driver logic for checking that selected traps have stackmaps.  r=bvisness.\n\nThis patch adds logic for checking that selected traps have stackmaps.  For\nboth Ion and baseline, this identifies trapsites created by compilation of each\nfunction, and passes that to new routine CheckStackMapsForTraps, which verifies\nthat selected trap kinds have a stackmap.\n\nCheckStackMapsForTraps is called after each function compilation, rather than\nat the end of a module, so as to make it easy to identify, in the\nIONFLAGS=codegen log, traps that have a missing stackmap.  Information about\nchecks and missing stackmaps is also emitted in-line into the IONFLAGS=codegen\nlog.\n\nFixing all missing stackmaps (in future) in one pass is a big task.\nCheckStackMapsForTraps therefore takes a callback via which the caller can\nspecify which trap kinds to check.  Currently the callbacks are set up so that\nno stackmaps are checked; hence this entire patch is infrastructure but a\nfunctional no-op (even in debug builds).\n\nFinally, as a ride-along, the wasm::InstructionBytes mechanism (a source class\nfor SummarizeTrapInstruction) is cleaned up, by moving both of its child\nclasses out of the assembler stack and into WasmSummarizeInsn.cpp, making them\nentirely private to that file.  As a result SummarizeTrapInstruction can offer\ntwo overloads in its external interface, one that takes a `void*` and another\nwhich takes a MacroAssembler and offset pair.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316785\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/MacroAssembler.cpp", "js/src/jit/shared/Assembler-shared.h", "js/src/wasm/WasmBaselineCompile.cpp", "js/src/wasm/WasmCodegenTypes.h", "js/src/wasm/WasmGC.cpp", "js/src/wasm/WasmGC.h", "js/src/wasm/WasmIonCompile.cpp", "js/src/wasm/WasmSummarizeInsn.cpp", "js/src/wasm/WasmSummarizeInsn.h"], "git_node": "f472e3c39b78294e503393f85b5046f01f1f085e", "git_parents": ["9914fa2d31a514d90c305603b2ba511dd90ed4a2"], "node": "ff1024a9efa928bc6cadddbcceee93d9c503aec0", "parents": ["6187c07db1d6b06dabd6ac8d161d523ea27f5c58"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julian Seward \u003cjseward@acm.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055525 - part 3: add new pref javascript.options.wasm_baseline_debug.  r=bvisness.\n\nIn practice, checking that all traps have suitable debug-mode stackmaps is\ndifficult, because it requires compiling arbitrary code inside a debug-enabled\ncontext.\n\nThis simple patch fixes that by adding a boolean pref\njavascript.options.wasm_baseline_debug, which forces baseline compilation with\ndebugging.\n\nIt also force-disables tiering and Ion compilation, since leaving them enabled\ncauses assertion failures down the line.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316786\n", "files": ["js/src/wasm/WasmCompile.cpp", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "334aa6e5825610e1a445f50bbe6eecb988ddce7e", "git_parents": ["f472e3c39b78294e503393f85b5046f01f1f085e"], "node": "f2da1d78124bf4c6676598d19ab5cbdf6f68e225", "parents": ["ff1024a9efa928bc6cadddbcceee93d9c503aec0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julian Seward \u003cjseward@acm.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055525 - part 4: selectively tolerate refs in regs in wasm stackmaps.  r=bvisness.\n\nwasm baseline's stackmap-creation logic release-asserts if it is asked to make\na stackmap at a point where there are refs in registers.  And rightly so!\n\nBut for debugging, we need to tolerate this; such stackmaps will be used to GC\nmemory-resident local variables in the wasm frame, whilst the register-bound\ntemporaries are dead.\n\nThe patch contains two logical parts:\n\n(1) Changes to StackMapGenerator::createStackMap, which is the core stack-map\n    creator for wasm baseline.  For situations where we are sure execution will\n    never resume after the (instruction associated with the) stackmap, it now\n    tolerates but ignores refs in registers.  If it cannot establish that,\n    behaviour is unchanged from before: refs in registers lead to a\n    release-assertion.\n\n(2) In order that (1) can decide whether execution might resume after the\n    stackmap, ::createStackMap now needs to be told the reason for creating the\n    stackmap.  This is specified as a `Maybe\u003cTrap\u003e` param, with `Nothing`\n    indicating the map is for a call instruction, and `Some(t)` indicating it\n    is a for a trap of kind `t`.\n\n    The changes are mostly plumbing.  Also, the `const char*` parameters passed\n    to ::createStackMap have been removed; they were never used for anything.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316787\n", "files": ["js/src/wasm/WasmBCClass.h", "js/src/wasm/WasmBCCodegen-inl.h", "js/src/wasm/WasmBCFrame.cpp", "js/src/wasm/WasmBCFrame.h", "js/src/wasm/WasmBaselineCompile.cpp", "js/src/wasm/WasmConstants.h", "js/src/wasm/WasmGC.cpp"], "git_node": "c5118eb5fc6206e139996fb9afa662e3d1f8cd2f", "git_parents": ["334aa6e5825610e1a445f50bbe6eecb988ddce7e"], "node": "b25392e4a41bc7af638f88fd5584a6f25a44eaa9", "parents": ["f2da1d78124bf4c6676598d19ab5cbdf6f68e225"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julian Seward \u003cjseward@acm.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055525 - part 5: rename BaseCompiler::createAbortingOutOfLineTrapStackMap.  r=bvisness.\n\nThis patch renames BaseCompiler::createAbortingOutOfLineTrapStackMap\nto ::createDebugOnlyStackMapForNonResumingTrap.\n\nThe original name is misleading:\n\n- It has nothing to do with inline-ness/out-of-line-ness; the routine\n  has no awareness of either bytecode or assembler-buffer offsets.\n\n- It fails to indicate the important point that the stackmap is created only\n  for debug compilation.\n\n- `Aborting trap` is not our normal terminology; that is `Non-Resuming trap`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316788\n", "files": ["js/src/wasm/WasmBCClass.h", "js/src/wasm/WasmBCFrame.cpp", "js/src/wasm/WasmBaselineCompile.cpp"], "git_node": "a2150ca279580d6f279eef0f1360af6b15b0d723", "git_parents": ["c5118eb5fc6206e139996fb9afa662e3d1f8cd2f"], "node": "4acf6ebb51bed42b2e8cf74da82db9740ad29da4", "parents": ["b25392e4a41bc7af638f88fd5584a6f25a44eaa9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lando \u003clando@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055525: apply code formatting via Lando\n\n# ignore-this-changeset\n", "files": ["js/src/wasm/WasmBCFrame.cpp", "js/src/wasm/WasmCompile.cpp", "js/src/wasm/WasmGC.cpp", "js/src/wasm/WasmSummarizeInsn.h"], "git_node": "5d732e99d7caf62caab4d8d17f03eadd9f5b7f32", "git_parents": ["a2150ca279580d6f279eef0f1360af6b15b0d723"], "node": "fa3badc226d363c76ee121fdd82ce43832e4bdfd", "parents": ["4acf6ebb51bed42b2e8cf74da82db9740ad29da4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "longsonr \u003clongsonr@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063998 - Allow SVGTransformList to be iterated over r=emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319047\n", "files": ["dom/svg/SVGElement.cpp", "dom/svg/SVGFEColorMatrixElement.cpp", "dom/svg/SVGNumberList.h", "dom/svg/SVGPathData.cpp", "dom/svg/SVGPointList.h", "dom/svg/SVGTransformList.h", "dom/svg/SVGTransformListSMILType.cpp"], "git_node": "466c20d2d01a91225c3345d3a15aa89ad211b8fa", "git_parents": ["5d732e99d7caf62caab4d8d17f03eadd9f5b7f32"], "node": "443ac5f5d7fcaa95d0e459a14f01710ae280b828", "parents": ["fa3badc226d363c76ee121fdd82ce43832e4bdfd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "longsonr \u003clongsonr@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063913 - Pass gradientUnits into methods that need it r=emilio\n\nGetGradientUnits can get expensive if there's a gradient chain as we need to iterate through the chain to read the units e.g.\n\n    \u003clinearGradient id=\"base\" gradientUnits=\"objectBoundingBox\"/\u003e\n    \u003clinearGradient href=\"#base\"/\u003e\n\nGradient chains can be arbitrarily long.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318954\n", "files": ["layout/svg/SVGGradientFrame.cpp", "layout/svg/SVGGradientFrame.h"], "git_node": "6c9248870e2fa6106dbf8cfbfd09e50e79e939f2", "git_parents": ["466c20d2d01a91225c3345d3a15aa89ad211b8fa"], "node": "2c92f618c776023a9d7970a0d932877dc713eac6", "parents": ["443ac5f5d7fcaa95d0e459a14f01710ae280b828"], "tags": []}, {"author": "giorga \u003cgiorga@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059494 - [TabGroups] Add TabGroups setting to tabs settings r=android-reviewers,android-l10n-reviewers,parker,007\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316489\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/SecretSettingsFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/TabsSettingsFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabstray/ui/TabManagementFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values/static_strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/xml/secret_settings_preferences.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/xml/tabs_preferences.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/debugsettings/info/SecretSettingsKeysProviderTest.kt"], "git_node": "8a7619eb3e03c48b3bd75e25b4fff229e092b123", "git_parents": ["6c9248870e2fa6106dbf8cfbfd09e50e79e939f2"], "node": "058fa1eba9085a96e91cff75e29d281371d10464", "parents": ["2c92f618c776023a9d7970a0d932877dc713eac6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "DrSeed Lu \u003cdr.seed.lu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2039602 - Add a setting for the open tabs hover preview to Customize Sidebar r=fluent-reviewers,kcochrane,bolsson\n\nCustomize Sidebar now shows a \"Show preview on hover\" option nested under\nthe Open Tabs tool. It is checked by default and controls the\nsidebar.openTabsPanel.hoverPreview.enabled pref that was added in Bug 2039601.\n\nThe option only renders while Open Tabs is enabled, following how expand on\nhover and hide tabs and sidebar are nested under vertical tabs.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318262\n", "files": ["browser/components/sidebar/sidebar-customize.mjs", "browser/components/sidebar/tests/browser/browser_customize_sidebar.js", "browser/components/sidebar/tests/browser/head.js", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/sidebar.ftl"], "git_node": "1615511fffc7a78d62dd49aab34d1565fda6a8c7", "git_parents": ["8a7619eb3e03c48b3bd75e25b4fff229e092b123"], "node": "302f712807774674a1714ae5a99daf163d133d0e", "parents": ["058fa1eba9085a96e91cff75e29d281371d10464"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dimi \u003cdlee@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063599 - Only enable ML address form field detection on pre-release channels. r=joschmidt\n\nTelemetry on 154 shows a regression in credit card expiry date detection\nsince ML field detection was enabled for all channels.\n\nGate the extensions.formautofill.useml default on the update channel so it\nstays enabled on Nightly, Dev Edition and Beta, and is disabled on Release\nand ESR.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318986\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/all.js"], "git_node": "d6966d4a93e6292d42ba26e4faddf1110c17e22a", "git_parents": ["1615511fffc7a78d62dd49aab34d1565fda6a8c7"], "node": "91b6b986e26c5b2c12d27f143218b0a394690055", "parents": ["302f712807774674a1714ae5a99daf163d133d0e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "t-p-white \u003ctowhite@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2051230 - Move Sync to continuous onboarding day 5 and IP Protection to day 7. r=android-reviewers,gmalekpour\n\nRenumbers the sync sign-in stage from day 7 to day 5, and moves the\nIP Protection onboarding prompt trigger from the standalone bindings\nin BrowserFragment/HomeFragment into ContinuousOnboardingFeature's new\nday 7 stage.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318744\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/browser/BrowserFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/HomeFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/onboarding/continuous/ContinuousOnboardingFeature.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/onboarding/continuous/ContinuousOnboardingStage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/onboarding/continuous/ContinuousOnboardingStageProvider.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/utils/Settings.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values/preference_keys.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/onboarding/continuous/ContinuousOnboardingFeatureTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/onboarding/continuous/ContinuousOnboardingStageProviderTest.kt"], "git_node": "0ff46701934e985add9824dcec385e6a08e5cb59", "git_parents": ["d6966d4a93e6292d42ba26e4faddf1110c17e22a"], "node": "6427cde974caffe47f0c38c0cfce71631f43cbcb", "parents": ["91b6b986e26c5b2c12d27f143218b0a394690055"], "tags": []}, {"author": "giorga \u003cgiorga@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058574 - [TabGroups] Remove TabGroups from android-components r=android-reviewers,007\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316016\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/session-storage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/browser/session/storage/AutoSave.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/session-storage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/browser/session/storage/RecoverableBrowserState.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/session-storage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/browser/session/storage/serialize/BrowserStateReader.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/session-storage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/browser/session/storage/serialize/BrowserStateWriter.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/session-storage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/browser/session/storage/serialize/Keys.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/session-storage/src/test/java/mozilla/components/browser/session/storage/AutoSaveTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/session-storage/src/test/java/mozilla/components/browser/session/storage/SessionStorageTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/session-storage/src/test/java/mozilla/components/browser/session/storage/serialize/BrowserStateWriterReaderTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/state/src/main/java/mozilla/components/browser/state/action/BrowserAction.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/state/src/main/java/mozilla/components/browser/state/reducer/BrowserStateReducer.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/state/src/main/java/mozilla/components/browser/state/reducer/TabGroupReducer.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/state/src/main/java/mozilla/components/browser/state/reducer/TabListReducer.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/state/src/main/java/mozilla/components/browser/state/state/BrowserState.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/state/src/main/java/mozilla/components/browser/state/state/TabPartition.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/state/src/main/java/mozilla/components/browser/state/state/UndoHistoryState.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/state/src/test/java/mozilla/components/browser/state/action/TabGroupActionTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/state/src/test/java/mozilla/components/browser/state/action/TabListActionTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/state/src/test/java/mozilla/components/browser/state/state/TabPartitionTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/state/src/test/java/mozilla/components/browser/state/store/BrowserStoreExceptionTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/tabstray/src/main/java/mozilla/components/browser/tabstray/TabsAdapter.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/tabstray/src/main/java/mozilla/components/browser/tabstray/TabsTray.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/tabstray/src/test/java/mozilla/components/browser/tabstray/TabsAdapterTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/session/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/session/middleware/undo/UndoMiddleware.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/tabs/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/tabs/TabPartitionKeys.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/tabs/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/tabs/TabsUseCases.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/tabs/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/tabs/ext/BrowserState.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/tabs/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/tabs/tabstray/TabsFeature.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/tabs/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/tabs/tabstray/TabsTrayPresenter.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/tabs/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/tabs/TabsUseCasesTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/tabs/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/tabs/tabstray/TabsFeatureTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/tabs/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/tabs/tabstray/TabsTrayPresenterTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/docs/changelog.md", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/usecases/FenixBrowserUseCases.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/usecases/FenixBrowserUseCasesTest.kt"], "git_node": "6c52d03fb63836fcde7b42b3671854ed09020e8d", "git_parents": ["0ff46701934e985add9824dcec385e6a08e5cb59"], "node": "2ec8a4061db76d9a91f23d363617139fa4e2240b", "parents": ["6427cde974caffe47f0c38c0cfce71631f43cbcb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Mehic \u003cdmehic@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1853263 - Fix pre-existing clang-tidy warnings in ServiceWorkerManager.cpp r=dom-worker-reviewers,asuth\n\nsource-test-clang-tidy analyses every file a push touches, so removing the\nprivacy.partition.serviceWorkers pref in this bug makes it report two\nperformance-unnecessary-copy-initialization errors that predate the change:\n\n  ServiceWorkerManager.cpp:933   policyContainerArgs\n  ServiceWorkerManager.cpp:1873  content\n\nBoth are copy-initialised from accessors that already return a const reference -\nClientInfo::GetPolicyContainerArgs() returns const Maybe\u003cPolicyContainerArgs\u003e&\nand PrincipalInfo::get_ContentPrincipalInfo() returns const ContentPrincipalInfo&\n- and both locals are only read. The owning objects are const& parameters of the\nenclosing functions, so they outlive the locals and binding a const reference is\nsafe rather than lifetime-extending a temporary.\n\nNo behaviour change; this only keeps the lint job green for the pref removal.\n\nTry (targeted: source-test-clang-tidy + linux64 debug/opt builds):\nhttps://treeherder.mozilla.org/jobs?repo=try&landoInstance=lando-prod-2025&landoCommitID=79255\n\n22/22 green, including source-test-clang-tidy, which is the job this patch\nexists to fix. Note the push used c52eaa9c6798 as its base rather than current\ncentral; the two lines changed here are the only change to the file, so the lint\nresult is unaffected by that, but the run does not speak for the rest of the\ntree.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318742\n", "files": ["dom/serviceworkers/ServiceWorkerManager.cpp"], "git_node": "722fc27bd5d4e5f0dd0390fb9dbd3e530421f321", "git_parents": ["6c52d03fb63836fcde7b42b3671854ed09020e8d"], "node": "8feb1a129eb749785ee62acc1a31e1842f112789", "parents": ["2ec8a4061db76d9a91f23d363617139fa4e2240b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Mehic \u003cdmehic@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1853263 - Remove the privacy.partition.serviceWorkers pref r=timhuang,dom-worker-reviewers,asuth\n\nThe pref gated partitioning of service workers under dFPI. It has defaulted to\ntrue since bug 1784900 landed in August 2022, and nothing in the tree writes it:\nno Nimbus feature, no enterprise policy, no profile or harness default. The only\nwriters were two test files.\n\nAll thirteen reads were therefore constant, and each reduces mechanically: five\nternaries selecting between eForeignPartitionedPrincipal and eRegularPrincipal\ncollapse to the former, four \"&& pref\" conjuncts drop out, three \"if (!pref)\nreturn ...\" early exits go away, and one \"if (pref) { ... }\" wrapper in\nDispatchFetchEvent unwraps.\n\nThe pref was also redundant. Everywhere it gated a decision it sat beside a\ncheck that already required dFPI - either StoragePartitioningEnabled, which\nitself tests for BEHAVIOR_PARTITION_FOREIGN, or an explicit cookieBehavior\ncomparison in ShouldUsePartitionPrincipalForServiceWorker. Its only reachable\neffect was to leave service workers unpartitioned while the user had asked for\npartitioned cookies, which is precisely the state it should not have been able\nto produce. Anyone wanting unpartitioned service workers still has\nnetwork.cookie.cookieBehavior and the per-site exception list.\n\nFive files lose their last privacy_ pref use, so the now-unused\nStaticPrefs_privacy.h include goes with them. nsDocShell.cpp keeps its include\nfor privacy_window_name_update_enabled.\n\nThree of the thirteen cases in browser_partitionedServiceWorkers.js drove the\nremoved branch. Each was run against the patched build before being deleted:\n\"disable partitioning\" and \"Private Browsing with partitioning disabled with SW\nPBM enabled\" both fail, since each asserts a third-party service worker is gated\non storage access, which is no longer true. \"Private Browsing with partitioning\ndisabled with SW PBM disabled\" still passes - it duplicates the surviving\nSW-PBM-disabled case, being gated by dom.serviceWorkers.privateBrowsing.enabled\nrather than by this pref - so it is dropped as redundant rather than obsolete.\nThe remaining ten cases keep the full private-browsing matrix and lose only the\npref line; three whose names described the pref are renamed.\n\nTry (mach try auto):\nhttps://treeherder.mozilla.org/jobs?repo=try&landoInstance=lando-prod-2025&landoCommitID=79172\n\nNo failures in dom/serviceworkers, dom/clients, toolkit/components/antitracking,\nor web-platform-tests service-workers. The failing jobs are in unrelated\nsubsystems (fullscreen, layout, devtools, extensions, WebTransport, HTTP/3,\ncustomizable-select) and one android build hit an sccache startup timeout.\nsource-test-clang-tidy is red on two pre-existing\nperformance-unnecessary-copy-initialization errors at ServiceWorkerManager.cpp\nlines 933 and 1873; both are byte-identical on main and are reported only\nbecause this patch touches that file. The macosx1500-aarch64 test jobs did not\nget workers and never ran.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318730\n", "files": ["docshell/base/nsDocShell.cpp", "dom/base/nsGlobalWindowInner.cpp", "dom/clients/manager/ClientChannelHelper.cpp", "dom/security/test/csp/test_service_worker.html", "dom/serviceworkers/ServiceWorkerInterceptController.cpp", "dom/serviceworkers/ServiceWorkerManager.cpp", "dom/serviceworkers/ServiceWorkerUtils.cpp", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "toolkit/components/antitracking/StoragePrincipalHelper.cpp", "toolkit/components/antitracking/test/browser/browser_partitionedServiceWorkers.js"], "git_node": "8097706c0e0ce25b727efd44ed5fa9bb9085eeab", "git_parents": ["722fc27bd5d4e5f0dd0390fb9dbd3e530421f321"], "node": "56608a32f9e9c9440dfb939e907ec81dd55f1fff", "parents": ["8feb1a129eb749785ee62acc1a31e1842f112789"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2051282 - Add back peer connection H264 telemetry on PCImpl Init. r=dbaker\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D309693\n", "files": ["dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/PeerConnectionImpl.cpp"], "git_node": "fc93c6fac825520f9d9e9172404f7098dbc676be", "git_parents": ["8097706c0e0ce25b727efd44ed5fa9bb9085eeab"], "node": "97616c50f1837adad3bfcce2af319574b3561c89", "parents": ["56608a32f9e9c9440dfb939e907ec81dd55f1fff"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Timothy Nikkel \u003ctnikkel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063872. Drop pipewire's obsolete conf.h include workaround. r=webrtc-reviewers,grulja,pehrsons\n\n00-pipewire-dont-include-conf-header.patch removes the `#include \u003cpipewire/conf.h\u003e`\nline from pipewire/pipewire.h, but the update to 1.6.8 in bug 2054620 has that line in\nthe tree, so vendoring pipewire no longer reproduces what is committed. That one line is\nthe only difference.\n\nThe patch came from bug 1953080, where PipeWire 1.4 included math.h inside an extern \"C\"\nblock in spa/utils/json-core.h, which conf.h pulls in. Including that from C++ broke the\nbuild, since mozalloc's throw_gcc.h then sees no _LIBCPP_VERSION. Upstream 1.6.8 includes\nmath.h before opening the extern \"C\" block, so the workaround is no longer needed, which\nis why the include could come back without breaking anything.\n\nDrop the patch rather than removing the include again. The header in the tree already has\nthe include and is unchanged by this, so no compiled output moves; only vendoring stops\ndiverging from it. Nothing checked that vendoring reproduced the tree until now, so there\nwas nothing to notice when the include returned.\n\nWith this, `./mach vendor third_party/pipewire/moz.yaml -r 1.6.8 --patch-mode check\n--force` reproduces the committed tree exactly.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318918\n", "files": ["third_party/pipewire/00-pipewire-dont-include-conf-header.patch", "third_party/pipewire/moz.yaml"], "git_node": "b1367a601021f7e8ebbe41b873437da3d50dd5c1", "git_parents": ["fc93c6fac825520f9d9e9172404f7098dbc676be"], "node": "45a2a02d927658999fc97f81588885aedc24869e", "parents": ["97616c50f1837adad3bfcce2af319574b3561c89"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sajid Anwar \u003csajidanwar94@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063909 - Fix text-box-trim last line detection for lines with pending overflow frames. r=layout-reviewers,emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318955\n", "files": ["layout/generic/nsBlockFrame.cpp", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-inline/text-box-trim/text-box-trim-first-line-pseudo-004-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-inline/text-box-trim/text-box-trim-first-line-pseudo-004.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-inline/text-box-trim/text-box-trim-first-line-pseudo-005-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-inline/text-box-trim/text-box-trim-first-line-pseudo-005.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-inline/text-box-trim/text-box-trim-fragmented-last-inline-box-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-inline/text-box-trim/text-box-trim-fragmented-last-inline-box-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-inline/text-box-trim/text-box-trim-fragmented-last-inline-box-002-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-inline/text-box-trim/text-box-trim-fragmented-last-inline-box-002.html"], "git_node": "910768ab0d8c2fe6ec70ef9b69b573235d61afc8", "git_parents": ["b1367a601021f7e8ebbe41b873437da3d50dd5c1"], "node": "6d85bef9801c986412443ea2fbb3d10aa0915eaf", "parents": ["45a2a02d927658999fc97f81588885aedc24869e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Erik Nordin \u003cenordin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063912 - Fix about:translations clear button alignment r=desktop-theme-reviewers,emilio\n\nThis commit fixes the CSS around the `about:translations`\nclear-source-text button so that the `X` within the clear\nbutton correctly aligns with the chevron of the menulists.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318951\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/translations/content/about-translations.css"], "git_node": "cb0c81eee6fdf131625106011365b0261de1c8da", "git_parents": ["910768ab0d8c2fe6ec70ef9b69b573235d61afc8"], "node": "d41715b0f68f11395d185346040f28968b7edaf5", "parents": ["6d85bef9801c986412443ea2fbb3d10aa0915eaf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dave Townsend \u003cdtownsend@oxymoronical.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2045811: Add a site policy to disable service workers. r=mkaply,dom-worker-reviewers,necko-reviewers,jesup,edenchuang\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316778\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/test/performance/browser_startup_content.js", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/Policies.sys.mjs", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/schemas/policies-schema.json", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/browser/browser_policy_sitepolicies_serviceworkers.js", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/browser/sitepolicies_sw_fetch.html", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/browser/sitepolicies_sw_framed.html", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/browser/sw_fetch_intercept.js", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/xpcshell/test_sitepolicies.js", "docshell/base/BrowsingContext.h", "docshell/base/nsDocShellLoadState.cpp", "dom/chrome-webidl/BrowsingContext.webidl", "dom/serviceworkers/ServiceWorkerUtils.cpp", "dom/serviceworkers/ServiceWorkerUtils.h", "netwerk/ipc/DocumentLoadListener.cpp", "toolkit/components/enterprisepolicies/EnterprisePoliciesContent.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/EnterprisePolicyTesting.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "8286795994275ff66da4428935d7dc2493cae840", "git_parents": ["cb0c81eee6fdf131625106011365b0261de1c8da"], "node": "9e0972a9d3fd21c38b866e7d0d2df2770dc589cb", "parents": ["d41715b0f68f11395d185346040f28968b7edaf5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054044 - Vendor static-dumps for doh-config and doh-providers r=necko-reviewers,jesup\n\nPreviously the doh providers would only be used after the first\nremote settings update.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316769\n", "files": ["services/settings/static-dumps/main/doh-config.json", "services/settings/static-dumps/main/doh-providers.json", "testing/profiles/common/user.js", "toolkit/components/doh/test/browser/head.js"], "git_node": "05ca50796bd95f44c486986a62dd81db7cca898c", "git_parents": ["8286795994275ff66da4428935d7dc2493cae840"], "node": "e37d375b7f398aa1022cec83b2a3ccb20788b731", "parents": ["9e0972a9d3fd21c38b866e7d0d2df2770dc589cb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2043211 - Rename members and args in jsep_track_unittest to match Mozilla style. r=webrtc-reviewers,bwc\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D304689\n", "files": ["media/webrtc/signaling/gtest/jsep_track_unittest.cpp"], "git_node": "a9bbd18b04ffe70b75d043cc8ffa2e4d1f07d960", "git_parents": ["05ca50796bd95f44c486986a62dd81db7cca898c"], "node": "ff76fd56a535d148f46682ad092f319cf6e2cef9", "parents": ["e37d375b7f398aa1022cec83b2a3ccb20788b731"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2043211 - In jsep, move codecs to nsTArray. r=we