9ad093a1e2b7"], "node": "0f7e3766b5e3c80757adfea7e61431019cd8c569", "parents": ["2f5598ff6f6c7732c807ee9857ef3b1f0f4529f5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew McCreight \u003ccontinuation@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061893 - Inline MOZ_STORAGE_CONTRACTID_PREFIX. r=asuth\n\nXPCOM contract IDs are magic strings and the only way to find them is to search\nthe codebase for the string. Breaking up the string like this makes them harder\nto find. I've been auditing these across the code base and this is the only\nplace that breaks out the component part of it, and it is not used outside of\nthis file. This appears to date to 2004 so hopefully nobody is too attached\nto this.\n\nThere are a few macros like NS_NETWORK_PROTOCOL_CONTRACTID_PREFIX used to\nconstruct different protocols, but for those at least they are the same except\nfor the very end of it, and they are used in more than one file, so they feel\nmore useful.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317203\n", "files": ["storage/build/mozStorageCID.h"], "git_node": "9b799259180234ffc1d3a36def324f0374b498af", "git_parents": ["db406cab0b43e37d546ce21429e16d1b3dd7d3a3"], "node": "401f9b6cb6eaf5c8f6589d2febc9e32eb0a41112", "parents": ["0f7e3766b5e3c80757adfea7e61431019cd8c569"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sam Foster \u003csfoster@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2051576 - Leave expand-on-hover sidebar in flow to fix launcher splitter. r=desktop-theme-reviewers,jsudiaman,emilio\n\n- Add test for launcher splitter with expand-on-hover\n- Remove position:absolute for expand-on-hover #sidebarContainer\n- Fix stale launcher width measurement which can result in a jump when expand animation starts\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318562\n", "files": ["browser/components/sidebar/browser-sidebar.js", "browser/components/sidebar/tests/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/sidebar/tests/browser/browser_launcher_splitter_expand_on_hover.js", "browser/themes/shared/sidebar.css"], "git_node": "6a5df8d9af714d020d4269608e8169ffbadb3c67", "git_parents": ["9b799259180234ffc1d3a36def324f0374b498af"], "node": "8ffad0a7562000d31aae7a2d20b19c68701ea1ec", "parents": ["401f9b6cb6eaf5c8f6589d2febc9e32eb0a41112"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049770 - Reach the tabbrowser's window and document through its own handles. r=tabbrowser-reviewers,jsudiaman\n\n`ownerDocument` stays as an alias, since consumers outside the module -- the\nnewtab train among them -- are updated under a separate bug.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318767\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tabbrowser.js"], "git_node": "b46a4c69ef8ed2339b17934bda481373aa9dfb58", "git_parents": ["6a5df8d9af714d020d4269608e8169ffbadb3c67"], "node": "d2d44d2ec558c581942780e39ef0f04fb4f1f9ab", "parents": ["8ffad0a7562000d31aae7a2d20b19c68701ea1ec"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049770 - Reach per-window objects through the tabbrowser's window. r=tabbrowser-reviewers,jsudiaman\n\n`getTabDialogBox` stays free of `this`: ContentDispatchChooser captures it off\n`gBrowser` and calls it receiverless, which a class method can't survive. And\n`TabDialogBox` is a class declaration, hence a lexical binding, so browser.js has\nto hand it to the window before anything outside its own scripts can reach it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318769\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tabbrowser.js"], "git_node": "fe8c68a7221b68bcc8dcdb3bceb68e0f55730513", "git_parents": ["b46a4c69ef8ed2339b17934bda481373aa9dfb58"], "node": "d5f6fc32b43d0d6f0dc43c002bf97637c980b1ba", "parents": ["d2d44d2ec558c581942780e39ef0f04fb4f1f9ab"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Matthew Gaudet \u003cmgaudet@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063645 - Add label for blink image loader r=mstange,perftest-reviewers,kshampur DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318836\n", "files": ["testing/raptor/raptor/browser_function_labels.toml"], "git_node": "b125ad09057dd6372e8a0d364a1cc085b1e825b0", "git_parents": ["fe8c68a7221b68bcc8dcdb3bceb68e0f55730513"], "node": "d4c89e71437822755993b70a2e3b813e0a912e92", "parents": ["d5f6fc32b43d0d6f0dc43c002bf97637c980b1ba"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Kaply \u003cmozilla@kaply.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1470570 - Resolve installer /INI= paths relative to the installer EXE. r=cdupuis,browser-installer-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D300593\n", "files": ["browser/installer/windows/nsis/installer.nsi"], "git_node": "067860c6ee4cc53a741ac6126d0a1b93b0380287", "git_parents": ["b125ad09057dd6372e8a0d364a1cc085b1e825b0"], "node": "4b5a69f4371d3303f283dcac2ec16a871a42a789", "parents": ["d4c89e71437822755993b70a2e3b813e0a912e92"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Naz\u0131m Can Alt\u0131nova \u003ccanaltinova@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063992 - Pass Chrome's symbol server to samply in ETW profiles r=kshampur,perftest-reviewers\n\nChrome ships without PDBs, so samply had nothing to symbolicate\nchrome.dll with and every native frame showed up as fun_\u003caddress\u003e.\n\nNote that this didn't affect CaR profiles since we handled their symbol\ndir here properly. It was only for Chrome profiles.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319039\n", "files": ["testing/raptor/raptor/etw_profile.py"], "git_node": "b497b695a4a00b73a653da9b0c95387c4a846bde", "git_parents": ["067860c6ee4cc53a741ac6126d0a1b93b0380287"], "node": "7ddba31291de17d881da7f0ca63cfe17c254eb8c", "parents": ["4b5a69f4371d3303f283dcac2ec16a871a42a789"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Naz\u0131m Can Alt\u0131nova \u003ccanaltinova@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063992 - Pass Windows symbol server to samply for ETW profiles r=kshampur,perftest-reviewers,mstange\n\nsymbols.mozilla.org only has user-mode system libraries, so ntoskrnl and\nthe drivers were coming out as fun_\u003caddress\u003e.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319040\n", "files": ["testing/raptor/raptor/etw_profile.py"], "git_node": "810651da0292e07367d37386bbcf4a1cb50cab43", "git_parents": ["b497b695a4a00b73a653da9b0c95387c4a846bde"], "node": "f2663b23d0b827ed8e938524d96bc73d065c0ca6", "parents": ["7ddba31291de17d881da7f0ca63cfe17c254eb8c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Maryam \u003cmomar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1999534 - Move MOZ_DIAGNOSTIC_ASSERT above early return in UpdateAntiTrackingInfoForChannel. r=emz\n\nMoving the assert above the early return allows it to\nactually fire when the function is called on the wrong process.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319063\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/antitracking/AntiTrackingUtils.cpp"], "git_node": "df4ab95e717a0fd0363e08a43a4b847f3983c707", "git_parents": ["810651da0292e07367d37386bbcf4a1cb50cab43"], "node": "140b34e4ee99db741548b22e23d6c70c6e831fd2", "parents": ["f2663b23d0b827ed8e938524d96bc73d065c0ca6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Eitan Isaacson \u003ceitan@monotonous.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1894410 - Remove whitespace from role string tokens before localizing. r=Jamie,geckoview-reviewers,m_kato\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318279\n", "files": ["accessible/android/Platform.cpp", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/test/AccessibilityTest.kt"], "git_node": "767bc9520c96c4cbca50fb71ddefcf4451c9457e", "git_parents": ["df4ab95e717a0fd0363e08a43a4b847f3983c707"], "node": "0eb38e65a90832db0b00224920f602c09f8706aa", "parents": ["140b34e4ee99db741548b22e23d6c70c6e831fd2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Segun Famisa \u003csfamisa@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2041554 - Use sync invocation count to infer if sync is active r=markh,jonalmeida,android-reviewers,ansinha\n\nThe bug happens because when we return a \"retry\" work manager result, the worker state changes into enqued state without ever first reaching any terminal state. As a result, we do not update the \"isSyncActive\" state, leaving the UI and observers in a different state from the actual state of the work.\nThe work remains \"enqueued\" but the last known state for isSyncActive is true.\n\nThe solution for this bug is using a \"counter\" to infer whether or not a sync is\nin progress because the work manager state on Android is not enough to tell us whether or not sync is actually in progress.\nFor example, the calls to rust's sync manager are not cancellable, and as a result, continue to run even if the work manager work has been cancelled.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316344\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/service/firefox-accounts/build.gradle", "mobile/android/android-components/components/service/firefox-accounts/src/main/java/mozilla/components/service/fxa/manager/FxaAccountManager.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/service/firefox-accounts/src/main/java/mozilla/components/service/fxa/manager/GlobalAccountManager.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/service/firefox-accounts/src/main/java/mozilla/components/service/fxa/sync/RustSyncManager.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/service/firefox-accounts/src/main/java/mozilla/components/service/fxa/sync/SyncManager.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/service/firefox-accounts/src/main/java/mozilla/components/service/fxa/sync/SyncOperationTracker.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/service/firefox-accounts/src/main/java/mozilla/components/service/fxa/sync/WorkManagerSyncManager.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/service/firefox-accounts/src/test/java/mozilla/components/service/fxa/TestOAuthAccount.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/service/firefox-accounts/src/test/java/mozilla/components/service/fxa/sync/WorkManagerSyncDispatcherTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/service/firefox-accounts/src/test/java/mozilla/components/service/fxa/sync/WorkManagerSyncManagerTest.kt"], "git_node": "85eb9f01f0e379b110b61365eb65bdf8cac41304", "git_parents": ["767bc9520c96c4cbca50fb71ddefcf4451c9457e"], "node": "37760c121db997bd8179e3f8532e521429a79312", "parents": ["0eb38e65a90832db0b00224920f602c09f8706aa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "stransky \u003cstransky@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063521 [Linux] Use gfxVars::CanUseVulkanHardwareVideoDecoding() to check vulkan status r=jld,sandbox-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318671\n", "files": ["security/sandbox/linux/broker/SandboxBrokerPolicyFactory.cpp"], "git_node": "0d4da57c64dec515a6180efc9385bce09e566361", "git_parents": ["85eb9f01f0e379b110b61365eb65bdf8cac41304"], "node": "20a9321d39c3f8c2fb618afaec366b8bf1dc7f2c", "parents": ["37760c121db997bd8179e3f8532e521429a79312"], "tags": []}, {"author": "andyh \u003candhuang@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1977006 - Added ProfileImpression to asrouter-devtools. r=omc-reviewers,sachung\n\nAdd a Profile Impressions editor to about:asrouter#devtools-impressions for viewing, editing, and saving multiProfileMessageImpressions (the message impressions shared across a profile group for messages with a profileScope). Editing routes through editState, which persists per-message rows to the shared ProfilesDatastore and deletes any entries removed by the edit.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311893\n", "files": ["browser/components/asrouter/content-src/components/ASRouterAdmin/ASRouterAdmin.jsx", "browser/components/asrouter/content-src/components/ASRouterAdmin/ImpressionsSection.jsx", "browser/components/asrouter/content/asrouter-admin.bundle.js", "browser/components/asrouter/docs/debugging-docs.md", "browser/components/asrouter/modules/ASRouter.sys.mjs", "browser/components/asrouter/tests/unit/ASRouter.test.js", "browser/components/asrouter/tests/unit/content-src/components/ASRouterAdmin.test.jsx"], "git_node": "ab188597a59c54126d1162e4d5d2368258bb0ce6", "git_parents": ["0d4da57c64dec515a6180efc9385bce09e566361"], "node": "7d2e21d6ce2a835e781bee6fc7e162203c2227cc", "parents": ["20a9321d39c3f8c2fb618afaec366b8bf1dc7f2c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Brian Smith \u003cbrian@smith.berlin\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2051921 - Add ESR compat info for DefaultBrowserSettingEnabled. r=mkaply DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319157\n", "files": ["browser/components/enterprisepolicies/schemas/policies-schema.json"], "git_node": "73156ef55d9a08d997c4fc15fc7ebb677d94e6bf", "git_parents": ["ab188597a59c54126d1162e4d5d2368258bb0ce6"], "node": "81a82229c31eb3f0483a9801c88084cf143f9317", "parents": ["7d2e21d6ce2a835e781bee6fc7e162203c2227cc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064109 - Make RemoteMediaDataEncoder::Construct honour failures. r=media-playback-reviewers,padenot\n\nWhen we fail to construct a remote encoder, it is supposed to\ngracefully fail and fallback to the next option. This patch fixes\na bug in RemoteMediaDataEncoder::Construct where we ignored the\nMediaResult from the Construct resolver that would allow us to\nfallback as expected.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319154\n", "files": ["dom/media/ipc/RemoteMediaDataEncoder.cpp"], "git_node": "bdfe92df0ad404c9a53b340fd1262edb32403abb", "git_parents": ["73156ef55d9a08d997c4fc15fc7ebb677d94e6bf"], "node": "b2e3378e52d7c6c0093c8c0e640e09455021b198", "parents": ["81a82229c31eb3f0483a9801c88084cf143f9317"], "tags": []}, {"author": "rperta \u003crperta@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 1999534 - Move MOZ_DIAGNOSTIC_ASSERT above early return in UpdateAntiTrackingInfoForChannel. r=emz\" for causing multiple failures at AntiTrackingUtils.cpp\n\nThis reverts commit df4ab95e717a0fd0363e08a43a4b847f3983c707.\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/antitracking/AntiTrackingUtils.cpp"], "git_node": "6aa03466ccb37c65d46b707d8b5c7d96220b8620", "git_parents": ["bdfe92df0ad404c9a53b340fd1262edb32403abb"], "node": "1eb1627e378381ad890d7b8b1debd401fd12bb4d", "parents": ["b2e3378e52d7c6c0093c8c0e640e09455021b198"], "tags": []}, {"author": "serge-sans-paille \u003csguelton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062968 - Move vendoring of Decimal.{h,cpp} to `mach vendor` r=emilio,vhilla\n\nMove all patches to patches/ directory. Add two patches there that were\npart of Bug 868874 and 1893532 but not registered (which means that the\nupdate script would have lost them).\n\nRemove now obsolete UPSTREAM-GIT-SHA and update.sh.\n\nDecimal.{h,cpp} are untouched, which is normal for such a move.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318106\n", "files": ["mozglue/misc/decimal/LICENSE", "mozglue/misc/decimal/UPSTREAM-GIT-SHA", "mozglue/misc/decimal/add-doubleconversion-impl.patch", "mozglue/misc/decimal/comparison-with-nan.patch", "mozglue/misc/decimal/fix-wshadow-warnings.patch", "mozglue/misc/decimal/mfbt-abi-markers.patch", "mozglue/misc/decimal/moz-constexpr-decimal.patch", "mozglue/misc/decimal/moz.yaml", "mozglue/misc/decimal/patches/add-doubleconversion-impl.patch", "mozglue/misc/decimal/patches/comparison-with-nan.patch", "mozglue/misc/decimal/patches/fix-wshadow-warnings.patch", "mozglue/misc/decimal/patches/mfbt-abi-markers.patch", "mozglue/misc/decimal/patches/moz-constexpr-decimal.patch", "mozglue/misc/decimal/patches/moz-constexpr-nan.patch", "mozglue/misc/decimal/patches/to-moz-dependencies.patch", "mozglue/misc/decimal/patches/zero-serialization.patch", "mozglue/misc/decimal/to-moz-dependencies.patch", "mozglue/misc/decimal/update.sh", "mozglue/misc/decimal/zero-serialization.patch"], "git_node": "5e04fc4144f61155137a9f792ca34ff69c9dd3fe", "git_parents": ["6aa03466ccb37c65d46b707d8b5c7d96220b8620"], "node": "92a8a77f8a25765bc1759423f1484c60408f9f49", "parents": ["1eb1627e378381ad890d7b8b1debd401fd12bb4d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063981 - Don't try MoveGroup tail duplication for LGoto if we can fall through to the target block. r=jseward\n\nIf we can fall through to the target, that's always more efficient than cloning\nmove groups.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319065\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/CodeGenerator.cpp"], "git_node": "14d518a53cd2303e1c985f0ef33852cb8e0f450d", "git_parents": ["5e04fc4144f61155137a9f792ca34ff69c9dd3fe"], "node": "00900cd2f50a1ef55264f25b6aef6c5e6af64608", "parents": ["92a8a77f8a25765bc1759423f1484c60408f9f49"], "tags": []}, {"author": "serge-sans-paille \u003csguelton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063976 - Fix performance-unnecessary-copy-initialization warning in dom r=media-playback-reviewers,padenot\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319013\n", "files": ["dom/filesystem/GetDirectoryListingTask.cpp", "dom/filesystem/GetFileOrDirectoryTask.cpp", "dom/filesystem/GetFilesTask.cpp", "dom/gamepad/GamepadManager.cpp", "dom/ipc/BrowserChild.cpp", "dom/ipc/BrowserParent.cpp", "dom/media/ExternalEngineStateMachine.cpp", "dom/media/MediaStreamTrack.cpp", "dom/media/gmp/GMPServiceParent.cpp", "dom/media/mediasource/ContainerParser.cpp", "dom/media/webspeech/synth/nsSynthVoiceRegistry.cpp", "dom/serviceworkers/ServiceWorkerPrivate.cpp", "dom/urlpattern/URLPattern.cpp", "dom/workers/remoteworkers/RemoteWorkerManager.cpp"], "git_node": "37b1e5467618851b7d95f54611c66402b48a28c7", "git_parents": ["14d518a53cd2303e1c985f0ef33852cb8e0f450d"], "node": "608e455055b6e72425ce3932f93b1366630d8084", "parents": ["00900cd2f50a1ef55264f25b6aef6c5e6af64608"], "tags": []}, {"author": "serge-sans-paille \u003csguelton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063976 - Fix performance-unnecessary-copy-initialization warning in gfx r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319014\n", "files": ["gfx/gl/Colorspaces.h", "gfx/layers/apz/src/SmoothScrollAnimation.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxPlatform.cpp"], "git_node": "18fb1c389abe3634da870236be23b0188d6fdff8", "git_parents": ["37b1e5467618851b7d95f54611c66402b48a28c7"], "node": "5bb3cf611c4776aae484ddb2f58df03df113e8d0", "parents": ["608e455055b6e72425ce3932f93b1366630d8084"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1925105 - Use interpreter-entry trampoline for JSOp::Resume in the C++ interpreter. r=spidermonkey-reviewers,mgaudet\n\nAfter the generator-resume rewrite in bug 2058411, we now support interpreter-entry\ntrampolines (for profiling Nightly builds).\n\nThe only place still missing support for this was the `JSOp::Resume` code in the\nC++ interpreter. This patch adds code for that similar to what we do for\n`JSOp::Call` etc.\n\nThis code is covered by the `resume-interpreter-entry-trampoline.js` jit-test.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319024\n", "files": ["js/src/vm/Interpreter.cpp"], "git_node": "2fcc4cf798cb1bf4160fb9b69800fac8e4fba7b8", "git_parents": ["18fb1c389abe3634da870236be23b0188d6fdff8"], "node": "6d9fd038678cc9ad4dc461b8797ff5b8aa1634cb", "parents": ["5bb3cf611c4776aae484ddb2f58df03df113e8d0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Kaply \u003cmozilla@kaply.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2041238 - Lock extensions.getAddons.showPane when InstallAddonsPermission blocks installs. r=jneuberger\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318248\n", "files": ["browser/components/enterprisepolicies/Policies.sys.mjs", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/xpcshell/test_simple_pref_policies.js"], "git_node": "d69461e41ec3f70f4b871584662b2108aa5b76d9", "git_parents": ["2fcc4cf798cb1bf4160fb9b69800fac8e4fba7b8"], "node": "d7a8a599b0872aa4a7ab39b80df0430b24f2756e", "parents": ["6d9fd038678cc9ad4dc461b8797ff5b8aa1634cb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Janika \u003cjneuberger@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061452 - Disable cookie permission controls in Page Info when set by policy r=emz,mkaply\n\nWhen initializing the Cookies row on the Page Info, disable the checkbox and\ncmd_cookieToggle command when scope == SitePermissions.SCOPE_POLICY, in addition to\nthe existing prefIsLocked(\"network.cookie.cookieBehavior\") check. This locks cookie\npermissions set by the Cookies policy (EXPIRE_POLICY), matching the other permissions\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316902\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/pageinfo/permissions.js", "browser/base/content/test/pageinfo/browser_pageinfo_permissions.js", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/browser/browser_policy_pageinfo_permissions.js"], "git_node": "c42c850a0fb35b2a1f2d67ffd9274b4157cc376e", "git_parents": ["d69461e41ec3f70f4b871584662b2108aa5b76d9"], "node": "0041d2791c20119d008da4561d857f23f2ff6f6e", "parents": ["d7a8a599b0872aa4a7ab39b80df0430b24f2756e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dre Grant \u003cdgrant@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2022264 - Remove the IAB leaderboard devtools toggle. r=ini\n\nLeaderboard is no longer a supported ad size (Bug 2030401), so drop its\ntoggle from the Discovery Stream devtools panel, along with the pref\nconstant, the placement branches and the contextual banner branch that\nfed it.\n\nToggling an ad size now refreshes the cache, so the placement change\ntakes effect without a manual \"Refresh Cache\" click.\n\nThe Karma test file for this component was migrated to Jest while this\nsat in review, so the coverage moved to test/jest as RTL tests.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D287248\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/DiscoveryStreamAdmin/DiscoveryStreamAdmin.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/DiscoveryStreamAdmin.test.jsx"], "git_node": "e090cde01a032714f72085d9b9fec8a38c81e9af", "git_parents": ["c42c850a0fb35b2a1f2d67ffd9274b4157cc376e"], "node": "6e0b3a37f14fbcfac3913d8447d2302af762c668", "parents": ["0041d2791c20119d008da4561d857f23f2ff6f6e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062141 - Don't start a link preview long press for a mousedown with no button held, r=omarg.\n\nA mousedown synthesized to activate an element reports no held button and is\nnot followed by a mouseup, so the long press timer it armed was only ever\ncancelled by the next unrelated mouse event.\n\nThe existing long press subtest armed the timer with a buttons: 0 mousedown,\nencoding the behaviour being removed here, so it now passes the buttons value\na real press would have.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317402\n", "files": ["browser/components/genai/LinkPreview.sys.mjs", "browser/components/genai/tests/browser/browser_link_preview.js"], "git_node": "72c81341fdb6a650a007a8a8e1109a52627bd058", "git_parents": ["e090cde01a032714f72085d9b9fec8a38c81e9af"], "node": "e867c11b0becc4fae316f7d467aa9b04ecf2fe4a", "parents": ["6e0b3a37f14fbcfac3913d8447d2302af762c668"], "tags": []}, {"author": "AndiAJ \u003candiaj@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064089 - Swap out obsolete UI tests from the legacy flank config r=aaronmt\n\nAll UI tests running on the legacy task successfully passed 3x on Firebase \u2705\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319138\n", "files": ["mobile/android/test_infra/flank-configs/fenix/arm-legacy-api-tests.yml"], "git_node": "9cfd1c5de1a09ba45c5c6d39307019b0f692764b", "git_parents": ["72c81341fdb6a650a007a8a8e1109a52627bd058"], "node": "19725b6ced59740f2d07019fc92a8be11e5da482", "parents": ["e867c11b0becc4fae316f7d467aa9b04ecf2fe4a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Olivia Hall \u003cohall@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049757 - Remove nimbus_qa_prefs after Firefox Labs QA validation r=geckoview-reviewers,android-reviewers,tcampbell\n\nThese preferences were only present for QA purposes.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310107\n", "files": ["mobile/android/app/geckoview-prefs.js", "mobile/android/fenix/app/nimbus.fml.yaml"], "git_node": "7cb99020f2c17d243f3d15419494d779f18e83f2", "git_parents": ["9cfd1c5de1a09ba45c5c6d39307019b0f692764b"], "node": "6cbbc2724c96c7b09490645c5d8f7746ff33a66a", "parents": ["19725b6ced59740f2d07019fc92a8be11e5da482"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Maile Lucks \u003cmaile.lucks@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2024015 - Add a catch for MLEngine.runWithGenerator completionPromise and reset ChatStore before the chat_storage assertion r=ai-platform-reviewers,jlewis,cdipersio,gregtatum\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316887\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_smartwindow_telemetry.js", "toolkit/components/ml/actors/MLEngineParent.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ml/tests/browser/browser_ml_openai.js"], "git_node": "eab7cdd693e5a9f5fe35a7667731e6212bd638ae", "git_parents": ["7cb99020f2c17d243f3d15419494d779f18e83f2"], "node": "9bb49a11f13e27845bb5849ffa0d4dd88213e0a3", "parents": ["6cbbc2724c96c7b09490645c5d8f7746ff33a66a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chris DuPuis \u003ccdupuis@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058359 - Re-enable \"update service\" setting for auto-disabled installations r=aborondo,application-update-reviewers,mossop\n\nWe currently have a large population of installations where the setting \"app.update.service.enabled\" was automatically set to false due to there being more than 10 update failures. One effect of this, though, is that these installs will no longer use staged updates.\n\nMake a change to re-enable the update service setting for any such installation, and add telemetry to notice if errors are auto-disabling the feature again.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314549\n", "files": ["browser/components/BrowserGlue.sys.mjs", "browser/components/ProfileDataUpgrader.sys.mjs", "toolkit/modules/UpdateUtils.sys.mjs", "toolkit/mozapps/update/UpdateService.sys.mjs", "toolkit/mozapps/update/metrics.yaml", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/unit_aus_update/updateManagerXMLReader.js", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/unit_aus_update/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "c0ec1750c4b8a29e05a313809a176733603e08e7", "git_parents": ["eab7cdd693e5a9f5fe35a7667731e6212bd638ae"], "node": "4a399fb7863a66a6052436c4d5b69becadd0905a", "parents": ["9bb49a11f13e27845bb5849ffa0d4dd88213e0a3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Bryan Johns \u003cbjohns@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063620 - Updated relevant-memories-context to v2 prompts r=cdipersio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318780\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/models/ChatUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/Utils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_relevant_memories.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/ChatConversation.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/head.js"], "git_node": "48c594ac74d07fc8082cd252a350ad42448f6028", "git_parents": ["c0ec1750c4b8a29e05a313809a176733603e08e7"], "node": "ea8e9a684c94c9fa65db1342a0245cbdffbe8b41", "parents": ["4a399fb7863a66a6052436c4d5b69becadd0905a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Aaron Train \u003caaron.train@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063615 - Add tae-arm to Fenix related Try presets r=jajohnson\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318799\n", "files": ["tools/tryselect/try_presets.yml"], "git_node": "3bfaaf08ada74b514edb6bf17c92cb94f189201f", "git_parents": ["48c594ac74d07fc8082cd252a350ad42448f6028"], "node": "8b0083f6c33025ba7da01320ea1703a2f8096c13", "parents": ["ea8e9a684c94c9fa65db1342a0245cbdffbe8b41"], "tags": []}, {"author": "rperta \u003crperta@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2060500 - [devtools] Add some basic telemetry for the stylesheets in the debugger r=devtools-reviewers,jdescottes\" for causing dt failures at browser_dbg-telemetry-stylesheets.js\n\nThis reverts commit 8673a8f5795b9003b76e3ed8d5429ad093a1e2b7.\n", "files": ["devtools/client/debugger/src/actions/sources/select.js", "devtools/client/debugger/src/actions/sources/stylesheets.js", "devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/browser_dbg-telemetry-stylesheets.js", "devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/browser_qz.toml", "devtools/client/framework/toolbox-options.html", "devtools/client/framework/toolbox-options.js", "devtools/client/framework/toolbox.js", "devtools/client/shared/metrics.yaml"], "git_node": "26451d32eada752b5facbcc112527524ed62b906", "git_parents": ["3bfaaf08ada74b514edb6bf17c92cb94f189201f"], "node": "964c2640fe9dad5e2ab32db2ba60212cb264c2e0", "parents": ["8b0083f6c33025ba7da01320ea1703a2f8096c13"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049606 - Avoid VPX hardware encoding on Windows for realtime applications unless hardware is forced. r=media-playback-reviewers,padenot\n\nThe frame to frame latency with the hardware VP9 hardware is\nsignificantly higher than that of the software encoders. This patch\nmakes it so that we prefer to fallback to the software VPX encoders\nfor realtime applications, unless the caller specifically requests\nhardware encoders.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318166\n", "files": ["dom/media/platforms/wmf/WMFDataEncoderUtils.cpp"], "git_node": "13ab6d9c69462c440b0863efd22b9991937ead36", "git_parents": ["26451d32eada752b5facbcc112527524ed62b906"], "node": "e61c0de59a3a95b076363da151b1a4b74061cf3b", "parents": ["964c2640fe9dad5e2ab32db2ba60212cb264c2e0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Updatebot \u003cupdatebot@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063762 - Update dav1d to 52b9d3d3ec525f5a20849145fa0e879d585f4911 r=chunmin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318867\n", "files": ["media/libdav1d/moz.yaml", "media/libdav1d/vcs_version.h", "third_party/dav1d/src/arm/64/util.S"], "git_node": "891a755c80d747d4bcdf155fa7f0002350723284", "git_parents": ["13ab6d9c69462c440b0863efd22b9991937ead36"], "node": "256131fbdd598bc6bdde3a174ad4ce124cabc154", "parents": ["e61c0de59a3a95b076363da151b1a4b74061cf3b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2046609 - Part 1. Add support for exposing encoder information for testing purposes. r=media-playback-reviewers,webidl,smaug,alwu\n\nThis mirrors what we already do for HTMLMediaElement but for\nWebCodecs encoders.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317575\n", "files": ["dom/media/MediaUtils.cpp", "dom/media/MediaUtils.h", "dom/media/mediaelement/HTMLMediaElement.cpp", "dom/media/mediaelement/HTMLMediaElement.h", "dom/media/moz.build", "dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVideoEncoder.cpp", "dom/media/webcodecs/AudioEncoder.cpp", "dom/media/webcodecs/EncoderAgent.cpp", "dom/media/webcodecs/EncoderAgent.h", "dom/media/webcodecs/EncoderTemplate.cpp", "dom/media/webcodecs/EncoderTemplate.h", "dom/media/webcodecs/VideoEncoder.cpp", "dom/webidl/AudioEncoder.webidl", "dom/webidl/HTMLMediaElement.webidl", "dom/webidl/MediaDebugInfo.webidl", "dom/webidl/VideoEncoder.webidl"], "git_node": "00265aa8d42ac70159e9934db11f4a2ec06b103f", "git_parents": ["891a755c80d747d4bcdf155fa7f0002350723284"], "node": "aff0614c640ba515b30787ef7fa9f5e681439aa8", "parents": ["256131fbdd598bc6bdde3a174ad4ce124cabc154"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2046609 - Part 2. Fix static string leak in MFTEncoder. r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nThis is an existing leakcheck failure tripped by the new tests.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317628\n", "files": ["dom/media/platforms/wmf/MFTEncoder.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/wmf/MFTEncoder.h"], "git_node": "daca384344f7da00ef7109c76df2df4c93718f53", "git_parents": ["00265aa8d42ac70159e9934db11f4a2ec06b103f"], "node": "f6c64cd74608f09f96ab6c02d27ceb94a91ad5b5", "parents": ["aff0614c640ba515b30787ef7fa9f5e681439aa8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2046609 - Part 3. Implement encoding test to verify what process encoding runs in. r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317629\n", "files": ["dom/media/webcodecs/test/encoding_process.js", "dom/media/webcodecs/test/mochitest.toml", "dom/media/webcodecs/test/test_encoding_process.html", "dom/media/webcodecs/test/test_encoding_process_gpu.html"], "git_node": "0ee870cec9499abb725a6a2dd6cad4a4c124b6ad", "git_parents": ["daca384344f7da00ef7109c76df2df4c93718f53"], "node": "f570ee93395e10c4a87b690ca76f9cc76f343d16", "parents": ["f6c64cd74608f09f96ab6c02d27ceb94a91ad5b5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Vanessa Prema \u003cvprema@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063372 - feat(trustpanel): Add telemetry for breach alert shield animation r=vinilla\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318527\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser-trustPanel.js", "browser/components/controlcenter/metrics.yaml"], "git_node": "450055e7d9ae39acfe78706971b8aaa14d82ce5b", "git_parents": ["0ee870cec9499abb725a6a2dd6cad4a4c124b6ad"], "node": "9f177746d00fae3a7cf8ddd4882ad443a9638fed", "parents": ["f570ee93395e10c4a87b690ca76f9cc76f343d16"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Irene Ni \u003cini@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056255 - Remove root level \u003chr\u003e styles from weather forecast widget. r=maxx\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319176\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/WeatherForecast/WeatherForecast.scss"], "git_node": "baaa8caff48e553e76e07de45fedd164576a54ea", "git_parents": ["450055e7d9ae39acfe78706971b8aaa14d82ce5b"], "node": "4735b8ae6d4f7052f3f8ad5bffe4cb95f631601e", "parents": ["9f177746d00fae3a7cf8ddd4882ad443a9638fed"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Olivia Hall \u003cohall@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2052287 - Remove Firefox Labs from Secret Settings r=gl,android-reviewers\n\nPatch removes Firefox Labs from Secret Settings.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310139\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/FeatureFlags.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/Components.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/SettingsSearchProviders.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/SecretSettingsFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/SettingsFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/labs/FirefoxLabsSettingsSearchProvider.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/utils/Settings.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values/preference_keys.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values/static_strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/xml/preferences.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/xml/secret_settings_preferences.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/labs/FirefoxLabsSettingsSearchProviderTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/settingssearch/SettingsSearchProviderRegistrationTest.kt"], "git_node": "3bfca537aa8bc7a6cb410face3e645b064bfb92b", "git_parents": ["baaa8caff48e553e76e07de45fedd164576a54ea"], "node": "6343e41900d27583da547717e0441792b578cdbd", "parents": ["4735b8ae6d4f7052f3f8ad5bffe4cb95f631601e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "rperta \u003crperta@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2063372 - feat(trustpanel): Add telemetry for breach alert shield animation r=vinilla\" for causing build bustages\n\nThis reverts commit 450055e7d9ae39acfe78706971b8aaa14d82ce5b.\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser-trustPanel.js", "browser/components/controlcenter/metrics.yaml"], "git_node": "9d931e2643c5ed8678880dcd2f0924ffa709b1eb", "git_parents": ["3bfca537aa8bc7a6cb410face3e645b064bfb92b"], "node": "adfef0ffb82fca9ec624944f84f99ad4de6a2f1b", "parents": ["6343e41900d27583da547717e0441792b578cdbd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "AndiAJ \u003candiaj@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064068 - Remove noNetworkConnectionStartupTest UI test from flank configs r=aaronmt\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319113\n", "files": ["mobile/android/test_infra/flank-configs/fenix/arm-beta.yml", "mobile/android/test_infra/flank-configs/fenix/arm-smoke-tests.yml", "mobile/android/test_infra/flank-configs/fenix/arm-start-test.yml", "mobile/android/test_infra/flank-configs/fenix/armeabi-v7a-start-test.yml"], "git_node": "f7fd014c1815a50f7c651975583b3357a452da0e", "git_parents": ["9d931e2643c5ed8678880dcd2f0924ffa709b1eb"], "node": "95568ebbe0f1a040b39494c11daa88b990f43865", "parents": ["adfef0ffb82fca9ec624944f84f99ad4de6a2f1b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Parks \u003cdaparks@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058018 - Check the payload length in DragEnter before using r=win-reviewers,gstoll\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318224\n", "files": ["widget/windows/nsNativeDragTarget.cpp"], "git_node": "f5b0004d31ed032be715a29c354be554ce205cf5", "git_parents": ["f7fd014c1815a50f7c651975583b3357a452da0e"], "node": "ea24df4fce074d9cde622a1f9e72fd6d0b672f43", "parents": ["95568ebbe0f1a040b39494c11daa88b990f43865"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063043 - [efficiency] Convert SearchTest.verifyTabsSearchWithOpenTabsTest to ui/efficiency r=aaronmt\n\nPorts the legacy smoke test onto ui/efficiency and annotates the legacy method\nwith @Converted.\n\nHarness additions: four SearchBarSelectors entries (search shortcut, Firefox\nSuggest header, suggestion row, clear button) and TabDrawerPage.verifyOpenTabsOrder(),\nsince tab ordering cannot be expressed with the mozVerify* family - those only\nanswer \"does any node match\", not \"which position is it in\".\n\nTwo deliberate deviations from the legacy assertions, both equivalent or stricter:\nthe negative suggestion check asserts that no suggestion row contains the term,\nwhere legacy matched the plural container tag with assertAny(hasText().not()) and\nso passed whenever any node lacked the text; and the typed-toolbar check is a\nsubstring text match rather than a normalized semantics read.\n\nThe URL-based suggestion assertions only hold because SearchMockServerRule's\ndispatcher 404s everything except searchResults.html, so the tabs never load, have\nno title, and the awesomebar row renders the URL instead. The port keeps that rule\nso the legacy assertions carry over verbatim; the dependency is accidental rather\nthan intended and is worth revisiting separately.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318290\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/SearchTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/TabDrawerPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/SearchBarSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/SearchTest.kt"], "git_node": "2694497550fd70f9dd2a3adfede40f31550355af", "git_parents": ["f5b0004d31ed032be715a29c354be554ce205cf5"], "node": "8f54eae832f47c7706ccfcb6dd995ffd2a1dd88f", "parents": ["ea24df4fce074d9cde622a1f9e72fd6d0b672f43"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063045 - [efficiency] Convert SearchTest.searchEnginesCanBeChangedTemporarilyFromSearchSelectorMenuTest to ui/efficiency r=aaronmt\n\nPorts the legacy smoke test onto ui/efficiency and annotates the legacy method\nwith @Converted. Full parity, no deviations.\n\nNo harness additions were needed - SearchBarSelectors.SEARCH_SHORTCUT,\nToolbarSelectors.SEARCH_ENGINE_SELECTOR_ICON and BrowserPage.verifyUrl already\ncover every legacy verb.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318291\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/SearchTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/SearchTest.kt"], "git_node": "26e8514389993469ba235bd2b82d15b038863e6e", "git_parents": ["2694497550fd70f9dd2a3adfede40f31550355af"], "node": "6d18e5e22e6c42079808c9086f22e20f01b0c64a", "parents": ["8f54eae832f47c7706ccfcb6dd995ffd2a1dd88f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063046 - [efficiency] Convert SearchTest.verifyHistorySearchWithBrowsingHistoryTest to ui/efficiency r=aaronmt\n\nPorts the legacy smoke test onto ui/efficiency and annotates the legacy method\nwith @Converted. No harness additions - reuses the selectors added for bug 2063043.\n\nTwo deliberate deviations, as in bug 2063043 and both equivalent or stricter: the\nnegative suggestion check asserts that no suggestion row contains the term, where\nlegacy matched the plural container tag with assertAny(hasText().not()) and so\npassed whenever any node lacked the text; and the typed-toolbar check is a\nsubstring text match rather than a normalized semantics read.\n\nKeeps SearchMockServerRule deliberately: its dispatcher 404s everything except\nsearchResults.html, so the seeded pages never load and the awesomebar renders the\nURL, which is what the suggestion assertions match on.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318292\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/SearchTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/SearchTest.kt"], "git_node": "3470b43f7fd7a8244555e7e721bb289bac7a2970", "git_parents": ["26e8514389993469ba235bd2b82d15b038863e6e"], "node": "7e8d13deed043c7eae20571841aacaad4cacb1fd", "parents": ["6d18e5e22e6c42079808c9086f22e20f01b0c64a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063052 - [efficiency] Convert SearchTest.scanQRCodeToOpenAWebpageTest to ui/efficiency r=aaronmt\n\nPorts the legacy smoke test onto ui/efficiency and annotates the legacy method\nwith @Converted. Full parity, no deviations.\n\nAdds SearchBarSelectors.SCAN_BUTTON and SearchBarComponent.verifyScannerOpen().\nThe helper accepts either the view finder or the camera-error view, matching the\nlegacy robot: that alternation is deliberate, since a device with no usable camera\nshows an error and the test still means \"the scanner was launched\". mozVerify*\ncannot express alternation, so the helper drops to UIAutomator as legacy does.\n\nThe legacy Assume guard on cameraIdList is carried over, so the test skips rather\nthan fails where there is no camera.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318293\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/SearchTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/SearchBarComponent.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/SearchBarSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/SearchTest.kt"], "git_node": "21091c799c63c7777c3b58584d942fea8fee8bf5", "git_parents": ["3470b43f7fd7a8244555e7e721bb289bac7a2970"], "node": "7e06230adc2f4ede22538385167ca26cf709cc17", "parents": ["7e8d13deed043c7eae20571841aacaad4cacb1fd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063066 - [efficiency] Convert SearchTest.searchHistoryNotRememberedInPrivateBrowsingTest to ui/efficiency r=aaronmt\n\nPorts the legacy smoke test onto ui/efficiency and annotates the legacy method\nwith @Converted. Full parity on the flow and the assertions, with one legacy\nassertion strengthened as noted below.\n\nAdds two harness pieces the legacy assertions need:\n\n- BasePage.mozVerifyElementCount, the framework's first counting primitive. It\n  polls until the match count settles on the expected value rather than sampling\n  once, because a list still being populated passes through the expected count on\n  its way to a larger one.\n- SearchBarSelectors.SUGGESTIONS_HEADER(text), a parameterized form of the\n  existing FIREFOX_SUGGEST_HEADER, for the per-engine \"\u003cengine\u003e search\" header.\n\nThree workarounds carry the flow, all for nav-graph gaps tracked in MTE-5818:\n\n- forceNavigation on the SearchBarComponent hops. Its arrival check is\n  SEARCH_ENGINE_SELECTOR, which also renders on the home toolbar once a custom\n  search engine is registered, so the default already-visible check false-positives\n  and skips the click into edit mode.\n- mozWaitUntilAbsent(TOOLBAR_IN_EDIT_MODE) after each query submit. This was the\n  real blocker: BrowserPage's arrival check resolves the engine view underneath the\n  edit-mode overlay, so without it the run reports arrival on a page it never\n  reached, and the subsequent toolbar click toggles edit mode off instead of on.\n  The failure then surfaces several steps later, somewhere unrelated.\n- mozClickIfPresent for the toolbar click that re-opens edit mode. UiObject.click()\n  returns false there because the node goes stale as the toolbar swaps, even though\n  the click itself lands; mozClick turns that into a spurious failure.\n\nThe return to the homepage uses mozPressBackUntilGone(ENGINE_VIEW) instead of the\nregistered BrowserPage -\u003e HomePage edge, which clicks \"New tab\". That button is not\nreliably present after a search and opens a tab the legacy flow never opens.\n\nOne deliberate strengthening: legacy verifySuggestionsAreNotDisplayed asserts over\nthe awesomebar suggestions *container* rather than the suggestion rows, so it passes\ntrivially. This port keeps mozVerifyNoneContainText over the rows, consistent with\nthe two conversions already landed in this batch.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318294\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/SearchTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/BasePage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/SearchBarSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/SearchTest.kt"], "git_node": "b0f9c2ebf05ab5da831eb1e00366fe284e6a128a", "git_parents": ["21091c799c63c7777c3b58584d942fea8fee8bf5"], "node": "d09da0caf3ddb576d59284fcd9dda21fc4bf9259", "parents": ["7e06230adc2f4ede22538385167ca26cf709cc17"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063072 - [efficiency] Convert SearchTest.searchResultsOpenedInNewTabsGenerateSearchGroupsTest to ui/efficiency r=aaronmt\n\nPorts the legacy smoke test onto ui/efficiency and annotates the legacy method with\n@Converted. Full parity on the flow and the assertions.\n\nThe legacy test has been @Ignore'd since bug 1930244 for a rare CI intermittent\n(~1 per 3000-4500 pushes) in a legacy robot's refresh-retry fallback. The port is\nnot ignored, so this restores the coverage: the flow is entirely mock-server driven\nand the port asserts the results-page link is present before long-pressing it\nrather than relying on the fallback that flaked.\n\nMost of this patch is the shared search-group capability the remaining two\nsearch-group conversions also need, built once here:\n\n- BrowserPageSelectors.PAGE_LINK(text) - a web-content link keyed on exact text.\n  Exact and not CONTAINS, because PAGE_CONTENT(text) cannot tell \"Link 1\" from\n  \"Link 10\" and these tests long-press both links on one page.\n- BrowserPageSelectors.CONTEXT_MENU_ITEM(text) - a web-content context menu item,\n  UiObject2 like the legacy By.text, since these items open a tab without\n  necessarily updating the window.\n- BrowserPage.longClickPageObjectUntilContextMenu - restores the legacy\n  longClickPageObject retry, which is load-bearing: mozLongClick is single-shot,\n  and a long press landing before GeckoView settles opens no menu. The legacy\n  fallback between attempts is a three-dot-menu Refresh, reproduced here.\n- TabDrawerPage.closeAllTabs plus CLOSE_ALL_TABS_BUTTON and\n  CLOSE_ALL_TABS_CONFIRM_BUTTON. The confirmation dialog is not optional: \"Close\n  all tabs\" only arms it, and skipping the confirm leaves every tab open, which\n  would turn any later \"no tabs\" or search-group assertion into a false pass.\n- HomeSelectors.RECENTLY_VISITED_HEADER and RECENTLY_VISITED_SEARCH_GROUP(term).\n  The group's \"N pages\" caption is a sibling text node, asserted with the existing\n  mozVerifyElementHasSiblingWithText.\n- BasePage.mozPressBack - a single back press. mozPressBackUntilGone cannot stand in\n  when what is being left has no selector to poll (here, closing a tab whose page\n  404s), and \"back until X is gone\" would press again if the first press has not\n  landed yet.\n\nTwo changes beyond the new capability:\n\n- Pocket is disabled class-wide, matching the legacy SearchTest rule, which runs\n  every test in this class with isPocketEnabled = false. It matters here: with\n  Pocket on, \"Recently visited\" can sit below the fold and mozVerify does not\n  scroll, so a \"group is displayed\" assertion fails and a \"group is gone\" assertion\n  passes for the wrong reason. All six tests in the class were run together to\n  confirm the five already converted are unaffected.\n- BrowserPageSelectors.SNACKBAR_EDIT_BUTTON is renamed to SNACKBAR_ACTION_BUTTON\n  (mechanical, 2 call sites in BookmarksTest and MainMenuTest). It is the snackbar's\n  single action button and its label varies with the snackbar - \"Edit\", \"SWITCH\",\n  \"UNDO\" - so clicking SWITCH through a selector named EDIT would make the run logs\n  misleading. No behavior change: same tag, same strategy.\n\nNote the legacy verifyUrl swallows its timeout and never fails; the efficiency\nBrowserPage.verifyUrl used here throws. That strengthening predates this patch and\nis unchanged by it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318295\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/SearchTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/BasePage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/BrowserPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/TabDrawerPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/BrowserPageSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/HomeSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/TabDrawerSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/BookmarksTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/MainMenuTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/SearchTest.kt"], "git_node": "6fd88e92047759c018cd079a1fe59cec9b008ec0", "git_parents": ["b0f9c2ebf05ab5da831eb1e00366fe284e6a128a"], "node": "ebfe2d9842c3c1fdbcd555c6b20deba6be2952d7", "parents": ["d09da0caf3ddb576d59284fcd9dda21fc4bf9259"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063074 - [efficiency] Convert SearchTest.searchGroupIsNotGeneratedForLinksOpenedInPrivateTabsTest to ui/efficiency r=aaronmt\n\nPorts the legacy smoke test onto ui/efficiency and annotates the legacy method with\n@Converted. Reuses the search-group capability added in bug 2063072; the only new\npieces are two small ones:\n\n- TabDrawerPage.openPrivateTab(position) - positional, like verifyOpenTabsOrder, and\n  for the same reason: the mozClick family can say \"click something matching\" but not\n  \"click the nth child\". Each private tab has to actually be opened, not merely\n  created: the pages are lazily loaded until selected, and loading them is what would\n  leak into history if private browsing did not isolate it.\n- HistorySelectors.HISTORY_ITEM_WITH_TEXT(text) - any History row containing text,\n  mirroring the legacy generic verifyHistoryItemExists.\n\nEvery return to the tab manager is re-anchored through BrowserPage, because a\nTabDrawerPage -\u003e TabDrawerPage path resolves to an empty step list and would silently\ndo nothing (MTE-5818).\n\nOne deliberate deviation, worth a reviewer's eye. Legacy finishes with\n\n    verifyHistoryItemExists(shouldExist = false, item = \"3 sites\")\n\nbut the History screen renders a group's size through\nhistory_search_group_sites_1 = \"%d pages\" (HistoryListItemViewHolder.kt:80-88), and\ngrepping the tree finds no \"%d sites\" string in any locale. The legacy assertion\ntherefore checks for the absence of text the app can never render: it passes even if\nthe search group is present, so it contributes no coverage. This port asserts the\nabsence of the caption the app actually renders (\"3 pages\"). It asserts the caption\nrather than the group title because the title is the search term, which also appears\ninside the visited search-results URL and so is present on that screen either way.\n\nNote also that the homepage caption is \"N pages\" while the legacy test's wording\nsuggested \"N sites\" - there is only one string, used by both screens.\n\nGreen on the first device attempt, no retries.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318296\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/SearchTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/TabDrawerPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/HistorySelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/SearchTest.kt"], "git_node": "c48d9359e0dc41da77b0dd5317ba9b26caccadf5", "git_parents": ["6fd88e92047759c018cd079a1fe59cec9b008ec0"], "node": "aee54c70e73201c0be8bcb8bbae814ce0cd9df48", "parents": ["ebfe2d9842c3c1fdbcd555c6b20deba6be2952d7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063080 - [efficiency] Convert SearchTest.deleteIndividualHistoryItemsFromSearchGroupTest to ui/efficiency r=aaronmt\n\nPorts the legacy smoke test onto ui/efficiency and annotates the legacy method with\n@Converted. Reuses the search-group capability from bug 2063072; the group-building\nsteps are duplicated from searchResultsOpenedInNewTabsGenerateSearchGroupsTest rather\nthan shared, because the legacy tests duplicate them too and are reviewed side by side.\n\nAdds HistorySearchGroupPage and HistorySearchGroupSelectors for the search-group\nhistory screen. It cannot reuse HistoryPage: that page's arrival check requires the\nliteral \"History\" toolbar title, and this screen's title is the search term. It is\nalso deliberately absent from PageContext and registers no navigation edge, because it\nis entered by clicking a *dynamic* label - the group's title - which NavigationRegistry\ncannot express. Tests instantiate it directly, as ReaderViewTest does for\nReaderViewPage, through a get() property so it binds to the composeRule of the current\nretry attempt.\n\nThe two delete paths are kept distinct, as legacy has them: the per-row cross for the\nfirst item and long-press multi-selection for the second. Three details are worth a\nreviewer's attention, each found on device:\n\n- The per-row delete control is the row's overflow view, repurposed on this screen as a\n  delete cross carrying the content description \"Delete\"\n  (HistoryMetadataGroupItemViewHolder). Rows are identified by their sibling URL text,\n  as the legacy robot does, via the existing ESPRESSO_BY_ID_WITH_SIBLING_TEXT strategy.\n- The multi-select long press must go through Espresso, not UiAutomator.\n  UiObject.longClick() is not held long enough for this row: the row treats it as a tap\n  and opens the page, which silently moves the test to the browser and makes the\n  following overflow click open the app's main menu instead. Espresso's longClick()\n  honours the platform long-press timeout, which is what legacy relies on.\n- The multi-select overflow is reached by selector rather than by Espresso's\n  openActionBarOverflowOrOptionsMenu, which finds no matching view on this screen. Going\n  through a selector also means a failure produces a screen dump rather than a bare\n  NoMatchingViewException - which is how the long-press problem above was diagnosed.\n\nBoth deletions wait the undo snackbar out (mozWaitUntilAbsent) before continuing, since\na delete only commits once it is gone; legacy waits only after the multi-select delete.\nThe final assertion uses mozWaitUntilAbsent rather than mozVerifyElementAbsent because\nthe homepage rebuilds asynchronously after the deletions - legacy covers that with a 1s\nwindow wait before a single-shot check. The assertion is not vacuous: the same test\nasserts the group present with its \"3 pages\" caption earlier in the run.\n\nVerified with a full-class run: all 8 tests in SearchTest pass, the 2 pre-existing\n@Ignore'd ones skipped.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318297\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/SearchTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/HistorySearchGroupPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/HistorySearchGroupSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/SearchTest.kt"], "git_node": "4c5aa03c7c03c74b8dca93edbe5f818dcc738fd9", "git_parents": ["c48d9359e0dc41da77b0dd5317ba9b26caccadf5"], "node": "780111df34828568ba32ee0d112858e42b0a719a", "parents": ["aee54c70e73201c0be8bcb8bbae814ce0cd9df48"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063102 - [efficiency] Convert SearchTest.verifyQRScanningCameraAccessDialogTest to ui/efficiency r=aaronmt\n\nPorts the legacy smoke test onto ui/efficiency and annotates the legacy method with\n@Converted. This is the first ui/efficiency test that drives windows outside the app\nprocess: the Android permission controller and the Settings app.\n\nAdds BasePage.mozVerifyElementStaysAbsent, and it is load-bearing rather than\ndefensive. With camera permission denied, the FIRST \"Ready to scan\" click still\nnavigates to PairFragment - Fenix only consults the permission after the one-shot\npref_key_camera_permissions_needed has been consumed - PairFragment's own request is\nauto-denied and it pops straight back, so the button REAPPEARS. Only the second click\nreaches the permission dialog. Requiring the button to stay absent for a sustained\nwindow is what distinguishes \"the dialog is covering it\" from \"we bounced through\nPairFragment and came back\"; an instantaneous absence check cannot tell those apart and\ndesynchronises the rest of the flow. SettingsTurnOnSyncPage.clickReadyToScanUntilPermissionDialog\nreproduces the legacy retry that this drives.\n\nAlso adds BasePage.mozPressBackUntilPresent, the counterpart to mozPressBackUntilGone,\nfor backing out of an unknown number of screens. Two places needed it: returning from the\nSettings app (legacy presses back a fixed three times, which assumes an exact back-stack\ndepth in an app we do not control) and returning to the homepage after the denials, where\nhow deep we are depends on whether the scanner fragment appeared first.\n\nNote which anchor that second one uses: HomeSelectors.MAIN_MENU_BUTTON, not\nHOMEPAGE_VIEW. The homepage view resolves *behind* the search overlay, so anchoring on it\nreturns immediately while the toolbar is still covered - and since HomePage's arrival\ncheck needs the menu button, the following navigateToPage then routes through the\n\"New tab\" edge and fails. Same family as the overlay problem in bug 2063066.\n\nNew system selectors, in SystemSettingsSelectors: the permission controller's Deny and\n\"Deny and don't ask again\" buttons, the App info \"Permissions\" row, a named app-permission\nrow, and the Allow option. Plus a new UIAUTOMATOR2_BY_RAW_RES strategy: these ids belong\nto com.android.permissioncontroller, so UIAUTOMATOR2_BY_RES cannot address them (it\nprefixes the app's own package), and the UiObject strategies click through clickAndSync,\nwhich intermittently reported a successful dialog dismissal as a failure. The Fenix\ncamera-permission dialog's own buttons are UiObject2 for the same reason.\n\nSystemSettingsPage gains openAppPermissions and allowAppPermission. openAppPermissions\nwaits for the Permissions row before clicking: the caller has just left Fenix via an\nintent and the Settings activity may not have drawn yet, which the legacy helper races.\n\nThe test resets camera permission itself rather than relying on the orchestrator's\nclearPackageData, because BaseTest retries in the same process. Both halves matter: the\nflow ends with \"Deny and don't ask again\", which sets FLAG_PERMISSION_USER_FIXED, and a\nplain revoke leaves that set - a second attempt is then auto-denied with no dialog at all\nand fails looking for a Deny button that never appears. It is scoped to this app and this\npermission; the device-wide `pm reset-permissions` strips permissions the instrumentation\nitself relies on and crashes the test process.\n\nFixes a copy-paste in SettingsTurnOnSyncSelectors: READY_TO_SCAN_BUTTON was described as\n\"Use email instead button\", which made every run log for it misleading.\n\nTwo clean runs. Note the emulator's virtual camera fails intermittently with\n\"CaptureRequest contains unconfigured Input/Output Surface!\" from QrFragment - it hit this\ntest once and scanQRCodeToOpenAWebpageTest once today, and is unrelated to the port.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318299\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/SearchTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/BasePage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/Selector.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/SettingsTurnOnSyncPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/SystemSettingsPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/SettingsTurnOnSyncSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/SystemSettingsSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/SearchTest.kt"], "git_node": "fa8fcf4ea22cd99cdb50ef8142fb27ec488f383a", "git_parents": ["4c5aa03c7c03c74b8dca93edbe5f818dcc738fd9"], "node": "60f2da1e6707ebe0bd5cd29d8091fbb2af3fe8bb", "parents": ["780111df34828568ba32ee0d112858e42b0a719a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Parks \u003cdaparks@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058013 - Only resolve non-filesystem picker results as shell libraries r=win-reviewers,gstoll\n\nA genuine shell library is a virtual item with no filesystem path.  A\n.library-ms file is an ordinary file whose XML can name any local directory.\n\nfiledialog::GetFolderResults was passing whatever IFileDialog::GetResult\nreturned to IShellLibrary::LoadLibraryFromItem and, on success, replacing it\nwith the library's embedded default save folder.\n\nGating the resolution on the item being affirmatively not a filesystem object\nkeeps real libraries selectable and resolving as before, while a .library-ms\nfile \"resolves\" to itself -- the .library-ms file, not its target.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318246\n", "files": ["widget/windows/filedialog/WinFileDialogCommands.cpp"], "git_node": "a9b3ed869e3233c164be54ff5dbe313ee417152d", "git_parents": ["fa8fcf4ea22cd99cdb50ef8142fb27ec488f383a"], "node": "f5498890236c25b7684bac26deab7fb001fa0790", "parents": ["60f2da1e6707ebe0bd5cd29d8091fbb2af3fe8bb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Parks \u003cdaparks@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058006 - Call Destroy() unconditionally in ~StatusBarEntry. r=win-reviewers,gstoll\n\nAllow Destroy() to tear down mIconLoader, even if Init() does not successfully\ncomplete initialization.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318206\n", "files": ["widget/windows/SystemStatusBar.cpp"], "git_node": "947572bf2d1d2967c73050165c67b226284acfd5", "git_parents": ["a9b3ed869e3233c164be54ff5dbe313ee417152d"], "node": "68817ed84048993f211e0f5c28289aa40b450752", "parents": ["f5498890236c25b7684bac26deab7fb001fa0790"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Parks \u003cdaparks@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057990: Part 1 - Check Windows DROPFILES data r=win-reviewers,gstoll\n\nAdds nsClipboard::IsValidDropFilesData to sanity check that we were given a\nvalid DROPFILES structure.  An invalid structure would have to be posted\nby whatever application owns the clipboard or starts the drag; Gecko's own\nwriter always emits a well-formed DROPFILES.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318849\n", "files": ["widget/windows/nsClipboard.cpp", "widget/windows/nsClipboard.h", "widget/windows/nsDragService.cpp", "widget/windows/tests/gtest/TestWinDND.cpp"], "git_node": "1a8e53c86ab442d2ac9cce1e1626f974c0890cc8", "git_parents": ["947572bf2d1d2967c73050165c67b226284acfd5"], "node": "4a8a2a8b82b19f7dac29f6216340dbf5452e4c67", "parents": ["68817ed84048993f211e0f5c28289aa40b450752"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Parks \u003cdaparks@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057990: Part 2 - Validate Web Custom Format Map slot names on Windows. r=win-reviewers,gstoll\n\nThe Web Custom Format Map maps to web custom format names, which must follow the\nclipboard spec (https://www.w3.org/TR/clipboard-apis/#to-write-web-custom-formats).\nWhen looking them up in map in the Windows clipboard, verify that the name is a\nvalid Web Custom Format name.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318850\n", "files": ["widget/windows/nsClipboard.cpp"], "git_node": "80f37afa6f5e3ccc7a2aab040e93cbbc3d6ebba1", "git_parents": ["1a8e53c86ab442d2ac9cce1e1626f974c0890cc8"], "node": "abf7a096349dce1631a81cf44358c06bc02d12fe", "parents": ["4a8a2a8b82b19f7dac29f6216340dbf5452e4c67"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Parks \u003cdaparks@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061231 - Use PathCchCanonicalize in WinUtils::CanonicalizePath. r=win-reviewers,gstoll\n\nPathCchCanonicalize is documented by Microsoft as preferable to\nPathCanonicalize, for buffer safety reasons.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318223\n", "files": ["widget/windows/WinUtils.cpp", "widget/windows/WinUtils.h", "widget/windows/moz.build", "widget/windows/tests/gtest/TestWinUtils.cpp"], "git_node": "4233e7b2be3242de0f9dcd4ec4bf9d399260cfcb", "git_parents": ["80f37afa6f5e3ccc7a2aab040e93cbbc3d6ebba1"], "node": "b1ac87e89d1a4048fc046e4cdc404d88e4eb358b", "parents": ["abf7a096349dce1631a81cf44358c06bc02d12fe"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Release Engineering Landoscript \u003crelease+landoscript@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug - Bumping Firefox l10n changesets r=release a=l10n-bump DONTBUILD CLOSED TREE\n\nach -\u003e 1fcb38aadaf2b8783e282606b3d402d6e0fdabd7\naf -\u003e 1fcb38aadaf2b8783e282606b3d402d6e0fdabd7\nan -\u003e 1fcb38aadaf2b8783e282606b3d402d6e0fdabd7\nar -\u003e 1fcb38aadaf2b8783e282606b3d402d6e0fdabd7\nast -\u003e 1fcb38aadaf2b8783e282606b3d402d6e0fdabd7\naz -\u003e 1fcb38aadaf2b8783e282606b3d402d6e0fdabd7\nbe -\u003e 1fcb38aadaf2b8783e282606b3d402d6e0fdabd7\nbg -\u003e 1fcb38aadaf2b8783e282606b3d402d6e0fdabd7\nbn -\u003e 1fcb38aadaf2b8783e282606b3d402d6e0fdabd7\nbo -\u003e 1fcb38aadaf2b8783e282606b3d402d6e0fdabd7\nbq