tAnimationFrame`\nand `performance` genuinely aren't, which is why those go through the window.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318770\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tabbrowser.js"], "git_node": "9b0ea367814c150c54f7511b8afbc0d620b9cb7c", "git_parents": ["22e9944c39b21f07ef147acede52168c333cddf9"], "node": "b137f59e9809016fc9e8021f9fc10c041445546f", "parents": ["70666e03ec52ed6afaba9547d3ea7ad1fd715408"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049770 - Construct the tabbrowser's events in its own window. r=tabbrowser-reviewers,jsudiaman\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318771\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tabbrowser.js"], "git_node": "19b4db5ae569bd947e9115ec69caeaa59050fd32", "git_parents": ["9b0ea367814c150c54f7511b8afbc0d620b9cb7c"], "node": "b73f8bad3ac2e26053fb8742e65339eb0a085d7e", "parents": ["b137f59e9809016fc9e8021f9fc10c041445546f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049770 - Move the Tabbrowser class to a shared module. r=tabbrowser-reviewers,frontend-codestyle-reviewers,jsudiaman,mossop\n\n`BrowserUtils.callModulesFromCategory` imports a module entry itself, so the\nwindow stops loading the file and the two category lines carry the new URI\ninstead.\n\nThe private scope block stays wrapped, which is what keeps the rename detectable\nand the file's blame intact; unwrapping it is a whitespace-only follow-up. The\nmodule getters defined on the instance stay on the instance, since\n`gBrowser.TabMetrics` and friends are reached from ~95 call sites outside this\nfile.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318772\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser-main.js", "browser/components/BrowserComponents.manifest", "browser/components/tabbrowser/Tabbrowser.sys.mjs", "browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tabbrowser.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/docs/async-tab-switcher.md", "browser/components/tabbrowser/docs/index.md", "browser/components/tabbrowser/jar.mn", "browser/components/tabbrowser/moz.build", "eslint-file-globals.config.mjs", "eslint-rollouts.config.mjs"], "git_node": "c3400aa1740563efb4a772068275864848968f96", "git_parents": ["19b4db5ae569bd947e9115ec69caeaa59050fd32"], "node": "bcc02bc321088fdc55d908c6caca115451073c20", "parents": ["b73f8bad3ac2e26053fb8742e65339eb0a085d7e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049770 - Drop the cross-window progress listener accessors. r=tabbrowser-reviewers,jsudiaman\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318773\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/Tabbrowser.sys.mjs", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser_swapBrowsers.js"], "git_node": "ffe1fd57f09722c153a0b25622055ad68d8c04bc", "git_parents": ["c3400aa1740563efb4a772068275864848968f96"], "node": "a290a492d7ca358fc0c49f6bb000dad2bae45c82", "parents": ["bcc02bc321088fdc55d908c6caca115451073c20"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ben Visness \u003cbvisness@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2013741: Add regression test. r=rhunt\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D282423\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/gc/regress-2013741.js"], "git_node": "bd5161aeffe1246d9acd2213735183d93246c4a9", "git_parents": ["ffe1fd57f09722c153a0b25622055ad68d8c04bc"], "node": "3e9d5db433538190bad3c2442e382c8e687f3c44", "parents": ["a290a492d7ca358fc0c49f6bb000dad2bae45c82"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Niklas Baumgardner \u003cnbaumgardner@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059854 - Make profile avatar selector a proper dialog. r=mossop\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318755\n", "files": ["browser/components/profiles/content/edit-profile-card.css", "browser/components/profiles/content/edit-profile-card.mjs", "browser/components/profiles/content/profile-avatar-selector.css", "browser/components/profiles/content/profile-avatar-selector.mjs", "browser/components/profiles/tests/browser/browser_custom_avatar_test.js", "browser/components/profiles/tests/browser/browser_edit_profile_test.js"], "git_node": "643e22c0ae199b98e1e0ba85dbd9c13ee4c23f3b", "git_parents": ["bd5161aeffe1246d9acd2213735183d93246c4a9"], "node": "a1f9bf2ec4eca7fe20daee2fbceca7bbee6caa24", "parents": ["3e9d5db433538190bad3c2442e382c8e687f3c44"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Niklas Baumgardner \u003cnbaumgardner@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059853 - Add aria label for profile avatar selector dialog. r=morgan,fluent-reviewers,mossop,bolsson\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318756\n", "files": ["browser/components/profiles/content/profile-avatar-selector.mjs", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/profiles.ftl"], "git_node": "8ef94d9f0b21668ed336106bb4bd14599773a6fb", "git_parents": ["643e22c0ae199b98e1e0ba85dbd9c13ee4c23f3b"], "node": "d092e45649f0cc55d83d01ee6c399d67d9975d7c", "parents": ["a1f9bf2ec4eca7fe20daee2fbceca7bbee6caa24"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ben Visness \u003cbvisness@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2028009: Update wasm GLB tests. r=rhunt\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D291229\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/gc/ref-gvn.js", "js/src/jit/MIR-wasm.cpp", "js/src/jit/ValueNumbering.cpp", "js/src/jit/WasmRefTypeAnalysis.cpp", "js/src/jsapi-tests/testWasmRefSubtypes.cpp", "js/src/wasm/WasmValType.cpp"], "git_node": "d1cb09129982d1ac7c965a574e9ecbc61e5cf941", "git_parents": ["8ef94d9f0b21668ed336106bb4bd14599773a6fb"], "node": "9376e5ba1009feefc02ea82067f6028b6ad5f831", "parents": ["d092e45649f0cc55d83d01ee6c399d67d9975d7c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1816023 - Allow the onMoveToNewWindow rejection in browser_ext_tabs_move_array_multiple_windows.js, r=extension-reviewers,robwu.\n\nThis test moves tabs between windows and hits the same rejection nine other\ntests in this folder already allow. The analysis is in bug 1938594 comment 6.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318267\n", "files": ["browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_ext_tabs_move_array_multiple_windows.js"], "git_node": "04a77960970a72de2186e5b0f58803942b62d415", "git_parents": ["d1cb09129982d1ac7c965a574e9ecbc61e5cf941"], "node": "1d475b732091d1a1d2e540c0e8810030c194c74f", "parents": ["9376e5ba1009feefc02ea82067f6028b6ad5f831"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1816023 - Re-enable browser_ext_tabs_move_array_multiple_windows.js on the Windows coverage build, r=extension-reviewers,robwu.\n\nThe condition cites bug 1786601, which is browser_ext_tabs_events.js's tracking bug.\nIt was created by a win11 greenup carrying annotations forward, but this test had no\nskip-if to carry.\n\nThe only way coverage instrumentation could fail this test is the harness timeout,\nand browser-chrome gets 45s on opt with no ccov branch and no timeoutfactor from\nenable_code_coverage. A slower sibling doing the same thing already passes there\nunskipped.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318268\n", "files": ["browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser-tabstrip.toml"], "git_node": "6e34272ad8d8a2232925766461abcb821dbfbdac", "git_parents": ["04a77960970a72de2186e5b0f58803942b62d415"], "node": "c3700e4487a2902300279dba448c4c56d5071a28", "parents": ["1d475b732091d1a1d2e540c0e8810030c194c74f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Parks \u003cdaparks@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059027 - Create the DLL blocklist shared section with an empty DACL. r=win-reviewers,gstoll\n\nSharedSection::Init() creates the section with no security descriptor.\nGive the object a present-but-empty DACL, as ipc/glue does for freezable\nshared memory.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318252\n", "files": ["browser/app/winlauncher/freestanding/SharedSection.cpp", "browser/app/winlauncher/freestanding/moz.build", "browser/app/winlauncher/test/TestCrossProcessWin.cpp", "browser/app/winlauncher/test/moz.build"], "git_node": "bd6ad7cc738a7578cd15b65bb8ccdec739c4dd39", "git_parents": ["6e34272ad8d8a2232925766461abcb821dbfbdac"], "node": "01b34d7ffdbc56f253b0cb9e8fc465533531ef0c", "parents": ["c3700e4487a2902300279dba448c4c56d5071a28"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063751 - Use preserveAspectRatio=\"none\" for download animations. r=desktop-theme-reviewers,sfoster\n\nSee comment 16 and bug 2063903 for why this fixes the issue.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318944\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/downloads/notification-finish-animation.svg", "browser/themes/shared/downloads/notification-start-animation.svg"], "git_node": "3e6c5d70380a1edad0cf03e9f9ed1dad7b3022b9", "git_parents": ["bd6ad7cc738a7578cd15b65bb8ccdec739c4dd39"], "node": "f02cd1d3a8cbe583a2ee89730e7bec3266ef10b6", "parents": ["01b34d7ffdbc56f253b0cb9e8fc465533531ef0c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Halberstadt \u003cahal@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058156 - Make android-lint tasks clone with Git, r=taskgraph-reviewers,Eijebong\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317876\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/source-test/android-lint.yml"], "git_node": "57257274d6e8183c93186b0e5732bc4e0b79a29a", "git_parents": ["3e6c5d70380a1edad0cf03e9f9ed1dad7b3022b9"], "node": "99a7d9522b6c961c26086bdba4da26eae1aad40b", "parents": ["f02cd1d3a8cbe583a2ee89730e7bec3266ef10b6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Halberstadt \u003cahal@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058156 - Make lint tasks clone with Git, r=taskgraph-reviewers,Eijebong\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317615\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/source-test/mozlint-android.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/source-test/mozlint.yml"], "git_node": "c9d70707abb254bfc21272eeff0e8aac3028dccb", "git_parents": ["57257274d6e8183c93186b0e5732bc4e0b79a29a"], "node": "394133362ca30dbf92c68fcb73d571f6fb37c380", "parents": ["99a7d9522b6c961c26086bdba4da26eae1aad40b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dana Keeler \u003cdkeeler@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063132 - properly determine TLS handshake auth curve for ECDSA r=jschanck\n\nThis also takes the opportunity to avoid some unnecessary work when gathering\nkey exchange and auth curve telemetry.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318852\n", "files": ["security/manager/ssl/metrics.yaml", "security/manager/ssl/nsNSSCallbacks.cpp"], "git_node": "b8a8005b3210c54a96618f1cc7cf3f019e074020", "git_parents": ["c9d70707abb254bfc21272eeff0e8aac3028dccb"], "node": "36a863cd50fa1fdc3bc12441abc8df4aad4b8d6c", "parents": ["394133362ca30dbf92c68fcb73d571f6fb37c380"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063726 - Set done from a finally so a raise in the xpcshell timeout cleanup can't strand the run, r=ahal.\n\ntestTimeout runs on the timer thread, and everything between marking a test timed\nout and marking it done -- killing the process, processing its dump, reporting the\ntimeout, cleaning the temp dirs -- can raise. When it does, the thread dies without\nsetting done and without releasing the lock. The test's own thread is typically\nblocked forever on a stdout pipe a surviving child process holds open, so nothing\nelse will ever set done and the scheduler waits for that test until mozharness kills\nthe job on its 1000 second output timeout.\n\nA try push hit this on Windows, where mozcrash raised PermissionError copying a\nminidump the OS still had open.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318833\n", "files": ["testing/xpcshell/runxpcshelltests.py"], "git_node": "7b113835e4816c4b0f816e286cf3eeef1f8e66ba", "git_parents": ["b8a8005b3210c54a96618f1cc7cf3f019e074020"], "node": "9d13cd75518c040684b6d9518fed24b00c423461", "parents": ["36a863cd50fa1fdc3bc12441abc8df4aad4b8d6c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ting-Yu Lin \u003ctlin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063787 - Update anchor-pos-transform-01.html to use a translate transform. r=layout-reviewers,emilio\n\nThe bounding box of a rotated `.scroller` cannot be expressed with integer\npixels in the reference file once the anchor's transform is taken into account.\nThis patch changes `rotate` to `translate`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318632\n", "files": ["layout/reftests/transform/anchor-pos-transform-01-ref.html", "layout/reftests/transform/anchor-pos-transform-01.html", "layout/reftests/transform/reftest.list"], "git_node": "388ab760d43ac0727d48e555aa66395ea05a12a8", "git_parents": ["7b113835e4816c4b0f816e286cf3eeef1f8e66ba"], "node": "11012e5b79b4290d364bbfbde75398e795f46411", "parents": ["9d13cd75518c040684b6d9518fed24b00c423461"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Roger Yang \u003croyang@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061603 - Don't crash when Android rejects a notification post. r=android-reviewers,twhite\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318594\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/support/base/src/main/java/mozilla/components/support/base/android/NotificationsDelegate.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/support/base/src/test/java/mozilla/components/support/base/android/NotificationsDelegateTest.kt"], "git_node": "4e7a5f14b1de6689a685878189dadc92a1d8abb0", "git_parents": ["388ab760d43ac0727d48e555aa66395ea05a12a8"], "node": "285922857e2a455b600696f2a32411b63a1e78b5", "parents": ["11012e5b79b4290d364bbfbde75398e795f46411"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Beth Rennie \u003cbeth@brennie.ca\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2048365 - MOZ_DIAGNOSTIC_ASSERT when calling the NimbusFeature API with an unsupported feature r=nimbus-reviewers,chumphreys\n\nPreviously it was possible to use the Nimbus C++ API with features that\nwere not marked with `isEarlyStartup: true`. This would result in always\nreturning the default value, even when enrolled in an experiment. Now we\nwill throw a `MOZ_DIAGNOSTIC_ASSERT`, which will cause a crash in\nNightly and early Beta, which should hopefully result in these cases\nbeing caught before making it to release.\n\nWhile I was here I cleaned a few things up:\n\n* `NimbusFeatureManifest.inc.h` does not need to exist -- these functions\n  are only used inside `NimbusFeatures.cpp`;\n* the private static methods of the NimbusFeatures class can be static\n  functions inside `NimbusFeatures.cpp` -- it maintains essentially the\n  same isolation boundary and removes implementation details from the\n  public API;\n* likewise, the static constants inside `NimbusFeatures` were moved into\n  `NimbusFeatures.cpp` for the same reason.\n* `GetPrefName()` was renamed to `GetNimbusPrefName()` to be more\n  specific and prevent potential future naming conflicts with unified\n  builds;\n* the generated members have been moved to the `mozilla::nimbus`\n  namespace as to not pollute the global `mozilla` namespace;\n* generated code has been updated to use constinit `std::array`;\n* code generation has been cleaned up, producing human-readable\n  artifacts;\n* code generation has been refactored to use list comprehensions to make\n  the code more idiomatic; and\n* variable names are now more idiomatic (`snake_case` vs mixed\n  `snake_case` and `camelCase`).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D307417\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/nimbus/generate/generate_feature_manifest.py", "toolkit/components/nimbus/lib/NimbusFeatureManifest.inc.h", "toolkit/components/nimbus/lib/NimbusFeatures.cpp", "toolkit/components/nimbus/lib/NimbusFeatures.h", "toolkit/components/nimbus/test/gtest/NimbusFeatures_GetTest.cpp", "toolkit/components/nimbus/test/gtest/NimbusFeatures_RecordExposure.cpp"], "git_node": "3a069da85cf5b6073183b7a3ffab74d8e8f7abf1", "git_parents": ["4e7a5f14b1de6689a685878189dadc92a1d8abb0"], "node": "5c1b97d43142920afa8b0fcddaa1b6ea43b1279b", "parents": ["285922857e2a455b600696f2a32411b63a1e78b5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "acreskeyMoz \u003cacreskey@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060983 - Identify prefetched resources in profiler network markers. r=necko-reviewers,profiler-reviewers,ipc-reviewers,canova,kershaw\n\nAdds secPurpose (the Sec-Purpose request header) and deliveryType\n(\"navigational-prefetch\") to the Network marker payload, so the profiler\ncan tell a speculative prefetch from the navigation served from it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317511\n", "files": ["ipc/glue/BackgroundUtils.cpp", "netwerk/base/LoadInfo.h", "netwerk/base/nsILoadInfo.idl", "netwerk/ipc/DocumentLoadListener.cpp", "netwerk/ipc/NeckoChannelParams.ipdlh", "netwerk/protocol/http/HttpBaseChannel.h", "netwerk/protocol/http/HttpChannelChild.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/InterceptedHttpChannel.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/NetworkMarker.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/NetworkMarker.h", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpAtomList.inc", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpChannel.cpp", "tools/profiler/tests/browser/browser.toml", "tools/profiler/tests/browser/browser_test_marker_network_prefetch.js", "tools/profiler/tests/browser/speculation_rules_prefetch.html", "tools/profiler/tests/gtest/GeckoProfiler.cpp"], "git_node": "19364ece9322ea291bf8e16acf3dd0b360610257", "git_parents": ["3a069da85cf5b6073183b7a3ffab74d8e8f7abf1"], "node": "a7176b64e6d292d6b7701c47d4df53c4340146a2", "parents": ["5c1b97d43142920afa8b0fcddaa1b6ea43b1279b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Niklas Baumgardner \u003cnbaumgardner@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2052265 - Add QR code button to share panel. r=jprickett\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317131\n", "files": ["browser/components/sharing/SharePageAction.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sharing/SharingUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sharing/tests/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/sharing/tests/browser/browser_testSharePanelQRCode.js"], "git_node": "4eb65f802a63552142329f37723802aa09cf014a", "git_parents": ["19364ece9322ea291bf8e16acf3dd0b360610257"], "node": "f395dc375427429b2edb798d0f9568a50868b648", "parents": ["a7176b64e6d292d6b7701c47d4df53c4340146a2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Niklas Baumgardner \u003cnbaumgardner@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2052263 - Add windows sharing functionality to share panel. r=jprickett\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318243\n", "files": ["browser/components/sharing/SharePageAction.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sharing/tests/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/sharing/tests/browser/browser_testSharePanelWindowsShare.js"], "git_node": "a1d03e82e8944828f4b45301705534a32a2cd9ae", "git_parents": ["4eb65f802a63552142329f37723802aa09cf014a"], "node": "5477936fddcee5a8017a10e9e4940ca6c7aef705", "parents": ["f395dc375427429b2edb798d0f9568a50868b648"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Niklas Baumgardner \u003cnbaumgardner@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2052268 - Toggle share panel button visibility depending on the url. r=jprickett\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318488\n", "files": ["browser/components/sharing/SharePageAction.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sharing/tests/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/sharing/tests/browser/browser_testSharePanelButtonVisibility.js"], "git_node": "e707ac311a178433076e4f953b049f09f563c9d6", "git_parents": ["a1d03e82e8944828f4b45301705534a32a2cd9ae"], "node": "205f690f4830606823f2d6a8927e5d99bbcb7aed", "parents": ["5477936fddcee5a8017a10e9e4940ca6c7aef705"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jed Davis \u003cjld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059702 - Fix some Tier-3 build issues in SharedMemoryPlatform_posix. r=nika,gaston\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317966\n", "files": ["ipc/glue/SharedMemoryPlatform_posix.cpp"], "git_node": "59a7cfde7ac9277b2e19ba20340411a6fc2ed24c", "git_parents": ["e707ac311a178433076e4f953b049f09f563c9d6"], "node": "93626f0b4a699ca032a54df802e678e922d32611", "parents": ["205f690f4830606823f2d6a8927e5d99bbcb7aed"], "tags": []}, {"author": "rperta \u003crperta@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2048365 - MOZ_DIAGNOSTIC_ASSERT when calling the NimbusFeature API with an unsupported feature r=nimbus-reviewers,chumphreys\" for causing gtest failures related to gtest.NimbusTelemetryFixture\n\nThis reverts commit 3a069da85cf5b6073183b7a3ffab74d8e8f7abf1.\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/nimbus/generate/generate_feature_manifest.py", "toolkit/components/nimbus/lib/NimbusFeatureManifest.inc.h", "toolkit/components/nimbus/lib/NimbusFeatures.cpp", "toolkit/components/nimbus/lib/NimbusFeatures.h", "toolkit/components/nimbus/test/gtest/NimbusFeatures_GetTest.cpp", "toolkit/components/nimbus/test/gtest/NimbusFeatures_RecordExposure.cpp"], "git_node": "e4ee0947236a89b58b303deb4516daca94240328", "git_parents": ["59a7cfde7ac9277b2e19ba20340411a6fc2ed24c"], "node": "293aca64634c0f579bb39e40520025ccc91ddfbf", "parents": ["93626f0b4a699ca032a54df802e678e922d32611"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emily McMinn \u003cemcminn@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060283 - Basic layout and image positioning for FRO template r=omc-reviewers,mviar,emcminn\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317122\n", "files": ["browser/components/aboutwelcome/assets/backdrop-adaptive.svg", "browser/components/aboutwelcome/content/aboutwelcome.bundle.js", "browser/components/aboutwelcome/content/aboutwelcome.css", "browser/components/aboutwelcome/jar.mn", "browser/components/aboutwelcome/tests/browser/browser_aboutwelcome_configurable_ui.js", "browser/components/asrouter/content-src/components/MultiStageProtonScreen.jsx", "browser/components/asrouter/content-src/styles/_multistage.scss", "browser/components/asrouter/content/components/asrouter-newtab-multistage/asrouter-newtab-multistage.bundle.js", "browser/components/asrouter/content/components/asrouter-newtab-multistage/asrouter-newtab-multistage.css"], "git_node": "46200c6e7e095eb87dc205f9dc6721fef7e99e2f", "git_parents": ["e4ee0947236a89b58b303deb4516daca94240328"], "node": "0e228062e4cf030d7a07caa11aadfa6fd78ac081", "parents": ["293aca64634c0f579bb39e40520025ccc91ddfbf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jeremy Swinarton \u003cjswinarton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1980036 - Retry the hover in testTabAndTabGroupsWorkTogether if the preview is dismissed while opening r=tabbrowser-reviewers,sthompson\n\nA synthesized mouseover sets the hover target without moving the OS pointer.\ndisableNonTestMouseEvents drops most of the platform input that would\ncontradict that, but not all of it, and what remains resynchronises hover to\nwherever the pointer physically is. Showing the panel is enough to produce it.\n(Example:\nhttps://treeherder.mozilla.org/jobs?repo=try&author=jswinarton%40mozilla.com&selectedTaskRun=CmLH4JZ9QDWLKXIgdF6WOQ.0)\n\nTo be honest, I'm not sure what's really causing this at the platform\nlevel. My instinct is that the best way to actually solve this would be\nto use native mouse events in place of synthetic ones, but this seems\nlike a ton of work, and there are some tests that make use of hover\nstates that aren't possible using real mouse movement (for example\nhovering a tab that has a panel already positioned over the tab strip,\nwhich is done in the panelSuppression tests). So, for now, I decided to\nfudge it, by re-hovering the panel repeatedly if it gets closed before\nthe open completes. Maybe at a future date we can look at a full\nrefactor.\n\nI can also see from the links below that there are some other tests that\nseem to have to do similar things:\n\nhttps://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/source/browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/head.js#206-235\nhttps://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/source/toolkit/content/tests/browser/head.js#145-174\n\nSeems like extending and refactoring some of these helper methods might\nbe a good candidate for a follow-up bug.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317870\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser_tab_preview.js"], "git_node": "504e53877d9f09a76fd71b73b5632c126cfa30ce", "git_parents": ["46200c6e7e095eb87dc205f9dc6721fef7e99e2f"], "node": "b4ee45cddffae5f5475b67bdf998cd12f8555f56", "parents": ["0e228062e4cf030d7a07caa11aadfa6fd78ac081"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andy Leiserson \u003caleiserson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059002. r=webgpu-reviewers,ErichDonGubler\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318640\n", "files": ["dom/webgpu/Device.cpp", "dom/webgpu/Utility.cpp", "dom/webgpu/Utility.h", "dom/webgpu/ipc/WebGPUParent.cpp", "gfx/wgpu_bindings/src/client.rs", "gfx/wgpu_bindings/src/lib.rs", "gfx/wgpu_bindings/src/server.rs", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/webgpu/cts/webgpu/api/validation/capability_checks/features/texture_formats/cts.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/webgpu/cts/webgpu/api/validation/render_pipeline/fragment_state/cts.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/webgpu/cts/webgpu/shader/validation/decl/var/cts.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/webgpu/cts/webgpu/shader/validation/types/pointer/cts.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "b15b0a6382673b4f651297229c92f1b339c93662", "git_parents": ["504e53877d9f09a76fd71b73b5632c126cfa30ce"], "node": "5ddef4ea94c200f4568d5cca6156a5ecec3af881", "parents": ["b4ee45cddffae5f5475b67bdf998cd12f8555f56"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062140 - Don't hand a closing tab's hover to a tab the pointer isn't over, r=tabbrowser-reviewers,jswinarton.\n\ntab._hover records the last mouseover/mouseout the tab saw rather than where\nthe pointer is, and no mouseout is delivered during a drag session. Ask the\nevent state manager whether the pointer is still over the tab strip before\nhanding the hover over, and end a hover given without a pointer event from the\nnext mouse event if the event state manager hasn't agreed by then.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317401\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/Tabbrowser.sys.mjs", "browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tab.js"], "git_node": "0811b072b11882b842ff1cbccfb51dd403541320", "git_parents": ["b15b0a6382673b4f651297229c92f1b339c93662"], "node": "812fd39b201aa43ffa3b3d3673ccd6b48fefe68d", "parents": ["5ddef4ea94c200f4568d5cca6156a5ecec3af881"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Thomas Wisniewski \u003ctwisniewski@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1898935 - remove our UA override for mysunlife.sunlife.com.hk; r=ksenia,webcompat-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319254\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/webcompat/data/interventions/1898935-mysunlife.sunlife.com.hk.json", "browser/extensions/webcompat/manifest.json", "testing/webcompat/interventions/tests/test_1898935_mysunlife_sunlife_com_hk.py"], "git_node": "f4bd9c8c2256d909ed53543f8fa8409518230e77", "git_parents": ["0811b072b11882b842ff1cbccfb51dd403541320"], "node": "9750b9fc24ef9dacc19c0a1c1d9b9ccd9fae8c11", "parents": ["812fd39b201aa43ffa3b3d3673ccd6b48fefe68d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Thomas Wisniewski \u003ctwisniewski@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1902415 - update our webcompat intervention for kaigetsu.staysee.jp; r=ksenia,webcompat-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319255\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/webcompat/data/interventions/1902415-kaigetsu.staysee.jp.json", "browser/extensions/webcompat/preprocessed_intervention_files.mozbuild", "testing/webcompat/interventions/tests/test_1902415_kaigetsu_staysee_jp.py"], "git_node": "2de106bba6984de1c8be6aa53ba7f1c08851d3fc", "git_parents": ["f4bd9c8c2256d909ed53543f8fa8409518230e77"], "node": "6f009a46ec97ba4d10f95835b15477bde7bf0cfa", "parents": ["9750b9fc24ef9dacc19c0a1c1d9b9ccd9fae8c11"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Thomas Wisniewski \u003ctwisniewski@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1930440 - remove our webcompat intervention for online.singaporepools.com; r=ksenia,webcompat-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319256\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/webcompat/data/interventions/1930440-online.singaporepools.com.json", "browser/extensions/webcompat/preprocessed_intervention_files.mozbuild", "testing/webcompat/interventions/tests/test_1930440_singaporepools_com.py"], "git_node": "ebc7f845142d471933bbd6ac672b59369ddab4d0", "git_parents": ["2de106bba6984de1c8be6aa53ba7f1c08851d3fc"], "node": "00c3ab12765ca3eba0267fe35ffad47cdd2b5ad3", "parents": ["6f009a46ec97ba4d10f95835b15477bde7bf0cfa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Thomas Wisniewski \u003ctwisniewski@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2051501 - update our CSS webcompat intervention for community.acer.com; r=ksenia,webcompat-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319257\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/webcompat/data/interventions/2051501-community.acer.com.json", "testing/webcompat/interventions/tests/test_2051501_community_acer_com.py"], "git_node": "0ac58cad3df6bbe08acf965b1f00ae0657d75c08", "git_parents": ["ebc7f845142d471933bbd6ac672b59369ddab4d0"], "node": "e5c7497a3ed56da59c84e6577d5f17cbc9a92e80", "parents": ["00c3ab12765ca3eba0267fe35ffad47cdd2b5ad3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Thomas Wisniewski \u003ctwisniewski@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1800241 - remove our UA override for mms.telekom.de; r=ksenia,webcompat-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319258\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/webcompat/data/interventions/1743429-Sites_with_issues_with_Firefox_versions_over_99.json", "testing/webcompat/interventions/tests/test_1800241_mms_telekom_de.py"], "git_node": "1a5fa88fab22eb40ead40be88cdd080890901529", "git_parents": ["0ac58cad3df6bbe08acf965b1f00ae0657d75c08"], "node": "3f485398b48a5d1b5d2e1ac66211f8e173bfc1e1", "parents": ["e5c7497a3ed56da59c84e6577d5f17cbc9a92e80"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Thomas Wisniewski \u003ctwisniewski@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2008115 - remove our webcompat intervention for pge.com; r=ksenia,webcompat-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319259\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/webcompat/data/interventions/2008115-pge.com.json", "browser/extensions/webcompat/preprocessed_intervention_files.mozbuild", "testing/webcompat/interventions/tests/test_2008115_pge_com.py"], "git_node": "b002b677f0bcd9a65eba10f97377e27e1d0a9de6", "git_parents": ["1a5fa88fab22eb40ead40be88cdd080890901529"], "node": "a3d1a702992b4756b7aa1192c90811955aec52bc", "parents": ["3f485398b48a5d1b5d2e1ac66211f8e173bfc1e1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Thomas Wisniewski \u003ctwisniewski@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1941530 - remove our webcompat intervention for climate.rutgers.edu; r=ksenia,webcompat-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319260\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/webcompat/data/interventions/1941530-climate.rutgers.edu.json", "browser/extensions/webcompat/preprocessed_intervention_files.mozbuild", "testing/webcompat/interventions/tests/test_1941530_climate_rutgers_edu.py"], "git_node": "a3c96e5015b72733fa81ccc338432b62af12bb63", "git_parents": ["b002b677f0bcd9a65eba10f97377e27e1d0a9de6"], "node": "04e8fb9a1653a365b93c8409d58f6820ae573780", "parents": ["a3d1a702992b4756b7aa1192c90811955aec52bc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Thomas Wisniewski \u003ctwisniewski@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063633 - fix webcompat interventions automated tests; r=ksenia\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319261\n", "files": ["testing/webcompat/interventions/tests/test_1793761_schoolnutritionandfitness_com.py", "testing/webcompat/interventions/tests/test_1911253_qq_com.py", "testing/webcompat/interventions/tests/test_2009187_deadpixeltest_org.py", "testing/webcompat/interventions/tests/test_2042797_ftiunpam_com.py", "testing/webcompat/interventions/tests/test_2052837_bahn_de.py", "testing/webcompat/interventions/tests/test_2053077_jobs_abbott_com.py"], "git_node": "a07228e1d7b4b1ef35c55b142e5a489a398b20f5", "git_parents": ["a3c96e5015b72733fa81ccc338432b62af12bb63"], "node": "536b77d944a01aa8762cca7aa87ee96dc0f46d60", "parents": ["04e8fb9a1653a365b93c8409d58f6820ae573780"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lando \u003clando@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Merge mozilla-central to autoland\n", "files": [], "git_node": "9cc7a4de039994343e8fd94f4ce2a84f6eac0bc3", "git_parents": ["a07228e1d7b4b1ef35c55b142e5a489a398b20f5", "6fd3453f587cfcd74637bad0b7b67f3d4680e679"], "node": "a63f7125ff877572d3923cedb4dfd80cc497e278", "parents": ["536b77d944a01aa8762cca7aa87ee96dc0f46d60", "99db6c0ec8d03ff47fba0cb679ee2f759c53bc03"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064220 - Enable parallelism for Gradle Tooling API actions. r=android-reviewers,adhingra\n\nThis used to inherit from the org.gradle.parallel option automatically, but\nnow must be set separately as of Android Studio Quail 1.\nhttps://developer.android.com/studio/releases/past-releases/as-quail-1-release-notes#android_studio_quail_1_parallel_gradle_sync_execution_change\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319274\n", "files": ["gradle.properties", "mobile/android/android-components/gradle.properties", "mobile/android/fenix/gradle.properties", "mobile/android/focus-android/gradle.properties"], "git_node": "2a997fbcb125de59bfd59f35f1f533e41274053c", "git_parents": ["9cc7a4de039994343e8fd94f4ce2a84f6eac0bc3"], "node": "9b2b3d3d38c9c66975ebd86ce98018ce2cffa8bf", "parents": ["a63f7125ff877572d3923cedb4dfd80cc497e278"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062145 - Close the doorhangers and the account panel asrouter tests leave open, r=omc-reviewers,hanna_a.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317405\n", "files": ["browser/components/asrouter/tests/browser/browser_asrouter_toolbarbadge.js", "browser/components/asrouter/tests/browser/browser_trigger_messagesLoaded.js", "browser/components/asrouter/tests/browser/browser_trigger_nimbusUpdate.js", "browser/components/asrouter/tests/browser/head.js"], "git_node": "c8bed69fda044c7ba79ea0cfc182c209197771ba", "git_parents": ["2a997fbcb125de59bfd59f35f1f533e41274053c"], "node": "f9641bd2cb8a7076982018f266576524d26d1d10", "parents": ["9b2b3d3d38c9c66975ebd86ce98018ce2cffa8bf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jens Stutte \u003cjstutte@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062119 - Do not dereference gJarHandler after it has been cleared at shutdown. r=necko-reviewers,valentin\n\nnsJARChannel read the gJarHandler global directly in five places. Since bug\n1412726 that global is a StaticRefPtr cleared by ClearOnShutdown, so it can be\nnull while channels are still alive and opening a channel during late shutdown\ncrashes. The owning reference the channel takes in its constructor kept the\nhandler object alive but stopped protecting the global, and has had no readers\nsince that same bug.\n\nAdd shutdown safe accessors that return null once the singleton is gone, use\nthem for all of those accesses and fail the channel with\nNS_ERROR_ILLEGAL_DURING_SHUTDOWN instead. Drop the unused mJarHandler member.\n\nWhile here, EnsureCached can use the accessor instead of fetching the handler\nthrough the IO service and downcasting the result.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317420\n", "files": ["modules/libjar/nsJARChannel.cpp", "modules/libjar/nsJARChannel.h", "modules/libjar/nsJARProtocolHandler.cpp", "modules/libjar/nsJARProtocolHandler.h"], "git_node": "179ffe1f4a08bdaf801d4a2c9d903ac7898b0af7", "git_parents": ["c8bed69fda044c7ba79ea0cfc182c209197771ba"], "node": "b9f1178bfe27691afb91b278e1132105d7a13098", "parents": ["f9641bd2cb8a7076982018f266576524d26d1d10"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jens Stutte \u003cjstutte@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062119 - Clear the jar protocol handler after the JS module loader is gone. r=necko-reviewers,xpcom-reviewers,valentin,nika\n\nChrome JS module loading reads from omni.ja through jar channels, and\nmozJSModuleLoader::UnloadLoaders() runs after the XPCOMShutdownFinal phase,\nwhich is the default phase for ClearOnShutdown. The handler was therefore\ncleared while chrome JS modules could still be imported, leaving a window in\nwhich those imports and any other late jar access fail.\n\nClear it at CCPostLastCycleCollection instead, which runs after UnloadLoaders().\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317421\n", "files": ["modules/libjar/nsJAR.cpp", "modules/libjar/nsJARProtocolHandler.cpp"], "git_node": "838e0b20f403e9a5bff3e2449b051461bd23a7af", "git_parents": ["179ffe1f4a08bdaf801d4a2c9d903ac7898b0af7"], "node": "4d8543b2b14dea23b6ae2c6f9acc7716c306ebcc", "parents": ["b9f1178bfe27691afb91b278e1132105d7a13098"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Keith Cirkel \u003ckeithamus@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2018913 - Part 3: Refactor; rename Elem SetKeepCustomElementRegistryNull to SetNullCustomElementRegistry r=edgar\n\nNaming this method SetKeepCustomElementRegistryNull confuses it with the\n\"shadowroot keep custom element registry null\" flag, but a Null custom\nelement registry is a concrete capability for explicitly setting\n`customElements: null`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318679\n", "files": ["dom/base/Element.cpp", "dom/base/Element.h", "dom/base/nsContentUtils.cpp", "dom/base/nsINode.cpp", "dom/base/nsNameSpaceManager.cpp", "dom/xml/nsXMLContentSink.cpp", "parser/html/nsHtml5TreeOperation.cpp"], "git_node": "b92abf89abbfc2606c466c8d768449e1bf9a1e9b", "git_parents": ["838e0b20f403e9a5bff3e2449b051461bd23a7af"], "node": "d592b4493694438a44919041921719e239562685", "parents": ["4d8543b2b14dea23b6ae2c6f9acc7716c306ebcc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Bob Hood \u003cbhood@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063395 - Update ANGLE to 464fd3e879d6bb72fe8210b3e58b59836f711951 r=gfx-reviewers,ahale,ErichDonGubler\n\nRebase the local patch series from 9fa37b5e onto the new base revision.\n\nUpstream deleted the D3D9 backend, so drop patch 0001's renderer9_utils.cpp\nhunk and remove the now-nonexistent angle_enable_d3d9 GN arg.\n\nFour patches have landed upstream and are dropped from the series:\n  - D3D11: Avoid cache self-eviction for uniform buffers\n  - D3D11: Fix potential OOB read in StoreStaticAttrib\n  - use correct framebuffer var\n  - GL: Fix `invariant gl_FragColor;` + draw buffers\n\nAdd patch 0018 to guard the explicit context include in\negl_stubs_getprocaddress_autogen.cpp. Upstream made that #include\nunconditional while leaving its uses behind ANGLE_ENABLE_EXPLICIT_CONTEXT, which\nbreaks the build for any configuration with angle_enable_wgpu disabled.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318737\n", "files": ["gfx/angle/gn-configs/angle.json", "gfx/angle/moz.yaml", "gfx/angle/patches/0001-Restrict-the-slow-texture-upload-workaround-to-128bi.patch", "gfx/angle/patches/0002-Don-t-use-ClearView-if-we-previously-used-dual-sourc.patch", "gfx/angle/patches/0003-Don-t-assert-for-non-sampleable-non-ms-sources-in-bl.patch", "gfx/angle/patches/0004-build-linux-disable-PoolAlloc-to-work-around-asan-fa.patch", "gfx/angle/patches/0005-Import-cmath-in-SymbolTable_ESSL_autogen.cpp.patch", "gfx/angle/patches/0006-Disable-ClearView-with-scissor-on-Skylake-iGPU-becau.patch", "gfx/angle/patches/0007-Add-ShCompileOptions.initGLPointSize.patch", "gfx/angle/patches/0008-Add-GLSL-variable-byte-size-limits-to-ShBuiltInResou.patch", "gfx/angle/patches/0009-D3D11-Avoid-cache-self-eviction-for-uniform-buffers.patch", "gfx/angle/patches/0009-call-SafeDelete-only-if-onDestroy-has-not-errored.patch", "gfx/angle/patches/0010-D3D11-Fix-potential-OOB-read-in-StoreStaticAttrib.patch", "gfx/angle/patches/0010-eliminate-static_cast.patch", "gfx/angle/patches/0011-Revert-Translator-Do-not-validate-uniform-packing.patch", "gfx/angle/patches/0011-call-SafeDelete-only-if-onDestroy-has-not-errored.patch", "gfx/angle/patches/0012-Patch-build-scripts-for-Firefox-s-gn_processor.py.patch", "gfx/angle/patches/0012-use-correct-framebuffer-var.patch", "gfx/angle/patches/0013-Avoid-adding-disabled-backends-files-to-angle_code_a.patch", "gfx/angle/patches/0013-eliminate-static_cast.patch", "gfx/angle/patches/0014-Avoid-including-FunctionsCGL.cpp-h-unless-angle_enab.patch", "gfx/angle/patches/0014-GL-Fix-invariant-gl_FragColor-draw-buffers.patch", "gfx/angle/patches/0015-Restore-support-for-building-ANGLE-for-macOS-10.15.patch", "gfx/angle/patches/0015-Revert-Translator-Do-not-validate-uniform-packing.patc