ttps://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318832\n", "files": ["gfx/thebes/gfxFcPlatformFontList.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxFcPlatformFontList.h", "gfx/thebes/gfxFontEntry.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxFontEntry.h"], "git_node": "2590e54d443a574d6a0612b1de31762804377a98", "git_parents": ["f584debbe4c733f4b276a74683e4d284368d73c5"], "node": "6fd382a820bd1fe334997b8d4b1f49e8f897effd", "parents": ["d8a3ce8903920a1d84343e93cb34e844d81ac2e8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "unifolia \u003cjlewis@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056732 - automatically download smart tab grouping models for Auto Tab Grouping r=Mardak,tabbrowser-reviewers,niklas\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315309\n", "files": ["browser/app/profile/firefox.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/AIWindow.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/AutoTabGroupingSuggestions.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_group_tabs_button.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/SmartTabGrouping.sys.mjs", "testing/profiles/common/user.js"], "git_node": "f408c70154d57ed15aa870c908d4321f1cf07aaf", "git_parents": ["2590e54d443a574d6a0612b1de31762804377a98"], "node": "9364fd1dcbc0ba0ab5294a2d9a96091a3c859718", "parents": ["6fd382a820bd1fe334997b8d4b1f49e8f897effd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1901119 - Remove the checked-in .experimenter.yaml manifests from Fenix and Focus. r=beth\n\nExperimenter generates the feature manifest itself from the FML definitions now, so the copies checked in\nhere stopped being consumed when that changed. Nothing in the tree produces or checks them either: no task\nhas invoked `nimbus-fml generate-experimenter` since application-services commit 465af634f in October 2023,\nand the plugin setting that named the file, `experimenterManifest`, went away in bug 2061890.\n\nThat left them to be maintained by hand, which is what the Nimbus experiment doc asked contributors to do,\nso in practice they only changed when a feature was removed from the app. Delete both files along with the\ndocumentation step that asked for them.\n\nThis leaves `nimbus-fml`'s `generate-experimenter` command alone; it is still there, just with nothing\nin this repository calling it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318907\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/.experimenter.yaml", "mobile/android/fenix/docs/Implementing-a-Nimbus-Experiment.md", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/.experimenter.yaml"], "git_node": "a02f12c6f736736026e513b61a24df9f5f50c817", "git_parents": ["f408c70154d57ed15aa870c908d4321f1cf07aaf"], "node": "12e515d0f348202295c0b562cd9cbb42c7a0e833", "parents": ["9364fd1dcbc0ba0ab5294a2d9a96091a3c859718"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Elissa Cha \u003cecha@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062688 - Add resume prompt telemetry r=pdahiya\n\n- Added starter_type to quick_prompt_clicked and resume_prompts to quick_prompt_displayed\n- Moved the shared resume-pill test helpers to head.js so both test files can use them\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318736\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/metrics.yaml", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-window/ai-window.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_smartwindow_prompts.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_smartwindow_telemetry.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/head.js"], "git_node": "ff50105c16dda46d0714646d265cf490457c5039", "git_parents": ["a02f12c6f736736026e513b61a24df9f5f50c817"], "node": "219d3bba3d6eb0538c651c92bd1dbd9cbf73a3e4", "parents": ["12e515d0f348202295c0b562cd9cbb42c7a0e833"], "tags": []}, {"author": "rperta \u003crperta@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2060283 - Basic layout and image positioning for FRO template r=omc-reviewers,mviar,emcminn\" for causing bc failures at browser_all_files_referenced.js\n\nThis reverts commit 46200c6e7e095eb87dc205f9dc6721fef7e99e2f.\n", "files": ["browser/components/aboutwelcome/assets/backdrop-adaptive.svg", "browser/components/aboutwelcome/content/aboutwelcome.bundle.js", "browser/components/aboutwelcome/content/aboutwelcome.css", "browser/components/aboutwelcome/jar.mn", "browser/components/aboutwelcome/tests/browser/browser_aboutwelcome_configurable_ui.js", "browser/components/asrouter/content-src/components/MultiStageProtonScreen.jsx", "browser/components/asrouter/content-src/styles/_multistage.scss", "browser/components/asrouter/content/components/asrouter-newtab-multistage/asrouter-newtab-multistage.bundle.js", "browser/components/asrouter/content/components/asrouter-newtab-multistage/asrouter-newtab-multistage.css"], "git_node": "752db14263ae23453b0e1b237c5301502aea7b10", "git_parents": ["ff50105c16dda46d0714646d265cf490457c5039"], "node": "9e0135c0fc1b21ded098c25011031dcd28d258f0", "parents": ["219d3bba3d6eb0538c651c92bd1dbd9cbf73a3e4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "rperta \u003crperta@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2062119 - Clear the jar protocol handler after the JS module loader is gone. r=necko-reviewers,xpcom-reviewers,valentin,nika\" for causing build bustages at nsJARProtocolHandler.cpp\n\nThis reverts commit 838e0b20f403e9a5bff3e2449b051461bd23a7af.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2062119 - Do not dereference gJarHandler after it has been cleared at shutdown. r=necko-reviewers,valentin\"\n\nThis reverts commit 179ffe1f4a08bdaf801d4a2c9d903ac7898b0af7.\n", "files": ["modules/libjar/nsJAR.cpp", "modules/libjar/nsJARChannel.cpp", "modules/libjar/nsJARChannel.h", "modules/libjar/nsJARProtocolHandler.cpp", "modules/libjar/nsJARProtocolHandler.h"], "git_node": "416d6aad0511fb060470d521621b08589f2312ec", "git_parents": ["752db14263ae23453b0e1b237c5301502aea7b10"], "node": "109b49e056deb08e1e1d1701ed75812eba996e6a", "parents": ["9e0135c0fc1b21ded098c25011031dcd28d258f0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ben Visness \u003cbvisness@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064198: Use release asserts in MIR/LIR casts. r=spidermonkey-reviewers,mgaudet\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319253\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/LIR.h", "js/src/jit/MIR.h"], "git_node": "bfae3abb1dab1cecf2b035d0aac13a8b6c2601fa", "git_parents": ["416d6aad0511fb060470d521621b08589f2312ec"], "node": "59d974d9cbb496761cac2abd2054f1b2a4b88a2d", "parents": ["109b49e056deb08e1e1d1701ed75812eba996e6a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1993981 - Store ControlMessages as runnables. r=karlt\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D277173\n", "files": ["dom/media/MediaTrackGraph.cpp", "dom/media/MediaTrackGraph.h", "dom/media/MediaTrackGraphImpl.h"], "git_node": "00188974771053ee0b069f76d28e68a454ca72e9", "git_parents": ["bfae3abb1dab1cecf2b035d0aac13a8b6c2601fa"], "node": "0074d8c37b03a7a142ae93a606dd4592d855c333", "parents": ["59d974d9cbb496761cac2abd2054f1b2a4b88a2d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1993981 - Implement nsIDirectTaskDispatcher for MediaTrackGraphImpl. r=karlt\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D277174\n", "files": ["dom/media/MediaTrackGraph.cpp", "dom/media/MediaTrackGraphImpl.h"], "git_node": "73bbfc2af3db17a3c2026ae0c0bb96896fbf5764", "git_parents": ["00188974771053ee0b069f76d28e68a454ca72e9"], "node": "07992a96a786316d6dab423bbdb8f32042f368be", "parents": ["0074d8c37b03a7a142ae93a606dd4592d855c333"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1993981 - Allow canceling cancelable and discardable tail-dispatched runnables. r=xpcom-reviewers,nika\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D277175\n", "files": ["xpcom/threads/TaskDispatcher.h"], "git_node": "b6c1a23845f4aea5d0b7f355b96eff91f5ed55db", "git_parents": ["73bbfc2af3db17a3c2026ae0c0bb96896fbf5764"], "node": "057cda252e8bcdd04d15adf32cdf5fd54a9f199d", "parents": ["07992a96a786316d6dab423bbdb8f32042f368be"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1993981 - Rename MediaTrackGraphImpl::Dispatch to DispatchToMainThread to avoid naming conflicts with nsISerialEventTarget. r=karlt\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D301275\n", "files": ["dom/media/MediaTrackGraph.cpp", "dom/media/MediaTrackGraphImpl.h", "dom/media/gtest/TestAudioTrackGraph.cpp"], "git_node": "b104d50d22f057c9abfc83c8dbbe9af9d219487b", "git_parents": ["b6c1a23845f4aea5d0b7f355b96eff91f5ed55db"], "node": "7668d22f06ad5af8657fc4effc872593838efee1", "parents": ["057cda252e8bcdd04d15adf32cdf5fd54a9f199d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1993981 - Implement AbstractThread for MediaTrackGraphImpl. r=karlt\n\nThis patch makes MediaTrackGraphImpl implement AbstractThread and its base\ninterface nsISerialEventTarget.\n\nThis allows running nsIRunnables natively on the graph.\n\nTo facilitate runnables that need to run during graph shutdown, the graph will\ncall OnDiscard() on those runnables that QI to nsIDiscardableRunnable and they\nmay run then. Note that runnables dispatched through the nsISerialEventTarget\nand AbstractThread APIs (i.e. Dispatch()) will wrap runnables that don't\nimplement nsIDiscardableRunnable so they run on shutdown by default. This should\navoid silently dropping async tasks from e.g. MozPromise that require settling\nbefore being released.\nDuring shutdown, nsIRunnable's Run() will not be called directly by the graph,\nand all runnables will be processed (OnDiscard() and release) on the main\nthread to guarantee event order consistency.\n\nMessageBlocks are removed, as the graph no longer will manage the batching of\ntasks dispatched from main thread. The main thread's tail dispatcher will manage\nbatching instead, and dispatched per-thread group runnables will enter\nmBackMessageQueue regularly. The same mechanism now works from any thread. Only\nmain thread dispatches affect the graph's lifecycle, however.\n\nFor a non-main thread to dispatch tasks to the graph, it will have to be sure to\nkeep the graph alive. The only guarantee for this is still to hold onto a live\ntrack.\n\nAny thread that is used to dispatch a task to the graph must support tail\ndispatch. While not strictly required for the function of the graph, this\nenforces the old mechanism of running messages from main thread atomically, and\nspreads that behavior to any other thread. It also reduces contention on the\ngraph's Monitor.\n\nDispatching from the graph to any other thread should also use tail dispatch for\nperformance reasons -- e.g dispatching to the busy main thread may suffer from\nlock contention which is not ideal on the real-time audio thread. However,\nenforcing tail dispatch when dispatching *from* the graph thread is not possible\nwithout going through a proxy function. This is by convention for now.\n\nTail dispatch from the graph to the main thread means that the main thread state\nis updated before graph thread to main thread runnables run.\n\nThis requires some child revisions or it may render issues:\n- D277177: to allow non-tail dispatched messages to the graph from the\n           IPC I/O Child for AudioWorklet MessagePorts.\n- D277181: to maintain atomicity between all messages dispatched from a single\n           task on a given thread, as AbstractThread normally closes a target\n           group runnable for new tasks upon tail dispatch to another target.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D277176\n", "files": ["dom/media/MediaTrackGraph.cpp", "dom/media/MediaTrackGraph.h", "dom/media/MediaTrackGraphImpl.h", "dom/media/gtest/TestAudioCallbackDriver.cpp", "dom/media/gtest/TestAudioDecoderInputTrack.cpp", "dom/media/gtest/TestAudioTrackGraph.cpp", "dom/media/gtest/TestDecodedStream.cpp", "dom/media/gtest/TestDeviceInputTrack.cpp", "xpcom/threads/AbstractThread.h"], "git_node": "4cdd700b6db0e15dfef7bb54bd3c95ce0c96fcc6", "git_parents": ["b104d50d22f057c9abfc83c8dbbe9af9d219487b"], "node": "e7ad1bf729312c4017c98f7cf94f5f1940a3f585", "parents": ["7668d22f06ad5af8657fc4effc872593838efee1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1993981 - In MediaTrackGraphImpl natively support AudioWorklet's message passing. r=karlt\n\nThis patch does two things to support AudioWorklet:\n- Supports target shutdown tasks.\n- Exempts the IPC I/O Child thread from the tail dispatch requirement.\n\nThe IPC I/O Child thread does not support tail dispatch, and there are no\nordering requirements between those messages and any from other threads.\n\nPrior to D277176, these messages went through GraphRunner::mThread. It was\ngiven to the MessageChannel opened in the AudioWorklet through\nGetCurrentSerialEventTarget().\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D277177\n", "files": ["dom/media/MediaTrackGraph.cpp", "dom/media/MediaTrackGraphImpl.h"], "git_node": "e85a4933447c6fcae67baf0bcd0673ef5b4b31ad", "git_parents": ["4cdd700b6db0e15dfef7bb54bd3c95ce0c96fcc6"], "node": "1b7fbc53f0e057251a81a195f751f4312c455d9e", "parents": ["e7ad1bf729312c4017c98f7cf94f5f1940a3f585"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1993981 - To MockProcessedMediaTrack add mocks for {Add|Remove}ListenerImpl. r=karlt\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D277178\n", "files": ["dom/media/gtest/TestAudioTrackGraph.cpp"], "git_node": "926ffa5b4954d4f336da45d06bd41b62e96d67f0", "git_parents": ["e85a4933447c6fcae67baf0bcd0673ef5b4b31ad"], "node": "af7418e64820131567f7d04472d997b966744fb3", "parents": ["1b7fbc53f0e057251a81a195f751f4312c455d9e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1993981 - Unit test event ordering between the graph and main thread. r=karlt\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D277179\n", "files": ["dom/media/gtest/TestAudioTrackGraph.cpp"], "git_node": "534803c0da0f859187f8de99c33c493930f1fa8b", "git_parents": ["926ffa5b4954d4f336da45d06bd41b62e96d67f0"], "node": "7aaca6bbf089b2b8314360aee6b345c9cd837ea4", "parents": ["af7418e64820131567f7d04472d997b966744fb3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1993981 - Unit test message atomicity. r=karlt\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D277180\n", "files": ["dom/media/gtest/TestAudioTrackGraph.cpp"], "git_node": "d8fe367d2f2f5a0822e2a7683a48da85403e01da", "git_parents": ["534803c0da0f859187f8de99c33c493930f1fa8b"], "node": "16047aca2a0b4bf4c08bc133507abe6e73e63835", "parents": ["7aaca6bbf089b2b8314360aee6b345c9cd837ea4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1993981 - Introduce an atomicity policy for tail dispatch. r=karlt,xpcom-reviewers,nika,webrtc-reviewers,bwc,media-playback-reviewers\n\nFor MediaTrackGraph to be able to switch its manual batching of control\nmessages to tail dispatch, the message atomicity guarantee it provides needs to\nbe retained. This patch introduces an atomicity mode for tail dispatch to\nsupport the graph.\n\nTo tidy up the AbstractThread API, the old boolean aSupportsTailDispatch flag\npassed at construction is changed to a new TailDispatchPolicy enum. Converting\ncallers which passed that flag is the bulk of the change.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D277181\n", "files": ["dom/media/MediaDecoderStateMachineBase.cpp", "dom/media/MediaFormatReader.cpp", "dom/media/MediaManager.cpp", "dom/media/MediaTrackGraph.cpp", "dom/media/gtest/TestAudioTrackGraph.cpp", "dom/media/gtest/TestWebrtcTaskQueueWrapper.cpp", "dom/media/hls/HLSDemuxer.cpp", "dom/media/webcodecs/WebCodecsUtils.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/PeerConnectionCtx.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/libwebrtcglue/VideoConduit.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/libwebrtcglue/WebrtcTaskQueueWrapper.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/libwebrtcglue/WebrtcTaskQueueWrapper.h", "media/webrtc/signaling/gtest/mediapipeline_unittest.cpp", "xpcom/tests/gtest/TestAutoOwningEventTarget.cpp", "xpcom/tests/gtest/TestDelayedRunnable.cpp", "xpcom/tests/gtest/TestStateMirroring.cpp", "xpcom/tests/gtest/TestTargetShutdownTask.cpp", "xpcom/tests/gtest/TestTaskQueue.cpp", "xpcom/threads/AbstractThread.cpp", "xpcom/threads/AbstractThread.h", "xpcom/threads/TaskDispatcher.h", "xpcom/threads/TaskQueue.cpp", "xpcom/threads/TaskQueue.h"], "git_node": "4bfa0a6de22b598569a60f5e412d73b930542514", "git_parents": ["d8fe367d2f2f5a0822e2a7683a48da85403e01da"], "node": "b6637fb5585996026ce4baa2adc5b28de58462ff", "parents": ["16047aca2a0b4bf4c08bc133507abe6e73e63835"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1993981 - Unit test graph shutdown message ordering. r=karlt\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D288112\n", "files": ["dom/media/gtest/TestAudioTrackGraph.cpp"], "git_node": "a9e6367bff123ce970325af379707076d843e6d5", "git_parents": ["4bfa0a6de22b598569a60f5e412d73b930542514"], "node": "6b7d59a2dc946700d566ac20394d38c3475c70c8", "parents": ["b6637fb5585996026ce4baa2adc5b28de58462ff"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1993981 - Rename MediaTrackGraphImpl::LifecycleStateRef() -\u003e LifecycleState() and return state by value. r=karlt\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D305600\n", "files": ["dom/media/MediaTrackGraph.cpp", "dom/media/MediaTrackGraphImpl.h", "dom/media/gtest/TestDecodedStream.cpp"], "git_node": "62b91c19bd49eb052a81969e10a95e96a552b3ed", "git_parents": ["a9e6367bff123ce970325af379707076d843e6d5"], "node": "81f70526e4dc7f04a03fd42a52c392ac1f79ee3c", "parents": ["6b7d59a2dc946700d566ac20394d38c3475c70c8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrea Marchesini \u003camarchesini@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063048 - introduce a checkbox to manage external URLs and Container tabs r=tgiles,fluent-reviewers,bolsson\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318754\n", "files": ["browser/components/preferences/config/containers.mjs", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/preferences/preferences.ftl"], "git_node": "b93fa90006535b8a7465a2b3d2216d120c7abb74", "git_parents": ["62b91c19bd49eb052a81969e10a95e96a552b3ed"], "node": "6ce9082d5a250b794b2fa78a92d58c0a7452b82e", "parents": ["81f70526e4dc7f04a03fd42a52c392ac1f79ee3c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mark Striemer \u003cmstriemer@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056688 - Part 1: Support importing a subset of Figma tokens r=desktop-theme-reviewers,tgiles\n\nThis provides a way to import only some tokens from Figma, either\nthrough the `--match` flag (substring match) or by editing a list of\ntokens that would be imported (default). You can import all tokens by\npassing `--all`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313728\n", "files": ["toolkit/content/widgets/mach_commands.py", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/src/fetch-figma-variables.mjs", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/src/figma-import.mjs", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/src/figma-variables-all.json"], "git_node": "15e5c3eeb3407b2234c987e21b8cbae8c8490bc9", "git_parents": ["b93fa90006535b8a7465a2b3d2216d120c7abb74"], "node": "dd5cd541e60ae316bc6d062b722a4bd531bfe722", "parents": ["6ce9082d5a250b794b2fa78a92d58c0a7452b82e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mark Striemer \u003cmstriemer@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056688 - Part 2: Add support for importing from the Figma cache r=desktop-theme-reviewers,tgiles\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318793\n", "files": ["toolkit/content/widgets/mach_commands.py", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/package.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/src/fetch-figma-variables.mjs", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/src/import-figma-variables.mjs"], "git_node": "5e1e27d2d4cf6f8a1fcb82edd2e00b9cfe6e3ae5", "git_parents": ["15e5c3eeb3407b2234c987e21b8cbae8c8490bc9"], "node": "f965e98acc658802268bf65a7e6d05e6430d290c", "parents": ["dd5cd541e60ae316bc6d062b722a4bd531bfe722"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daniel Holbert \u003cdholbert@cs.stanford.edu\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064177: Remove recently-added viewBox attrs from outer SVG element in SVG assets, so we can benefit from the automatically synthesized one (and get preserveAspectRatio=\"none\" for free). r=sfoster,desktop-theme-reviewers\n\nThis viewBox attribute was unnecessary and slightly counterproductive, so\nit's nicer to just remove it.\n\nThe explicit viewBox was unnecessary because Gecko will automatically\nsynthesize an appropriate viewBox (if the attribute is missing) on the\noutermost SVG element in an SVG image, using the SVG element's declared 'width'\nand 'height' attributes.  So, it's nice for conciseness to benefit from this\nand avoid needing to manually repeat the width and height in two spots on the\nsame element.\n\nThe explicit viewBox was counter-productive because: if we omit it and instead\nallow Gecko to synthesize a viewBox, Gecko will also automatically apply\npreserveAspectRatio=\"none\" *by default*, which is essentially always the\nbehavior we really want our SVG assets to have. On the other hand, if a viewBox\nis explicitly provided on the outermost SVG element, then Gecko uses the SVG\nspec's default `preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid\"` behavior, which is essentially\na \"contain\" constraint and can cause subly unexpected positioning glitches like\nhttps://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2063751 in cases where slight\npixel-rounding issues can cause the aspect ratio to be ever-so-slightly off\nfrom the image's natural aspect ratio.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319252\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/downloads/notification-finish-animation.svg", "browser/themes/shared/downloads/notification-start-animation.svg", "browser/themes/shared/downloads/progress-ring-20.svg", "browser/themes/shared/icons/success-animation.svg"], "git_node": "393b667091620e84f09929f32c0f6c299d3f7dfd", "git_parents": ["5e1e27d2d4cf6f8a1fcb82edd2e00b9cfe6e3ae5"], "node": "a1a22b0464d2ddfcfe0375c26a3a8f72b2ad2b49", "parents": ["f965e98acc658802268bf65a7e6d05e6430d290c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "kpatenio \u003ckpatenio@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058570 \u2014 flush tab state for browser_should_restore_tab.js to address intermittent failures. r=sfoster\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318868\n", "files": ["browser/components/sessionstore/test/browser_should_restore_tab.js"], "git_node": "01fd74bd119ff3ff19e71bfca93d215b2886d62a", "git_parents": ["393b667091620e84f09929f32c0f6c299d3f7dfd"], "node": "fe8e322c5feb491f5287ad956a1945914a368714", "parents": ["a1a22b0464d2ddfcfe0375c26a3a8f72b2ad2b49"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Timothy Nikkel \u003ctnikkel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063409. Update libyuv to 1dac06e8c0442c466b431935a2e385ea07796689. r=chunmin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318876\n", "files": ["media/libyuv/libyuv/GEMINI.md", "media/libyuv/libyuv/README.chromium", "media/libyuv/libyuv/include/libyuv/convert_from_argb.h", "media/libyuv/libyuv/include/libyuv/cpu_support.h"