ml.ini"], "git_node": "1821c64db6430763e999d05b587f1e017c60a83a", "git_parents": ["2ff0e4e8ba89b3b0ce225011104b09c452346a73"], "node": "8addf675971bc41561cf8a6d7d928e4a37ec77a8", "parents": ["55af195a632a2d876917431faf8e73b65a62b741"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Christensen \u003cachristensen@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056409 [wpt PR 61428] - [WebTransport] Correctly test use of WebTransportOptions.datagramsReadableType, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[WebTransport] Correctly test use of WebTransportOptions.datagramsReadableType (#61428)\n\nhttps://www.w3.org/TR/webtransport/#dom-webtransportoptions-datagramsreadabletype\nsays to use a readable byte stream if datagramsReadableType is specified, but to\nuse a readable stream otherwise.  https://streams.spec.whatwg.org/#readable-byte-stream\nsays the former is needed to use byob buffers.\n\nThis change is from https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/pull/69795\n--\n\nwpt-commits: bc3fbed2de38813160e1aa12078dab7e2813835a\nwpt-pr: 61428\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webtransport/datagrams.https.any.js"], "git_node": "f747a0e19756031b5f5206eeb1990d0057d6bafc", "git_parents": ["1821c64db6430763e999d05b587f1e017c60a83a"], "node": "648038f29081a3fd7e6566f230934bb3e537f500", "parents": ["8addf675971bc41561cf8a6d7d928e4a37ec77a8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062843 [wpt PR 61872] - Make new-scroll-event-dispatched-at-next-updating-rendering-time.html easier to reason about., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nMake new-scroll-event-dispatched-at-next-updating-rendering-time.html easier to reason about. (#61872)\n\nThis removes microtask checkpoints from the equation and makes it\nclearer that chrome is just borked here.\n\nThe test keeps passing in Firefox and Safari. Also added more spec\nreferences.\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 63a6569beb0656f3dd80db7bbfefb048087904ae\nwpt-pr: 61872\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/webappapis/scripting/event-loops/new-scroll-event-dispatched-at-next-updating-rendering-time.html"], "git_node": "acde32ecc17ca6244d6abd5d7063cccc893f1f25", "git_parents": ["f747a0e19756031b5f5206eeb1990d0057d6bafc"], "node": "f1bdfcb8c881442d57e0b2f0743f5944bee626d9", "parents": ["648038f29081a3fd7e6566f230934bb3e537f500"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Blink WPT Bot \u003cblink-w3c-test-autoroller@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063137 [wpt PR 61890] - [highlights] Preserve insertion order when setting an existing name, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[highlights] Preserve insertion order when setting an existing name (#61890)\n\nHighlightRegistry is a maplike\u003cDOMString, Highlight\u003e, so setForBinding()\nmust follow Map.prototype.set semantics: when the name is already in the\nregistry, the value is replaced and the order of entries is not affected\n(ECMA-262 24.1.3.9).\n\nInstead, HighlightRegistry::SetForTesting() erased the existing entry\nand inserted a new one, which moved it to the end of the\nHeapLinkedHashSet and therefore to the end of the iteration order. Two\nconsequences:\n\n - CSS.highlights.keys()/values()/entries() reported the wrong order\n   after overwriting an existing name.\n - Overwriting the name an iterator is currently pointing at moved that\n   entry behind the cursor, so the iteration restarted and never\n   terminated.\n\nUpdate the existing entry in place instead. The registration position is\nstill bumped, so the highlight keeps stacking above previously\nregistered ones (highlights are stacked with\nCompareOverlayStackingPosition(), which reads registration_position and\nnot the position in the set), and painting behavior is unchanged.\nNotifying the iterators is no longer needed because nothing is removed:\nthey keep pointing at the same entry.\n\nBug: 544197475\nChange-Id: I79b44f4c39b86a658e6e26b86c8e5c94b2cdff6b\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8227847\nAuto-Submit: Fernando Fiori \u003cffiori@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Jacques Newman \u003cjanewman@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Fernando Fiori \u003cffiori@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Fernando Fiori \u003cffiori@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1678209}\n\nCo-authored-by: Fernando Fiori \u003cffiori@microsoft.com\u003e\n--\n\nwpt-commits: c4b802e6dc22f7601177c887209c8d729212d4bb\nwpt-pr: 61890\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-highlight-api/HighlightRegistry-iteration-with-modifications.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-highlight-api/HighlightRegistry-maplike.html"], "git_node": "7242be1d6af380b8276b885402188445db73c476", "git_parents": ["acde32ecc17ca6244d6abd5d7063cccc893f1f25"], "node": "833e64ad2ecf2e10513ae75dd4239a99254e7e49", "parents": ["f1bdfcb8c881442d57e0b2f0743f5944bee626d9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tommi \u003ctommi@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058131 [wpt PR 61544] - Fix rtp sender max bitrate, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFix rtp sender max bitrate\n\nReject maxBitrate = 0 in setParameters and addTransceiver.\n\nBug: 501881082, 501879826\nChange-Id: Ia2f70e2c561deff3ad00595a31089078f8417250\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8148539\nReviewed-by: Guido Urdaneta \u003cguidou@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1668537}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 4e92c71c9333f095fc487d868d56111c75847876\nwpt-pr: 61544\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webrtc/RTCPeerConnection-addTransceiver.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webrtc/RTCRtpSender-setParameters.html"], "git_node": "2208c559c52718ff8d31f17f027956fc2cf5c87d", "git_parents": ["7242be1d6af380b8276b885402188445db73c476"], "node": "5bf5e9935fa425184f428cefa1910b991bb74f71", "parents": ["833e64ad2ecf2e10513ae75dd4239a99254e7e49"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dominic Farolino \u003cdom@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063328 [wpt PR 61915] - WebMCP: Thread execution AbortSignal to tool implementation, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebMCP: Thread execution AbortSignal to tool implementation\n\nThis CL implements abortable WebMCP tools, by introducing a\n`ToolExecuteCallbackOptions` dictionary that is always passed to the\ntool execution callback, and always has an `AbortSignal` that the tool\ncan use to learn when its tool execution was cancelled.\n\nBacking the `AbortSignal` that's exposed to the tool's implementation,\nis an internal `AbortController`, and a few IPCs. The flow of aborting\na tool looks like so:\n\n 1. The caller passes an `AbortSignal` to `executeTool()`.\n     - This creates an invocation ID in the caller's renderer, and hands\n       it to the browser for storage in the pending executions map.\n       (This all happens before this CL.)\n 2. The tool owner's `ModelContext` document creates a new\n    `AbortController` associated with the pending execution ID, and\n    passes its signal into the tool execution callback.\n 3. Mid-execution, the caller aborts the execution signal.\n 4. This sends the `CancelRemoteScriptTool()` IPC, which requests\n    cancellation from `ModelContextUserData`.\n 5. This, and the page user data, send the `CancelScriptTool()` IPC to\n    the owner of the tool.\n 6. This enters a refactored `ModelContext::CancelTool()` which handles\n    imperative and declarative tool execution, as well as lifetime edge\n    pertaining to tool resolution and unregistration. For declarative\n    tools, this just involves invoking the `done_callback_` with the\n    `ScriptToolErrorCode::kToolCancelled` code. This flow automatically\n    cleans up the pending execution data, leaving nothing else to do.\n 7. Finally, the tool owner's `ModelContext` object looks up the\n   `AbortController` associated with the soon-cancelled execution, and\n    aborts it. For imperative tools, this signals to JavaScript that the\n    tool has been aborted.\n\nBrowser-side changes: The browser-side changes handle routing\ncancellation IPCs, tracking target document lifetime, and managing\nrenderer races:\n - Target document tracking: `PendingScriptToolExecution` now tracks a\n   `WeakDocumentPtr target_document` alongside document tokens, allowing\n   the browser to send `CancelScriptTool()` IPCs to the target tool\n   owner's renderer. This is to avoid having to look up the\n   target document from its token.\n - Handles renderer races where, when the browser receives a\n   cancellation request, the execution has already completed, or the\n   tool was already unregistered, or the target document was destroyed.\n - Cancellation on document teardown\n   (`CancelPendingScriptToolExecutionsForDocument()`):\n     - When a document that is the caller of a tool is destroyed, the\n       browser forwards a `CancelScriptTool()` IPC to the tool owner.\n     - If the destructing document owns the tool itself, we can't send\n       this IPC, since the RFHI's `ModelContextUserData` has already\n       been cleared. This is fine regardless, since the document is\n       being destroyed anyways.\n\nBefore this CL, there was a quirk that unregistration of a tool would\ncancel pending in-flight executions of that tool, thus rejecting the\ncaller's Promise. The tool would keep running however, because there was\nno AbortSignal to let the tool know to stop running.\n\nAfter this CL, we have the AbortSignal, but we do NOT abort it in this\ncase. This is because a follow-up CL will fix this quirk altogether, and\nNOT cancel pending executions of tools that get unregistered. This will\nresolve https://github.com/webmachinelearning/webmcp/issues/218.\n\nBug: 481899636\nChange-Id: I4971bb726e0dcf29e378d5d0bdae5f0e559aee94\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8025300\nReviewed-by: Alex Moshchuk \u003calexmos@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Khushal Sagar \u003ckhushalsagar@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Dominic Farolino \u003cdom@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Fr \u003cbeaufort.francois@gmail.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1678855}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 55052f031b17699803f0a9c3bc6a4ef162f15feb\nwpt-pr: 61915\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/declarative/executeTool-abort.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/imperative/cancel-reentrancy-crash.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/imperative/executeTool-abort.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/imperative/executeTool-same-document-navigation-crash.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/imperative/executeTool-signal-cross-origin.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/imperative/executeTool-unregister-resolution-race.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/imperative/resources/iframe-caller-and-target-crash.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/imperative/resources/iframe-caller.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/imperative/resources/iframe-register-tool.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/imperative/unregister-during-executeTool.https.html"], "git_node": "917208357328f6f6702f093ed934550303b46608", "git_parents": ["2208c559c52718ff8d31f17f027956fc2cf5c87d"], "node": "cfcae8311208aedbbbf18fc559ccdffc8a4b5a58", "parents": ["5bf5e9935fa425184f428cefa1910b991bb74f71"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063328 [wpt PR 61915] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61915\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webmcp/declarative/executeTool-abort.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webmcp/imperative/executeTool-abort.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webmcp/imperative/executeTool-signal-cross-origin.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webmcp/imperative/executeTool-unregister-resolution-race.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webmcp/imperative/unregister-during-executeTool.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "409582b053ef57a03320a640f12a6e2cce51b5c8", "git_parents": ["917208357328f6f6702f093ed934550303b46608"], "node": "12684f39edfbc9138d6b5644d5517ff141894790", "parents": ["cfcae8311208aedbbbf18fc559ccdffc8a4b5a58"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Blink WPT Bot \u003cblink-w3c-test-autoroller@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1728644 [wpt PR 30288] - Reland \"Fix test picture generation and add test.\", a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nReland \"Fix test picture generation and add test.\" (#30288)\n\nThis reverts commit 0faf3c11ea6a46cb28afa937064341191da3baec.\n\nReason for revert: Resurrected - added waiting for first stats.\n\nOriginal change's description:\n\u003e Revert \"Fix test picture generation and add test.\"\n\u003e\n\u003e This reverts commit 84222e05b7a97c034e40d2d118de4aac05a94c50.\n\u003e\n\u003e Reason for revert: caused test to fail external/wpt/webrtc/RTCPeerConnection-helper-test.html, ex build: https://ci.chromium.org/p/chromium/builders/ci/Mac10.15%20Tests\n\u003e\n\u003e Bug: 1245692\n\u003e Original change's description:\n\u003e \u003e Fix test picture generation and add test.\n\u003e \u003e\n\u003e \u003e This CL changes the test picture from a growing box to a small moving\n\u003e \u003e box. It adds a test that the expected bandwidth target is achieved at\n\u003e \u003e the expected resolution.\n\u003e \u003e\n\u003e \u003e In a browser, 640x480 is not reached within 5 seconds. This is odd.\n\u003e \u003e\n\u003e \u003e Bug: None.\n\u003e \u003e Change-Id: I2d94f1c190c26cec6759ecc0f788feea8e52ed7c\n\u003e \u003e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/3135833\n\u003e \u003e Commit-Queue: Harald Alvestrand \u003chta@chromium.org\u003e\n\u003e \u003e Reviewed-by: Florent Castelli \u003corphis@chromium.org\u003e\n\u003e \u003e Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#917211}\n\u003e\n\u003e Bug: None.\n\u003e Change-Id: I205c46cca2245f3f906d52cca87ad878b486ee82\n\u003e No-Presubmit: true\n\u003e No-Tree-Checks: true\n\u003e No-Try: true\n\u003e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/3137553\n\u003e Bot-Commit: Rubber Stamper \u003crubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n\u003e Reviewed-by: Kevin Marshall \u003ckmarshall@chromium.org\u003e\n\u003e Reviewed-by: Harald Alvestrand \u003chta@chromium.org\u003e\n\u003e Commit-Queue: Harald Alvestrand \u003chta@chromium.org\u003e\n\u003e Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#917317}\n\nBug: 1245692\nBug: None.\nChange-Id: If47e55d8b4d0c483a1fdfafa0793ac44fcb009e9\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/3137713\nReviewed-by: Guido Urdaneta \u003cguidou@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Harald Alvestrand \u003chta@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1650302}\n\nCo-authored-by: Harald Alvestrand \u003chta@chromium.org\u003e\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 4ee236a6823ec3726aece398fc12d7c421f901bf\nwpt-pr: 30288\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webrtc/RTCPeerConnection-helper-test.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webrtc/RTCPeerConnection-helper.js"], "git_node": "41bd770e7877a24b76bfb8a4a6d808033ea5b43c", "git_parents": ["409582b053ef57a03320a640f12a6e2cce51b5c8"], "node": "ac1c5d37361e5f2cc23757dfd7146cb3b7fbba94", "parents": ["12684f39edfbc9138d6b5644d5517ff141894790"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1728644 [wpt PR 30288] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 30288\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webrtc/RTCDataChannel-close.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webrtc/RTCPeerConnection-helper-test.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webrtc/RTCRtpReceiver-video-jitterBufferTarget-stats.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webrtc/RTCRtpTransceiver-setCodecPreferences.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webrtc/protocol/additional-codecs.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webrtc/protocol/codecs-subsequent-offer.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webrtc/protocol/rtp-demuxing.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webrtc/protocol/video-codecs.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webrtc/simulcast/h264.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "f364c27d2c1f1df403a7c3931c6904dff5c432d6", "git_parents": ["41bd770e7877a24b76bfb8a4a6d808033ea5b43c"], "node": "18985ae0c46bf8c38b42de5af8ba70132e30c04a", "parents": ["ac1c5d37361e5f2cc23757dfd7146cb3b7fbba94"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sam Weinig \u003csam@webkit.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063378 [wpt PR 61918] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=318632, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=318632 (#61918)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 23203b32059bed7af9f351003a31da54b0e7e91c\nwpt-pr: 61918\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/intersection-observer/root-margin-scroll-margin-units.html"], "git_node": "e64bf32498634f4d853ed98227f46a1659abb8b4", "git_parents": ["f364c27d2c1f1df403a7c3931c6904dff5c432d6"], "node": "24ca770803b5f5357ce529a2953c3142fcf59199", "parents": ["18985ae0c46bf8c38b42de5af8ba70132e30c04a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063378 [wpt PR 61918] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61918\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/intersection-observer/grow-height-and-scrolled.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/intersection-observer/root-margin-scroll-margin-units.html.ini"], "git_node": "7f714548425aaf53a8b36e38fc3af69df3eac253", "git_parents": ["e64bf32498634f4d853ed98227f46a1659abb8b4"], "node": "fea4d33a844f6d0eb848a2468f5e93e9cd324a9b", "parents": ["24ca770803b5f5357ce529a2953c3142fcf59199"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jessica Lee \u003cjlee53@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063186 [wpt PR 61906] - Add tests for lazy-loading cross-site iframes, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd tests for lazy-loading cross-site iframes (#61906)\n\nThis change adds cross-site variants of several of existing iframe-loading-lazy tests, along with two new tests that involve more than one cross-site frame.\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 975c7828058fbc0a7b6491a6a7cb29bded025c22\nwpt-pr: 61906\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-iframe-element/cross-site/iframe-loading-lazy-cross-site.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-iframe-element/cross-site/iframe-loading-lazy-in-scroller-cross-site.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-iframe-element/cross-site/iframe-loading-lazy-in-scroller-far-cross-site.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-iframe-element/cross-site/iframe-loading-lazy-multiple-queued-navigations-cross-site.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-iframe-element/cross-site/iframe-loading-lazy-nested-cross-site.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-iframe-element/cross-site/iframe-loading-lazy-siblings-cross-site.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-iframe-element/cross-site/resources/iframe-loading-lazy-nested-subframe.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-iframe-element/cross-site/resources/subframe-post-msg.html"], "git_node": "8c5d789535027f633a6b74cff9432dac996da651", "git_parents": ["7f714548425aaf53a8b36e38fc3af69df3eac253"], "node": "b8b9a90477f8d867c10344d044ec7fa3916043ad", "parents": ["fea4d33a844f6d0eb848a2468f5e93e9cd324a9b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dominik R\u00f6ttsches \u003cdrott@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063338 [wpt PR 61916] - Patch XML for supporting ATTLIST default attribute value definitions, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nPatch XML for supporting ATTLIST default attribute value definitions\n\nLocally patch in fix for upstreamm issue #86, see [1]. Patch landed in\nupstream but unreleased.\n\nSupply WPT test attlist-defaults.html which covers various shapes and\nforms of DTDs in which default values are used. In the test, we are not\ntesting DTD constraints, but we go over all sort of syntatical\ncombinations to ensure that the parser reaches the default values\ncorrectly.\n\n[1] https://github.com/kornelski/xml-rs/pull/87\n\nBug: 531787870\nFixed: 539929368\nChange-Id: Ieea2f622f9fedc20b256b9964f65c7222952f4b3\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8248778\nReviewed-by: \u0141ukasz Anforowicz \u003clukasza@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Dominik R\u00f6ttsches \u003cdrott@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1678869}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 83e0b81890839d5a7a5d2b5f2a23df46b7b87f00\nwpt-pr: 61916\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/xml/attlist-defaults.html"], "git_node": "8c9d0627f412409c6d974cef3429a69d399cdfdc", "git_parents": ["8c5d789535027f633a6b74cff9432dac996da651"], "node": "e7a008a07f2f627ffbf20dc02ecc3f6377e69ad7", "parents": ["b8b9a90477f8d867c10344d044ec7fa3916043ad"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sam Weinig \u003csam@webkit.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063397 [wpt PR 61921] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=319996, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=319996 (#61921)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: ff13b9b096667122516dfdc1990969ff6f444f16\nwpt-pr: 61921\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-viewport/zoom/grid.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-viewport/zoom/reference/grid-ref.html"], "git_node": "25ecdddf5f4687583cb6a9bc111a151a94b85ccc", "git_parents": ["8c9d0627f412409c6d974cef3429a69d399cdfdc"], "node": "cf6148c0df487b2aee5ede2b33cf30a838ae2ca7", "parents": ["e7a008a07f2f627ffbf20dc02ecc3f6377e69ad7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063397 [wpt PR 61921] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61921\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-viewport/zoom/grid.html.ini"], "git_node": "5dcd2b7550e4fa301722b63c718c70b8d61593da", "git_parents": ["25ecdddf5f4687583cb6a9bc111a151a94b85ccc"], "node": "4e40975616f985b5d52c391bb7f4147607184564", "parents": ["cf6148c0df487b2aee5ede2b33cf30a838ae2ca7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sam Weinig \u003csam@webkit.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063399 [wpt PR 61922] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=320921, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=320921 (#61922)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 6f28008619b2cece437d9d7915dc267bb984c8cf\nwpt-pr: 61922\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-viewport/zoom/line-height-computed.html"], "git_node": "39fc63669f539713d20b0e75c9cb789ed1c6a3d6", "git_parents": ["5dcd2b7550e4fa301722b63c718c70b8d61593da"], "node": "242a896a86f3e956d0a4852728b681d1a2c482c9", "parents": ["4e40975616f985b5d52c391bb7f4147607184564"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sam Weinig \u003csam@webkit.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063411 [wpt PR 61926] - Add tests for CSS color analogous sets, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=317497 (#61926)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: a7a8f0f9312950eace851d8ec4e58521d37984e6\nwpt-pr: 61926\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-color/parsing/color-computed-color-mix-function.html"], "git_node": "a7c57e1dd49ab0a15ef1eae0e0530f6e7d324343", "git_parents": ["39fc63669f539713d20b0e75c9cb789ed1c6a3d6"], "node": "760e014e893db4a21fbfc3f7ed2ccfabbc2a3ef3", "parents": ["242a896a86f3e956d0a4852728b681d1a2c482c9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063411 [wpt PR 61926] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61926\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-color/parsing/color-computed-color-mix-function.html.ini"], "git_node": "52fef62ccc4508bb9f1c082fc2da4f4ed6ffc872", "git_parents": ["a7c57e1dd49ab0a15ef1eae0e0530f6e7d324343"], "node": "572af3472413855c4a892f5f5c7423a983e64fe2", "parents": ["760e014e893db4a21fbfc3f7ed2ccfabbc2a3ef3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Joanne Pan \u003c71951015+J0pan@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063180 [wpt PR 61905] - [css-values-5] Add coverage for the random() caching key in custom properties, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[css-values-5] Add coverage for the random() caching key in custom properties (#61905)\n\nAdds cases pinning which random() usages share a base value inside custom\nproperties: two registered \u003clength\u003e custom properties on one element, the same\ncustom property on two elements, a custom property against a non-custom one at\nthe same index, property-scoped equality across elements, two random()\nfunctions within one custom property, and an author \u003cdashed-ident\u003e that happens\nto name the property an implicit key is scoped to.\n\nThe @property initial-value case read the computed value with bracket access on\nthe CSSStyleDeclaration, which never resolves a custom property, so it compared\nundefined to undefined and could not fail. Read it with getPropertyValue() and\nassert the property is left unregistered.\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 1a788d18840c82dfab3f4072bcbd3893e83fb5e6\nwpt-pr: 61905\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-values/random-computed.tentative.html"], "git_node": "c6eace10113043e3d964d6a5b9cd01099bdbe1c0", "git_parents": ["52fef62ccc4508bb9f1c082fc2da4f4ed6ffc872"], "node": "227562e50b7950625f85b03060821bc6e6e4329b", "parents": ["572af3472413855c4a892f5f5c7423a983e64fe2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063180 [wpt PR 61905] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61905\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-values/random-computed.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "8233086d2460099ba244bf97f034d67e63dc8987", "git_parents": ["c6eace10113043e3d964d6a5b9cd01099bdbe1c0"], "node": "fbc632516fd892315c34b987b929259c23b43ef6", "parents": ["227562e50b7950625f85b03060821bc6e6e4329b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063172 [wpt PR 61903] - [html-in-canvas] Add {get,set}CanvasTransform scaffolding, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[html-in-canvas] Add {get,set}CanvasTransform scaffolding\n\nThis patch adds the IDL for getCanvasTransform and setCanvasTransform,\nwires up storage, and adds some trivial tests. This has been done\nbehind a new flag, ElementCanvasTransform, which will be used to avoid\nbreaking current users. A virtual test suite has been added to ensure\nbasic coverage of the behavior without the new feature (e.g., users\nrelying on CSS transforms NOT affecting drawElementImage).\n\nThis patch only adds the ability to get and set the canvas transform,\nand followups will be needed to implement the logic for geometry\nmapping, hit testing, etc.\n\nSee: https://github.com/WICG/html-in-canvas/issues/135\n\nBug: 532229486\nChange-Id: I21a7a4955731fab40ab22aabf739f2a804b6e3fe\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8222805\nAuto-Submit: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1678879}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: ce4e5eb364dccefe28ce848679af0d758bbb0b75\nwpt-pr: 61903\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/canvas-transform-get-set.tentative.html"], "git_node": "27d04d8c766a8ef70bcda79d45de20e1b119a2c6", "git_parents": ["8233086d2460099ba244bf97f034d67e63dc8987"], "node": "58f54f082db5428aedec4a6728c5767490b03351", "parents": ["fbc632516fd892315c34b987b929259c23b43ef6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063172 [wpt PR 61903] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61903\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/canvas-transform-get-set.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "558b04237d37fa637b8f1619114876d3542d22e3", "git_parents": ["27d04d8c766a8ef70bcda79d45de20e1b119a2c6"], "node": "1675c00242079fdb65ca9586e892e56ce0c5b180", "parents": ["58f54f082db5428aedec4a6728c5767490b03351"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sam Weinig \u003csam@webkit.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063401 [wpt PR 61923] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=320744, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=320744 (#61923)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: f5675fc9405c8a6a07009ceaf7be538664f5a877\nwpt-pr: 61923\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-values/using-font-relative-units-in-font-properties.html"], "git_node": "883742e4557c433983da5f6ad22d1434b219ac25", "git_parents": ["558b04237d37fa637b8f1619114876d3542d22e3"], "node": "6f6e8c54d21d0c3c4c01b988ed8fbf96714416f9", "parents": ["1675c00242079fdb65ca9586e892e56ce0c5b180"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063401 [wpt PR 61923] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61923\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-values/using-font-relative-units-in-font-properties.html.ini"], "git_node": "15485185c3b8a66e43343feac13f2ae090c9defb", "git_parents": ["883742e4557c433983da5f6ad22d1434b219ac25"], "node": "c5cb144f75c482f2992fa9ecb334f49b2efe2fab", "parents": ["6f6e8c54d21d0c3c4c01b988ed8fbf96714416f9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kiet Ho \u003ckiet.ho@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063168 [wpt PR 61902] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=321555, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=321555\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: cc93f356fc3065040f1d48aff256d4046e0d0ef9\nwpt-pr: 61902\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-anchor-position/long-anchor-chain-crash.html"], "git_node": "d246a990650b4b09681cb7c470a471c0d09b5fbd", "git_parents": ["15485185c3b8a66e43343feac13f2ae090c9defb"], "node": "628df15df185715a966378c1c2a5ec17a05c0be0", "parents": ["c5cb144f75c482f2992fa9ecb334f49b2efe2fab"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063187 [wpt PR 61907] - [html-in-canvas] Include CanvasTransform in PaintLayer::Transform, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[html-in-canvas] Include CanvasTransform in PaintLayer::Transform\n\nThis patch makes PaintLayer::Transform include the transform from\nan Element's canvas transform, making geometry queries like\n`getBoundingClientRect` respect the canvas transform.\n\nSee: https://github.com/WICG/html-in-canvas/issues/135\n\nBug: 532229486\nChange-Id: Ib69e451ce51cbfd6a40a20fd88b5f641ba80d2d3\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8226106\nAuto-Submit: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1678898}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: fb587ab2ec2a085f3e1227773d7d69db79c79691\nwpt-pr: 61907\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/canvas-transform-get-bounding-client-rect.tentative.html"], "git_node": "eac3715797ac89875b39a587af702bb4dbaefe90", "git_parents": ["d246a990650b4b09681cb7c470a471c0d09b5fbd"], "node": "9760db040efecd07760307ff6db37f103cab8b30", "parents": ["628df15df185715a966378c1c2a5ec17a05c0be0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063187 [wpt PR 61907] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61907\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/canvas-transform-get-bounding-client-rect.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "37973645580f26ccbdb39b2eca1227043078247c", "git_parents": ["eac3715797ac89875b39a587af702bb4dbaefe90"], "node": "dac527ef46bb0f64510b3a3a02fd3c6b9a627124", "parents": ["9760db040efecd07760307ff6db37f103cab8b30"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Cameron McCormack \u003cheycam@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056453 [wpt PR 61434] - Move finished-promise-defers-cleanup.html to be tentative., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nMove finished-promise-defers-cleanup.html to be tentative. (#61434)\n\nThe test currently relies on an ordering of event loop task selection\n(with the setTimeout(... ,0)), which the HTML spec does not support and\nwhich differs between browsers.\n--\n\nwpt-commits: ed9e6a4f0ab5bcb900595ff0f79f13c5a59bde0c\nwpt-pr: 61434\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-view-transitions/finished-promise-defers-cleanup.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-view-transitions/finished-promise-defers-cleanup.tentative.html"], "git_node": "e9cef4cd674f56e0561e48fee82b949f9b7bfde9", "git_parents": ["37973645580f26ccbdb39b2eca1227043078247c"], "node": "09d576c94c3b8058abcd7e2517c23de8c89c7115", "parents": ["dac527ef46bb0f64510b3a3a02fd3c6b9a627124"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryuya \u003cryuyxx@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062939 [wpt PR 61885] - [css-text] Update text-fit parsing test spec links, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nfix: update text-fit spec links (#61885)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: dd8807219ed0adf3f8b99a84850033e451b89085\nwpt-pr: 61885\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text/parsing/text-fit-computed.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text/parsing/text-fit-invalid.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text/parsing/text-fit-valid.html"], "git_node": "0dc26a89c7d85558e8db3b6f1bf94c414835ea5c", "git_parents": ["e9cef4cd674f56e0561e48fee82b949f9b7bfde9"], "node": "878bc7538da9d2c66d712a1341f9ae680061ab3c", "parents": ["09d576c94c3b8058abcd7e2517c23de8c89c7115"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sam Weinig \u003csam@webkit.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063387 [wpt PR 61919] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=319682, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=319682 (#61919)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 13883dd50d8e347d0ad7267fcaf908967a79d2c9\nwpt-pr: 61919\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-viewport/zoom/animation-range.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-viewport/zoom/reference/animation-range-ref.html"], "git_node": "cf04d74f94c3a475851909d232003a9a85850b2c", "git_parents": ["0dc26a89c7d85558e8db3b6f1bf94c414835ea5c"], "node": "14d7061d2dd970f45a326066f230ea64250dba88", "parents": ["878bc7538da9d2c66d712a1341f9ae680061ab3c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063387 [wpt PR 61919] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61919\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-viewport/zoom/animation-range.html.ini"], "git_node": "24dcb4abe2c1fffed28281edb4663c4109660b4a", "git_parents": ["cf04d74f94c3a475851909d232003a9a85850b2c"], "node": "ddd18d09b22739c4f0b6d84f272f350231b4367f", "parents": ["14d7061d2dd970f45a326066f230ea64250dba88"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sam Weinig \u003csam@webkit.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063391 [wpt PR 61920] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=319905, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=319905 (#61920)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 467879eaa4055a5dd0f7a59ba195942930c2f570\nwpt-pr: 61920\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-viewport/zoom/reference/view-timeline-inset-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-viewport/zoom/view-timeline-inset.html"], "git_node": "2b7dffacd31daa7f4629eacfd0c612341c6a7a2a", "git_parents": ["24dcb4abe2c1fffed28281edb4663c4109660b4a"], "node": "98cabcd7efc0c8009811048c1a1768cfc179717c", "parents": ["ddd18d09b22739c4f0b6d84f272f350231b4367f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063391 [wpt PR 61920] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61920\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-viewport/zoom/view-timeline-inset.html.ini"], "git_node": "4454fe41405c87d3bc7073af974ba55af7ba62e2", "git_parents": ["2b7dffacd31daa7f4629eacfd0c612341c6a7a2a"], "node": "7a7b9f495e7cdecc8b422a272fb8ba329a384efc", "parents": ["98cabcd7efc0c8009811048c1a1768cfc179717c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Morten Stenshorne \u003cmstensho@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063461 [wpt PR 61928] - [RouteMatching] Upstream WPT tests for shippable parts of the spec., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[RouteMatching] Upstream WPT tests for shippable parts of the spec.\n\nMove them out of wpt_internal. Remove a couple of tests that weren't\nuseful.\n\nexternal/wpt/css/css-navigation/ now needs to be run as\nvirtual/threaded/ due to view transition tests. At the same time,\nwpt_internal/route/ no longer needs to run as virtual/threaded/ , since\nthere are no view transition tests left there.\n\nPlace everything under tentative/ for now. This also includes the one\ntest that existed in css-navigation/ prior to this CL.\n\nBug: 436805487\nChange-Id: I58a22024893aa8df40c92bf345d35002dc3fd477\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8244771\nCommit-Queue: Ian Kilpatrick \u003cikilpatrick@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@google.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Ian Kilpatrick \u003cikilpatrick@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1678946}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: c68236843363b878d6ceafbb43b712662d2004a5\nwpt-pr: 61928\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-navigation/crashtests/invalid-location-descriptor-value.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-navigation/crashtests/invalid-url-pattern-argument.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-navigation/crashtests/url-pattern-null-document.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-navigation/nav-source-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-navigation/resources/test-navigation.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-navigation/tentative/crossdoc-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-navigation/tentative/crossdoc-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-navigation/tentative/if-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-navigation/tentative/link-to-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-navigation/tentative/link-to-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-navigation/tentative/link-to-003.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-navigation/tentative/nav-source-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-navigation/tentative/navigation-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-navigation/tentative/navigation-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-navigation/tentative/navigation-003.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-navigation/tentative/navigation-004.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-navigation/tentative/parsing/link-to-invalid.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-navigation/tentative/parsing/link-to-valid.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-navigation/tentative/parsing/location-invalid-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-navigation/tentative/parsing/location-invalid-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-navigation/tentative/parsing/location-valid.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-navigation/tentative/parsing/navigation-rule-invalid.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-navigation/tentative/parsing/navigation-rule-location-valid.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-navigation/tentative/parsing/url-pattern-valid.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-navigation/tentative/parsing/url-valid.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-navigation/tentative/resources/crossdoc-001-helper.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-navigation/tentative/resources/crossdoc-002-helper.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-navigation/tentative/resources/test-navigation.js"], "git_node": "455d030a417782aa6f57442fcdf2d680cf9bd8f8", "git_parents": ["4454fe41405c87d3bc7073af974ba55af7ba62e2"], "node": "6977579ab7e573517b973259dee790cacc1a455d", "parents": ["7a7b9f495e7cdecc8b422a272fb8ba329a384efc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063461 [wpt PR 61928] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61928\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-navigation/nav-source-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-navigation/tentative/crossdoc-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-navigation/tentative/crossdoc-002.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-navigation/tentative/if-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-navigation/tentative/link-to-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-navigation/tentative/link-to-002.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-navigation/tentative/link-to-003.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-navigation/tentative/nav-source-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-navigation/tentative/navigation-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-navigation/tentative/navigation-002.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-navigation/tentative/navigation-003.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-navigation/tentative/navigation-004.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-navigation/tentative/parsing/link-to-valid.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-navigation/tentative/parsing/location-valid.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-navigation/tentative/parsing/navigation-rule-invalid.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-navigation/tentative/parsing/navigation-rule-location-valid.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-navigation/tentative/parsing/url-pattern-valid.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-navigation/tentative/parsing/url-valid.html.ini"], "git_node": "1d7f41b6c42d17b3e1386cca1ebe0ed38ab9df9e", "git_parents": ["455d030a417782aa6f57442fcdf2d680cf9bd8f8"], "node": "a2855dbb4da94b5a2099f1422508a0c0bc5c120e", "parents": ["6977579ab7e573517b973259dee790cacc1a455d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063423 [wpt PR 61927] - Fragment includes with \u003ctemplate for=\"...\" src\u003e, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFragment includes with \u003ctemplate for=\"...\" src\u003e\n\nWhen \u003ctemplate for=\"...\" has a src attribute, its content is fetched and\napplied at the template's destination location.\n\nIt respects fetching modifiers\n(nonce/integrity/crossorigin/referrerpolicy), though cannot be\ndowngraded to no-cors.\n\nAtm, \u003ctemplate src\u003e cannot be parser blocking.\n\nBug: 535664974\nChange-Id: I36ecde784bea292c73277cd1e8180206d1f47fd6\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8159342\nCommit-Queue: Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@google.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1679012}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 28edb7d441c4c2099d73af9fdfd154bafefd8ccc\nwpt-pr: 61927\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/dom/partial-updates/tentative/fragment/empty-for-streaming.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/dom/partial-updates/tentative/fragment/src-buffered.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/dom/partial-updates/tentative/fragment/src-cancel.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/dom/partial-updates/tentative/fragment/src-csp-cors.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/dom/partial-updates/tentative/fragment/src-csp.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/dom/partial-updates/tentative/fragment/src-nonce.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/dom/partial-updates/tentative/fragment/src-nonce.sub.html.headers", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/dom/partial-updates/tentative/fragment/src-parser-blocking.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/dom/partial-updates/tentative/fragment/src-referrerpolicy.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/dom/partial-updates/tentative/fragment/src-sri.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/dom/partial-updates/tentative/fragment/src-streaming.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/dom/partial-updates/tentative/resources/chunked-html.py"], "git_node": "04e112d5f77b6468130904d7c5203fe943aa0734", "git_parents": ["1d7f41b6c42d17b3e1386cca1ebe0ed38ab9df9e"], "node": "10785f51c95ba976183ae9f6e0a099d6fb3f09f8", "parents": ["a2855dbb4da94b5a2099f1422508a0c0bc5c120e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063423 [wpt PR 61927] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61927\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/dom/partial-updates/tentative/fragment/src-buffered.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/dom/partial-updates/tentative/fragment/src-csp-cors.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/dom/partial-updates/tentative/fragment/src-nonce.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/dom/partial-updates/tentative/fragment/src-parser-blocking.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/dom/partial-updates/tentative/fragment/src-referrerpolicy.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/dom/partial-updates/tentative/fragment/src-sri.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/dom/partial-updates/tentative/fragment/src-streaming.html.ini"], "git_node": "75a0efbddff51381c4569b5ec029025731df75e2", "git_parents": ["04e112d5f77b6468130904d7c5203fe943aa0734"], "node": "427985abb10444d44dc9c5f38c741eebd60b9a86", "parents": ["10785f51c95ba976183ae9f6e0a099d6fb3f09f8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Cameron McCormack \u003cheycam@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055844 [wpt PR 61360] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=319473, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=319473 (#61360)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: cc83751f80692b3ee4478b21b38407eb8f999c68\nwpt-pr: 61360\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-view-transitions/scroller-child.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-view-transitions/scroller.html"], "git_node": "b9d2c8c0863c0afb5646c81e8215d8b9a80c550a", "git_parents": ["75a0efbddff51381c4569b5ec029025731df75e2"], "node": "987e41eab865c24134631a2a2f99746d0c312df3", "parents": ["427985abb10444d44dc9c5f38c741eebd60b9a86"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Grogan \u003cdgrogan@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063515 [wpt PR 61932] - [menu a11y] Fix DCHECK failure for rapid add/remove mutations, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[menu a11y] Fix DCHECK failure for rapid add/remove mutations\n\nWhen a node is added to and removed from a \u003cmenubar\u003e or \u003cmenulist\u003e\nwithin the same microtask, MenuMutationObserver receives two separate\nmutation records for the detached node.\n\nPreviously, `CheckAddedNodes` failed to plumb the mutation record's\ntarget down to `CheckForIssue` as the `disconnected_parent`. Because the\ndetached node's parentNode is null, the ancestor loop exited\nimmediately. This caused it to fall through to the bottom of the\nfunction, hitting a `DCHECK(disconnected_root)` crash because\n`disconnected_root` was null.\n\nThis CL fixes the issue by plumbing the `disconnected_root` and\n`disconnected_parent` in the addition phase so it correctly evaluates\nthe node's simulated tree structure.\n\nAdditionally, this CL updates the fallback return value at the bottom of\n`CheckForIssue` to `kValidChild`. This fixes a secondary issue where\nmutations inside detached subtrees were incorrectly treated as\nviolations, which could cause the menu's violation count to decrement\nbelow zero.\n\nBug: 513637242\nFixed: 544947427\nChange-Id: I0ae399e28860966c016e58666dbf7e0e99aa3cf3\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8253357\nReviewed-by: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: David Grogan \u003cdgrogan@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1679082}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: b9843d6d3c6e5e07de8cd5c3e86d6139ae0d8496\nwpt-pr: 61932\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/menu/tentative/menu-content-model-violation.html"], "git_node": "3813132db2a65cfa784b5f0fd382f6e236320271", "git_parents": ["b9d2c8c0863c0afb5646c81e8215d8b9a80c550a"], "node": "5c4cd9c7fafb5d741155694913ef3a588057bc26", "parents": ["987e41eab865c24134631a2a2f99746d0c312df3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063515 [wpt PR 61932] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61932\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/menu/tentative/menu-content-model-violation.html.ini"], "git_node": "cb30ee94d530b6ce1bfd3f384feb384c468715f5", "git_parents": ["3813132db2a65cfa784b5f0fd382f6e236320271"], "node": "9e882b1fced3181feaf705a0ec21d1e025f3c3e0", "parents": ["5c4cd9c7fafb5d741155694913ef3a588057bc26"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Wonik Choi \u003cchoiwonik91@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063134 [wpt PR 61889] - Add crash test for focused iframe adopt into active document, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd crash test for focused iframe adopt into active document\n\nCover the active-document counterpart of iframe-document-move-crash.html:\non focusout, adopt the focused iframe into another iframe's\ncontentDocument while focus moves to a button. Passes if it does not crash.\n\nFixed: 40180911\nChange-Id: I4450859706177646c717f11f063729353a492d4d\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8221527\nReviewed-by: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Robert Flack \u003cflackr@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1679148}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 8645c8e2a8447f2037313a1d4d5b478c657be34a\nwpt-pr: 61889\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-iframe-element/iframe-document-move-to-active-crash.html"], "git_node": "09a3e7eae83d8758f9fa13d9ff28ba3885f23e6f", "git_parents": ["cb30ee94d530b6ce1bfd3f384feb384c468715f5"], "node": "a8d7a392b3f6c3d50a81453bf3e58f67bb87569c", "parents": ["9e882b1fced3181feaf705a0ec21d1e025f3c3e0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Awogbemila \u003cawogbemila@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063594 [wpt PR 61935] - [scroll-snap] Fix target Element IDs for mutual snap, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[scroll-snap] Fix target Element IDs for mutual snap\n\nWhen a scroll container snaps using mutual snap (where independent\nsearches on X and Y axes fail to find mutually visible targets, but a\ncombined search finds a valid snap area), the target snap area element\nIDs were not being populated on the SnapPositionData result.\n\nThis caused the compositor to lose track of the snap target, leading to\na DCHECK violation in ScrollOffsetAnimationFinished because\nwas_animating_for_snap was false.\n\nThis CL fixes FindSnapPositionForMutualSnap to populate\ntarget_element_ids with the selected area's element ID.\n\nBug: 546014641\nChange-Id: I52c5c353e55734583a9030c2f7ad5ce3705f59de\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8247122\nCommit-Queue: David A \u003cawogbemila@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Robert Flack \u003cflackr@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1679172}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 0f96572f18dac59d9744e14141e9e30abb4ba7a8\nwpt-pr: 61935\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-scroll-snap/snap-fling-past-furthest-area.html"], "git_node": "e30f4117fa5cd8af65bded2c7e7120a2165d8d59", "git_parents": ["09a3e7eae83d8758f9fa13d9ff28ba3885f23e6f"], "node": "5713502e366397d8323c901c4b7af649bbee6478", "parents": ["a8d7a392b3f6c3d50a81453bf3e58f67bb87569c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063594 [wpt PR 61935] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61935\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-scroll-snap/snap-fling-past-furthest-area.html.ini"], "git_node": "a0c9edbf8b19778a2762c1c7e9ba9af9f868fdbc", "git_parents": ["e30f4117fa5cd8af65bded2c7e7120a2165d8d59"], "node": "35f6a5648610a4111b62b930c791c6445878dfa5", "parents": ["5713502e366397d8323c901c4b7af649bbee6478"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Javier Contreras \u003cjaviercon@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063517 [wpt PR 61933] - [masonry] CrossGaps for grid lanes gap decorations (2/2), a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[masonry] CrossGaps for grid lanes gap decorations (2/2)\n\nThis CL implements the paint side for `CrossGap` gap decorations for\ngrid-lanes.\n\nFor a given cross gap we will ever only have two intersections (which\nwill denote the segments we paint). These are the intersection of where\nthe cross gap actually is located, and then the intersection past the\nend of the lane the cross gap belongs to.\n\nIn order to determine the \"end lane\" / end main gap for the end of a\ngiven cross gap, we generalize the same infra that Flex used. Basically,\nwe keep a running cursor which denotes which main gap (or lane) we are\ncurrently in, and we move that cursor along.\n\nThis CL adds tests as well as marks a big chunk of the tests as passing\nnow.\n\nBug: 343257585\nChange-Id: I2f895be9e063d53c7e49b43bad1ab3758ecc227e\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8211199\nReviewed-by: Ian Kilpatrick \u003cikilpatrick@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Kurt Catti-Schmidt \u003ckschmi@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Javier Contreras \u003cjaviercon@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1679184}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 7caa0df28c35287e553a7603746bff19abf325a9\nwpt-pr: 61933\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-014-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-030-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-030.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-031-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-031.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-033-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-033.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-036-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-036.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-037-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-037.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-038-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-038.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-019-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-019.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-020-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-020.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-021-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-021.html"], "git_node": "04f557403a8683ffd56ec5c9d0939ec23b2a12c0", "git_parents": ["a0c9edbf8b19778a2762c1c7e9ba9af9f868fdbc"], "node": "86bb76cb5f346c291aabc43e64d2c6ad7c6e8bf0", "parents": ["35f6a5648610a4111b62b930c791c6445878dfa5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063517 [wpt PR 61933] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61933\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-030.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-031.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-033.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-036.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-037.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-038.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-019.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-020.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-021.html.ini"], "git_node": "e8d985798a232f4a8406e721dd5aa7144acc6b34", "git_parents": ["04f557403a8683ffd56ec5c9d0939ec23b2a12c0"], "node": "0221615d0b62869641ed41973474ee1caf4e774b", "parents": ["86bb76cb5f346c291aabc43e64d2c6ad7c6e8bf0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dominic Farolino \u003cdom@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063484 [wpt PR 61931] - WebMCP: Preserve in-flight executions after unregistration, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebMCP: Preserve in-flight executions after unregistration\n\nThis CL changes the tool unregistration path to *not* cancel in-flight\ntool executions. This fixes a foot-gun that we experience especially\nwith some frameworks.\n\nSee also\nhttps://docs.google.com/document/d/1AynIaf7vPa10oo41Ygjoj7_mVhLETop9YstTesdeX_0/edit?resourcekey=0-wYoDTWIYO9GkIiprhC7sNA&disco=AAAB2atfW6k\nand https://github.com/webmachinelearning/webmcp/issues/218.\n\nThe spec change will come after this CL.\n\nR=beaufort.francois@gmail.com\n\nBug: 489045948,489045948\nChange-Id: I62467e9d4af55c8ea31e01aed213907899617306\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8224887\nReviewed-by: Alex Moshchuk \u003calexmos@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Fr \u003cbeaufort.francois@gmail.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Dominic Farolino \u003cdom@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1679193}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 6437d68e10721ed4b9b68101ec1ab1a1b67a3995\nwpt-pr: 61931\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/declarative/form_removal_submit_crash.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/declarative/unregister-during-executeTool.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/imperative/executeTool-unregister-resolution-race.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/imperative/resources/iframe-register-tool.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/imperative/unregister-during-executeTool.https.html"], "git_node": "c8858a96cfd08d87f8a59c204d49ef8d3983daf5", "git_parents": ["e8d985798a232f4a8406e721dd5aa7144acc6b34"], "node": "802db169bc8709a4aa34753c999777b81b4ba008", "parents": ["0221615d0b62869641ed41973474ee1caf4e774b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063484 [wpt PR 61931] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61931\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webmcp/declarative/unregister-during-executeTool.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webmcp/imperative/executeTool-unregister-resolution-race.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webmcp/imperative/unregister-during-executeTool.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "c1de2a0abfb29cefbc4381e5909262f836a44885", "git_parents": ["c8858a96cfd08d87f8a59c204d49ef8d3983daf5"], "node": "423ee9daa8a1db013d0d3192016d522f944ee559", "parents": ["802db169bc8709a4aa34753c999777b81b4ba008"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Shubham Gupta \u003cshubhamg13.work@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062901 [wpt PR 61880] - Add a test to check that modified text is not reconsidered for LCP., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd a new test to check that modified text is not reconsidered for LCP. (#61880)\n\nSigned-off-by: Shubham Gupta \u003cshubhamg13.work@gmail.com\u003e\n--\n\nwpt-commits: ab333ae270719ba7a4ebc4188e45752adeb1e0f2\nwpt-pr: 61880\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/largest-contentful-paint/modified-text-not-reconsidered.html"], "git_node": "1b70e5fbacf7425c8fa93626f89e9ca29f7dd483", "git_parents": ["c1de2a0abfb29cefbc4381e5909262f836a44885"], "node": "5ed9d73c30b650e3c996633a6aa74b8395da62d9", "parents": ["423ee9daa8a1db013d0d3192016d522f944ee559"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dominic Farolino \u003cdom@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060334 [wpt PR 61691] - DOM: Remove \"_current\" as a valid frame target, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nDOM: Remove \"_current\" as a valid frame target\n\nSee https://chromestatus.com/feature/5121089536262144 and\nhttps://chromestatus.com/metrics/feature/timeline/popularity/2835.\nSupport for the \"_current\" frame target keyword is far below the\nthreshold for removal from the web platform, so this CL removes support\nfor this keyword.\n\nBlink-dev PSA:\nhttps://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/g/blink-dev/c/CKB-NAH0cmM\n\nR=chrishtr\n\nBug: 539212797\nChange-Id: I9b321f87b480020cb460ff2c9933b06c5788a818\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8157779\nCommit-Queue: Dominic Farolino \u003cdom@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Chris Harrelson \u003cchrishtr@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1679285}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: a2704e608de78a1c9935f8afc5e37eed2fcf671d\nwpt-pr: 61691\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/browsers/windows/browsing-context-names/choose-_current-001.html"], "git_node": "addb6311aa20604bb3bba073f0bcb7ea73020e8b", "git_parents": ["1b70e5fbacf7425c8fa93626f89e9ca29f7dd483"], "node": "ab21d5cf22637cec8f0b9394b5c18261ddb12eef", "parents": ["5ed9d73c30b650e3c996633a6aa74b8395da62d9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nidhi Jaju \u003cnidhijaju@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063640 [wpt PR 61940] - Revert \"Fragment includes with \u003ctemplate for=\"...\" src\u003e\", a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nRevert \"Fragment includes with \u003ctemplate for=\"...\" src\u003e\"\n\nThis reverts commit 89bdeb2ef7b974c1429fc9456e50896e38f4486f.\n\nReason for revert: Causing consistent failures for external/wpt/html/dom/partial-updates/tentative/fragment/src-buffered.html on Linux Tests (dbg)(1)\n\nFailure Link: https://ci.chromium.org/ui/p/chromium/builders/ci/Linux%20Tests%20(dbg)(1)/133096/test-results\n\nOriginal change's description:\n\u003e Fragment includes with \u003ctemplate for=\"...\" src\u003e\n\u003e\n\u003e When \u003ctemplate for=\"...\" has a src attribute, its content is fetched and\n\u003e applied at the template's destination location.\n\u003e\n\u003e It respects fetching modifiers\n\u003e (nonce/integrity/crossorigin/referrerpolicy), though cannot be\n\u003e downgraded to no-cors.\n\u003e\n\u003e Atm, \u003ctemplate src\u003e cannot be parser blocking.\n\u003e\n\u003e Bug: 535664974\n\u003e Change-Id: I36ecde784bea292c73277cd1e8180206d1f47fd6\n\u003e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8159342\n\u003e Commit-Queue: Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@google.com\u003e\n\u003e Reviewed-by: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\n\u003e Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1679012}\n\nBug: 535664974\nNo-Presubmit: true\nNo-Tree-Checks: true\nNo-Try: true\nChange-Id: Ic5250143734a515bb668ca85c53cbe52a81db082\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8257450\nBot-Commit: rubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com \u003crubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Nidhi Jaju \u003cnidhijaju@chromium.org\u003e\nOwners-Override: Nidhi Jaju \u003cnidhijaju@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: rubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com \u003crubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1679203}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: f9ecd8a4a9c6e9865ea4aee4741e4b02f75fd476\nwpt-pr: 61940\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/dom/partial-updates/tentative/fragment/empty-for-streaming.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/dom/partial-updates/tentative/fragment/src-buffered.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/dom/partial-updates/tentative/fragment/src-cancel.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/dom/partial-updates/tentative/fragment/src-csp-cors.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/dom/partial-updates/tentative/fragment/src-csp.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/dom/partial-updates/tentative/fragment/src-nonce.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/dom/partial-updates/tentative/fragment/src-nonce.sub.html.headers", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/dom/partial-updates/tentative/fragment/src-parser-blocking.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/dom/partial-updates/tentative/fragment/src-referrerpolicy.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/dom/partial-updates/tentative/fragment/src-sri.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/dom/partial-updates/tentative/fragment/src-streaming.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/dom/partial-updates/tentative/resources/chunked-html.py"], "git_node": "252283b33d225c8cf9148e85da72de8f8beabf62", "git_parents": ["addb6311aa20604bb3bba073f0bcb7ea73020e8b"], "node": "28cacfdd4a7de44e2fb605f198d1f96bfbe3c3bb", "parents": ["ab21d5cf22637cec8f0b9394b5c18261ddb12eef"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chris Thompson \u003ccthomp@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063145 [wpt PR 61894] - Enforce LNA on Background Fetch requests, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nEnforce LNA on Background Fetch requests\n\nThis CL adds Local Network Access (LNA) enforcement for Background Fetch\nrequests. Before this CL, Background Fetch requests were executed by the\nbrowser-level Download subsystem without the originating Service\nWorker's ClientSecurityState, causing LNA restrictions to be bypassed.\n\nLeveraging the SharedURLLoaderFactory interface plumbed in prior CLs,\nthis change updates BackgroundFetchJobController to:\n\n- Extract the ClientSecurityState from the originating Service Worker\n  and create a bound SharedURLLoaderFactory from its StoragePartition.\n- Dynamically re-initialize the URLLoaderFactory upon job resumption or\n  browser restarts by retrieving the Service Worker registration.\n\nThis CL also adds tests for verifying the LNA restrictions:\n\n- Desktop LNA browser tests in background_fetch_browsertest.cc.\n- Web Platform Test (WPT) suite under virtual/lna-bg-fetch/.\n\nLNA enforcement is gated behind the kBackgroundFetchLocalNetworkAccess\nfeature flag.\n\nTAG=agy\nCONV=96c12324-004c-4da1-bec2-9436ea828a56\nBYPASS_LARGE_CHANGE_WARNING: misidentified tests as prod\n\nBug: 455486148\nChange-Id: I31532bd0ed2bf6765d9af2e66cb209a5b505abd1\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8103102\nCommit-Queue: Yoshisato Yanagisawa \u003cyyanagisawa@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Avi Drissman \u003cavi@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Yoshisato Yanagisawa \u003cyyanagisawa@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1679419}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 549e8d1b03655cccd2cc7152867ade7121c8658a\nwpt-pr: 61894\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/fetch/local-network-access/resources/service-worker.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fetch/local-network-access/resources/service-worker.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/fetch/local-network-access/service-worker-background-fetch.tentative.https.html"], "git_node": "d683ae76dfb87df0382641198e6b1811227a317b", "git_parents": ["252283b33d225c8cf9148e85da72de8f8beabf62"], "node": "6d2bc14e6a9807b740519bb08c030261facd5857", "parents": ["28cacfdd4a7de44e2fb605f198d1f96bfbe3c3bb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063145 [wpt PR 61894] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61894\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/fetch/local-network-access/service-worker-background-fetch.tentative.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "a7644d4d26b7990e5eb9ef505cbd90225ef1b2a6", "git_parents": ["d683ae76dfb87df0382641198e6b1811227a317b"], "node": "ed20e3ee9412d487da770f8e482b016d88a3756a", "parents": ["6d2bc14e6a9807b740519bb08c030261facd5857"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Koji Ishii \u003ckojii@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063699 [wpt PR 61944] - [iframe] Use `allow-origins` for tests and comments, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[iframe] Use `allow-origins` for tests and comments\n\ncrrev.com/c/8173946 renamed tests etc. to `alloworigins` to\nmatch the name change of the attribute.\n\nSince it now uses the `content` attribute, make it two words\nfor better readability.\n\nThis patch has no behavior changes.\n\nBug: 418397278\nChange-Id: I48beecf49929bb5f7411988a04a7471fb3bc19f9\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8260547\nReviewed-by: Kent Tamura \u003ctkent@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Koji Ishii \u003ckojii@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Koji Ishii \u003ckojii@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Kent Tamura \u003ctkent@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1679476}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 1309482f6fd0be408590547a0ac4532b66a84087\nwpt-pr: 61944\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/resources/iframe-contents-allow-origins-missing.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/resources/iframe-contents-allow-origins.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/resources/iframe-contents-alloworigins-missing.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/resources/iframe-contents-alloworigins.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/responsive-iframe-allow-origins.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/responsive-iframe-alloworigins.html"], "git_node": "f979d2b2f8a1397b1fe0b9a5b26b531371467825", "git_parents": ["a7644d4d26b7990e5eb9ef505cbd90225ef1b2a6"], "node": "c7f152d86b3d6544e81cea6e471fe859b4d9c5bd", "parents": ["ed20e3ee9412d487da770f8e482b016d88a3756a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063699 [wpt PR 61944] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61944\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/responsive-iframe-allow-origins.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/responsive-iframe-alloworigins.html.ini"], "git_node": "bbe01a3643e5185a7622110c1d4ba61f0394da9e", "git_parents": ["f979d2b2f8a1397b1fe0b9a5b26b531371467825"], "node": "bb5b5a0671a8968a59bc938c21973a54f70f5c77", "parents": ["c7f152d86b3d6544e81cea6e471fe859b4d9c5bd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Helmut Januschka \u003chelmut@januschka.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063702 [wpt PR 61948] - Make \u003carea\u003e display:none per the HTML rendering spec, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nMake \u003carea\u003e display:none per the HTML rendering spec\n\nThe stray inline box that \u003carea\u003e generated wherever its \u003cmap\u003e sat in\nthe document flow is gone, which also allows removing the AREA\nspecific culled-inline hacks in the inline items builder and the\npre-paint tree walk that existed to support it.\n\nBug: 41140071, 1231263\nChange-Id: I88fa0154a0a81d62fd12bb1042a8869c9ac5d8ff\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8212119\nCommit-Queue: Helmut Januschka \u003chelmut@januschka.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Morten Stenshorne \u003cmstensho@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1679565}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: d93d626fa094f2895450be4fc32ffb7312cdb64b\nwpt-pr: 61948\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/area-002-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/area-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/area-crash.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-multicol/crashtests/oof-in-area-004.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-multicol/crashtests/oof-in-area-005.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-area-element/area-offsets.html"], "git_node": "777a6cd46d45cb0ae88e1857bd1cb2832f448b27", "git_parents": ["bbe01a3643e5185a7622110c1d4ba61f0394da9e"], "node": "b519e206b2302b46aee91bd14df41d73fcf5fc77", "parents": ["bb5b5a0671a8968a59bc938c21973a54f70f5c77"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063702 [wpt PR 61948] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61948\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/area-002.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-area-element/area-offsets.html.ini"], "git_node": "57f4b57817a732a430942cd27416ee18051e1952", "git_parents": ["777a6cd46d45cb0ae88e1857bd1cb2832f448b27"], "node": "705d50b2e6d058f4ee865ea327383dc0cf59c1f3", "parents": ["b519e206b2302b46aee91bd14df41d73fcf5fc77"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063704 [wpt PR 61953] - Remove fuzzy matching from customizable select WPTs, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nRemove fuzzy matching from customizable select WPTs\n\nIt looks like this wasn't needed anymore, except for one of the dark\nmode tests, which was fixed by using will-change:transform\n\nFixed: 367755346\nChange-Id: If2d6cfc0a75d2cf877cf31b4d4cd469986f971e4\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8242448\nReviewed-by: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1679614}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: e57bac09d4c24e3a2233d72501cccd81cc5106d4\nwpt-pr: 61953\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select-multiple-popup/select-multiple-popup-appearance.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/border-rendering.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/checkmark-animation-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/picker-icon-and-slotted.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/picker-icon-animation-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-appearance-active.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-appearance-button-after-option.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-appearance-button-after-span.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-appearance-button-after-text.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-appearance-custom-button.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-appearance-dark-mode-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-appearance-dark-mode.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-appearance-default-button.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-appearance-disabled-option.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-appearance-disabled.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-appearance-font-inheriting.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-appearance-hover.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-appearance-optgroup-legend.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-appearance-optgroup-rendering.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-appearance-option-with-label.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-appearance-picker-select-border.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-appearance-switching-invalidation.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-display-block.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-explicit-size.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-font-size.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-icon-color.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-open-invalidation.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-option-images.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-popover-exit-animation.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-pseudo-ordering.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-second-child-button.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-text-only.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/selectedcontent-color.html"], "git_node": "2812e0ec1f8414a8e12c1653e89d47b4233a420a", "git_parents": ["57f4b57817a732a430942cd27416ee18051e1952"], "node": "abc31417ef1468f316aa908c2632903aec75b06f", "parents": ["705d50b2e6d058f4ee865ea327383dc0cf59c1f3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dominic Farolino \u003cdom@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063768 [wpt PR 61954] - WebMCP: Deflake document.domain test, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebMCP: Deflake document.domain test\n\nThe CL addresses the remaining part of https://crbug.com/521896358,\nnamely de-flaking\n`external/wpt/webmcp/imperative/document-domain-enabled.https.html`.\n\nAccording to the dashboard [1] and [2], this test isn't really flaky,\nbut as I understand Origin Agent Clustering, it could be based on\nprocess reuse across multiple executions of the test runner, so any\nstability we observe now might be transient.\n\nThis CL de-flakes this test by ensuring we use a dedicated origin for\nthe document hosting the test that requires `document.domain` access,\nand a site-keyed agent cluster.\n\n[1]:\nhttps://ci.chromium.org/ui/test/chromium/%3A%2F%2F%5C%3Achrome_wpt_tests!webtest%3A%3Aexternal%2Fwpt%2Fwebmcp%2Fimperative%23document-domain-enabled.https.html\n[2]:\nhttps://ci.chromium.org/ui/test/chromium/%3A%2F%2F%5C%3Aheadless_shell_wpt!webtest%3A%3Aexternal%2Fwpt%2Fwebmcp%2Fimperative%23document-domain-enabled.https.html\n\nR=mfoltz\n\nFixed: 521896358\nChange-Id: I8c3a647bbba935605497f7a0cfa2bb80927f29a2\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8257353\nCommit-Queue: Dominic Farolino \u003cdom@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Mark Foltz \u003cmfoltz@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1679622}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 964ddae49acd35592ae4c2a50ea1b9fc2edec686\nwpt-pr: 61954\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/declarative/document-domain-enabled-declarative.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/declarative/document-domain-enabled-declarative.https.html.headers", "testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/declarative/document-domain-enabled.sub.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/declarative/resources/document-domain-enabled-iframe.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/declarative/resources/document-domain-enabled-iframe.html.headers", "testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/imperative/document-domain-enabled.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/imperative/document-domain-enabled.https.html.headers", "testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/imperative/document-domain-enabled.sub.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/imperative/resources/document-domain-enabled-iframe.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/imperative/resources/document-domain-enabled-iframe.html.headers"], "git_node": "9b33df2d055a311d7e5bfa0f66071365d143622a", "git_parents": ["2812e0ec1f8414a8e12c1653e89d47b4233a420a"], "node": "d2114c07a06ccb3deb9c00fce7d3b0e3b082613c", "parents": ["abc31417ef1468f316aa908c2632903aec75b06f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063768 [wpt PR 61954] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61954\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webmcp/declarative/document-domain-enabled-declarative.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webmcp/declarative/document-domain-enabled.sub.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webmcp/imperative/document-domain-enabled.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webmcp/imperative/document-domain-enabled.sub.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "6d671ba62a832a8cb8c96c026be941d57b036919", "git_parents": ["9b33df2d055a311d7e5bfa0f66071365d143622a"], "node": "93fbebf38b691154a2cc55faf2d97071cdafead4", "parents": ["d2114c07a06ccb3deb9c00fce7d3b0e3b082613c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063793 [wpt PR 61960] - [html-in-canvas] Add WPT test for nested drawables, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[html-in-canvas] Add WPT test for nested drawables\n\nThis patch adds a WPT test that nested drawables do not paint as part\nof their ancestor drawables, and that nested drawables can be painted\non their own.\n\nBug: 532229486\nChange-Id: Ia73f058dc3cad94867309ff47f6e011cd9de1b6e\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8258890\nAuto-Submit: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1679985}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 2e37a16046c8f07e14db65308a8b260f02b8b7f1\nwpt-pr: 61960\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/nested-drawable-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/nested-drawable.tentative.html"], "git_node": "c3ca01880de66f6483a35b519a5325f185c55417", "git_parents": ["6d671ba62a832a8cb8c96c026be941d57b036919"], "node": "38fae34a46b3f9e32bd125b7b26b63614962c8bf", "parents": ["93fbebf38b691154a2cc55faf2d97071cdafead4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063791 [wpt PR 61959] - [html-in-canvas] Use element's canvas transform state for rendering, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[html-in-canvas] Use element's canvas transform state for rendering\n\nThis patch switches canvas child rendering to use the child element's\ncanvas transform state instead of the canvas's transform state, causing\nrendering to include CSS transforms.\n\nDesign doc about respecting CSS transforms:\nhttps://docs.google.com/document/d/170AxSYPrlFVrp1LlUl0lWQ6h0_hUAosAGtPexQkRg0U/edit?tab=t.0\n\nSee: https://github.com/WICG/html-in-canvas/issues/135\n\nBug: 532229486\nChange-Id: Ica9b9897fee2c2ce07f492b1022eb37e6259015c\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8228404\nCommit-Queue: Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1679994}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 92a794da495dde310f299d992b94ae02f47659cf\nwpt-pr: 61959\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/anchor-positioning.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/css-transform-on-div-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/css-transform-on-div.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/hit-test/elementsFromPoint.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/hit-test/low-dpi-hit-test.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/onpaint.tentative.html"], "git_node": "c7ccaba078bb0e1251d6aae1a420ffd3ef6bd5b5", "git_parents": ["c3ca01880de66f6483a35b519a5325f185c55417"], "node": "8c6c317e4ae66b6ca4e867fd96b06f75847f9578", "parents": ["38fae34a46b3f9e32bd125b7b26b63614962c8bf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063791 [wpt PR 61959] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61959\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/hit-test/elementsFromPoint.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/hit-test/low-dpi-hit-test.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/onpaint.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "168cd63a14fb4b8f177e7456ec6500c839428bf8", "git_parents": ["c7ccaba078bb0e1251d6aae1a420ffd3ef6bd5b5"], "node": "464ee1081468b1410b8f9fb39ce1eb443cbb3b6e", "parents": ["8c6c317e4ae66b6ca4e867fd96b06f75847f9578"], "tags": []}, {"author": "tannal \u003cmtan@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063764 [wpt PR 61952] - [wpt] Add attributeStyleMap Typed OM tests for SVG elements, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[wpt] Add attributeStyleMap Typed OM tests for SVG elements\n\nAdds attributeStyleMap read, write, delete, and DOM sync tests for all\nSVG elements based on CSS Typed OM specification.\n\nBug: 542025183\nChange-Id: I6068017542f4b072a846b741321d6a84a06860b5\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8173850\nCommit-Queue: Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Wang N\u00e9lar \u003cfwang@igalia.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Stephen Chenney \u003cschenney@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Wang N\u00e9lar \u003cfwang@igalia.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1680150}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 4bd4ef8b6a2dbb3f4b2bc0b22054db63e2795786\nwpt-pr: 61952\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/svg/idlharness.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/resources/svg-tags.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/svg-element-attributeStyleMap.html"], "git_node": "15e8a5ffdc292561702e60a89868483584df7efd", "git_parents": ["168cd63a14fb4b8f177e7456ec6500c839428bf8"], "node": "b476b8a9aaad21c3c01b4afbf280d56ecd04d8c5", "parents": ["464ee1081468b1410b8f9fb39ce1eb443cbb3b6e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063795 [wpt PR 61961] - Fix chunked parser-blocking scripts in stream*HTMLUnsafe, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFix chunked parser-blocking scripts in stream*HTMLUnsafe\n\nThe state machine had a DCHECK for parser-blocking in the middle of the\nscript, assuming we were not in the fragment parser.\n\nThe DCHECK should specifically allow the parser policy used for\nstreamHTMLUnsafe with runScripts.\n\nBug: 545823947\nChange-Id: If4412d8e781db244349bb4d87184536bf025a85b\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8257431\nCommit-Queue: Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@google.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1680158}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 27c619af234cb834defa10edfc24e92d495adc7f\nwpt-pr: 61961\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/domparsing/tentative/resources/slow.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/domparsing/tentative/stream-html-parser-blocking-script.html"], "git_node": "be27a8b62457bfc33ee65253b098a9c31857cc88", "git_parents": ["15e8a5ffdc292561702e60a89868483584df7efd"], "node": "5ef174eead9d879e4158c0b98c83735ed973e037", "parents": ["b476b8a9aaad21c3c01b4afbf280d56ecd04d8c5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063795 [wpt PR 61961] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61961\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/domparsing/tentative/stream-html-parser-blocking-script.html.ini"], "git_node": "f66913ecaf4b87c4c1d0501fc135db319cbe7479", "git_parents": ["be27a8b62457bfc33ee65253b098a9c31857cc88"], "node": "71d70acff36ec65f89156703e490d57f159e79f9", "parents": ["5ef174eead9d879e4158c0b98c83735ed973e037"], "tags": []}, {"author": "lumiscosity \u003caveryrudelphe@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063841 [wpt PR 61968] - script: Avoid binding link element with empty href, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nadd crashtest\n\nSigned-off-by: lumiscosity \u003caveryrudelphe@gmail.com\u003e\n\n--\nmove test to preload\n\nSigned-off-by: lumiscosity \u003caveryrudelphe@gmail.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 23e8d74c1de414729342b661857711d653d15d92, 0f06c2fe263dad92292a51af330645f2c3126bc2\nwpt-pr: 61968\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/preload/link-preload-empty-href-attribute-crash.html"], "git_node": "671340b0256d9ded31c8215a12e6e536505fa2fb", "git_parents": ["f66913ecaf4b87c4c1d0501fc135db319cbe7479"], "node": "5f5bc1d86636b138a4e12630da4bf22569555a6d", "parents": ["71d70acff36ec65f89156703e490d57f159e79f9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063707 [wpt PR 61943] - Fix some edge cases with nested \u003ctemplate for\u003e and custom elements, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFix some edge cases with nested \u003ctemplate for\u003e and custom elements\n\nMake sure the owner document is correct in that scenario, so that\ncustom elements can be initialized properly.\n\nBug: 431374376\nChange-Id: I05e877fd6f571640000b8211f9854cda3ec125aa\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8250821\nReviewed-by: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@google.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1680219}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 40f78009c81558c6ff89915cb2546c2fe3ef3b97\nwpt-pr: 61943\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/dom/partial-updates/tentative/chained-streaming-templates-with-custom-element.html"], "git_node": "c08d2e6d9a4b96f97c146290b6688fb714d44289", "git_parents": ["671340b0256d9ded31c8215a12e6e536505fa2fb"], "node": "be6c811b6ddfcb4c599f8a23dc037c9bbd3cd678", "parents": ["5f5bc1d86636b138a4e12630da4bf22569555a6d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063707 [wpt PR 61943] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61943\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/dom/partial-updates/tentative/chained-streaming-templates-with-custom-element.html.ini"], "git_node": "7d0a608548ada1f3818ae0bcfdc772bb6ba2ab43", "git_parents": ["c08d2e6d9a4b96f97c146290b6688fb714d44289"], "node": "342d87b4c76a7e2b6edaab15b655e580ef0501b0", "parents": ["be6c811b6ddfcb4c599f8a23dc037c9bbd3cd678"], "tags": []}, {"author": "tannal \u003cmtan@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063819 [wpt PR 61967] - Support `rel` and `relList` IDL attributes for MathMLAnchorElement, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nSupport `rel` and `relList` IDL attributes for MathMLAnchorElement\n\nThis patch exposes the `rel` and `relList` IDL attributes on\nMathMLAnchorElement.\n\nNote that the C++ side processing of `rel` link relations for MathML\nanchor elements was already implemented in a previous patch.[1]\n\nThe implementation is reusing the `AnchorElementUtils` class, which\nis shared by HTML/SVG/MathML anchor element.\n\nThis patch also adds WPT for IDL reflection and navigation tests.\n\n[1] https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/7940188\n\nBug: 510487697\nChange-Id: Ib15827824aece4ec234bfbc781e10fa5634abdec\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8220070\nCommit-Queue: Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Wang N\u00e9lar \u003cfwang@igalia.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Wang N\u00e9lar \u003cfwang@igalia.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Stephen Chenney \u003cschenney@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1680243}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 20a7bd3ff395ff6140de6a566e18d488d8b3c386\nwpt-pr: 61967\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/dom/lists/DOMTokenList-coverage-for-attributes.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/mathml/relations/html5-tree/a-rel-getter-setter.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/mathml/relations/html5-tree/a-rel-policy.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/mathml/relations/html5-tree/support/a-rel-target.html"], "git_node": "b7fe41ccf672461aa86013090adcd4985888053a", "git_parents": ["7d0a608548ada1f3818ae0bcfdc772bb6ba2ab43"], "node": "9fc0bfce2ee38a879a891e652c79694e86deb870", "parents": ["342d87b4c76a7e2b6edaab15b655e580ef0501b0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063819 [wpt PR 61967] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61967\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/dom/lists/DOMTokenList-coverage-for-attributes.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/mathml/relations/html5-tree/a-rel-getter-setter.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/mathml/relations/html5-tree/a-rel-policy.html.ini"], "git_node": "26d795d09781d378336f582a214faa39d780bf7f", "git_parents": ["b7fe41ccf672461aa86013090adcd4985888053a"], "node": "cd86d84783ed769ff1f17643fbc86dbad2dbd385", "parents": ["9fc0bfce2ee38a879a891e652c79694e86deb870"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jiacheng Guo \u003cgjc@google.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063694 [wpt PR 61942] - Use GET request for PreloadActivationReportManager, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nUse GET request for PreloadActivationReportManager\n\nUpdates PreloadActivationReportManager to send GET requests instead of\nHEAD requests for activation report beacons.\n\nThis updates PreloadActivationReportManager to issue credentialless GET\nrequests when reporting page activation, updates redirect validations\nto preserve the GET method, and updates associated unit, browser,\nand WPT tests.\n\nBug: 546370728\nChange-Id: Ib9aa6ee38d2303f55b8b42b9ba19fa7a8cd0d6fc\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8260309\nReviewed-by: Hiroki Nakagawa \u003cnhiroki@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Jiacheng Guo \u003cgjc@google.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1680304}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 0cc6a7e1904a69dae98c86412b15bc81256279f8\nwpt-pr: 61942\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/speculation-rules/activation-header/resources/activation_beacon.py"], "git_node": "dfd6ec6e0d68e44e8e73737dea32d9fe279950b3", "git_parents": ["26d795d09781d378336f582a214faa39d780bf7f"], "node": "33bee4c8349b71a71f3ae6d6afcc3df987084061", "parents": ["cd86d84783ed769ff1f17643fbc86dbad2dbd385"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Karl Dubost \u003ckarlcow@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063942 [wpt PR 61979] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=321588, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=321588 (#61979)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: fac2c0e60863e8a831cf0059540f52074d678ab8\nwpt-pr: 61979\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/CSS2/visufx/visibility-descendants-002-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/CSS2/visufx/visibility-descendants-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/CSS2/visufx/visibility-descendants-003-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/CSS2/visufx/visibility-descendants-003.html"], "git_node": "90a74f16c4dd6978367b9b6f565397995fe6b9d5", "git_parents": ["dfd6ec6e0d68e44e8e73737dea32d9fe279950b3"], "node": "17fae87dfd67ac21cf810e412ec584f4d1cc8b61", "parents": ["33bee4c8349b71a71f3ae6d6afcc3df987084061"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063942 [wpt PR 61979] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61979\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/CSS2/visufx/visibility-descendants-002.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/CSS2/visufx/visibility-descendants-003.html.ini"], "git_node": "fa74a6a711af4ce7d025abca31cf959258e6e096", "git_parents": ["90a74f16c4dd6978367b9b6f565397995fe6b9d5"], "node": "f4bb56edeb9a39e472f4eaa334531f6d4fe6d7d4", "parents": ["17fae87dfd67ac21cf810e412ec584f4d1cc8b61"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tim van der Lippe \u003ctvanderlippe@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063888 [wpt PR 61969] - script: Fix iframe name for initial navigation, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nscript: Fix iframe name for initial navigation\n\nDuring the initial load of an iframe, the name wasn't\navailable yet. Now, we set the name immediately when\ncreating the child navigable, following the spec.\n\nFixes #47259\n\nTesting: new WPT passes\n\nCo-authored-by: Josh Matthews \u003cjosh@joshmatthews.net\u003e\nSigned-off-by: Tim van der Lippe \u003ctvanderlippe@gmail.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 839aa8b291e849230055c253b7f086f458044f85\nwpt-pr: 61969\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/browsers/browsing-the-web/history-traversal/window-name-after-cross-origin-sub-frame-navigation.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/browsers/browsing-the-web/history-traversal/window-name-after-same-origin-sub-frame-navigation.sub.html"], "git_node": "f6e0c89482b1aa9026d1d5c3741c1234a847386d", "git_parents": ["fa74a6a711af4ce7d025abca31cf959258e6e096"], "node": "6f11d1cfe089783159e8f176c4b56c4950ecbf9f", "parents": ["f4bb56edeb9a39e472f4eaa334531f6d4fe6d7d4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yoshisto Yanagisawa \u003cyyanagisawa@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063600 [wpt PR 61938] - Implement async AllowStorageAccess in Service and Shared Worker content settings proxies, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nImplement async AllowStorageAccess in Service and Shared Worker content settings proxies\n\nPreviously, ServiceWorkerContentSettingsProxy and\nSharedWorkerContentSettingsProxy only overrode the synchronous\nAllowStorageAccessSync method from WebContentSettingsClient, relying on\nthe base default implementation for asynchronous queries. Additionally,\nsynchronous checks for CacheStorage and WebLocks were not routed through\nthe IPC proxy in ServiceWorkerContentSettingsProxy.\n\nThis CL implements the asynchronous AllowStorageAccess method in both\nproxy classes to route IndexedDB, CacheStorage, and WebLocks queries to\nthe browser process via Mojo IPC. This ensures consistent and accurate\ncontent settings evaluation across both synchronous and asynchronous\nAPIs. It also adds the missing synchronous IPC routings for CacheStorage\nand WebLocks in ServiceWorkerContentSettingsProxy.\n\nA unit test is added to verify that storage access queries in\nServiceWorkerContentSettingsProxy correctly propagate responses from\nthe browser process.\n\nTAG=agy\nCONV=afbe35fe-485c-4ef6-853f-1874ce409f0e\n\nBug: 503624894\nChange-Id: I4d9e862a2b88c71f628afba61ab706d0180c1e4d\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8062387\nReviewed-by: Hiroki Nakagawa \u003cnhiroki@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Yoshisato Yanagisawa \u003cyyanagisawa@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Hidehiko Abe \u003chidehiko@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1680367}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: b80a9ddcbae8b5a7b5d9b1425ca9862a990dabbe\nwpt-pr: 61938\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/IndexedDB/idbfactory_open.any.js"], "git_node": "ddc337c1992efe04736e5eeb57f147f3fd14cc96", "git_parents": ["f6e0c89482b1aa9026d1d5c3741c1234a847386d"], "node": "bd9ec30cd1289381d83b80cba52bc6cbec87f76a", "parents": ["6f11d1cfe089783159e8f176c4b56c4950ecbf9f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Morten Stenshorne \u003cmstensho@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063474 [wpt PR 61930] - Remove support for \"inline*\" values in margin-trim., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nRemove support for \"inline*\" values in margin-trim.\n\nSee https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/13731\n\nSince margin-trim now only applies to block containers and multicol\ncontainers, inline margins may never be trimmable (that was only\npossible with flex and grid).\n\nBug: 40886857\nChange-Id: Ic7d2f1b9149cceab3bc8274cf33072a602569760\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8256869\nReviewed-by: Ian Kilpatrick \u003cikilpatrick@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Morten Stenshorne \u003cmstensho@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1680433}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: cfe661184a504e4b992c4599ab233153686e7cfa\nwpt-pr: 61930\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-box/parsing/margin-trim-computed.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-box/parsing/margin-trim.html"], "git_node": "9c6670bbcdb68043c61c6efbc4306a2641594bfe", "git_parents": ["ddc337c1992efe04736e5eeb57f147f3fd14cc96"], "node": "478cb8b0399f4469e72b98d007a34c7096d5f81c", "parents": ["bd9ec30cd1289381d83b80cba52bc6cbec87f76a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Morten Stenshorne \u003cmstensho@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063927 [wpt PR 61975] - [RouteMatching] href attribute changes may affect :link-to() matching., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[RouteMatching] href attribute changes may affect :link-to() matching.\n\nThere was no support for this. Yet, we had a passing test for it in\nwpt_internal/ . When attempting to move it into external/wpt/ it started\nfailing. Not sure why this passed at all.\n\nPseudoStateChanged() needs to be called with CSSSelector::kPseudoLinkTo\nwhen the href attribute on a link changes.\n\nBug: 436805487\nChange-Id: I8c6a1efe095129d5eed2531ca39118c5058f9d3c\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8243771\nReviewed-by: Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@google.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Morten Stenshorne \u003cmstensho@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1680448}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 2956deb44ab8bdbab5fff3e558d9db14eac5d960\nwpt-pr: 61975\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-navigation/tentative/link-to-004.html"], "git_node": "f5742b6facfd398a6fb3241fd77f18bed792894b", "git_parents": ["9c6670bbcdb68043c61c6efbc4306a2641594bfe"], "node": "3aaebc5249169739274c952f1cde770196ed2360", "parents": ["478cb8b0399f4469e72b98d007a34c7096d5f81c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063927 [wpt PR 61975] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61975\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-navigation/tentative/link-to-004.html.ini"], "git_node": "17f52ee2c013844bf34367f6002b8f93ab0f46d5", "git_parents": ["f5742b6facfd398a6fb3241fd77f18bed792894b"], "node": "43f4497a99ea829668ed7124010005a9705fba8e", "parents": ["3aaebc5249169739274c952f1cde770196ed2360"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Josh Matthews \u003cjosh@joshmatthews.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063966 [wpt PR 61982] - wpt: Make domInteractive timing tests fail better., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nwpt: Make domInteractive timing tests fail better.\n\nSigned-off-by: Josh Matthews \u003cjosh@joshmatthews.net\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 3a433f07ee607c41cf46d5a2860a486603cd3f59\nwpt-pr: 61982\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/navigation-timing/dom-interactive-image-document.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/navigation-timing/dom-interactive-media-document.html"], "git_node": "0074ef66e08af32be5a894ceef27d296b2a4d334", "git_parents": ["17f52ee2c013844bf34367f6002b8f93ab0f46d5"], "node": "a3a81639444fef14f3b1ea9c32db728b409a87d1", "parents": ["43f4497a99ea829668ed7124010005a9705fba8e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Josh Matthews \u003cjosh@joshmatthews.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063954 [wpt PR 61981] - wpt: Ensure javascript: URL produces a load event., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nwpt: Ensure javascript: URL produces a load event.\n\nSigned-off-by: Josh Matthews \u003cjosh@joshmatthews.net\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 3c11bf94db7b80098659b37d66d119f2a10ae122\nwpt-pr: 61981\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/fetch/fetch-later/new-window.https.window.js"], "git_node": "8f3600a8f0acdd606a0436506040c35a9f83689c", "git_parents": ["0074ef66e08af32be5a894ceef27d296b2a4d334"], "node": "e4836baed6c997618c38339804fdcd6101d9435d", "parents": ["a3a81639444fef14f3b1ea9c32db728b409a87d1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chris Thompson \u003ccthomp@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064045 [wpt PR 61985] - Support targetAddressSpace in WebSocket constructor, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nSupport targetAddressSpace in WebSocket constructor\n\nThis CL adds support for the targetAddressSpace option in the WebSocket\nconstructor's option bag, guarded by the\nLocalNetworkAccessWebSocketsTargetAddressSpace runtime feature.\n\nThe target address space is propagated to the network service's\nWebSocket implementation, where it is used to perform Local Network\nAccess (LNA) checks. Web platform tests and unit tests are added to\nverify the new functionality.\n\nChromeStatus entry: https://chromestatus.com/feature/4779920606756864\n\nIntent-to-Prototype:\nhttps://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/g/blink-dev/c/hVlq3XXExbU/m/FqxRLh0yBwAJ\n\nTAG=agy\nCONV=d49fff98-9ad5-4ac6-8a3f-c6022b98b1f9\n\nBug: 517413738\nBinary-Size: Generated base::Feature in features_generated.cc false-positive on mutable constants check.\nChange-Id: I9cff805719e3817d71fa12dbafaa3f086a7bbc48\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8191301\nReviewed-by: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Nate Chapin \u003cjaphet@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Ken Buchanan \u003ckenrb@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Mike Wittman \u003cwittman@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Ken Buchanan \u003ckenrb@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Chris Thompson \u003ccthomp@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Christian Dullweber \u003cdullweber@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1680595}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 3de9d775d719b1cd3b2bb8512baa83ef58b2c6dd\nwpt-pr: 61985\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/websockets/constructor/target-address-space.any.js"], "git_node": "9ec5c612c563559894d31ec5e56426976e746908", "git_parents": ["8f3600a8f0acdd606a0436506040c35a9f83689c"], "node": "c6f2fb4d93fe62ce32d3d6911b9e5348777612a5", "parents": ["e4836baed6c997618c38339804fdcd6101d9435d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064045 [wpt PR 61985] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61985\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/websockets/constructor/target-address-space.any.js.ini"], "git_node": "4c9cc69599d436aaf365309cd3f71a0950773001", "git_parents": ["9ec5c612c563559894d31ec5e56426976e746908"], "node": "91a81271e096b2e2d34ccf56ece4c26a3a154ed9", "parents": ["c6f2fb4d93fe62ce32d3d6911b9e5348777612a5"],