71273ed529cb3fe69dcc06c4d18ca42d3c051c38", "parents": ["0eed59f29af7f5594c89415e75a2992e84da792d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Serban Stanca \u003csstanca@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2062209, Bug 2064279, Bug 2064185, Bug 2062987, Bug 2064277, Bug 2064276 - Scope the Urlbar actor to about:newtab and about:home. r=mconley,mbeier\" for causing mochitests failures in browser_searchbar_new.js.\n\nThis reverts commit e00a96bdf858dcb6fc29e585ef2f4f7fa72be048.\n\nThis reverts commit 69cdce10fed3779a93074dcc505acdf5d1114e81.\n\nThis reverts commit f1b48ae625b036bd642a34e44b13b35cbe714340.\n\nThis reverts commit e4fbb3f30c8e6cfee292f757516aa247e533b868.\n\nThis reverts commit d7435c3ede7e687f7fbcba938dbebf97968e78b1.\n\nThis reverts commit e0baa9504fa5f28c20496dcf8ac642cd49c5c412.\n\nThis reverts commit aa895826ce3d1c232358408e254d2127727db459.\n\nThis reverts commit e7e50f5e61bad7ee664a371954c9893b7e1d292a.\n\nThis reverts commit 56467e58ed367be5f21b138eb564f3e1804c26d8.\n\nThis reverts commit fcee5de428a020254b167e92a84e4e85932ab130.\n", "files": ["browser/actors/UrlbarChild.sys.mjs", "browser/base/content/browser-toolbarKeyNav.js", "browser/components/DesktopActorRegistry.sys.mjs", "browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_ext_tabs_create_url.js", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarChildController.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarContentPrefs.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInputBase.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarShared.mjs", "toolkit/content/editMenuOverlay.js"], "git_node": "4abe827f6c93b7fdc58e3001ede9c485519611ad", "git_parents": ["f8193142ac81ce0393d8fff03f5c1ca0c451f062"], "node": "2ba38cc409302e69d7c49953bc2e825ad9836660", "parents": ["71273ed529cb3fe69dcc06c4d18ca42d3c051c38"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Vincent Hilla \u003cvhilla@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055693 - Remove dead javascript: URI handling in LoadHistoryEntry. r=nika\n\nPer spec, javascript: URIs are never stored in SH. Neither has this code test\ncoverage, nor does the test on the bug that introduced it still pass.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314860\n", "files": ["docshell/base/nsDocShell.cpp", "docshell/shistory/SessionHistoryEntry.cpp"], "git_node": "45623555c7da72196c4490060c3b251e10cdad5e", "git_parents": ["4abe827f6c93b7fdc58e3001ede9c485519611ad"], "node": "2dfc69e678d8d8cd3760eb2e60ddc034bd855d04", "parents": ["2ba38cc409302e69d7c49953bc2e825ad9836660"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kershaw Chang \u003ckershaw@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058660 -  Retarget WebTransportSessionProxy before activating queued streams, r=necko-reviewers,jesup\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315245\n", "files": ["netwerk/protocol/webtransport/WebTransportSessionProxy.cpp"], "git_node": "b3ff65bfcf2872751eb94d5ec620e7e1754cd616", "git_parents": ["45623555c7da72196c4490060c3b251e10cdad5e"], "node": "03705f23d42527ef6cae279f05f3fad8f20b2c66", "parents": ["2dfc69e678d8d8cd3760eb2e60ddc034bd855d04"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063238 - doc: drop the GeckoView copy of the Firefox contributor guide r=nalexander,geckoview-reviewers DONTBUILD\n\nmobile/android/docs/geckoview/contributor/contributing-to-firefox.md was\ntitled \"Firefox Contributor Guide\" and contained nothing specific to\nGeckoView. It re-explained finding a bug, commit access levels,\nclang-format, pushing to try, creating a Phabricator account, submitting\nwith moz-phab and updating a patch, all of which docs/contributing covers.\n\nParts of the copy had gone stale and actively misled readers:\n\n- it told contributors to run \"pip install MozPhab\", while the tree\n  documents \"./mach install-moz-phab\"\n- it described commit access in terms of \"any mercurial or SVN\n  repository\" and \"Fennec\", and its level 1/2/3 descriptions disagreed\n  with contributing/levelling-up.md\n\nRemove the page and point its three referrers at docs/contributing\ninstead. Add a redirect so the published URL keeps working.\n\nThe three Phabricator registration screenshots it carried are removed\ntoo, as nothing else referenced them. The page also had two\n\"\u003cScreenshot Needed\u003e\" placeholders that were never filled in.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318453\n", "files": ["docs/config.yml", "mobile/android/docs/geckoview/assets/LogInBugzilla.png", "mobile/android/docs/geckoview/assets/LogInOrRegister.png", "mobile/android/docs/geckoview/assets/LogInPhab.png", "mobile/android/docs/geckoview/contributor/contributing-to-firefox.md", "mobile/android/docs/geckoview/contributor/geckoview-quick-start.md", "mobile/android/docs/geckoview/contributor/index.md", "mobile/android/docs/index.md"], "git_node": "750ccd686e5c2c2c3f248ac199845a199b1310fb", "git_parents": ["b3ff65bfcf2872751eb94d5ec620e7e1754cd616"], "node": "c91db0112aaf801899c3a5774d35fd69f0038243", "parents": ["03705f23d42527ef6cae279f05f3fad8f20b2c66"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Hommey \u003cmh+mozilla@glandium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062662 - Avoid a memset_pattern16 libcall in the collator's CollationElements::new. r=hsivonen\n\nrustc lowers the `['\\u{FFFF}'; 2]` array repeat expression in\n`CollationElements::new` to a two-iteration store loop, which LLVM ends\nup lowering to a `memset_pattern16` libcall, so every call ends up\ncalling into libSystem in order to initialise 8 bytes of stack.\n\nWriting the array out element by element gives a plain 8-byte immediate\nstore instead.\n\nThe exact conditions that trigger LLVM's behavior are still under\ninvestigation.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319664\n", "files": ["third_party/rust/icu_collator/src/elements.rs"], "git_node": "abdf99010e551c67a385f711f2efef132ca6d607", "git_parents": ["750ccd686e5c2c2c3f248ac199845a199b1310fb"], "node": "4444a82ee115c91029be5e9ab77ffffe600646a5", "parents": ["c91db0112aaf801899c3a5774d35fd69f0038243"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chris Vander Linden \u003ccvanderl@uiowa.edu\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063466 - Fix FileSearchBar nav button hover styling. r=devtools-reviewers,nchevobbe\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318823\n", "files": ["devtools/client/shared/components/SearchInput.css"], "git_node": "e157fac4e6ed132ebf4360b867533d25475eb2eb", "git_parents": ["abdf99010e551c67a385f711f2efef132ca6d607"], "node": "9926e5750ce69e6d83dc33ee85d90504ca231a2c", "parents": ["4444a82ee115c91029be5e9ab77ffffe600646a5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "serge-sans-paille \u003csguelton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063976 - Fix performance-unnecessary-copy-initialization warning in accessible r=emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319019\n", "files": ["accessible/ipc/RemoteAccessible.cpp"], "git_node": "3c1eff617e8b02573ca99fe9532116dd61a3ebdf", "git_parents": ["e157fac4e6ed132ebf4360b867533d25475eb2eb"], "node": "5d1bf6d43d87eaff21e58f41028c90b48abe3315", "parents": ["9926e5750ce69e6d83dc33ee85d90504ca231a2c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "serge-sans-paille \u003csguelton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063976 - Fix performance-unnecessary-copy-initialization warning in devtools r=emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319020\n", "files": ["devtools/shared/heapsnapshot/HeapSnapshot.cpp"], "git_node": "5991dee4fbdec1b0eae716f52695d550326cb159", "git_parents": ["3c1eff617e8b02573ca99fe9532116dd61a3ebdf"], "node": "79ab7c5a6330724fa92317b5ca32097a48fa7949", "parents": ["5d1bf6d43d87eaff21e58f41028c90b48abe3315"], "tags": []}, {"author": "serge-sans-paille \u003csguelton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063976 - Fix performance-unnecessary-copy-initialization warning in netwerk r=cookie-reviewers,valentin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319021\n", "files": ["netwerk/cookie/CookieServiceChild.cpp"], "git_node": "39bdd04cc47c2369f996b5147910afc1825ef7d8", "git_parents": ["5991dee4fbdec1b0eae716f52695d550326cb159"], "node": "ec214d077e60aca65f627ff2919f9189514a01d0", "parents": ["79ab7c5a6330724fa92317b5ca32097a48fa7949"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan-Erik Rediger \u003cjrediger@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064328 - Update h2 r=aryx,supply-chain-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319479\n", "files": ["Cargo.lock", "supply-chain/imports.lock", "third_party/rust/h2/.cargo-checksum.json", "third_party/rust/h2/.cargo_vcs_info.json", "third_party/rust/h2/.github/workflows/CI.yml", "third_party/rust/h2/CHANGELOG.md", "third_party/rust/h2/Cargo.lock", "third_party/rust/h2/Cargo.toml", "third_party/rust/h2/Cargo.toml.orig", "third_party/rust/h2/benches/main.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/client.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/codec/framed_read.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/codec/framed_write.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/codec/mod.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/frame/data.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/frame/headers.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/frame/mod.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/fuzz_bridge.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/hpack/decoder.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/hpack/encoder.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/hpack/huffman/mod.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/hpack/huffman/table.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/hpack/test/fixture.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/hpack/test/fuzz.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/lib.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/proto/connection.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/proto/mod.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/proto/streams/counts.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/proto/streams/mod.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/proto/streams/prioritize.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/proto/streams/recv.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/proto/streams/send.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/proto/streams/state.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/proto/streams/stream.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/proto/streams/streams.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/server.rs", "third_party/rust/h2/src/share.rs"], "git_node": "bfce76f4173745190a0a48bc2877a8ecafc0a878", "git_parents": ["39bdd04cc47c2369f996b5147910afc1825ef7d8"], "node": "c4114f0bcda7f6c763c5dc688bc59d023ed4fd37", "parents": ["ec214d077e60aca65f627ff2919f9189514a01d0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062572 - Fail tests that click inside a popup that is not open, r=firefox-desktop-core-reviewers ,mossop.\n\nA popup's contents are only interactive once it is open, so a click that lands\nin one that is still opening silently does nothing, and the test carries on as\nif it had. That is a source of low frequency intermittent failures, of which the\na11y checks were the only smoke: they run on a subset of the configurations and\nreport it as \"Node is not focusable via the accessibility API\", which sends\npeople looking for a missing tabindex.\n\nCheck it on every click in browser-chrome instead. This is a new file rather\nthan part of AccessibilityUtils, which only runs under a11y_checks.\n\nClicks on a node with no box are reported as a todo rather than a failure: those\nare popups the test never opened, which is the same mistake but too widespread\nto fail on yet, see bug 2063575.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317772\n", "files": ["testing/mochitest/browser-test.js", "testing/mochitest/moz.build", "testing/mochitest/tests/SimpleTest/ClickChecks.js", "testing/mochitest/tests/SimpleTest/EventUtils.js", "testing/mochitest/tests/SimpleTest/moz.build"], "git_node": "d9012211d4b9ccc9a53cf7d20fe47cf1cedbd6ca", "git_parents": ["bfce76f4173745190a0a48bc2877a8ecafc0a878"], "node": "86e264bf3f48b7b4767939eaba6e8ecbb26e371e", "parents": ["c4114f0bcda7f6c763c5dc688bc59d023ed4fd37"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064276 - Parse the input's markup with DOMParser. r=mbeier,urlbar-reviewers\n\n`parseXULToFragment` is chrome-only, as a content document can hold no XUL elements at all. So both realms parse with `DOMParser`, the markup naming the XHTML namespace by default and its one XUL element with a `xul:` prefix, which content resolves to XHTML.\n\nDropping the `html:` prefixes breaks whatever matched a qualified name, hence the fixes alongside.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319331\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser-toolbarKeyNav.js", "browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_ext_tabs_create_url.js", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInputBase.mjs", "toolkit/content/editMenuOverlay.js"], "git_node": "6f9220dcc14be23d5a39a4ace0145e8bbe2455ef", "git_parents": ["d9012211d4b9ccc9a53cf7d20fe47cf1cedbd6ca"], "node": "6f131671631beb1b206afb9130b46d3de3c9560b", "parents": ["86e264bf3f48b7b4767939eaba6e8ecbb26e371e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064276 - Drop the markup's whitespace text nodes. r=mbeier\n\n`DOMParser` keeps the whitespace between the markup's elements, and those text nodes change the accessibility tree the input exposes: the search bar gains an empty section child, which `browser_searchbar_new.js` catches. Only a build slow enough to assert the tree before it settles sees it, so opt is green while asan, tsan and debug fail; `MOZ_CHAOSMODE` with `--repeat` reproduces it on an opt build.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319669\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInputBase.mjs"], "git_node": "e3871704dde74a22fcb78aebf4303344450f1e19", "git_parents": ["6f9220dcc14be23d5a39a4ace0145e8bbe2455ef"], "node": "7a54558aa3b3832d22a590d4a8a25484c0945188", "parents": ["6f131671631beb1b206afb9130b46d3de3c9560b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064277 - Clone parent-sent payloads into the content realm. r=mbeier\n\nThe port's returns are already cloned; the parent's dispatches into the child controller weren't, so a content-realm input saw an Xray over an object in this realm and was denied even `Symbol.iterator` -- iterating the engine-store snapshot threw.\n\n`Notify` has the same gap and isn't fixed here: it carries a `UrlbarQueryContext` that `fromWire` builds in this realm, and cloning would flatten it. Content has the class, so deserializing there is likely the answer.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319332\n", "files": ["browser/actors/UrlbarChild.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "de9e8ba6b7a689b11d2e7173868af7398f7cbee9", "git_parents": ["e3871704dde74a22fcb78aebf4303344450f1e19"], "node": "93e144ed07d8f97832272da09321153360bceb8d", "parents": ["7a54558aa3b3832d22a590d4a8a25484c0945188"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064277 - Build the query context in the realm that reads it. r=mbeier,urlbar-reviewers\n\nThe remaining half of the previous patch, and the one a clone can't fix: the actor deserialized the wire form into a `UrlbarQueryContext` in its own realm, so a content-realm view got an Xray over it. That reads every property as `undefined` rather than throwing, so a query produced no rows and no error.\n\nThe wire form is plain data, so it crosses as one and the child controller builds the context from it, in an entry point of its own so that `notify` takes a real context whichever path delivered it. That has to happen before `notify` inspects `id` to drop the results of a stale query.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319413\n", "files": ["browser/actors/UrlbarChild.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarChildController.mjs"], "git_node": "85259daf3a6feb16001501aced19e3e02ad6c056", "git_parents": ["de9e8ba6b7a689b11d2e7173868af7398f7cbee9"], "node": "d1fc19ef81b3ae8cfd4053107fe33f1ed4c3fbce", "parents": ["93e144ed07d8f97832272da09321153360bceb8d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064279 - Gate the copy/cut controller on the address bar. r=mbeier,urlbar-reviewers\n\n`_trimValue` returns early unless the input is the address bar, so on the searchbar the controller only reimplements native copy/cut.\n\nThis is what lets a content-realm input work without a realm branch here: the controller needs `controllers` and `editor` on the input plus the clipboard service, all chrome-only.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319333\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInputBase.mjs"], "git_node": "4ef9eb707145832c2a8a961317f47800022c8ddc", "git_parents": ["85259daf3a6feb16001501aced19e3e02ad6c056"], "node": "58018de9cba7acd0b49169b8d1984bc835ff2db6", "parents": ["d1fc19ef81b3ae8cfd4053107fe33f1ed4c3fbce"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064279 - Defer the placeholder update to a tab switch only in the address bar. r=mbeier,urlbar-reviewers\n\nThe update waits for the user to look away, and a tab switch qualifies only for the address bar, which takes its value from the selected tab. Nothing gives the searchbar a value on `TabSelect`, so its listener could only ever fire with the guard already false -- and by then the `input` listener has removed both.\n\nA content-realm input, not being the address bar, is left with the same single cue, which is what this needs to not reach for a tabbrowser it doesn't have.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319334\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInputBase.mjs"], "git_node": "cc877b194274934219c63e161c92fe662e1a1c98", "git_parents": ["4ef9eb707145832c2a8a961317f47800022c8ddc"], "node": "d597e8bc5bc4301d9b20a4ec37c112165c591928", "parents": ["58018de9cba7acd0b49169b8d1984bc835ff2db6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064185 - Observe the AI window's state only from a chrome window. r=mbeier,urlbar-reviewers\n\n`observe` matches the notification's subject against the input's own window, so a content-realm input could never match it -- and `generateQI` and the observer service are chrome-only, so reaching for them threw before the engine-store observer below could be registered. That one a content realm does need.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319335\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInputBase.mjs"], "git_node": "77413f0a5fc42f3da119e4205876811966cfbff5", "git_parents": ["cc877b194274934219c63e161c92fe662e1a1c98"], "node": "d3f10b89b9a4a850952670e64ea9aa9f4d5b17e9", "parents": ["d597e8bc5bc4301d9b20a4ec37c112165c591928"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062987 - Give the content prefs shim getScotchBonnetPref. r=mbeier,urlbar-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319408\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarContentPrefs.mjs"], "git_node": "9e158acf0ff97f73d44485745e880170fa23e379", "git_parents": ["77413f0a5fc42f3da119e4205876811966cfbff5"], "node": "e28abfc8f4ef269c4e11aa1920715265fca39de2", "parents": ["d3f10b89b9a4a850952670e64ea9aa9f4d5b17e9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064185 - Read the default user context id without Ci. r=mbeier,urlbar-reviewers\n\n`UrlbarQueryContext`'s constructor normalizes the container id, so this sits on the path of every query -- a content-realm input couldn't run one at all. The value is spelled out beside the private-window sentinel the same file already carries.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319409\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarShared.mjs"], "git_node": "94c61e00ae3537ab448ea3c91c65b5d572d9a4a2", "git_parents": ["9e158acf0ff97f73d44485745e880170fa23e379"], "node": "227b02e057c10725a211f58fd637671da15df597", "parents": ["e28abfc8f4ef269c4e11aa1920715265fca39de2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064279 - Gate the search-terms persistence check on the address bar. r=mbeier,urlbar-reviewers\n\nIts state is keyed by the selected tab's browser, which a content-realm input has no way to reach.\n\n`handleEvent` wraps every `_on_*` in a try/catch and reports through `console.error`, so the exception left `_on_input` silently half-done: typing updated the value and started no query, with nothing in the parent-process log.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319410\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInputBase.mjs"], "git_node": "85641c7382b350a7bf99e68d845034e9c4966476", "git_parents": ["94c61e00ae3537ab448ea3c91c65b5d572d9a4a2"], "node": "2badfba80ef907a6a7eaded4584403bc498a5404", "parents": ["227b02e057c10725a211f58fd637671da15df597"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062209 - Scope the Urlbar actor to about:newtab and about:home. r=mconley,mbeier\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318748\n", "files": ["browser/actors/UrlbarChild.sys.mjs", "browser/components/DesktopActorRegistry.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "2249487a6342b58457ad6ef278f04dda550e1b92", "git_parents": ["85641c7382b350a7bf99e68d845034e9c4966476"], "node": "c7442cd238804015be9501d047436c512379468d", "parents": ["2badfba80ef907a6a7eaded4584403bc498a5404"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Keith Cirkel \u003ckeithamus@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064333 - Turn scoped registries on for nightly builds r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319462\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "testing/web-platform/meta/dom/idlharness.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/dom/idlharness.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "689c96ae48e835fc2d97e5ab4df74762d0403d7e", "git_parents": ["2249487a6342b58457ad6ef278f04dda550e1b92"], "node": "52bd03b8d67394c72c25af43b50a943705434583", "parents": ["c7442cd238804015be9501d047436c512379468d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063223 - [efficiency] Convert TranslationsTest.verifyTheDownloadLanguagesFunctionalityTest to ui/efficiency r=ajoltan\n\nDrives the same path as the legacy test: load a foreign-language page, open the translations options\nsheet, enter Translation settings, open Download languages, download a language.\n\nAdds TRANSLATION_SETTINGS_BUTTON for the options sheet, a pure languageToDownload(language) selector\nfor a row in the list, and ANY_LANGUAGE_DOWNLOADED.\n\nThe final assertion is deliberately stronger than the legacy one rather than a faithful port.\nverifyDownloadedLanguage(\"Bosnian\") re-matched the same content-description substring as the click\ntarget immediately above it, so it held whether or not anything downloaded \u2014 the test could not fail\nfor the reason it existed to catch. The port keeps that check and adds one that only holds once a\nmodel is really on disk.\n\nAsserting the downloaded state is less direct than it looks. Each row encodes it in its content\ndescription as \"\u003clanguage\u003e \u003csize\u003e\" plus \"Download\" or \"Delete\", so a content-description substring of\n\"Delete\" matches both the language row and the \"Delete all languages\" bulk row; Compose surfaces that\nambiguity as \"not found\", which reads exactly like a failed download (gotcha A41, and it cost a cycle\nhere). The bulk row's own label instead switches from \"All languages\" to \"Delete all languages\" only\nonce something is downloaded, so its text carries the state unambiguously and without depending on the\nsize, which comes from the models list.\n\nThe assertion is not vacuous: the app is not installed between runs, so each run starts from a fresh\nprofile and that row can only appear because the run itself downloaded a model.\n\nTwo clean runs on device, no retries.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319313\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/TranslationsTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/SettingsTranslationSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/TranslationsSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/TranslationsTest.kt"], "git_node": "af3efb5634c0dceb717c65fcc32547efbf1f99ea", "git_parents": ["689c96ae48e835fc2d97e5ab4df74762d0403d7e"], "node": "87aa009ad606c95e99aa60b437567ddc706a5736", "parents": ["52bd03b8d67394c72c25af43b50a943705434583"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063228 - [efficiency] Convert TranslationsTest.verifyTheNeverTranslateOptionTest to ui/efficiency r=ajoltan\n\nSets Never translate for the detected language from the translations options sheet, confirms it is\nreflected under Translation settings \u003e Automatic translation, then confirms a second page in that\nlanguage no longer offers to translate.\n\nBoth legacy checked-state assertions located their toggle purely by POSITION \u2014\nUiSelector().index(4) and index(2) on className android.view.View, with no identity \u2014 so a port that\nmatched on the visible label alone would have silently dropped them. They are now anchored to the row.\n\nGetting that right needed two things that are easy to get wrong:\n\n- The state is `semantics { selected = checked; role = Role.Switch }` on the row, and the Switch itself\n  is blanked with clearAndSetSemantics, so no ToggleableState exists anywhere in the tree and\n  assertIsOn can never pass. The assertion is on `selected`, not `checked`.\n- That state lives on the MERGED row node, which absorbs its label. COMPOSE_BY_TEXT forces\n  useUnmergedTree and therefore resolves a stateless descendant, reporting the row as simply \"not\n  checked\" \u2014 indistinguishable from a real failure. COMPOSE_BY_TEXT_MERGED is required. The second row\n  is a RadioButtonListItem rather than a switch, and its \"\u003clabel\u003e.radio.button\" testTag survives a\n  clearAndSetSemantics that strips the state, so that tag identifies the icon but cannot be asserted\n  against. No product-code change is needed once the merged tree is used.\n\nTwo further deviations from legacy, both deliberate:\n\n- The Automatic translation list is alphabetical and long, so the row starts below the fold. Legacy\n  scrolled only as a side effect of the retry loop inside its assertion; this scrolls explicitly and\n  keeps the assertion an assertion.\n- The final check used assertIsNotDisplayed with no wait, which Compose also satisfies when the node is\n  merely absent \u2014 so it could hold before the prompt had any chance to appear. It now waits out the\n  offer window and requires the sheet to never show.\n\nAlso adds a ScreenDump to mozVerifyElementIsChecked / mozVerifyElementIsNotChecked on failure. Every\nother verb dumps; these did not, so a checked-state failure produced no snapshot at all and could not\ndistinguish \"the toggle is off\" from \"this selector matched a label while the state lives elsewhere\".\nThat dump is what identified the merged-tree cause here, in one run rather than several.\n\nTwo clean runs on device, no retries.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319314\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/TranslationsTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/SettingsTranslationSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/TranslationsSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/TranslationsTest.kt"], "git_node": "8cdfce27a2e13d3f3c439cb2f732fbf6a511ee41", "git_parents": ["af3efb5634c0dceb717c65fcc32547efbf1f99ea"], "node": "fd15b3de3804b70184dd44bcc3dbbb479e2f277f", "parents": ["87aa009ad606c95e99aa60b437567ddc706a5736"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063232 - [efficiency] Convert CustomTabsTest.verifyLoginSaveInCustomTabTest to ui/efficiency r=ajoltan\n\nSubmits a login form inside a custom tab, saves it, re-enters the app through an external link, and\nconfirms the login is listed under Saved passwords.\n\nAdds CustomTabsPage.openUrlFromExternalLink(url), an ACTION_VIEW intent scoped to Firefox. Deliberately\ndistinct from the custom tab's own \"Open in Firefox\" menu item, which hands over the existing tab: a test\nthat means to exercise the external entry point cannot substitute one for the other. Not a\nNavigationRegistry edge, for the same reason launchCustomTab is not \u2014 it is an intent, not a click-path.\n\nThe login-form helpers are reused from BrowserPage rather than reimplemented on CustomTabsPage. They act\non device-wide web-id selectors, so they work inside a custom tab \u2014 the same reason\nCustomTabsPage.clickWebContent delegates to BrowserPageSelectors \u2014 and setLoginFormCredentials carries\nretry logic for a form that can reload and silently drop what was typed.\n\nThe route to Saved passwords is driven click-by-click instead of navigateToPage(). Every registered edge\nto SettingsSavedPasswordsPage ends in ClickIfPresent on the security dialog's Later button, so navigating\nthere would dismiss the dialog before it could be asserted \u2014 silently dropping a legacy assertion. This\nis the one place where the convenient path would have cost coverage.\n\nThree legacy assertions could not fail for the reason they were written, and are strengthened:\n\n- The save-prompt check asserted only the prompt container, which the preceding wait had already\n  required, so it was a tautology. The port also asserts the Save button, which the next click depends on.\n- The final check was a device-wide By.text wait rather than an assertion, and the same screen shows the\n  login's origin, so it could hold on the wrong row. The port asserts the saved-login entry scoped to the\n  list.\n- Nothing asserted that the external link reopened the app, so a failure there surfaced later and\n  obscurely. The port requires the login form to render.\n\nKeeps the legacy live external form (mozilla-mobile.github.io/testapp/loginForm), as the converted\nLoginsTest already does. The local password.html asset is not a substitute: it pre-fills a different\nusername and randomises the password, so it cannot cover these credentials.\n\nTwo clean runs on device, no retries.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319315\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/CustomTabsTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/CustomTabsPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/CustomTabsTest.kt"], "git_node": "344b1a00f139d3a1543b9026ed96f6e7e86d44d2", "git_parents": ["8cdfce27a2e13d3f3c439cb2f732fbf6a511ee41"], "node": "331bd403d5fee0fe52fc0fdcaef22f82f089f900", "parents": ["fd15b3de3804b70184dd44bcc3dbbb479e2f277f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063252 - [efficiency] Convert MainMenuTest.verifyTheMainMenuShareButtonFromCustomTabTest to ui/efficiency r=aaronmt\n\nLaunches a custom tab, opens the custom-tab main menu, taps Share, and verifies the share sheet renders its\nfull layout.\n\nPure assembly, with no new selectors or page-object methods. CustomTabsSelectors.MENU_SHARE and the\nShareOverlaySelectors \"shareTabLayout\" group both already exist, and the group covers all eight things legacy\nverifyShareTabLayout asserted: the share container, the send-to-device, recently-used and all-actions\nsections, their three headers, and the Save as PDF action. This contradicts the batch plan's estimate that the\ntest \"adds system share-sheet handling\" \u2014 that capability landed with an earlier conversion, so nothing\nstructural was left to build.\n\nOne deliberate parity note on that group, which predates this patch and is unchanged by it: legacy matched the\nthree section headers by res-id *and* text (accountHeaderText, recent_apps_link_header, apps_link_header),\nwhile the selectors match on text alone. The strings are unique to this sheet, so the assertions hold, but they\nare scoped to the screen rather than to the specific view.\n\nCarries @SmokeTest even though the legacy test is a plain @Test. The case is in the TestRail smoke pool and its\nthree already-converted custom-tab siblings are all annotated, so the missing legacy annotation reads as an\noversight rather than a signal that it should stay out of the smoke job.\n\nAdds a page-content wait that legacy did not have. Legacy opened the menu straight after launching the custom\ntab; the share sheet renders either way, so this is a stabiliser rather than a new assertion, and it keeps the\nsheet's contents derived from the intended page instead of whatever the tab happened to be showing.\n\nTwo clean runs on device, no retries. The second was a whole-class run of CustomTabsTest, so the other eight\nconverted custom-tab tests are confirmed unregressed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319316\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/MainMenuTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/CustomTabsTest.kt"], "git_node": "86cbc1c5d81be83275a373148ab8fd1e9ce17b12", "git_parents": ["344b1a00f139d3a1543b9026ed96f6e7e86d44d2"], "node": "54d624628dd6f2dd67106c5763eb5bd8a5a55eaf", "parents": ["331bd403d5fee0fe52fc0fdcaef22f82f089f900"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063263 - [efficiency] Convert UploadPermissionsTest.fileUploadPermissionTest to ui/efficiency r=ajoltan\n\nLoads a page with a file input, taps it, grants the storage permissions, steps through Android's chooser and\nconfirms the document picker opens.\n\nThe legacy test never verified any of that. Its only assertion goes through\nAppAndSystemHelper.assertExternalAppOpens, which catches the AssertionFailedError from intended() and only\nlogs it -- so on any device where the picker is installed, which is every supported image, the assertion\ncannot fail. Because it could not fail, two things it was supposed to catch went unnoticed for as long as it\nhas existed. Both were found on device, by reading the screen dumps the failing port produced:\n\n- grantSystemPermission() dismisses exactly one dialog, and tapping a bare \u003cinput type=\"file\"\u003e raises a chain\n  of them (audio, then music-and-audio). The legacy test ends parked on the second dialog.\n- A bare file input does not open a picker at all. Android shows a chooser first -- Camera, Camcorder,\n  Files -- so the picker package is not foreground until an option is chosen.\n\nSo the legacy test finishes on either a permission dialog or a chooser, and reports success. The port drains\nthe permission chain, asserts the chooser's Files option, clicks it, and only then asserts the picker's window\nis really present via mozVerifyNativeAppOpens, which also force-stops it -- the same cleanup legacy did in its\nfinally block.\n\nAdds SystemSettingsPage.grantAllPendingSystemPermissions() (drains the chain, returns the count),\nSystemSettingsSelectors.PERMISSION_GRANT_DIALOG and FILE_CHOOSER_FILES_OPTION, and\nBrowserPageSelectors.UPLOAD_FILE_WEB_INPUT. Constants gains DOCUMENTS_UI.\n\nThe dialog count is deliberately NOT asserted. Runtime grants are system state that outlives the app profile,\nso the dialogs appear on a fresh device and are absent on every run after; an assertion on them passes once\nand then fails forever. This was caught by the retry of an earlier attempt, not reasoned about. The chooser\nis identified by its Files label rather than by the chooser container's res-id, which is not reliably\npackage-qualifiable and has moved package across releases.\n\nLegacy also branched to \"com.android.documentsui\" below API 29. That branch is not carried: the package does\nnot exist on any image this suite runs on, so it was unreachable rather than coverage.\n\nAlso adds a ScreenDump on failure to mozVerifyNativeAppOpens and mozVerifyFileOpensInExternalApp. Neither\ndumped before, so \"\u003cpkg\u003e not found\" gave no way to tell \"the app did not open\" from \"something else is in\nfront of it\" -- which is the entire difficulty above, and it cost three cycles to see. The dumps' [windows]\nblock names the focused window and settles it in one read.\n\nTwo clean runs on device, no retries. The second was a whole-class run and, because the permissions granted\nby the first run persist, it exercised the zero-dialog path -- so both branches of the grant loop are covered.\n\nWorth flagging separately: three already-converted efficiency tests (DownloadTest.saveAsPdfFunctionalityTest\nand two in MainMenuTest) assert through the same swallowing helper via mozVerifyFileOpensInExternalApp, so\nthey currently carry an assertion that cannot fail. Not changed here; that is its own patch.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319317\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/helpers/Constants.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/helpers/SystemPickerCapabilities.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/UploadPermissionsTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/SystemSettingsPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/BrowserPageSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/SystemSettingsSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/UploadPermissionsTest.kt"], "git_node": "9882f3d26d096e2683ca729cc6e1bbcf75bbbec4", "git_parents": ["86cbc1c5d81be83275a373148ab8fd1e9ce17b12"], "node": "f670f571f34d5d06d4bd9d4b9c32bb08ac890f2c", "parents": ["54d624628dd6f2dd67106c5763eb5bd8a5a55eaf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064374 - Move existing gfxFontEntry::HasFontTable to HasFontTableInternal, and make HasFontTable a non-virtual function that uses Skrifa if available. r=AlaskanEmily\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319460\n", "files": ["gfx/fontations_glue/lib.rs", "gfx/thebes/CoreTextFontList.cpp", "gfx/thebes/CoreTextFontList.h", "gfx/thebes/gfxDWriteFontList.h", "gfx/thebes/gfxFT2FontList.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxFT2FontList.h", "gfx/thebes/gfxFcPlatformFontList.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxFcPlatformFontList.h", "gfx/thebes/gfxFontEntry.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxFontEntry.h"], "git_node": "2aff57ea99b9f6def15b9977b652732aab54954b", "git_parents": ["9882f3d26d096e2683ca729cc6e1bbcf75bbbec4"], "node": "3eb4913b37f85884f28835654f3eda392ad1245b", "parents": ["f670f571f34d5d06d4bd9d4b9c32bb08ac890f2c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063602 - [efficiency] Do not fail a test when closeSoftKeyboard() cannot hide the keyboard r=aaronmt\n\nEspresso's closeSoftKeyboard() throws PerformException when the focused view's root is not\nthe one it expects, which happens whenever no editable view has focus - on the homepage, or\nafter a dialog takes focus. Hiding the keyboard is only ever a convenience for the assertion\nthat follows, so failing to do it must not fail the test.\n\nTwo tests fail locally on this today, and pass in CI, so it only bites developers running\nthe suite: SettingsGeneralTest.verifyFontSizingChangeTest via\nBasePage.mozVerifyAnyContainsText, and\nSettingsSearchTest.verifyCustomSearchEngineCanBeAddedFromSearchEngineMenuTest via\nSettingsSearchAddSearchEnginePage.\n\nAdds BasePage.dismissSoftKeyboard(), which wraps the call in runCatching and logs what it\nswallowed, and routes the four call sites in the efficiency framework through it. It is\nprotected rather than private so the two page objects, which extend BasePage, use the same\nhelper instead of repeating the guard.\n\nA further 13 unguarded calls remain in the legacy ui/robots/* and ui/*Test.kt files. Left\nalone here to keep the patch reviewable.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319321\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/BasePage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/SettingsAutofillPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/SettingsSearchAddSearchEnginePage.kt"], "git_node": "2b6c7f4fe5c0a63da0831dbacff2f3b193b5243f", "git_parents": ["2aff57ea99b9f6def15b9977b652732aab54954b"], "node": "c7062dd0a2d9dac2c44cb96bcf832c155b7a8aa3", "parents": ["3eb4913b37f85884f28835654f3eda392ad1245b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055837 - use uv in test tasks. r=taskgraph-reviewers,bhearsum\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312753\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/test/kind.yml"], "git_node": "b4856d3df2dc532291581388cd3eea979f932058", "git_parents": ["2b6c7f4fe5c0a63da0831dbacff2f3b193b5243f"], "node": "d0ab24c5afe7af3f38c21a95585dac60c3b67ac8", "parents": ["c7062dd0a2d9dac2c44cb96bcf832c155b7a8aa3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055837 - use uv in web-platform-tests tasks. r=taskgraph-reviewers,bhearsum\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312754\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/web-platform-tests/kind.yml"], "git_node": "3a1e4ec2bb8b0598e49ecaa2882c77438a23839a", "git_parents": ["b4856d3df2dc532291581388cd3eea979f932058"], "node": "1843d07e0716d190b2460dd8fb40d13650e3c493", "parents": ["d0ab24c5afe7af3f38c21a95585dac60c3b67ac8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "akizu matsuo \u003cpettyblue@proton.me\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053212 - Don't clear the status bar just because the frame was reframed. r=smaug\n\nClearFrameRefs unconditionally cleared the status bar even if the\ncontent was still in the document (e.g. when a CSS change caused the\nframe to be reframed).\nInstead of clearing the status bar immediately, defer the check to after\nthe RefreshDriver tick.\n\nRegressed by: Bug 2023374\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310891\n", "files": ["dom/events/EventStateManager.cpp", "dom/events/EventStateManager.h"], "git_node": "899a7381c0b1f83a7bc445376c7e08f070c0ecac", "git_parents": ["3a1e4ec2bb8b0598e49ecaa2882c77438a23839a"], "node": "738c1faa1af5cdac77209ac6648673f7ba7c5b0d", "parents": ["1843d07e0716d190b2460dd8fb40d13650e3c493"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Serban Stanca \u003csstanca@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2064333 - Turn scoped registries on for nightly builds r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug\" for causing devtools failures in browser_webconsole_object_inspector_entries.js.\n\nThis reverts commit 689c96ae48e835fc2d97e5ab4df74762d0403d7e.\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "testing/web-platform/meta/dom/idlharness.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/dom/idlharness.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "f83dfa0103163018c2b26f4cf15f50fda0b9bc52", "git_parents": ["899a7381c0b1f83a7bc445376c7e08f070c0ecac"], "node": "4c9cf8a24c5605a5c24525834a165204331be403", "parents": ["738c1faa1af5cdac77209ac6648673f7ba7c5b0d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sebastian Hengst \u003caryx.github@gmx-topmail.de\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2062209 - Scope the Urlbar actor to about:newtab and about:home. r=mconley,mbeier\" for causing merge conflict with its own backout\n\nThis reverts commit 2249487a6342b58457ad6ef278f04dda550e1b92.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2064279 - Gate the search-terms persistence check on the address bar. r=mbeier,urlbar-reviewers\"\n\nThis reverts commit 85641c7382b350a7bf99e68d845034e9c4966476.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2064185 - Read the default user context id without Ci. r=mbeier,urlbar-reviewers\"\n\nThis reverts commit 94c61e00ae3537ab448ea3c91c65b5d572d9a4a2.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2062987 - Give the content prefs shim getScotchBonnetPref. r=mbeier,urlbar-reviewers\"\n\nThis reverts commit 9e158acf0ff97f73d44485745e880170fa23e379.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2064185 - Observe the AI window's state only from a chrome window. r=mbeier,urlbar-reviewers\"\n\nThis reverts commit 77413f0a5fc42f3da119e4205876811966cfbff5.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2064279 - Defer the placeholder update to a tab switch only in the address bar. r=mbeier,urlbar-reviewers\"\n\nThis reverts commit cc877b194274934219c63e161c92fe662e1a1c98.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2064279 - Gate the copy/cut controller on the address bar. r=mbeier,urlbar-reviewers\"\n\nThis reverts commit 4ef9eb707145832c2a8a961317f47800022c8ddc.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2064277 - Build the query context in the realm that reads it. r=mbeier,urlbar-reviewers\"\n\nThis reverts commit 85259daf3a6feb16001501aced19e3e02ad6c056.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2064277 - Clone parent-sent payloads into the content realm. r=mbeier\"\n\nThis reverts commit de9e8ba6b7a689b11d2e7173868af7398f7cbee9.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2064276 - Drop the markup's whitespace text nodes. r=mbeier\"\n\nThis reverts commit e3871704dde74a22fcb78aebf4303344450f1e19.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2064276 - Parse the input's markup with DOMParser. r=mbeier,urlbar-reviewers\"\n\nThis reverts commit 6f9220dcc14be23d5a39a4ace0145e8bbe2455ef.\n", "files": ["browser/actors/UrlbarChild.sys.mjs", "browser/base/content/browser-toolbarKeyNav.js", "browser/components/DesktopActorRegistry.sys.mjs", "browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_ext_tabs_create_url.js", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarChildController.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarContentPrefs.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInputBase.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarShared.mjs", "toolkit/content/editMenuOverlay.js"], "git_node": "449eb52bd6318f8b2d06d1aaec5b2dca30f59c25", "git_parents": ["f83dfa0103163018c2b26f4cf15f50fda0b9bc52"], "node": "04c5149b0b49301f18e2fa7c2174fbc1c3b489c5", "parents": ["4c9cf8a24c5605a5c24525834a165204331be403"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lando \u003clando@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Merge mozilla-central to autoland\n", "files": [], "git_node": "4ee53a8b8c82dbecdd18107a2581f726cdbd8a67", "git_parents": ["449eb52bd6318f8b2d06d1aaec5b2dca30f59c25", "91c8ca3faa6ccbb72d65d89401fd31fd3313afc4"], "node": "75ac2cc52b4647488bef0c609071849a2b273b30", "parents": ["04c5149b0b49301f18e2fa7c2174fbc1c3b489c5", "1125f63f232f593f2987571c954f08752584c222"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Naz\u0131m Can Alt\u0131nova \u003ccanaltinova@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064053 - Don't allocate a PageInformation when re-registering a known page r=profiler-reviewers,mstange\n\nprofiler_register_page() allocated a PageInformation before checking\nwhether that inner window ID was already registered, then dropped it\nagain. Every history.replaceState() hit that path. Pass the fields down\ninstead and only allocate on insert.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319135\n", "files": ["tools/profiler/core/PageInformation.cpp", "tools/profiler/core/PageInformation.h", "tools/profiler/core/platform.cpp"], "git_node": "e0f9303e26f0ca29266ce53de49f00647129dbc1", "git_parents": ["4ee53a8b8c82dbecdd18107a2581f726cdbd8a67"], "node": "d9f75f057eb16c6b86a29a088facdcaaca966ab4", "parents": ["75ac2cc52b4647488bef0c609071849a2b273b30"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Naz\u0131m Can Alt\u0131nova \u003ccanaltinova@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064046 - Add more Raptor browser function labels r=mstange,perftest-reviewers,sparky\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319430\n", "files": ["testing/raptor/raptor/browser_function_labels.toml"], "git_node": "99cbe2a1dbe7e589b07827cc8af20a697bc187c2", "git_parents": ["e0f9303e26f0ca29266ce53de49f00647129dbc1"], "node": "858ba92e3c6e818b69316467693a2b1e9e08d69a", "parents": ["d9f75f057eb16c6b86a29a088facdcaaca966ab4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055837 - use uv in browsertime tasks. r=taskgraph-reviewers,bhearsum\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312750\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/browsertime/kind.yml"], "git_node": "e8b089ad96130d861a753af6d62ee96c6a8ee545", "git_parents": ["99cbe2a1dbe7e589b07827cc8af20a697bc187c2"], "node": "33a43d362f16266dc2b75df2a19b176886757d75", "parents": ["858ba92e3c6e818b69316467693a2b1e9e08d69a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Bob Owen \u003cbobowencode@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058087 p1 - Pre-create shader-cache to allow read only rule. r=handyman,sandbox-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317559\n", "files": ["security/sandbox/win/src/sandboxbroker/sandboxBroker.cpp"], "git_node": "e10c28b6089829a4021f979cb878ead9224a1a89", "git_parents": ["e8b089ad96130d861a753af6d62ee96c6a8ee545"], "node": "064ea3fcec9a46eeb082abb12935a8df231837d4", "parents": ["33a43d362f16266dc2b75df2a19b176886757d75"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Bob Owen \u003cbobowencode@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058087 p2 - Block directory creation and only allow read access. r=handyman,sandbox-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317560\n", "files": ["security/sandbox/chromium-shim/patches/55_dont_broker_dir_creation_or_write.patch", "security/sandbox/chromium/sandbox/win/src/filesystem_dispatcher.cc"], "git_node": "a38fbc3460761804047f3c1bf171122095d389ea", "git_parents": ["e10c28b6089829a4021f979cb878ead9224a1a89"], "node": "bb02939ecbad14f729bca65c4323e622c67f929d", "parents": ["064ea3fcec9a46eeb082abb12935a8df231837d4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "serge-sans-paille \u003csguelton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063812 - Do not override size_t definition in static-analysis test r=sylvestre\n\nSome compilers disregard this practice when they don't match their\nplatform-specific definition.\n\nUse a simpler signature for memcpy instead. It's just for a check test.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319704\n", "files": ["tools/clang-tidy/test/bugprone-bitwise-pointer-cast.cpp"], "git_node": "c108651cf7d5c97ec44dc828295001f1156ac6fb", "git_parents": ["a38fbc3460761804047f3c1bf171122095d389ea"], "node": "c2453baba1b1d2bfbba9ca8dc02746b4dcf9cc4c", "parents": ["bb02939ecbad14f729bca65c4323e622c67f929d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063545 - Tidy the tabbrowser docs. r=sthompson,tabbrowser-reviewers\n\nThe page told the `\u003cxul:tabbrowser\u003e` story four times over; it now says once that the name survives in older code, and describes what `gBrowser` is today. The `gBrowser` prose moves to a page of its own, so it sits in the menu beside the other pages rather than only under the index.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319190\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/docs/async-tab-switcher.md", "browser/components/tabbrowser/docs/gbrowser.md", "browser/components/tabbrowser/docs/index.md"], "git_node": "dbdf04183a63bcf4c29637465c4505ef84849290", "git_parents": ["c108651cf7d5c97ec44dc828295001f1156ac6fb"], "node": "59ca3cf789cbbaafe8cda755193ded30d148368e", "parents": ["c2453baba1b1d2bfbba9ca8dc02746b4dcf9cc4c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063545 - Document gBrowser's progress listener infrastructure. r=sthompson,tabbrowser-reviewers\n\nThe replay on a tab switch reaches global listeners only, and a listener that implements `onRefreshAttempted` without returning true cancels the refresh -- neither is guessable, and both are in the page.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319191\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/Tabbrowser.sys.mjs", "browser/components/tabbrowser/docs/index.md", "browser/components/tabbrowser/docs/progress-listeners.md"], "git_node": "d156ac96af44b95513e932100da782133289b63e", "git_parents": ["dbdf04183a63bcf4c29637465c4505ef84849290"], "node": "473b8a090d9bae12ee05cc5240d77c536d6f4210", "parents": ["59ca3cf789cbbaafe8cda755193ded30d148368e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064136 - Fix the JSDoc type expressions jsdoc can't parse. r=sthompson,tabbrowser-reviewers\n\nThe tuple in `#tabSelectTimestamps` stays unparseable on purpose: the field is `#`-private, so it never reaches the rendered page, and the type is worth more there than the parse error costs in the build log.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319242\n", "files": ["browser/components/sessionstore/TabGroupState.sys.mjs", "browser/components/tabbrowser/Tabbrowser.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "de27885a28ef27a3a21893410de6b35e5a4f83b4", "git_parents": ["d156ac96af44b95513e932100da782133289b63e"], "node": "2e9de8db4961ff147a6f39d0e0cf3e8355188c4c", "parents": ["473b8a090d9bae12ee05cc5240d77c536d6f4210"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Erich Gubler \u003cerichdongubler@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060712 - fix(webgpu): adjust baseline expected outcomes to actual r=webgpu-reviewers,nical\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319432\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/webgpu/cts/webgpu/api/operation/command_buffer/copyTextureToTexture/cts.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/webgpu/cts/webgpu/api/operation/command_buffer/image_copy/cts.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/webgpu/cts/webgpu/api/operation/rendering/3d_texture_slices/cts.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/webgpu/cts/webgpu/api/validation/capability_checks/limits/maxInterStageShaderVariables/cts.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/webgpu/cts/webgpu/api/validation/state/device_lost/destroy/cts.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/webgpu/cts/webgpu/shader/execution/expression/call/builtin/subgroupAdd/cts.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/webgpu/cts/webgpu/shader/execution/expression/call/builtin/subgroupMinMax/cts.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/webgpu/cts/webgpu/shader/execution/expression/call/builtin/subgroupMul/cts.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/webgpu/cts/webgpu/shader/execution/expres