Erich Gubler \u003cerichdongubler@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062837 - test(webgpu): update CTS to 535149e23e538e4f8fe3d6266e32c68b7017ccc0 r=webgpu-reviewers,teoxoy\n\nSome new tests, and some new `PASS`es for Windows in texture tests, yay!\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318906\n", "files": ["dom/webgpu/tests/cts/checkout/CONTRIBUTING.md", "dom/webgpu/tests/cts/checkout/README.md", "dom/webgpu/tests/cts/checkout/src/webgpu/api/operation/rendering/depth.spec.ts", "dom/webgpu/tests/cts/checkout/src/webgpu/api/operation/sampling/sampler_texture.spec.ts", "dom/webgpu/tests/cts/checkout/tools/gen_version", "dom/webgpu/tests/cts/moz.yaml", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/webgpu/cts/webgpu/api/operation/rendering/3d_texture_slices/cts.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/webgpu/cts/webgpu/api/operation/rendering/depth/cts.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/webgpu/cts/webgpu/api/operation/sampling/sampler_texture/cts.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/webgpu/cts/webgpu/api/validation/state/device_lost/destroy/cts.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/webgpu/cts/webgpu/shader/execution/expression/call/builtin/subgroupMinMax/cts.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/webgpu/cts/webgpu/shader/execution/expression/call/builtin/subgroupMul/cts.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/webgpu/cts/webgpu/shader/execution/expression/call/builtin/textureLoad/cts.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/webgpu/cts/webgpu/shader/execution/expression/call/builtin/textureSample/cts.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/webgpu/cts/webgpu/shader/execution/expression/call/builtin/textureSampleCompare/cts.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/webgpu/cts/webgpu/shader/execution/expression/call/builtin/textureSampleCompareLevel/cts.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/webgpu/cts/webgpu/shader/execution/expression/call/builtin/textureSampleGrad/cts.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/webgpu/cts/webgpu/web_platform/copyToTexture/ImageBitmap/dedicated.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/webgpu/cts/webgpu/web_platform/copyToTexture/ImageBitmap/service.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/webgpu/cts/webgpu/web_platform/copyToTexture/ImageBitmap/shared.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "9965ea3fd96678b77d41ac87ed9db8ef1f348930", "git_parents": ["8b6cdc4f7726bdcc388416a35dfa76e4ec24a202"], "node": "775234cbed62634705b22fadce1b14f835c02749", "parents": ["167cb4639095ad2bc36489a7b16e3a6e37ae7568"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Reem H \u003c42309026+reemhamz@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063958 - Privacy widget UX fixes. r=nina-py\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319011\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Privacy/_Privacy.scss"], "git_node": "38780cdbd05866583cc6c4c707d8fc6fa3074fd0", "git_parents": ["9965ea3fd96678b77d41ac87ed9db8ef1f348930"], "node": "2b276ab6ad2848ab08badb16807a1aaf94570a7e", "parents": ["775234cbed62634705b22fadce1b14f835c02749"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ayoub hedri \u003cahedri@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064067  - Removed all references and usage of REFERRER_POLICY_COUNT r=necko-reviewers,freddyb,valentin,janerik\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319143\n", "files": ["dom/security/ReferrerInfo.cpp", "dom/security/ReferrerInfo.h", "dom/security/metrics.yaml", "dom/security/test/referrer-policy/browser.toml", "dom/security/test/referrer-policy/browser_referrer_telemetry.js", "netwerk/protocol/http/HttpBaseChannel.cpp", "toolkit/components/telemetry/Histograms.json"], "git_node": "dde9a2caae5443ffefede0b9cd34369647693c10", "git_parents": ["38780cdbd05866583cc6c4c707d8fc6fa3074fd0"], "node": "8758f04716d2d55ce5135d1b3d5585138b1b6015", "parents": ["2b276ab6ad2848ab08badb16807a1aaf94570a7e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Keith Cirkel \u003ckeithamus@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064014 - Commit Option value on mouse event for base select r=dom-core-reviewers,jjaschke\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319091\n", "files": ["dom/html/HTMLSelectElement.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-click-drag-option.optional.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-events-2.optional.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-mouse-behavior.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-mousedown-slot-mutation.optional.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/switch-picker-appearance.html.ini"], "git_node": "8559849fc3aca36ae0e34a84b73757854e6f7591", "git_parents": ["dde9a2caae5443ffefede0b9cd34369647693c10"], "node": "d70765eefd9628c014360c55abed311d1a955d25", "parents": ["8758f04716d2d55ce5135d1b3d5585138b1b6015"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan-Niklas Jaeschke \u003cjjaschke@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061960 - Fall back to exact matching if a too-long range contains only one word. r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug\n\nA range with a single word cannot be divided into a start and an end term.\nRange-based matching did so anyway, which made the word boundary algorithms\ncompute an inverted search range and assert in nsFind.\n\nExact matching now handles those ranges, bounded by kMaxContextTermLength so\nthat the resulting URL stays short.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319545\n", "files": ["dom/base/TextDirectiveCreator.cpp", "dom/base/TextDirectiveUtil.cpp", "dom/base/TextDirectiveUtil.h", "dom/base/test/test_text-fragments-create-text-directive.html"], "git_node": "7d2a196be4c7edab4a02c157adfef8bd4d1fe9a6", "git_parents": ["8559849fc3aca36ae0e34a84b73757854e6f7591"], "node": "a5fb9063142a390237f29f738bd6b1bc022b33a8", "parents": ["d70765eefd9628c014360c55abed311d1a955d25"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tymur Boiko \u003ctboiko@nvidia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063678 - Allow setsockopt/getsockopt in the RDD sandbox for Vulkan. r=jld,sandbox-reviewers\n\nSome Vulkan ICDs in RDD may pull CUDA, which calls setsockopt. That syscall was unlisted.\nContent already allows these.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318787\n", "files": ["security/sandbox/linux/SandboxFilter.cpp"], "git_node": "5ec295466d2b561c2ae22d6e3539110365438413", "git_parents": ["7d2a196be4c7edab4a02c157adfef8bd4d1fe9a6"], "node": "bbdaf4e3b2c28d7ee61690bdfd25c2d48aacc01e", "parents": ["a5fb9063142a390237f29f738bd6b1bc022b33a8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063903 - Support fractional SVG viewports. r=firefox-svg-reviewers,longsonr\n\nThis prevents images getting distorted aspect ratios, which can cause\nthings like bug 2063386 or bug 2063903.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319066\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/CanvasRenderingContext2D.cpp", "image/BlobSurfaceProvider.cpp", "image/ClippedImage.cpp", "image/ClippedImage.h", "image/ImageOps.cpp", "image/ImageOps.h", "image/OrientedImage.cpp", "image/SVGDocumentWrapper.cpp", "image/SVGDocumentWrapper.h", "image/SVGDrawingCallback.h", "image/SVGDrawingParameters.h", "image/VectorImage.cpp", "image/imgLoader.cpp", "image/remote/RemoteImageProtocolHandler.cpp", "image/test/reftest/downscaling/reftest.list", "layout/base/nsLayoutUtils.cpp", "layout/painting/nsCSSRenderingBorders.cpp", "layout/painting/nsImageRenderer.cpp", "layout/painting/nsImageRenderer.h", "layout/reftests/svg/as-image/zoom/reftest.list", "layout/svg/SVGImageContext.h", "layout/svg/SVGImageFrame.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/CSS2/backgrounds/background-intrinsic-004.xht.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/CSS2/backgrounds/background-intrinsic-005.xht.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-sizing/image-fractional-height-with-wide-aspect-ratio.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/as-image/sprite-sheet-fractional-size-helper.svg", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/as-image/sprite-sheet-fractional-size-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/as-image/sprite-sheet-fractional-size.html"], "git_node": "8b48097b3f889135a619471608fe899550603bc4", "git_parents": ["5ec295466d2b561c2ae22d6e3539110365438413"], "node": "8d95685461cae7c53defe3e3fcacf41e86998942", "parents": ["bbdaf4e3b2c28d7ee61690bdfd25c2d48aacc01e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064650 - Make -moz-native-theme match only with the default theme. r=dao,desktop-theme-reviewers\n\nThis reduces a bit the combinations the front-end needs to deal with and\nmakes lwthemes work the same on macOS / Windows and Linux.\n\nThis will allow to simplify some of the rules in a follow-up (e.g. a lot\nof the (-moz-native-theme) media queries might not need :not([lwtheme])\n(but we might need those for specificity, so not changing those yet).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319721\n", "files": ["browser/themes/BuiltInThemeConfig.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_ext_themes_pbm.js", "toolkit/modules/LightweightThemeConsumer.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "578ad3ac373f47c8bd80c0ebf973cc45fec94d13", "git_parents": ["8b48097b3f889135a619471608fe899550603bc4"], "node": "e58d92ed02145fa306c92f11d30789aa8a0a43c2", "parents": ["8d95685461cae7c53defe3e3fcacf41e86998942"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064276 - Parse the input's markup with DOMParser. r=mbeier,urlbar-reviewers\n\n`parseXULToFragment` is chrome-only, as a content document can hold no XUL elements at all. So both realms parse with `DOMParser`, the markup naming the XHTML namespace by default and its one XUL element with a `xul:` prefix, which content resolves to XHTML.\n\nDropping the `html:` prefixes breaks whatever matched a qualified name, hence the fixes alongside.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319331\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser-toolbarKeyNav.js", "browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_ext_tabs_create_url.js", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInputBase.mjs", "toolkit/content/editMenuOverlay.js"], "git_node": "5053db6c195d6ea05212910a3243a6fa6e052144", "git_parents": ["578ad3ac373f47c8bd80c0ebf973cc45fec94d13"], "node": "fe7ccfaec3cb8b94f423e3adca2fee2644378b7e", "parents": ["e58d92ed02145fa306c92f11d30789aa8a0a43c2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064276 - Drop the markup's whitespace text nodes. r=mbeier\n\n`DOMParser` keeps the whitespace between the markup's elements, and those text nodes change the accessibility tree the input exposes: the search bar gains an empty section child, which `browser_searchbar_new.js` catches. Only a build slow enough to assert the tree before it settles sees it, so opt is green while asan, tsan and debug fail; `MOZ_CHAOSMODE` with `--repeat` reproduces it on an opt build.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319669\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInputBase.mjs"], "git_node": "931086a872ff61071d1aca7a6fcc04548b199ffb", "git_parents": ["5053db6c195d6ea05212910a3243a6fa6e052144"], "node": "daea5ef944fd0156d38b4edf4c775eed00165ca9", "parents": ["fe7ccfaec3cb8b94f423e3adca2fee2644378b7e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064277 - Clone parent-sent payloads into the content realm. r=mbeier\n\nThe port's returns are already cloned; the parent's dispatches into the child controller weren't, so a content-realm input saw an Xray over an object in this realm and was denied even `Symbol.iterator` -- iterating the engine-store snapshot threw.\n\n`Notify` has the same gap and isn't fixed here: it carries a `UrlbarQueryContext` that `fromWire` builds in this realm, and cloning would flatten it. Content has the class, so deserializing there is likely the answer.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319332\n", "files": ["browser/actors/UrlbarChild.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "2e0668e5e2a13070b43192dc3dfe0aeccfd4697e", "git_parents": ["931086a872ff61071d1aca7a6fcc04548b199ffb"], "node": "740a839c9a478bbb237ab4c18dee74a639572541", "parents": ["daea5ef944fd0156d38b4edf4c775eed00165ca9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064277 - Build the query context in the realm that reads it. r=mbeier,urlbar-reviewers\n\nThe remaining half of the previous patch, and the one a clone can't fix: the actor deserialized the wire form into a `UrlbarQueryContext` in its own realm, so a content-realm view got an Xray over it. That reads every property as `undefined` rather than throwing, so a query produced no rows and no error.\n\nThe wire form is plain data, so it crosses as one and the child controller builds the context from it, in an entry point of its own so that `notify` takes a real context whichever path delivered it. That has to happen before `notify` inspects `id` to drop the results of a stale query.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319413\n", "files": ["browser/actors/UrlbarChild.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarChildController.mjs"], "git_node": "c467263c0c55eea622015b59557b2131d312bb7e", "git_parents": ["2e0668e5e2a13070b43192dc3dfe0aeccfd4697e"], "node": "21500cc03d914af578db1b850708180c01a9052d", "parents": ["740a839c9a478bbb237ab4c18dee74a639572541"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064279 - Gate the copy/cut controller on the address bar. r=mbeier,urlbar-reviewers\n\n`_trimValue` returns early unless the input is the address bar, so on the searchbar the controller only reimplements native copy/cut.\n\nThis is what lets a content-realm input work without a realm branch here: the controller needs `controllers` and `editor` on the input plus the clipboard service, all chrome-only.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319333\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInputBase.mjs"], "git_node": "2422c061bacac7afa8caf1297c127aa653c97841", "git_parents": ["c467263c0c55eea622015b59557b2131d312bb7e"], "node": "8df4863f6ccdaa2194acef346a2a4ff0b695949d", "parents": ["21500cc03d914af578db1b850708180c01a9052d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064279 - Defer the placeholder update to a tab switch only in the address bar. r=mbeier,urlbar-reviewers\n\nThe update waits for the user to look away, and a tab switch qualifies only for the address bar, which takes its value from the selected tab. Nothing gives the searchbar a value on `TabSelect`, so its listener could only ever fire with the guard already false -- and by then the `input` listener has removed both.\n\nA content-realm input, not being the address bar, is left with the same single cue, which is what this needs to not reach for a tabbrowser it doesn't have.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319334\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInputBase.mjs"], "git_node": "7cdffe1b72d12f4931505040231ab5aca27c2154", "git_parents": ["2422c061bacac7afa8caf1297c127aa653c97841"], "node": "3b1a89228845a5121c45e10b9fad5dfb651b23cc", "parents": ["8df4863f6ccdaa2194acef346a2a4ff0b695949d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064185 - Observe the AI window's state only from a chrome window. r=mbeier,urlbar-reviewers\n\n`observe` matches the notification's subject against the input's own window, so a content-realm input could never match it -- and `generateQI` and the observer service are chrome-only, so reaching for them threw before the engine-store observer below could be registered. That one a content realm does need.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319335\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInputBase.mjs"], "git_node": "07e610166ebf3171f332aa353a710d2fe6edc7ce", "git_parents": ["7cdffe1b72d12f4931505040231ab5aca27c2154"], "node": "9c491cbf895804408b6908e16d5d7598dee7b487", "parents": ["3b1a89228845a5121c45e10b9fad5dfb651b23cc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062987 - Give the content prefs shim getScotchBonnetPref. r=mbeier,urlbar-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319408\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarContentPrefs.mjs"], "git_node": "1cfe21df62403b9e80b265279a2925476028dce1", "git_parents": ["07e610166ebf3171f332aa353a710d2fe6edc7ce"], "node": "1e9da0e14df6634d94b58a4733dbeb5431da6826", "parents": ["9c491cbf895804408b6908e16d5d7598dee7b487"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064185 - Read the default user context id without Ci. r=mbeier,urlbar-reviewers\n\n`UrlbarQueryContext`'s constructor normalizes the container id, so this sits on the path of every query -- a content-realm input couldn't run one at all. The value is spelled out beside the private-window sentinel the same file already carries.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319409\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarShared.mjs"], "git_node": "e262bff3cd25ac7d3523892df4dcb16ed5a137ea", "git_parents": ["1cfe21df62403b9e80b265279a2925476028dce1"], "node": "e3d0ccb17050e9f60ce84f2e5b6466a348c6b3d4", "parents": ["1e9da0e14df6634d94b58a4733dbeb5431da6826"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064279 - Gate the search-terms persistence check on the address bar. r=mbeier,urlbar-reviewers\n\nIts state is keyed by the selected tab's browser, which a content-realm input has no way to reach.\n\n`handleEvent` wraps every `_on_*` in a try/catch and reports through `console.error`, so the exception left `_on_input` silently half-done: typing updated the value and started no query, with nothing in the parent-process log.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319410\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInputBase.mjs"], "git_node": "49548db7628dda81c74623c36289de7ecc071620", "git_parents": ["e262bff3cd25ac7d3523892df4dcb16ed5a137ea"], "node": "9400c5c7ca2a0e6806a26e56a50c722c23d08b77", "parents": ["e3d0ccb17050e9f60ce84f2e5b6466a348c6b3d4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062209 - Scope the Urlbar actor to about:newtab and about:home. r=mconley,mbeier\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318748\n", "files": ["browser/actors/UrlbarChild.sys.mjs", "browser/components/DesktopActorRegistry.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "4b2111d9ec127046dd0804580acbda71a9d9405a", "git_parents": ["49548db7628dda81c74623c36289de7ecc071620"], "node": "fd6defb82b68bbfae1ce2f9bb38c2ae57c81107f", "parents": ["9400c5c7ca2a0e6806a26e56a50c722c23d08b77"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062209 - Register \u003cmoz-urlbar\u003e as New Tab's search component behind a feature gate. r=mconley,urlbar-reviewers,search-reviewers,daleharvey\n\nThe element mounts on about:newtab and runs a query, but its results don't render there yet and it carries no styling, so with the gate on New Tab gets a search box that can't finish a search. That is what the gate defaulting off buys.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318749\n", "files": ["browser/app/profile/firefox.js", "browser/components/BrowserComponents.manifest", "browser/components/search/SearchUIUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarNewTabComponentRegistrant.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarPrefs.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/moz.build", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/unit/test_UrlbarNewTabComponentRegistrant.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/unit/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "82def3f8a6f009cf831b79cf38bf7d7f0a0b506d", "git_parents": ["4b2111d9ec127046dd0804580acbda71a9d9405a"], "node": "7c36dc8533d1d3b164e827f871d06b34020bc02d", "parents": ["fd6defb82b68bbfae1ce2f9bb38c2ae57c81107f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062210 - Wire the newtab_searchbar SAP through result groups and providers. r=urlbar-reviewers,jteow\n\nTwo places enumerate SAPs, and a query needs both: `getResultGroups` throws on a name it doesn't know, so the new SAP shares the searchbar's placeholder config until the searchbar gets its own, and providers are selected per SAP, so a new one starts with none. Suggest results carry a `suggestedIndex`, which the muxer places outside the group tree, so the shared config needs no slot for them.\n\nThe provider set is the one we mean to launch with: a subset of the searchbar's, plus URL navigation, and no history beyond autofill. Recognizing the SAP as a search source for telemetry is the rest of the bug.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319411\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarPrefs.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarProvidersManager.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/SmartbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInputBase.mjs"], "git_node": "a59d6c4e18264bed6e022ece60a654828c60e359", "git_parents": ["82def3f8a6f009cf831b79cf38bf7d7f0a0b506d"], "node": "4135d90bd6df3c0264107c28a2a257716ee70dd0", "parents": ["7c36dc8533d1d3b164e827f871d06b34020bc02d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Serban Stanca \u003csstanca@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2063602 - [efficiency] Do not fail a test when closeSoftKeyboard() cannot hide the keyboard r=aaronmt\" as requested by @jajohnson for wrongly assigned the bug number.\n\nThis reverts commit 2b6c7f4fe5c0a63da0831dbacff2f3b193b5243f.\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/BasePage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/SettingsAutofillPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/SettingsSearchAddSearchEnginePage.kt"], "git_node": "1080686d04e8327a666ff48422a10c68cb777c42", "git_parents": ["a59d6c4e18264bed6e022ece60a654828c60e359"], "node": "e80846c2e67de7b28f0f481d4441b23004ccdd51", "parents": ["4135d90bd6df3c0264107c28a2a257716ee70dd0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Serban Stanca \u003csstanca@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2053212 - Don't clear the status bar just because the frame was reframed. r=smaug\" for causing bp-nu bustages.\n\nThis reverts commit 899a7381c0b1f83a7bc445376c7e08f070c0ecac.\n", "files": ["dom/events/EventStateManager.cpp", "dom/events/EventStateManager.h"], "git_node": "999464fe3c9d9e9852a62af6d16fd72f9607cb05", "git_parents": ["1080686d04e8327a666ff48422a10c68cb777c42"], "node": "53c625ca1242d96b916e8519acb7daa15076b2f3", "parents": ["e80846c2e67de7b28f0f481d4441b23004ccdd51"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Serban Stanca \u003csstanca@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2062837, Bug 2060712 - test(webgpu): update CTS to 535149e23e538e4f8fe3d6266e32c68b7017ccc0 r=webgpu-reviewers,teoxoy\" for causing vendor failures.\n\nThis reverts commit 9965ea3fd96678b77d41ac87ed9db8ef1f348930.\n\nThis reverts commit 8b6cdc4f7726bdcc388416a35dfa76e4ec24a202.\n\nThis reverts commit 3fc847b28bcf892f1a5a5c4663753dd68674051e.\n", "files": ["dom/webgpu/tests/cts/checkout/CONTRIBUTING.md", "dom/webgpu/tests/cts/checkout/README.md", "dom/webgpu/tests/cts/checkout/src/webgpu/api/operation/rendering/depth.spec.ts", "dom/webgpu/tests/cts/checkout/src/webgpu/api/operation/sampling/sampler_texture.spec.ts", "dom/webgpu/tests/cts/checkout/src/webgpu/capability_info.ts", "dom/webgpu/tests/cts/checkout/src/webgpu/shader/execution/statement/swizzle_assignment.spec.ts", "dom/webgpu/tests/cts/checkout/src/webgpu/shader/validation/shader_io/builtins.spec.ts", "dom/webgpu/tests/cts/checkout/src/webgpu/shader/validation/statement/swizzle_assignment.spec.ts", "dom/webgpu/tests/cts/checkout/tools/gen_version", "dom/webgpu/tests/cts/moz.yaml", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/webgpu/cts/webgpu/api/operation/command_buffer/copyTextureToTexture/cts.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/webgpu/cts/webgpu/api/operation/command_buffer/image_copy/cts.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/webgpu/cts/webgpu/api/operation/rendering/3d_texture_slices/cts.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/webgpu/cts/webgpu/api/operation/rendering/depth/cts.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/webgpu/cts/webgpu/api/operation/sampling/sampler_texture/cts.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/webgpu/cts/webgpu/api/validation/capability_checks/limits/maxInterStageShaderVariables/cts.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/webgpu/cts/webgpu/api/validation/state/device_lost/destroy/cts.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozill