n for mfbt/ r=nika\n\nNo code generation impact expected, just easier maintenance.\n\nIn a few case, the spaceship operator could be used, but that's out of\nscope for this patch.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319166\n", "files": ["mfbt/Array.h", "mfbt/BitSet.h", "mfbt/Char16.h", "mfbt/CompactPair.h", "mfbt/DoublyLinkedList.h", "mfbt/EnumSet.h", "mfbt/EnumeratedRange.h", "mfbt/IntegerRange.h", "mfbt/LinkedList.h", "mfbt/Opaque.h", "mfbt/Saturate.h", "mfbt/ThreadSafeWeakPtr.h", "mfbt/UniquePtrExtensions.h", "mfbt/tests/TestCumulativeAverage.cpp", "mfbt/tests/TestRollingMean.cpp", "mfbt/tests/gtest/TestTainting.cpp"], "git_node": "ec70b754d810cb502c72f8e491c4455bfdb12fcc", "git_parents": ["1e2add2941ebb162e76648ee79f45969d0fcb5cb"], "node": "45b757dd72cf5c202b6ed50d3e988bd3cdfd3e5e", "parents": ["18af062c146505f7fae84936d4bbbdf0f74914c2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sajid Anwar \u003csajidanwar94@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064596 - Exclude border/padding when applying text-box-trim to inline boxes. r=layout-reviewers,dshin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319661\n", "files": ["layout/generic/nsLineLayout.cpp", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-inline/text-box-trim/text-box-trim-inline-box-004-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-inline/text-box-trim/text-box-trim-inline-box-004.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-inline/text-box-trim/text-box-trim-inline-box-005-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-inline/text-box-trim/text-box-trim-inline-box-005.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-inline/text-box-trim/text-box-trim-inline-box-006-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-inline/text-box-trim/text-box-trim-inline-box-006.html"], "git_node": "f60720040c58c42fd2a59e414bf78447638f2408", "git_parents": ["ec70b754d810cb502c72f8e491c4455bfdb12fcc"], "node": "a756f9aef18b7bfca087370a55afcd82b18b2bac", "parents": ["45b757dd72cf5c202b6ed50d3e988bd3cdfd3e5e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064026 - Check if iterator has reached the end of the string r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319073\n", "files": ["dom/base/MimeType.cpp"], "git_node": "c02b8e574951e9608e2a7f35808d366e8d771a57", "git_parents": ["f60720040c58c42fd2a59e414bf78447638f2408"], "node": "3f1e8298df8f1e4d144d79b40f1bc387217b0894", "parents": ["a756f9aef18b7bfca087370a55afcd82b18b2bac"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Benjamin Peterson \u003cbenjamin@python.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064482 - Remove empty browser_ipprotection_usage.js. r=ip-protection-reviewers,apopov\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319588\n", "files": ["browser/components/ipprotection/tests/browser/browser_ipprotection_usage.js"], "git_node": "900e996f98029e4d1d4a713ff283677c94bdd245", "git_parents": ["c02b8e574951e9608e2a7f35808d366e8d771a57"], "node": "6aad9a902123d83abadd14854f98f546cd5fa41a", "parents": ["3f1e8298df8f1e4d144d79b40f1bc387217b0894"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Janika \u003cjneuberger@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2046462 - Add x-restart-required flag to the policies schema r=bsmth,mkaply\n\nDeclare a required boolean \"x-restart-required\" on every policy describing\nwhether it only takes effect after a restart.\n\nContext: Firefox applies all policies once at startup and ignores this flag;\nit is consumed by downstream tooling that can apply policies live.\n\n- policies-schema.json: set the flag on BlockAboutConfig, BlockAboutSupport, ContentAnalysis, Cookies, DisableDeveloperTools, ExtensionSettings, HttpsOnlyMode, Proxy, SitePolicies, WebsiteFilter to true, and false for the rest.\n- policies-schema.meta.json: require the field and document its meaning.\n- test_policies_schema.js: cover the new required field.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319767\n", "files": ["browser/components/enterprisepolicies/schemas/policies-schema.json", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/schemas/policies-schema.meta.json", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/xpcshell/test_policies_schema.js"], "git_node": "8900a74e38528986453058402e520c57725cf988", "git_parents": ["900e996f98029e4d1d4a713ff283677c94bdd245"], "node": "a7ced021e33eabc95b8b85267899b4e13977cc23", "parents": ["6aad9a902123d83abadd14854f98f546cd5fa41a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Updatebot \u003cupdatebot@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064686 - Update android nightly application-services version bump to 13780acebfc945cc2d80e35d7cf732b097d58d28 r=dmeehan\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319748\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/plugins/dependencies/src/main/java/ApplicationServices.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/plugins/dependencies/src/main/java/moz.yaml"], "git_node": "3466a98b4fde02020bda4e7bc3cb7234215bc353", "git_parents": ["8900a74e38528986453058402e520c57725cf988"], "node": "1fe237ee60667a2b086d2cd3a8f76f67f2be136f", "parents": ["a7ced021e33eabc95b8b85267899b4e13977cc23"], "tags": []}, {"author": "nico.burns \u003cnico@nicoburns.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063602: Implement `flex-wrap: balance` and `flex-line-count` parsing (Servo-only) (r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio,layout-reviewers,dshin)\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318746\n", "files": ["layout/generic/nsFlexContainerFrame.cpp", "layout/style/ServoBindings.toml", "layout/style/nsStyleConsts.h", "layout/style/nsStyleStruct.cpp", "servo/components/style/properties/data.py", "servo/components/style/properties/longhands.toml", "servo/components/style/values/computed/mod.rs", "servo/components/style/values/computed/position.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/mod.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/position.rs", "servo/ports/geckolib/cbindgen.toml"], "git_node": "ff5db46b553f8407c7475449bb221770ebcb8dcf", "git_parents": ["3466a98b4fde02020bda4e7bc3cb7234215bc353"], "node": "17f42f0210795d6d9cf6141a15755a319726a0e2", "parents": ["1fe237ee60667a2b086d2cd3a8f76f67f2be136f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "mimi \u003cmjung@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059393 - Revert using uncached defaultBrowserCheck for set to default app menu messages r=omc-reviewers,sachung\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319181\n", "files": ["browser/components/asrouter/modules/OnboardingMessageProvider.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "4094cdf25b2e4245b4f42361c2566d2fae0a1978", "git_parents": ["ff5db46b553f8407c7475449bb221770ebcb8dcf"], "node": "5dac7cf429b7d943129813a30651e699c7eb22f9", "parents": ["17f42f0210795d6d9cf6141a15755a319726a0e2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Mehic \u003cdmehic@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1964322 - Wait for the IdP cookie popup in setupTest r=baku\n\nsetupTest opens helper_set_cookie.html to set credential=authcookieval, but\nnothing waits for it. focusPromise is created before window.open and resolves\non the test window, so it says nothing about the popup, and fetchPromise is\nthe unrelated set_test request. navigator.credentials.get() therefore races\nthe cookie.\n\n11 of the 15 server_*_accounts.sjs endpoints answer 400 when the cookie is\nabsent, which fails the FedCM flow and rejects get(), surfacing as\n\"must not have an error\".\n\nHave the popup postMessage its opener before closing and wait for that. The\ncookie comes from the popup's response headers, so it is already committed by\nthe time the popup's script runs.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317329\n", "files": ["dom/credentialmanagement/identity/tests/mochitest/head.js", "dom/credentialmanagement/identity/tests/mochitest/helper_set_cookie.html"], "git_node": "92cd30db1024545541f9c7b661e6fb839b85c957", "git_parents": ["4094cdf25b2e4245b4f42361c2566d2fae0a1978"], "node": "6fc41a5c7df61f90098be1dc478d43f9f23c01a7", "parents": ["5dac7cf429b7d943129813a30651e699c7eb22f9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "alin lastun \u003calastun@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1969984 - Part 1: Add retry action to the \"send to device\" failure snackbar from Tabs Tray r=android-reviewers,twhite\n\nReplace the plain Toast in SendToDevicesDialogFragment.sendAndDismiss with a\n      Snackbar, and add a RETRY action on failure.\n\n   Note: There will be more patches where we will add retry buttons to different snackbars.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316763\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/share/SendToDevicesDialogFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/share/SendToDevicesDialogFragmentTest.kt"], "git_node": "921fd8d35a1313efca648f58fb0068ec8665a496", "git_parents": ["92cd30db1024545541f9c7b661e6fb839b85c957"], "node": "ce98bfb626f5d4a9b53a4c15ef12064104e3312a", "parents": ["6fc41a5c7df61f90098be1dc478d43f9f23c01a7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "alin lastun \u003calastun@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1969984 - Part 2: Add retry action to add-on enable/disable/uninstall failure snackbars r=android-reviewers,android-l10n-reviewers,android-addons-reviewers,lmccracken,parker,rpl\n\nAdd a 'Retry' button to error snackbars for add-on operations (enable, disable, uninstall), allowing the user to retry the failed operation directly instead of manually repeating the action\n\n   Note: There will be more patches where we will add retry buttons to different snackbars.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317431\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/addons/Extensions.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/addons/InstalledAddonDetailsFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/addons/InstalledAddonDetailsFragmentTest.kt"], "git_node": "2c525ed89199c45414d54ffb6d8e8b888edacc09", "git_parents": ["921fd8d35a1313efca648f58fb0068ec8665a496"], "node": "6eb79d489b34a1dd8007013f5e3bfd048e667dc9", "parents": ["ce98bfb626f5d4a9b53a4c15ef12064104e3312a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Markus Stange \u003cmstange.moz@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064208 - Update samply toolchain revision. r=perftest-reviewers,kshampur\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319266\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/fetch/toolchains.yml"], "git_node": "f75e25f9727765c54afb0148c56a661c1da7de01", "git_parents": ["2c525ed89199c45414d54ffb6d8e8b888edacc09"], "node": "914c0b950bd9108e6d51b368e1d2a58adf28a4ca", "parents": ["6eb79d489b34a1dd8007013f5e3bfd048e667dc9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Markus Stange \u003cmstange.moz@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063683 - Emit ETW SourceLoad events and report the JIT function's source location separately from its name. r=profiler-reviewers,canova\n\nOur previous Windows ETW JIT instrumentation was appending \" (file:line:col)\"\nto the MethodLoad name leaving the SourceID, Line and Column fields at zero.\n\nTo allow samply to emit cleaner profiles, where the function location is stored\nin the usual place and not in the name, let's emit those things separately.\n\nWe emit the JScript SourceLoad event once per ScriptSource, fill in the\nMethodLoad SourceID/Line/Column fields, and drop the location from the\nname. This matches what V8 does in src/diagnostics/etw-jit-win.cc.\n\nUnlike V8, we still keep the JIT tier in the name.\n\nOn non-Windows, jitdump still wants the source location in the name (for now),\nso that behavior is retained.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318837\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/