3500901ce96f7fa5f27bec22", "git_parents": ["4ab5e7cbcbd712a18a5a24bc9dce3729bd7bef9a"], "node": "0158c4f5aa00b9e2bac2471f1ef62817a4218778", "parents": ["cbc216bce2d6707eef6bcecf698cb7e5ea27f594"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kershaw Chang \u003ckershaw@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064432 - Capture DNS fromStaleCache at serve time r=mxinden,necko-reviewers,valentin\n\nnsIDNSAddrRecord::fromStaleCache is currently derived from CheckExpiration() at read time, which can make fresh 0-TTL answers look stale because they enter the grace window immediately.\nThis patch stores the flag on nsHostRecord instead: set it only when serving a grace-period entry from cache, and clear it on every fresh resolution.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319847\n", "files": ["netwerk/dns/nsHostRecord.cpp", "netwerk/dns/nsHostRecord.h", "netwerk/dns/nsHostResolver.cpp", "netwerk/test/unit/test_dns_stale_zero_ttl.js", "netwerk/test/unit/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "8b0df7e4211e48b441bc762d5dfd698ef1ed9eec", "git_parents": ["73989f1e3f9752653500901ce96f7fa5f27bec22"], "node": "97e22c7d0c0276dc4484709f0f1f416d0c01d4c4", "parents": ["0158c4f5aa00b9e2bac2471f1ef62817a4218778"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1892761 - Fold the SessionStore shell object into SessionStoreInternal and export that under the public name. r=sfoster\n\nThe accessors over internal state, the split view id counter and the tab group reopen telemetry did more than forward, and some members lose their underscore prefix as the public API. The object is no longer frozen, since it now holds the mutable session state, and the browser-taking getCurrentEpoch is gone for lack of callers.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318434\n", "files": ["browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_ext_tabs_events.js", "browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStore.sys.mjs", "browser/components/tabbrowser/Tabbrowser.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "1bbb5d7b3d6fd019fb99e1106c31f691f821ff84", "git_parents": ["8b0df7e4211e48b441bc762d5dfd698ef1ed9eec"], "node": "1c01e9e1d9117a3b1abc42ac884f410a19c84d3b", "parents": ["97e22c7d0c0276dc4484709f0f1f416d0c01d4c4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060837 part 1 - Don't add Uint8Array.prototype.equals in IOUtils tests. r=robwu\n\nAdding properties to builtin prototypes no longer works when we enable `freezeBuiltins` for chrome windows.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318388\n", "files": ["xpcom/ioutils/tests/file_ioutils_test_fixtures.js", "xpcom/ioutils/tests/test_ioutils_read_write.html"], "git_node": "885c3e7dca9ce10144620c7c6596d162176d0350", "git_parents": ["1bbb5d7b3d6fd019fb99e1106c31f691f821ff84"], "node": "7d4b1dd23fe7d96a127e733f1f02dcb6550d5ef0", "parents": ["1c01e9e1d9117a3b1abc42ac884f410a19c84d3b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060837 part 2 - Change import map tests for bug 1979050 to plain mochitests. r=allstarschh\n\nWe want to enable `freezeBuiltins` for chrome windows, and with that change we can no\nlonger add properties to `Object.prototype`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318389\n", "files": ["dom/base/test/jsmodules/importmaps/chrome.toml", "dom/base/test/jsmodules/importmaps/mochitest.toml", "dom/base/test/jsmodules/importmaps/test_1979050.html", "dom/base/test/jsmodules/importmaps/test_1979050_2.html"], "git_node": "4e5be12bb16273702d91e5e26d7e161e095f0c80", "git_parents": ["885c3e7dca9ce10144620c7c6596d162176d0350"], "node": "b6ab1489c146a71d2fbe12468722c166fbaa2586", "parents": ["7d4b1dd23fe7d96a127e733f1f02dcb6550d5ef0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064136 - Document the tabbrowser's undocumented parameters. r=sthompson,tabbrowser-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319243\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/Tabbrowser.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "13cdd9bc6db050a8bc08b2eb97247a618f66faa0", "git_parents": ["4e5be12bb16273702d91e5e26d7e161e095f0c80"], "node": "1a74b76f3daabd0d8863a6040ec5b7b6e6a29e66", "parents": ["b6ab1489c146a71d2fbe12468722c166fbaa2586"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064136 - Reconcile the documented parameter names with the signatures. r=sthompson,tabbrowser-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319244\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/Tabbrowser.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "542a59d01fc2ff2a333ecf3e99e3fe42ef2b5761", "git_parents": ["13cdd9bc6db050a8bc08b2eb97247a618f66faa0"], "node": "338c316b8b89feec07754e445ae11861c97d878e", "parents": ["1a74b76f3daabd0d8863a6040ec5b7b6e6a29e66"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064136 - Describe the documented properties of the tabbrowser's typedefs. r=sthompson,tabbrowser-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319245\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/Tabbrowser.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "1c6d7758de5da78a0308217ee22c4f836067f251", "git_parents": ["542a59d01fc2ff2a333ecf3e99e3fe42ef2b5761"], "node": "b915a5bdea30a4ad88eba579d7ec498a882253ff", "parents": ["338c316b8b89feec07754e445ae11861c97d878e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064136 - Generate a gBrowser API reference from the tabbrowser's JSDoc. r=sthompson,tabbrowser-reviewers,frontend-codestyle-reviewers,mossop\n\ndocs/config.yml requires that anything in js_source_paths lints under the strict jsdoc rules, which is what the eslint-rollouts.config.mjs change is for and what the commits below make possible.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319246\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/Tabbrowser.sys.mjs", "browser/components/tabbrowser/docs/api.md", "browser/components/tabbrowser/docs/index.md", "docs/config.yml", "eslint-rollouts.config.mjs"], "git_node": "bbb47ddbe05166242d7d4265e93446b830846245", "git_parents": ["1c6d7758de5da78a0308217ee22c4f836067f251"], "node": "ab57b34b4b66ff30100a41e1713de82ed8a57b52", "parents": ["b915a5bdea30a4ad88eba579d7ec498a882253ff"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060837 part 3 - Enable freezeBuiltins for chrome windows. r=robwu,webidl,emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318390\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsGlobalWindowOuter.cpp", "js/xpconnect/tests/browser/browser_freeze_builtins.js"], "git_node": "ce2d524da1a182bab73c7a78f7b036467d89cd28", "git_parents": ["bbb47ddbe05166242d7d4265e93446b830846245"], "node": "917c67f157165b00b5a620297e992d08d1ea1d70", "parents": ["ab57b34b4b66ff30100a41e1713de82ed8a57b52"], "tags": []}, {"author": "rperta \u003crperta@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2064596 - Exclude border/padding when applying text-box-trim to inline boxes. r=layout-reviewers,dshin\" for causing wr failures at text-box-trim-inline-box-005.html\n\nThis reverts commit bec057ba804ef1beeb181accc925097cbb8a1360.\n", "files": ["layout/generic/nsLineLayout.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-inline/text-box-trim/text-box-trim-inline-box-005.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-inline/text-box-trim/text-box-trim-inline-box-004-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-inline/text-box-trim/text-box-trim-inline-box-004.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-inline/text-box-trim/text-box-trim-inline-box-005-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-inline/text-box-trim/text-box-trim-inline-box-005.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-inline/text-box-trim/text-box-trim-inline-box-006-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-inline/text-box-trim/text-box-trim-inline-box-006.html"], "git_node": "52dab2f70d34604d7c3205d055ba709cf55f88fb", "git_parents": ["ce2d524da1a182bab73c7a78f7b036467d89cd28"], "node": "d7cf11611536df7219a251cb1834e086cce05453", "parents": ["917c67f157165b00b5a620297e992d08d1ea1d70"], "tags": []}, {"author": "rperta \u003crperta@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2062852 part 4: Start accessibility when accessibility.force_disabled changes to -1 at runtime. r=eeejay,geckoview-reviewers,m_kato\" for causing ThreadSanitizer failures\n\nThis reverts commit 9752743055a8a98ef1bcab3c68302d0651bd6e05.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2062852 part 3: Enable ATK to be reinitialised after it is shut down. r=eeejay\"\n\nThis reverts commit c8ef71edc46b7f2b144cb2a566aa2472b80b4151.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2062852 part 2: Remove the Windows specific accessibility force enable priming hack. r=eeejay\"\n\nThis reverts commit 3595a736aa06fb2915a4eb6e4c53f31f0327aadf.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2062852 part 1: Centrally handle accessibility.force_disabled=-1 (force enable) for all platforms. r=eeejay\"\n\nThis reverts commit 2e9006c7240bfbc413a1ee5bd717f8aec350f8c1.\n", "files": ["accessible/android/SessionAccessibility.cpp", "accessible/atk/Platform.cpp", "accessible/base/Platform.h", "accessible/base/nsAccessibilityService.cpp", "accessible/moz.build", "accessible/tests/browser/atk/browser.toml", "accessible/tests/browser/atk/browser_forceEnabled.js", "accessible/tests/browser/browser_shutdown_pref.js", "accessible/tests/browser/forceEnabled/browser.toml", "accessible/tests/browser/forceEnabled/browser_forceEnabled.js", "accessible/tests/browser/windows/ia2/browser.toml", "accessible/tests/browser/windows/ia2/browser_forceEnabled.js", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/test/AccessibilityTest.kt", "modules/libpref/init/all.js", "toolkit/xre/nsAppRunner.cpp", "widget/windows/WinMessages.h", "widget/windows/nsWindow.cpp"], "git_node": "c1e376bfc07a58900d1dd34008718d6e5efd2237", "git_parents": ["52dab2f70d34604d7c3205d055ba709cf55f88fb"], "node": "b64bd3f67d32aaaab1da4b3e8c1b87f251d74511", "parents": ["d7cf11611536df7219a251cb1834e086cce05453"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Rubino \u003cdrubino@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064113 - Remove the two-stage launch-on-login infobar. r=omc-reviewers,aminomancer\n\nINFOBAR_LAUNCH_ON_LOGIN and INFOBAR_LAUNCH_ON_LOGIN_FINAL asked users from\nabout:newtab to turn on launch on login, the second one re-asking 14 days after\nthe first. Now that new installs are defaulted into launch on login by the\ndefaultWindowsLaunchOnLogin rollouts, a user who has the setting off has chosen\nto have it off, so the prompt has no audience left worth interrupting.\n\nRemoves both messages along with the strings only they used. The \"show and\ntell\" strings stay: they belong to a separate, remotely delivered message.\n\nbrowser_asrouter_infobar.js referenced launch-on-login-infobar-message only as\na sample Fluent ID while exercising the array form of formatMessageConfig, so\nit now points at another string in the same file.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319207\n", "files": ["browser/components/asrouter/modules/OnboardingMessageProvider.sys.mjs", "browser/components/asrouter/tests/browser/browser_asrouter_infobar.js", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/newtab/asrouter.ftl"], "git_node": "ecffd2eaca1e047c65aa681c2011cb3a8d84a18d", "git_parents": ["c1e376bfc07a58900d1dd34008718d6e5efd2237"], "node": "28970ff85a04afb5b64c8a6d8ed0117983da9b3d", "parents": ["b64bd3f67d32aaaab1da4b3e8c1b87f251d74511"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Rubino \u003cdrubino@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064113 - Remove the launch-on-login prompt suppression pref. r=omc-reviewers,mconley,aminomancer\n\nbrowser.startup.windowsLaunchOnLogin.disableLaunchOnLoginPrompt existed only to\nstop the two-stage launch-on-login infobar from asking again, so with those\nmessages gone nothing reads it.\n\nMost of it was written from LaunchOnLogin.enablementDetails(), which set the\npref as a side effect of being asked for the current state. That made a\nread-only-looking API mutate the profile, and it was also the only thing\nkeeping the prompt away from users who had launch on login enabled at install\nand later turned it off. Removing the prompt removes the need for both.\n\nOne live recipe reads this pref: the suppress-legacy-launch-on-login-infobars\nrollout, which neutralizes these two messages in the field by shipping the same\nmessage IDs with no content at a higher priority. With the pref gone its\ntargeting clause stops matching on builds carrying this patch, which is\nharmless because the messages it suppresses are removed here; on 152-156 the\npref still exists and the rollout keeps working unchanged. Nothing else in the\nnimbus-desktop-experiments collection references the pref, so dropping it from\nthe SET_PREF allowlist changes no other remotely delivered message.\n\nThe urlbar suppress-tips harness set the pref so the infobar would not take the\nnotification box that the search tip assertions depend on. That workaround is\nno longer needed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319208\n", "files": ["browser/app/profile/firefox.js", "browser/components/preferences/main.js", "browser/components/shell/StartupOSIntegration.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-tips/suppress-tips/browser.toml", "toolkit/components/messaging-system/lib/SpecialMessageActions.sys.mjs", "toolkit/modules/launchonlogin/LaunchOnLogin.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "02aa8f1bcf8a3bf34f359b2391d8eefc5da98b0c", "git_parents": ["ecffd2eaca1e047c65aa681c2011cb3a8d84a18d"], "node": "97b37e70d0294875c6ce5a7790d4fd810f936441", "parents": ["28970ff85a04afb5b64c8a6d8ed0117983da9b3d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rong Bao \u003cwebmaster@csmantle.top\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065007 - Redefine X11's Success macro to X11Success to avoid conflicts. r=gfx-reviewers,gtk-reviewers,lsalzman,emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319993\n", "files": ["gfx/gl/GLContextProviderGLX.cpp", "gfx/src/X11UndefineNone.h", "gfx/thebes/gfxPlatformGtk.cpp", "widget/gtk/WidgetUtilsGtk.cpp"], "git_node": "27def1ef41e52d649470661dd2e1f35631a2c53e", "git_parents": ["02aa8f1bcf8a3bf34f359b2391d8eefc5da98b0c"], "node": "a1dc598c7f1bab4589abd4d040304a31cac18fa5", "parents": ["97b37e70d0294875c6ce5a7790d4fd810f936441"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Hommey \u003cmh+mozilla@glandium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064602 - Fix the imply_option for MOZ_LD64_KNOWN_GOOD. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sylvestre\n\nUsing moz_automation directly makes it forcefully disabled on\nnon-automation builds (with no way to override), which wasn't the\noriginal intent before bug 1686880.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319671\n", "files": ["build/moz.configure/lto-pgo.configure"], "git_node": "558255a948f6798296be39533d56a8b05bf20b77", "git_parents": ["27def1ef41e52d649470661dd2e1f35631a2c53e"], "node": "552ca82b71f111375e7b7a179d5d5c17591213fc", "parents": ["a1dc598c7f1bab4589abd4d040304a31cac18fa5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "mayankleoboy1 \u003cmayankleoboy1@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062885 - Fix O(N^2) complexity in BytecodeAnalysis JSOp::Try handling by using a sorted two-pointer approach. r=jandem\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318528\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/BytecodeAnalysis.cpp", "js/src/jit/BytecodeAnalysis.h"], "git_node": "dbcab79eab7cb1105f734958875663028acd7f44", "git_parents": ["558255a948f6798296be39533d56a8b05bf20b77"], "node": "3b5910af9f5a85a69cac5dea9ef3942b4b788866", "parents": ["552ca82b71f111375e7b7a179d5d5c17591213fc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055837 - set PYTHON env variable in gtests runner. r=ci-and-tooling,aryx\n\nWe set PYTHON to `python3` when using taskcluster-built python in CI.\nWhen inherited by a gtest that uses ShellExecuteExW, that doesn't\nresolve to the right thing.  Explicitly set it to sys.executable instead\nso the tests use the same python as the harness.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315548\n", "files": ["testing/gtest/rungtests.py"], "git_node": "667bdb839726cf613a8ee525f3b10152c17fbf2c", "git_parents": ["dbcab79eab7cb1105f734958875663028acd7f44"], "node": "e6aff764bebfabb244e82157aa14617e9b0a0998", "parents": ["3b5910af9f5a85a69cac5dea9ef3942b4b788866"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055837 - build python3.9 wheels for pycairo and pygobject. r=taskgraph-reviewers,bhearsum\n\nAs we're moving wpt to use taskcluster-built python, those tasks need\ncorresponding libs.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315549\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/fetch/python-wheels.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/toolchain/python-wheels.yml"], "git_node": "dc159f38da928989ba2e7775f11c8d37f4dc6602", "git_parents": ["667bdb839726cf613a8ee525f3b10152c17fbf2c"], "node": "9b774edef14d564e64b1119a932382d471dfaf54", "parents": ["e6aff764bebfabb244e82157aa14617e9b0a0998"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Gaul \u003candrew@gaul.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064314 - jit/arm64: store xzr for storePtr(ImmPtr(nullptr)). r=jandem\n\nstorePtr(ImmPtr, Address) was the only arm64 store-immediate variant\nwithout a zero check: it materialized 0 into a scratch (mov xN,#0) and\nstored that, whereas store8/16/32 and storePtr(ImmWord) already store\nwzr/xzr directly. Add the same check so a null pointer is stored as str\nxzr.\n\nDominant caller is profilerEnterFrame, which stores null to\nJitActivation::lastProfilingCallSite in every method prologue (also\nNativeIterator init and other nullptr stores). Removes ~3.5k mov\ninstructions across Octane's Baseline tier. Code-size win (most are in\nthe normally-skipped profiler-enter stub); wall-clock neutral on M4.\n\nFound via armlint.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319400\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/arm64/MacroAssembler-arm64.h"], "git_node": "afa65dfecbe55c2495dd572e2cd3599111a764aa", "git_parents": ["dc159f38da928989ba2e7775f11c8d37f4dc6602"], "node": "277e26d0dbdeeabe6fbafa39a8965d3013a48ef3", "parents": ["9b774edef14d564e64b1119a932382d471dfaf54"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2050672 - Make mozscreenshots screenshot crop lossless. r=Gijs\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310342\n", "files": ["browser/tools/mozscreenshots/mozscreenshots/extension/TestRunner.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "5b0bcf1ddb62d381a395288e3af78dd01ec63965", "git_parents": ["afa65dfecbe55c2495dd572e2cd3599111a764aa"], "node": "375d07dcae52c3925128caaae6b8f1923f681c2a", "parents": ["277e26d0dbdeeabe6fbafa39a8965d3013a48ef3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2050672 - Add Nova and ColorScheme mozscreenshots configurations. r=sclements,sthompson,dao\n\nThe identifier referenced were given by design people, possibly\nreferencing some other document / figma, I kept them verbatim.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310343\n", "files": ["browser/tools/mozscreenshots/moz.build", "browser/tools/mozscreenshots/mozscreenshots/extension/configurations/ColorScheme.sys.mjs", "browser/tools/mozscreenshots/mozscreenshots/extension/configurations/Nova.sys.mjs", "browser/tools/mozscreenshots/mozscreenshots/extension/moz.build", "browser/tools/mozscreenshots/nova/browser.toml", "browser/tools/mozscreenshots/nova/browser_nova.js"], "git_node": "ce7643fa12d1f231a2abc947129c8a248719135a", "git_parents": ["5b0bcf1ddb62d381a395288e3af78dd01ec63965"], "node": "6c3df00a52a1136ec766b0ac3ba58a9ecf6b40c3", "parents": ["375d07dcae52c3925128caaae6b8f1923f681c2a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2050672 - Add a no-nova variant to mochitest-browser-screenshots. r=jlorenzo\n\nNova is now enabled by default, so the plain task already produces the Nova\nscreenshots. The variant is flipped to no-nova to keep capturing the classic\nUI as well. layout.css.devPixelsPerPx is pinned on the task rather than on\nthe variant so both runs are captured at 1x.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310344\n", "files": ["taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/transforms/test/__init__.py", "taskcluster/kinds/mochitest/kind.yml"], "git_node": "c3708d2466d96dd697bbe60551e08d71999f58c5", "git_parents": ["ce7643fa12d1f231a2abc947129c8a248719135a"], "node": "df4da10218b44a6a519297c1535139c31be7928c", "parents": ["6c3df00a52a1136ec766b0ac3ba58a9ecf6b40c3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2050672 - Re-enable font antialiasing for mozscreenshots on Linux. r=jcristau\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310345\n", "files": ["taskcluster/docker/ubuntu2404-test/Dockerfile", "taskcluster/docker/ubuntu2404-test/fonts-aa.conf", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/transforms/test/worker.py"], "git_node": "40e5c7fcb0cf6d94abed7219c36296563e05e0ae", "git_parents": ["c3708d2466d96dd697bbe60551e08d71999f58c5"], "node": "bd737214a3e8dcd4508b1c8ae1f4a01e8b07b1d2", "parents": ["df4da10218b44a6a519297c1535139c31be7928c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandra Borovova \u003caborovova@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064782 - Update metadata for fetch/local-network-access/service-worker.tentative.https.html.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320022\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/fetch/local-network-access/service-worker.tentative.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "b8e66c28fbd5afe0a0a8a4086be4122c44ddb678", "git_parents": ["40e5c7fcb0cf6d94abed7219c36296563e05e0ae"], "node": "a0e283e0ec7d32e347993e48d1a9f5253726090c", "parents": ["bd737214a3e8dcd4508b1c8ae1f4a01e8b07b1d2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mugurell \u003cMugurell@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2051483 - Record telemetry about the trackers protection dashboard being opened where this happens r=android-reviewers,jdelorenzo\n\nThis comes to fix 2 issues:\n- avoid `ProtectionsDashboardFragment` knowing of all the features in the app\nthat can request the dashboard to be shown\n- remove from GlobalDirections.ProtectionsDashboard the \"deep_link\" hardcoded\nsource since this direction is meant to be reusable.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313488\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/metrics.yaml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/GlobalDirections.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/intent/HomeDeepLinkIntentProcessor.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/logo/TrackingProtectionController.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/trustpanel/middleware/TrustPanelTelemetryMiddleware.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabstray/controller/TabManagerController.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/trackingprotection/ProtectionsDashboardFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/navigation/nav_graph.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/intent/HomeDeepLinkIntentProcessorTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/logo/TrackingProtectionControllerTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/trustpanel/TrustPanelTelemetryMiddlewareTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabstray/controller/DefaultTabManagerControllerTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/trackingprotection/ProtectionsDashboardFragmentTest.kt"], "git_node": "60e216b95bb3b4bfc9c07abf2f476d1a19cf8fc7", "git_parents": ["b8e66c28fbd5afe0a0a8a4086be4122c44ddb678"], "node": "1250df6f404cf94a9cd5015118ea67d751fb4483", "parents": ["a0e283e0ec7d32e347993e48d1a9f5253726090c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "mayankleoboy1 \u003cmayankleoboy1@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1968416 - Collapse to the focused node's start directly on focus move. r=masayuki,layout-reviewers,emilio\n\nnsFocusManager::MoveCaretToFocus() cleared the selection, added a new range\ncovering the focused node, and then collapsed to that range's start.  Adding\nthe range in between marked, and then immediately unmarked, the whole\nflattened subtree of its closest common inclusive ancestor, which is what\nmakes focusing a huge dropdown slow.\n\nCollapse to the range's start directly instead.  Adding the range also set\nthe interline position to StartOfNextLine, and collapsing then kept it,\nbecause ComputeCaretAssociationHint() returns the hint it is given untouched\nunless that hint is Before.  Set it explicitly so the caret keeps ending up\nwhere it did.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315876\n", "files": ["dom/base/Selection.cpp", "dom/base/Selection.h", "dom/base/nsFocusManager.cpp", "layout/base/tests/mochitest.toml", "layout/base/tests/test_caret_browsing_focus_move.html"], "git_node": "7c518c648ee0fb721729aa0b2052e20a11fe5ebf", "git_parents": ["60e216b95bb3b4bfc9c07abf2f476d1a19cf8fc7"], "node": "0ba488c40776bc1fc3101595f855acf95821ba1e", "parents": ["1250df6f404cf94a9cd5015118ea67d751fb4483"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Gaul \u003candrew@gaul.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064420 - jit/arm64: zero through wzr/xzr for xor-with-self. r=jandem\n\nShared code zeroes a register x86-style with xor32/xorPtr(reg, reg),\nwhich arm64 emitted verbatim as eor r,r,r. Unlike x86's xor idiom, eor\nwith itself is not dependency-breaking on ARM cores: it reads the old\nvalue, so the zeroing serializes behind whatever last wrote the register.\nEmit mov from wzr/xzr instead, which register renaming handles.\n\nThe callers are emitMegamorphicCacheLookup's miss path (the bulk),\nconvertValueToWasmAnyRef's null case, and a few trampolines. Found via\narmlint: the 139 'self-op identity' findings on Octane (111 Ion / 22\ntrampoline / 6 Baseline) drop to zero. Instruction count and code size\nare unchanged (one instruction replaces one); the win is removing the\nfalse dependency. A 12-run interleaved Octane A/B against origin/main\nwas flat on an M4 (total-score medians within 0.2%, every per-benchmark\nmedian within +/-0.6% except a +2.0% Richards outlier whose per-run\ndistributions overlap, i.e. noise).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319521\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/arm64/MacroAssembler-arm64-inl.h"], "git_node": "853094920ea608b5e81443c0040c7ac3a0121047", "git_parents": ["7c518c648ee0fb721729aa0b2052e20a11fe5ebf"], "node": "b8b61f39a8b20161e9bd91dd288f87f7e906b6b2", "parents": ["0ba488c40776bc1fc3101595f855acf95821ba1e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Timothy Nikkel \u003ctnikkel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063947. Reapply libFuzzer's local patches to the vendored sources. r=truber\n\nThe five patches listed in moz.yaml are not applied to the vendored sources. FuzzerIO.cpp\nin the tree is byte for byte identical to compiler-rt/lib/fuzzer/FuzzerIO.cpp at the\nrevision moz.yaml records, and the same holds for the other fourteen files this touches, so\nthe sources went in without the patch step when libFuzzer was upgraded in bug 1996685.\n\nIt does not seem like it was an intentional decision to drop them. The same change rebased\nall five patch files against the new upstream and deleted a sixth,\n14-explicit-allocator.patch, which is the opposite of what retiring the rest would look\nlike. They were added deliberately too: bug 1635762 added four of them along with vendoring\nlibFuzzer from git, and bug 1695761 added 15-return-to-exit so that libFuzzer returns\ninstead of calling exit(), as its title says.\n\nPatches are applied by a separate `mach vendor --patch-mode only` step, so it is easy for\nthe sources to go in without them, and until now nothing checked that vendoring reproduced\nwhat is committed.\n\nAlso point the moz.yaml at Core :: Fuzzing rather than Core :: General, which is where\nlibFuzzer bugs are filed anyway, including the upgrade in bug 1996685. Updatebot files from\nthat block, so its update bugs were going to the wrong place.\n\nThis is what `./mach vendor tools/fuzzing/libfuzzer/moz.yaml -r\n5b7a5f7c5f3c1dcd8ea9debf56983b85e393bc86 --patch-mode check --force` produces, so the\npatches still apply cleanly and no rebasing was needed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318987\n", "files": ["taskcluster/scripts/misc/vendor-verify-expected-fail.yml", "tools/fuzzing/libfuzzer/FuzzerDataFlowTrace.cpp", "tools/fuzzing/libfuzzer/FuzzerDataFlowTrace.h", "tools/fuzzing/libfuzzer/FuzzerDriver.cpp", "tools/fuzzing/libfuzzer/FuzzerFork.cpp", "tools/fuzzing/libfuzzer/FuzzerFork.h", "tools/fuzzing/libfuzzer/FuzzerIO.cpp", "tools/fuzzing/libfuzzer/FuzzerIO.h", "tools/fuzzing/libfuzzer/FuzzerIOPosix.cpp", "tools/fuzzing/libfuzzer/FuzzerIOWindows.cpp", "tools/fuzzing/libfuzzer/FuzzerInternal.h", "tools/fuzzing/libfuzzer/FuzzerLoop.cpp", "tools/fuzzing/libfuzzer/FuzzerMerge.cpp", "tools/fuzzing/libfuzzer/FuzzerMerge.h", "tools/fuzzing/libfuzzer/FuzzerTracePC.cpp", "tools/fuzzing/libfuzzer/FuzzerTracePC.h", "tools/fuzzing/libfuzzer/moz.yaml"], "git_node": "f957f67a08a7872d2eb64e69e15d06d7a9c773cc", "git_parents": ["853094920ea608b5e81443c0040c7ac3a0121047"], "node": "7ca75bcf0bbd51856fff240d74946a811c5bad0a", "parents": ["b8b61f39a8b20161e9bd91dd288f87f7e906b6b2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandra Borovova \u003caborovova@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064756 - Enable \"layout.css.scroll-driven-animations.enabled\" preference for css/css-viewport/zoom/animation-range.html. r=emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320018\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-viewport/zoom/animation-range.html.ini"], "git_node": "ee2694aa86322f609287de45064105979b8de7bf", "git_parents": ["f957f67a08a7872d2eb64e69e15d06d7a9c773cc"], "node": "79fdf7c7492d8612adc59911ea22d35dde2eef84", "parents": ["7ca75bcf0bbd51856fff240d74946a811c5bad0a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dale Harvey \u003cdale@arandomurl.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062783 - Use moz-src for sessionstore. r=Gijs,omc-reviewers,migration-reviewers,firefox-desktop-core-reviewers ,jswinarton,hsohaney,sclements,aminomancer,perftest-reviewers,kshampur\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317956\n", "files": ["browser/actors/AboutTabCrashedParent.sys.mjs", "browser/base/content/browser-places.js", "browser/base/content/browser.js", "browser/base/content/test/about/browser_aboutCertError.js", "browser/base/content/test/tabPrompts/browser_prompt_close_groups.js", "browser/base/content/test/tabcrashed/browser_autoSubmitRequest.js", "browser/components/BrowserComponents.manifest", "browser/components/BrowserContentHandler.sys.mjs", "browser/components/BrowserGlue.sys.mjs", "browser/components/DefaultBrowserCheck.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/AIWindow.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/AIWindowTabStatesManager.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/TabManagementService.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwind