4de7ee0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Atila Butkovits \u003cabutkovits@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2063759 - Avoid line-clamp style adjustment for displays that aren't block/inline. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio,layout-reviewers\" for causing failures at webkit-line-clamp-016.html.\n\nThis reverts commit c0e30ee6b7d3a74774a61e1ff685cad2ef1aa72c.\n", "files": ["layout/generic/nsBlockFrame.cpp", "servo/components/style/style_adjuster.rs", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/webkit-line-clamp-bug-2063759-crash.html"], "git_node": "b24081a77576ba0e451da29f42ab118b3f84a925", "git_parents": ["609c4cf1fabf8297f084b3eac338b6c78475b873"], "node": "a2caac044137370923b8d150b21858dd70a80fc7", "parents": ["1a7f6c0bf483e4d1be4bfe1d0c6a1c131b09b663"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Cristian Tuns \u003cctuns@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2055837 - use taskcluster-built python for web-platform-tests tasks. r=taskgraph-reviewers,bhearsum\"\n\nThis reverts commit 6c323749e63591cd33fc2d121e3c130dd0d6907f.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2055837 - use taskcluster-built python for reftest tasks. r=taskgraph-reviewers,bhearsum\"\n\nThis reverts commit 2b7c61324e7f95c1fe18db8688e3f0e1e93163a5.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2055837 - use taskcluster-built python for mochitest tasks. r=taskgraph-reviewers,bhearsum\"\n\nThis reverts commit 12415db457fc7adc6c13fda6b3ccc6a9e724b3bc.\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/mochitest/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/reftest/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/web-platform-tests/kind.yml"], "git_node": "b7a4077d9860931302f91ad00da5a2c1511893f0", "git_parents": ["b24081a77576ba0e451da29f42ab118b3f84a925"], "node": "91f41217f4da4db50f1b7b154dddfe88d9e7f3cf", "parents": ["a2caac044137370923b8d150b21858dd70a80fc7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "unifolia \u003cjlewis@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064840 - Fix flaky test for browser_smartwindow_beta_badge and browser_aiwindow_switcher r=gcardieri\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319967\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_switcher.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_smartwindow_beta_badge.js"], "git_node": "bb06c115c3fb5533bab5dd6d5ef42facc0c7856d", "git_parents": ["b7a4077d9860931302f91ad00da5a2c1511893f0"], "node": "45b78da86f284df079415367fe134e2c92b77e97", "parents": ["91f41217f4da4db50f1b7b154dddfe88d9e7f3cf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan-Niklas Jaeschke \u003cjjaschke@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064792 - Bound the number of interfaces in an XPCNativeSet. r=dom-core-reviewers,mccr8\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320210\n", "files": ["js/xpconnect/src/XPCWrappedNativeInfo.cpp", "js/xpconnect/src/xpcprivate.h", "js/xpconnect/tests/unit/test_classinfo_too_many_interfaces.js", "js/xpconnect/tests/unit/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "a6e0324a44fd39ecd7b461bd0421eacc4122bb92", "git_parents": ["bb06c115c3fb5533bab5dd6d5ef42facc0c7856d"], "node": "c0c7d4d7fcbafd58fd1724b669564711b37f2fb7", "parents": ["45b78da86f284df079415367fe134e2c92b77e97"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kelly Cochrane \u003ckcochrane@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063778 - Remove min-height for .tab-background for horizontal split view tabs within tab groups r=desktop-theme-reviewers,tabbrowser-reviewers,nsharpley,dao\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319922\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/tabbrowser/tabs.css"], "git_node": "31eb0d29c480b37664e6a65ec839e06b47726250", "git_parents": ["a6e0324a44fd39ecd7b461bd0421eacc4122bb92"], "node": "71e6389516e1ff08fac02ed8d683b44ff1401f5a", "parents": ["c0c7d4d7fcbafd58fd1724b669564711b37f2fb7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex G \u003cagain@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062346 - [Monitor Agent][Models] Store an initial page snapshot and include it in the monitor check prompt r=tetchart\n\nFor monitor agent, when a task is created, this feature does the following:\n\n- Creates an initial snapshot of the page content and stores it in the\n  local monitor-store IndexedDB, via a new initialSnapshot field holding a\n  captured-at timestamp plus the extracted page text. Multiple watched\n  pages are extracted together and stored as one page-break-separated\n  blob, matching the format checks feed the model.\n- On every invocation of a monitor task, injects the stored initial page\n  content into the model context so change-type prompts (\"notify me when\n  the price drops\") can compare the latest page against the baseline.\n\nOf note:\n\n- No additional or recurring snapshots are created, except that any\n  committed edit of the monitor's definition (title, prompt, schedule, or\n  watch URLs) replaces the snapshot with one captured at edit time.\n  Pause/resume toggles keep the baseline. An edit also cancels any\n  in-flight capture, so a capture started for the previous definition can\n  never become the new baseline.\n- Failures are graceful and do not block creation or running of the task.\n- Backwards compatible: monitors created before this feature self-heal by\n  capturing a snapshot at run time.\n- If no snapshot is available due to error, a \"no initial snapshot is\n  available\" note is injected into the context instead.\n\nBumps the agent-monitor feature major version to 2; the packaged RS dump\ngains the v2 params and module records while older clients keep matching\nthe v1 records. Also covers the storage half tracked in bug 2062348.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318764\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/models/Utils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/agents/Monitor.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/agents/MonitorAgent.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/agents/MonitorStore.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_monitor_agent.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_monitor_store.js", "services/settings/dumps/main/ai-window-prompts.json"], "git_node": "418173ce145ae715d3d2944f843d4c7d12379f33", "git_parents": ["31eb0d29c480b37664e6a65ec839e06b47726250"], "node": "c06fadc88de7c7fa8bee1f1d96e9ae424b402323", "parents": ["71e6389516e1ff08fac02ed8d683b44ff1401f5a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Christopher DiPersio \u003ccdipersio@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064844 - PUWYLO v0: Gate feature to en locale r=cmurray,pdahiya\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319937\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/models/ConversationSuggestions.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_conversation_starters.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/head.js"], "git_node": "eaf0a0ed2cd9afaf4c2e7003df8732a96363904c", "git_parents": ["418173ce145ae715d3d2944f843d4c7d12379f33"], "node": "65dc49986bf625c65c6131c0b031278e29a98eab", "parents": ["c06fadc88de7c7fa8bee1f1d96e9ae424b402323"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Vincent Tunru \u003cgit@vincenttunru.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062876, Bug 2060155 - Update tracker count on page load panel opens. r=kandres,desktop-theme-reviewers,dao,daleharvey DONTBUILD\n\nApparently `onContentBlockingEvent` only gets called when a new category\nof trackers (e.g. fingerprinters) gets blocked, so if multiple trackers\nin the same category get blocked, the tracker count in the address bar\ndoesn't get updated anymore.\n\nTo compensate, this patch also manually recomputes the number of blocked\ntrackers on navigation complete, and when the trust panel gets opened,\nto ensure the two are always aligned.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319818\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser-trustPanel.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-trustPanel/browser_trust_panel_icon.js", "browser/themes/shared/identity-block/identity-block.css"], "git_node": "969f1fd2d807c7db379558b7469bb57dee877ecd", "git_parents": ["eaf0a0ed2cd9afaf4c2e7003df8732a96363904c"], "node": "7a6366eeb5c86fc4f52e80ee5fb98be0fb917cb3", "parents": ["65dc49986bf625c65c6131c0b031278e29a98eab"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Harveer Singh \u003chsingh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054702: Perform principal validation in PQuotaRequests.r=dom-storage-reviewers,jari,ArnaudBienner\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316654\n", "files": ["dom/quota/QuotaParent.cpp", "dom/quota/QuotaParent.h", "dom/tests/mochitest/localstorage/localStorageCommon.js", "toolkit/components/extensions/test/mochitest/test_ext_browsingData_indexedDB.html"], "git_node": "91ab66d3860f1a4870b05958ec276b5fa4f7e084", "git_parents": ["969f1fd2d807c7db379558b7469bb57dee877ecd"], "node": "0d75e3db15d6e0ba3da74b865be1ba1d44b21733", "parents": ["7a6366eeb5c86fc4f52e80ee5fb98be0fb917cb3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Beth Rennie \u003cbeth@brennie.ca\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058947 - Sort AboutRedirector's kRedirMap r=Gijs\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314996\n", "files": ["browser/components/about/AboutRedirector.cpp"], "git_node": "14aa4c808e098e1b15dc9808956c728994f7a9c3", "git_parents": ["91ab66d3860f1a4870b05958ec276b5fa4f7e084"], "node": "dba850b46a9230d5929d0dd00e74b2a51f702b61", "parents": ["0d75e3db15d6e0ba3da74b865be1ba1d44b21733"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064882 - Remove the android-gradle-dependencies-lite toolchain. r=ahochheiden\n\nBug 2063115 pointed the last of its consumers, the geckoview-lite builds, at the full dependency cache,\nso the Lite toolchain has been building an archive nothing fetches. Remove it along with the mozconfig\nand the enumeration scoping that existed only to serve it: every remaining pass covers a whole Gradle\nbuild, so the per-pass project list and the --gecko-only flag that populated it have no callers left.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319981\n", "files": ["mobile/android/config/mozconfigs/android-arm-gradle-dependencies/nightly-lite", "mobile/android/mach_commands.py", "taskcluster/kinds/toolchain/android.yml", "taskcluster/scripts/misc/android-gradle-dependencies-lite.sh"], "git_node": "04d7c4e93d0b4543c3f8cf285a4ea3baf20d885b", "git_parents": ["14aa4c808e098e1b15dc9808956c728994f7a9c3"], "node": "6fc2a55b2ed0a00fc91ce977c6371163f5da8891", "parents": ["dba850b46a9230d5929d0dd00e74b2a51f702b61"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Omar Gonzalez \u003cs9tpepper@apache.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058221 - Add Smart Form Fill autocomplete row item to trigger SFF r=desktop-theme-reviewers,credential-management-reviewers,mlucks,fluent-reviewers,flod,kcochrane,dimi,Mardak,mshillabeer\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316453\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/models/SmartFormFillModel.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/actors/SmartFormFillChild.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/actors/SmartFormFillParent.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/assets/sff-autofill-icon.svg", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/jar.mn", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/SmartFormFillAutocomplete.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/SmartFormFillController.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/SmartFormFillDocument.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/SmartFormFillUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/moz.build", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_smartwindow_smartformfill_autocomplete.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_smartwindow_smartformfill_metadata_lifecycle.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/head_smartformfill_autocomplete.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/test_smartformfill_autocomplete.html", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/browser_autocomplete_footer.js", "browser/locales-preview/aiWindow.ftl", "toolkit/actors/AutoCompleteParent.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/FormAutofillChild.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/FormAutofillParent.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/passwordmgr/LoginAutoComplete.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/passwordmgr/LoginManagerChild.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/passwordmgr/LoginManagerParent.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/passwordmgr/test/unit/test_login_autocomplete_result.js", "toolkit/components/satchel/FillHelpers.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/satchel/FormHistoryChild.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/satchel/FormHistoryParent.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/satchel/autocomplete-row-item/autocomplete-row-item.css", "toolkit/components/satchel/autocomplete-row-item/autocomplete-row-item.mjs", "toolkit/components/satchel/test/browser/browser_autocomplete.js", "toolkit/content/widgets/autocomplete-popup.js"], "git_node": "f62170256e3495b81d41d70fbf4b963dddd0c06c", "git_parents": ["04d7c4e93d0b4543c3f8cf285a4ea3baf20d885b"], "node": "fe2c7f8d562a8f3189fd543a2c5d8b98edc6e5f9", "parents": ["6fc2a55b2ed0a00fc91ce977c6371163f5da8891"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064891 - Stop the Gradle dependency proxies caching what they failed to fetch. r=ahochheiden\n\nEach proxy remembers a not-found response for a day, which outlives the proxy itself. They exist for\nthe length of one task, so that cache is only ever read by the run that wrote it, and there a single\ntransient miss becomes an absence every later enumeration pass sees too. Shortening how long it is\nremembered rather than not remembering it turns out to buy little: the passes run back to back, a\nsecond apart, and three of the four take under a minute, so a window worth having can still span a\nwhole pass.\n\nThat is the most likely reading of the incident this comes from rather than a proven one: four\nappservices AARs never arrived, every pass agreed they were not there, and a rerun on a fresh proxy\nfetched them without trouble.\n\nLeft alone on apache-snapshots, which nothing resolves through and this task does not package.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319977\n", "files": ["taskcluster/scripts/misc/android-gradle-dependencies/nexus.xml"], "git_node": "eca39e0abf6a4a40d66bd0dbdc5a2ec188de1eb0", "git_parents": ["f62170256e3495b81d41d70fbf4b963dddd0c06c"], "node": "c90979bbff0b6b0d58f09ab1e56d7dfe73509951", "parents": ["fe2c7f8d562a8f3189fd543a2c5d8b98edc6e5f9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064891 - Upload the dependency inventories and Nexus logs from the toolchain task. r=ahochheiden\n\nAn archive can come out incomplete without anything saying so, because the inventories the\ncompleteness check compares it against are written by the same resolution that fills it, and Gradle\nkeeps quiet about a resolution it gave up on. What is left to establish afterwards is whether an\nartifact was ever asked for and what came back, which Nexus records with status codes in\nlogs/request.log. Those logs and the inventories were both being discarded with the task.\n\nCopied before the check rather than after it, so that a run which fails ships the evidence for its\nown failure.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319978\n", "files": ["taskcluster/scripts/misc/android-gradle-dependencies/after.sh"], "git_node": "e95565ec70c4c52c5f4ca17f48d0c05b2825679e", "git_parents": ["eca39e0abf6a4a40d66bd0dbdc5a2ec188de1eb0"], "node": "850cc2ab1c70d8f908b004c7455245f6b7e56469", "parents": ["c90979bbff0b6b0d58f09ab1e56d7dfe73509951"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Eitan Isaacson \u003ceitan@monotonous.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 757384 - Introduce containerTitle for named groupings. r=Jamie,geckoview-reviewers,m_kato\n\nFall back to contentDescription for APIs lesser that 34.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318831\n", "files": ["accessible/android/SessionAccessibility.cpp", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/assets/www/forms2.html", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/test/AccessibilityTest.kt", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/SessionAccessibility.java"], "git_node": "93828bb34e60e4833ed99f51b7d38b2dd3440cf8", "git_parents": ["e95565ec70c4c52c5f4ca17f48d0c05b2825679e"], "node": "ba3ae676a667181ffb14744165b60bac5dfd6397", "parents": ["850cc2ab1c70d8f908b004c7455245f6b7e56469"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Eitan Isaacson \u003ceitan@monotonous.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1742619 - Expose \"mixed\" state checkables in Android. r=Jamie,geckoview-reviewers,m_kato\n\nIn API 36 or later use the new tristate `getChecked()`, otherwise use a\nlocalized string state like we do for `required`.\n\nThis also introduces use of the `isRequiredField` property added in API 36.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319241\n", "files": ["accessible/android/AccessibleWrap.cpp", "accessible/android/Platform.cpp", "accessible/android/SessionAccessibility.cpp", "dom/locales/en-US/chrome/accessibility/AccessFu.properties", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/test/AccessibilityTest.kt", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/SessionAccessibility.java"], "git_node": "7706ec1d92bd03219fb6d410305229a53a25e6d0", "git_parents": ["93828bb34e60e4833ed99f51b7d38b2dd3440cf8"], "node": "d5e37242e0ba2e66af3bab4ade5ce167e5e689dd", "parents": ["ba3ae676a667181ffb14744165b60bac5dfd6397"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dre Grant \u003cdgrant@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064564 - Remove orphaned custom wallpaper files. r=mconley\n\nUploading a custom wallpaper leaves the previous file in \u003cprofile\u003e/wallpaper/ unreferenced and unreachable and nothing in Firefox ever removes it. This deletes the replaced file after a successful upload and clears existing leftovers before each future upload. It writes the identifier pref only after the file lands, and takes a web lock so an upload and a reset can't overlap.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319655\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/lib/Wallpapers/WallpaperFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/xpcshell/test_WallpaperFeed.js"], "git_node": "1009fe49afe4e6a86d97878fa66b351dfbeb6b43", "git_parents": ["7706ec1d92bd03219fb6d410305229a53a25e6d0"], "node": "a25bb0567c76d37d309485dbb301782fb5754616", "parents": ["d5e37242e0ba2e66af3bab4ade5ce167e5e689dd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Moss \u003cjmoss@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1811277 - Clean up settings action telemetry test r=urlbar-reviewers,adw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320163\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-engagementTelemetry/browser_glean_telemetry_engagement_selected_result.js"], "git_node": "499f6d9b0d021c76fb2824e24a8d3e5ba535a239", "git_parents": ["1009fe49afe4e6a86d97878fa66b351dfbeb6b43"], "node": "b724c103c3ee2e41886d93ea208c0c3d8c2ebb04", "parents": ["a25bb0567c76d37d309485dbb301782fb5754616"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lando \u003clando@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Merge Mozilla-central to autoland\n", "files": [], "git_node": "6e5a2154036a0b485f531ac49d7b3a9a4b2ae64f", "git_parents": ["499f6d9b0d021c76fb2824e24a8d3e5ba535a239", "04b29f9c2d2dbf5639c3f45ea812bb4c21dc81c6"], "node": "2a633584d70fba2be119ec37bae188c172c84ba6", "parents": ["b724c103c3ee2e41886d93ea208c0c3d8c2ebb04", "dbb1fe4e9cc4ae0f4779ce8073d7bf4b40a0e22c"], "tags": []}, {"au