"desc": "Revert \"Bug 2060524 - [experiment] Part 4: Added a secret setting to force the number of trackers to meet the threshold for showing the privacy report notification. r=android-reviewers,sfamisa\" for causing fenix-debug failures HomeDeepLinkIntentProcessorTest.kt.\n\nThis reverts commit 23dcd6082f85e1e2885962e40b87a335045b6005.\n\nThis reverts commit 21561cf875fddc891aacf776f052590cd65b27b1.\n\nThis reverts commit 87edd1493edac48c61367f5d2d03752480753883.\n\nThis reverts commit 46cb70efb3681aea0ac28220e6e49939cc312a0b.\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/nimbus.fml.yaml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/FenixApplication.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/HomeActivity.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/intent/HomeDeepLinkIntentProcessor.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/privacyreport/PrivacyReportNotificationHelper.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/privacyreport/PrivacyReportNotificationReceiver.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/privacyreport/PrivacyReportNotificationWorker.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/privacyreport/PrivacyReportWorkerFactory.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/SecretSettingsFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/utils/Settings.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values/preference_keys.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values/static_strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/xml/secret_settings_preferences.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/HomeActivityTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/intent/HomeDeepLinkIntentProcessorTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/privacyreport/PrivacyReportNotificationHelperTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/privacyreport/PrivacyReportNotificationReceiverTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/privacyreport/PrivacyReportNotificationWorkerTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/privacyreport/PrivacyReportWorkerFactoryTest.kt"], "git_node": "a0d5cc32241495286691f9ea753362406be086ea", "git_parents": ["f2252c1b95672c90c447470c25d9257f98c1c308"], "node": "df7f5a14c32e68ee6b1ace0dc99a79f11f930eec", "parents": ["c04278911fcf2f8a1d85793b70a373284667200c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Shin \u003cdshin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065166: Disallow parsing of `anchor-center` in `(align|justify)-items`. r=emilio\n\nPull request: https://github.com/mozilla-firefox/firefox/pull/340\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/values/specified/align.rs", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-align/parsing/align-items-invalid.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-align/parsing/justify-items-invalid.html.ini"], "git_node": "23144cdbc93adbd34cee6d1b8edb6a42a7c28c7b", "git_parents": ["a0d5cc32241495286691f9ea753362406be086ea"], "node": "bd8d11420f5bd3e8e8c0ccbad0f4c4a17a8442f2", "parents": ["df7f5a14c32e68ee6b1ace0dc99a79f11f930eec"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew McCreight \u003ccontinuation@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065279 - Remove some unnecessary uses of GetClassObject from gtests. r=xpcom-reviewers,necko-reviewers,valentin,nika\n\nIn TestPACMan, currently at the start of the test it checks if there's a\nnon-static factory registered and then unregisters it if there is.\nHowever, we know there's never going to be anything registered to the\ntest CID before we start the test. This patch changes the test so instead\nof conditionally unregistering at the start of the test, we always unregister\nat the end of the test. We can keep a pointer to the factory to do so.\nThis is cleaner and avoids the GetClassObject method which I am trying to eliminate.\n\nWhen we start ProcessIsolationTest, there is never going to be anything registered\nto MOCK_ENTERPRISE_POLICIES_CID, and we unregister when we're done in\nUnregisterMockPolicyService(), so the UnregisterFactory RegisterMockPolicyService()\nwon't do anything, so let's remove it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320271\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/gtest/ProcessIsolationTest.cpp", "netwerk/test/gtest/TestPACMan.cpp"], "git_node": "2fbd87f990a40dd35e57a399d88c4522e866ff17", "git_parents": ["23144cdbc93adbd34cee6d1b8edb6a42a7c28c7b"], "node": "b01723b1ddf6a98969814cdaeaa8fd30998953a7", "parents": ["bd8d11420f5bd3e8e8c0ccbad0f4c4a17a8442f2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Caleb Chan \u003ccachan@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2044707 - Fix bookmarks moving out of their folder when the folder and a bookmark inside it are selected together r=places-reviewers,daisuke\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317078\n", "files": ["browser/components/places/content/places-tree.js", "browser/components/places/tests/browser/browser_controller_onDrop_sidebar.js"], "git_node": "eb35c6d4e232efae1a11549e9025b1d509e22bb0", "git_parents": ["2fbd87f990a40dd35e57a399d88c4522e866ff17"], "node": "a3a41abc42ab01bc8b9af9541829e4d0b30828eb", "parents": ["b01723b1ddf6a98969814cdaeaa8fd30998953a7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nora Liu \u003cnliu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2044163 - Remove Debugger.onNewPromise r=mgaudet,devtools-reviewers,jdescottes\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318786\n", "files": ["devtools/docs/user/debugger-api/debugger/index.md", "dom/promise/tests/chrome.toml", "dom/promise/tests/test_on_new_promise.html", "js/src/builtin/Promise.cpp", "js/src/debugger/DebugAPI-inl.h", "js/src/debugger/DebugAPI.h", "js/src/debugger/Debugger.cpp", "js/src/debugger/Debugger.h", "js/src/doc/Debugger/Debugger.md", "js/src/jit-test/lib/debuggerNXHelper.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/debug/DebuggeeWouldRun-01.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/debug/Debugger-onNewPromise-01.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/debug/Debugger-onNewPromise-02.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/debug/Debugger-onNewPromise-03.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/debug/Debugger-onNewPromise-04.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/debug/Debugger-onNewPromise-05.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/debug/Debugger-onNewPromise-06.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/debug/Debugger-onNewPromise-07.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/debug/Debugger-onNewPromise-08.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/debug/noExecute-06.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/js-promise-integration/promising-sync-reject-onnewpromise.js"], "git_node": "2333213cde582f4e2c84da8a0a56c29d30197e45", "git_parents": ["eb35c6d4e232efae1a11549e9025b1d509e22bb0"], "node": "261f7d57e70807c2b0b99a6270538787f4c7c514", "parents": ["a3a41abc42ab01bc8b9af9541829e4d0b30828eb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julian Descottes \u003cjdescottes@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062429 - [remote] Write marionette port under firefox-devtools-mcp home r=Sasha\n\nMeant to be used with https://github.com/mozilla/firefox-devtools-mcp/pull/149\n\nAdds an option to Marionette.startAtRuntime to also write the port to a specified file.\nThe caller is responsible for ensuring the parent folder exists.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316534\n", "files": ["remote/components/Marionette.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "9614b0315d41626370cbad57bffaab86e7d2144b", "git_parents": ["2333213cde582f4e2c84da8a0a56c29d30197e45"], "node": "536799973cb427438743e988ad44d43a634ce265", "parents": ["261f7d57e70807c2b0b99a6270538787f4c7c514"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julian Descottes \u003cjdescottes@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054128 - Display a banner when a RemoteAgent/Marionette server starts dynamically r=fluent-reviewers,Sasha,firefox-desktop-core-reviewers ,bolsson,mossop\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312606\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser.xhtml", "browser/components/BrowserGlue.sys.mjs", "browser/components/moz.build", "browser/components/remotecontrol/RemoteControlBanner.sys.mjs", "browser/components/remotecontrol/moz.build", "browser/locales-preview/remoteControl.ftl", "browser/locales/jar.mn", "modules/libpref/init/all.js", "remote/shared/webdriver/Session.sys.mjs", "remote/shared/webdriver/test/xpcshell/test_Session.js"], "git_node": "c558a2aefd00a5a3d781fc1b5fe343b72f9cc471", "git_parents": ["9614b0315d41626370cbad57bffaab86e7d2144b"], "node": "0309eadf0abf0f5c9ec886abcccd0c81c2545478", "parents": ["536799973cb427438743e988ad44d43a634ce265"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julian Descottes \u003cjdescottes@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2032343 - [remote] Prompt user explicitly when an application attempts to connect r=Sasha,fluent-reviewers,bolsson,mossop\n\nThe connection prompt will allow users to accept or refuse the incoming connection.\nWith a checkbox they can decide to remember this choice until the browser is closed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314052\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/all.js", "remote/jar.mn", "remote/locales-preview/remote-agent.ftl", "remote/locales/jar.mn", "remote/locales/moz.build", "remote/marionette/driver.sys.mjs", "remote/moz.build", "remote/shared/webdriver/ConnectionPrompt.sys.mjs", "remote/webdriver-bidi/WebDriverBiDi.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "b85545994bc7b5cba59bfdfc0f657a01863feef3", "git_parents": ["c558a2aefd00a5a3d781fc1b5fe343b72f9cc471"], "node": "50b846c831742c9d1eb9f6fc9446bd75fe1076a7", "parents": ["0309eadf0abf0f5c9ec886abcccd0c81c2545478"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julian Descottes \u003cjdescottes@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059367 - Add Nightly-only AI assistant popup to start/stop remote agent servers r=fluent-reviewers,Sasha,desktop-theme-reviewers,sfoster,bolsson,mossop\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316046\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/appmenu-viewcache.inc.xhtml", "browser/components/BrowserComponents.manifest", "browser/components/remotecontrol/RemoteControlBanner.sys.mjs", "browser/components/remotecontrol/RemoteControlPanel.sys.mjs", "browser/components/remotecontrol/RemoteControlServers.sys.mjs", "browser/components/remotecontrol/content/remoteControlPanel.inc.xhtml", "browser/components/remotecontrol/moz.build", "browser/locales-preview/remoteControl.ftl", "browser/themes/shared/customizableui/panelUI-shared.css", "browser/themes/shared/icons/remote-control.svg", "browser/themes/shared/jar.inc.mn", "browser/themes/shared/toolbarbutton-icons.css", "modules/libpref/init/all.js", "remote/components/Marionette.sys.mjs", "remote/components/RemoteAgent.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "2c77b6b8fc7c9dd88a3b094f176f9ee5a4201d05", "git_parents": ["b85545994bc7b5cba59bfdfc0f657a01863feef3"], "node": "c282fb8b6ef34c99de00972ccfe6ae17f4246bdd", "parents": ["50b846c831742c9d1eb9f6fc9446bd75fe1076a7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julian Descottes \u003cjdescottes@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059367 - [remote] Only remove before-cancel-download-prompt observer if necessary r=Sasha\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318495\n", "files": ["remote/components/Marionette.sys.mjs", "remote/components/RemoteAgent.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "2a4302caaa1e7e56e4aba3deddfc577dc103e51c", "git_parents": ["2c77b6b8fc7c9dd88a3b094f176f9ee5a4201d05"], "node": "f2c2f2eca66d7efdbafcb8693a6b7ba1d5eaf7ae", "parents": ["c282fb8b6ef34c99de00972ccfe6ae17f4246bdd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan Hunt \u003crhunt@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056796 - Root ImportValues at wasm ComponentInstance instantiate call sites r=bvisness\n\nComponentInstance::init and the export-object helper passed a stack-local,\nunrooted ImportValues to Module::instantiate. Module::instantiate stores\nnewly allocated GC objects (e.g. WasmGlobalObject) into that structure, so a\nGC during instantiation could sweep them, leaving CreateExportObject to read\nand write through a stale pointer. ImportValues must live in a Rooted, as its\nown comment notes; use Rooted\u003cImportValues\u003e at both call sites.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320485\n", "files": ["js/src/wasm/WasmComponent.cpp"], "git_node": "7ad6d22212b1ad94eba031c93c604f91ab6d0573", "git_parents": ["2a4302caaa1e7e56e4aba3deddfc577dc103e51c"], "node": "91b741f9c312f27271703956efa2a35d927ac744", "parents": ["f2c2f2eca66d7efdbafcb8693a6b7ba1d5eaf7ae"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062210 - Resolve the newtab searchbar's sap without a browser window. r=Standard8\n\nThe fallthrough reads a window the newtab bar does not have, so the recorder threw and dropped all four engagement-family events.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319886\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarParentController.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/metrics.yaml"], "git_node": "b81219c57bfa475d1e2bcff5aba20aa49c8c6873", "git_parents": ["7ad6d22212b1ad94eba031c93c604f91ab6d0573"], "node": "2a5d036af7efbaab31e2199430cb5ea5d3d4a994", "parents": ["91b741f9c312f27271703956efa2a35d927ac744"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kelly Cochrane \u003ckcochrane@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065276 - Ensure sidebar width is sized as expected when switching between compact and standard UI densities r=jsudiaman\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320270\n", "files": ["browser/components/sidebar/browser-sidebar.js", "browser/components/sidebar/tests/browser/browser_sidebar_expand_on_hover.js"], "git_node": "2eefd44e53262edcb9eacb85f2f19f4d471e8f48", "git_parents": ["b81219c57bfa475d1e2bcff5aba20aa49c8c6873"], "node": "d4d6d3e94128801f854533a5a3a1e4420cfbd660", "parents": ["2a5d036af7efbaab31e2199430cb5ea5d3d4a994"], "tags": []}, {"author": "sarah541 \u003csarahkhan1107@hotmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065188 - Remove the Top Sites pager layout and its secret setting r=android-reviewers,gl\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320179\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/topsites/TopSites.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/topsites/TopSitesTestTag.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/ui/Homepage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/SecretSettingsFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/utils/Settings.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values/preference_keys.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values/static_strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/xml/secret_settings_preferences.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/topsites/TopSitesPagerComposableTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/topsites/TopSitesPagerTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/config/detekt-baseline.xml"], "git_node": "cfa562ccc770c268c4b51dd4c255396a29cd1b4e", "git_parents": ["2eefd44e53262edcb9eacb85f2f19f4d471e8f48"], "node": "eb2e9419539d33643ee71db396b534d21643811d", "parents": ["d4d6d3e94128801f854533a5a3a1e4420cfbd660"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Almeida \u003cjonalmeida942@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065582 - Update default list of allowed regions for IPProtection r=Roger,android-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320516\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/nimbus.fml.yaml"], "git_node": "177e81809ffea8d2c42adb860db7a28e725d234c", "git_parents": ["cfa562ccc770c268c4b51dd4c255396a29cd1b4e"], "node": "ee6baf18066bf6bb6fb906836457f59b3db871e3", "parents": ["eb2e9419539d33643ee71db396b534d21643811d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mark Kennedy \u003cmkennedy@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057851 - Re-enable search scroll test on Linux 22.04 opt nova r=intermittent-reviewers,ahal\n\nThe reported failure appears to be a Wayland issue specific to Linux 22.04, which doesn't run in production by default. So skip is no longer needed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319832\n", "files": ["browser/components/preferences/tests/search/browser.toml"], "git_node": "5295cf607aba4c501e238840d8d2cd273ae04015", "git_parents": ["177e81809ffea8d2c42adb860db7a28e725d234c"], "node": "879a1e59d1e3322fdd87dc517867a61cf6672db6", "parents": ["ee6baf18066bf6bb6fb906836457f59b3db871e3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065332 - Explicitly disable user-selection for moz-urlbar, moz-button, and panel-list. r=desktop-theme-reviewers,tgiles\n\nxul.css has :root { user-select: none; }, but in about:newtab xul.css is not loaded, so things like the search mode switcher button, panel-list contents, and other urlbar elements like the go button become use-selectable, which is odd for a widgets that are basically native to Firefox.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320296\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/urlbar.css", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-button/moz-button.css", "toolkit/content/widgets/panel-list/panel-list.css"], "git_node": "20822127b179016969a05813936173eeec4e8b83", "git_parents": ["5295cf607aba4c501e238840d8d2cd273ae04015"], "node": "4efb3baababb86723c81f391fb57fb3094b76d0f", "parents": ["879a1e59d1e3322fdd87dc517867a61cf6672db6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sam Foster \u003csfoster@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063204 - Hide the menu when clicking on the 'turn on sync' button. r=skhamis,nsharpley\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319309\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser-sync.js"], "git_node": "20dbec4024aff6a7e2dcac0a6a4b4cefec0b00e2", "git_parents": ["20822127b179016969a05813936173eeec4e8b83"], "node": "2a6deebd3e2517d0be236b013b8f0d7104f84371", "parents": ["4efb3baababb86723c81f391fb57fb3094b76d0f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jack Brown \u003cjbrown@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056278 - Resize the sidebar launcher division lines - r=desktop-theme-reviewers,tabbrowser-reviewers,sclements,dao\n\nThis fixes the two short divider lines in Firefox's collapsed vertical-tabs sidebar (one below the pinned tabs, one above the tools) which were being drawn 1px tall and roughly twice as wide as the design spec.\n\nExpand on hover is getting its own design pass after the Nova release, so when the launcher is expanded in that mode the divider keeps the full width line it has today, with the existing hover state drawn on top of it. Only the pinned tabs divider is involved there, as the tools and extensions divider is not rendered in that mode.\n\nCollapsing the launcher holds it at its expanded width so that clip-path has content to clip, which left the divider drawn around the width it was animating away from until the animation finished. Both dividers now wait for the real width to be restored.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316938\n", "files": ["browser/components/sidebar/sidebar-main.css", "browser/themes/shared/sidebar.css", "browser/themes/shared/tabbrowser/tabs.css"], "git_node": "b564e020632847c8edb7bdd19cfc7e57c2831321", "git_parents": ["20dbec4024aff6a7e2dcac0a6a4b4cefec0b00e2"], "node": "2614fc62fbd04dc36b2f197f5055af0364d9d97d", "parents": ["2a6deebd3e2517d0be236b013b8f0d7104f84371"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anna Kulyk \u003cakulyk@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062663 - close icon isn't centered on Nova r=desktop-theme-reviewers,jules\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320133\n", "files": ["toolkit/themes/shared/icons/close.svg"], "git_node": "16ccbf4657a00bd5a06cb2f7afe25de458afc672", "git_parents": ["b564e020632847c8edb7bdd19cfc7e57c2831321"], "node": "f6284e2103bff1ddff5fd5074f4e7c5bcae08eeb", "parents": ["2614fc62fbd04dc36b2f197f5055af0364d9d97d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jens Stutte \u003cjstutte@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065561 - Fix a typo in the nsIAppStartup AppShutdownTelemetry phase constant. r=beth\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320493\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/startup/nsAppStartup.cpp", "toolkit/components/startup/public/nsIAppStartup.idl"], "git_node": "a59e0ee7a2adac4b4ff3ca0f771f5640a1b81659", "git_parents": ["16ccbf4657a00bd5a06cb2f7afe25de458afc672"], "node": "943f43e94492029b04c74304ac543ba14254d1e8", "parents": ["f6284e2103bff1ddff5fd5074f4e7c5bcae08eeb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jens Stutte \u003cjstutte@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065575 - Update the generated ts typelibs (Linux). r=Standard8\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320503\n", "files": ["tools/@types/generated/lib.gecko.dom.d.ts", "tools/@types/generated/lib.gecko.glean.d.ts", "tools/@types/generated/lib.gecko.services.d.ts", "tools/@types/generated/lib.gecko.xpcom.d.ts", "tools/ts/config/error_list.json"], "git_node": "351c08aca484b8b44095974412399b82a194e12a", "git_parents": ["a59e0ee7a2adac4b4ff3ca0f771f5640a1b81659"], "node": "3364eb8c968596abc9f338ab88bddf7691e4845f", "parents": ["943f43e94492029b04c74304ac543ba14254d1e8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nika Layzell \u003cnika@thelayzells.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065236 - Remove EmbedderInnerWindowId field from BrowsingContext, r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug\n\nThis field has been redundant since WindowContext was introduced, and\ncan be removed.\n\nThis also improves the behaviour of GetEmbedderWindowGlobal to not\nreturn null when GetParentWindowContext wouldn't if the parent\nWindowContext is discarded due to navigation.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320240\n", "files": ["docshell/base/BrowsingContext.cpp", "docshell/base/BrowsingContext.h", "docshell/base/CanonicalBrowsingContext.cpp", "docshell/base/CanonicalBrowsingContext.h", "docshell/base/WindowContext.cpp", "dom/ipc/WindowGlobalChild.cpp", "dom/ipc/WindowGlobalParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/WindowGlobalParent.h"], "git_node": "b1c11649010b66c9157551332c5dd3c182a3c404", "git_parents": ["351c08aca484b8b44095974412399b82a194e12a"], "node": "8e181671cbade646aaff93f16a5f2fea90f70957", "parents": ["3364eb8c968596abc9f338ab88bddf7691e4845f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "kpatenio \u003ckpatenio@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2048382 \u2014 update tab mute and close buttons for Nova r=desktop-theme-reviewers,tabbrowser-reviewers,niklas,dao\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314533\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/tabbrowser/tabs.css"], "git_node": "75f04a72c569348fad273f816ce016c2d12f9729", "git_parents": ["b1c11649010b66c9157551332c5dd3c182a3c404"], "node": "92313f0da4ac2be64931f19407ea87705dfb5e7b", "parents": ["8e181671cbade646aaff93f16a5f2fea90f70957"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Steve Fink \u003csfink@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2042790 followup - correct the string sizes, and be more explicit about \"why 30 bits?\" r=jandem\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320298\n", "files": ["js/src/doc/constraints.md"], "git_node": "c77bbd18adb76dc1dd16561762f53c527c223f2f", "git_parents": ["75f04a72c569348fad273f816ce016c2d12f9729"], "node": "ae42876220cdf03bb88d774cec0e4d50f63443af", "parents": ["92313f0da4ac2be64931f19407ea87705dfb5e7b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Sutherland \u003casutherland@asutherland.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064648 - Don't apply the file:// URI allowlist to worker process selection. r=nika,ipc-reviewers\n\nIsolationBehaviorForURI() maps any origin in the file:// URI allowlist to\nIsolationBehavior::File so that a document which is permitted to link to local\nfiles renders in the file content process, in case it uses file:// sub-resources.\nThat allowlist is built from the capability.policy.* prefs which the\nLocalFileLinks enterprise policy writes, which intranet deployments use so that\nan internal portal (typically SharePoint) may link to files on a network share.\n\nThe rule was never meant to apply to workers. Before worker process selection\nmoved to ProcessIsolation in bug 1850589, E10SUtils.validatedWebRemoteType()\nguarded the equivalent check with !aIsWorker. Losing that guard was silent until\nbug 2050536 added ValidateBehaviorForWorker(), whose File case requires the\ncurrent remote type to be the file remote type. ServiceWorkerPrivate::Initialize()\nruns in the parent but passes the shared \"web\" remote type, so it now fails, and\nin release builds MOZ_ALWAYS_SUCCEEDS() lets construction continue with a\ndefault-constructed mRemoteWorkerData that crashes on the first intercepted fetch.\n\nThread an aIsWorker argument through IsolationBehaviorForURI() and skip the\nallowlist lookup for workers, restoring the pre-bug-1850589 behavior of selecting\nan ordinary web remote type. Genuine file: principals are unaffected; they are\nmatched earlier by scheme, which the new test also covers. Documents are\nunaffected as well, as browser_new_file_whitelisted_http_tab.js continues to\nverify.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320314\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/ProcessIsolation.cpp", "dom/ipc/gtest/ProcessIsolationTest.cpp"], "git_node": "82be20cb059e7c77b4a455952f4c266475e1f645", "git_parents": ["c77bbd18adb76dc1dd16561762f53c527c223f2f"], "node": "e49e349979ddabe98218f133d79b2467b81916c1", "parents": ["ae42876220cdf03bb88d774cec0e4d50f63443af"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Sutherland \u003casutherland@asutherland.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064648 - Neutralize a ServiceWorkerPrivate whose Initialize() failed. r=dom-worker-reviewers,edenchuang\n\nInitialize() is called only from the constructor and has no retry, but in\nrelease builds MOZ_ALWAYS_SUCCEEDS() does not stop construction. A\nServiceWorkerPrivate therefore survives a failed Initialize() with a\ndefault-constructed mRemoteWorkerData whose OptionalServiceWorkerData union is\nstill T__None, and RefreshRemoteWorkerData() then fatally asserts in\nget_ServiceWorkerData() the first time the worker is asked to spawn.\n\nClear mInfo on any early return from Initialize(). That is the same state\nNoteDeadServiceWorkerInfo() already establishes, so the existing guards do the\nwork: SpawnWorkerIfNeeded() bails before touching mRemoteWorkerData, and since\nExecServiceWorkerOp() and SendFetchEventInternal() both go through it, every\noperation now fails cleanly. A failed fetch interception resets the interception\nand the request goes to the network, so the site loads without its service\nworker rather than taking down the parent process.\n\nSendPushEvent() and SendCookieChangeEvent() are the only entry points which\ndereference mInfo before delegating to SpawnWorkerIfNeeded(), so give them the\nsame null check SendFetchEvent() already has. Everything else which asserts\nmInfo requires a spawned worker or mControllerChild and so is unreachable.\n\nThe MOZ_DIAGNOSTIC_ASSERT in the constructor is deliberately kept, so an\nunexpected Initialize() failure remains loud on Nightly and Dev Edition.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320315\n", "files": ["dom/serviceworkers/ServiceWorkerPrivate.cpp"], "git_node": "64c500f9b5c1282fc136ff3591539540b9ba3e5c", "git_parents": ["82be20cb059e7c77b4a455952f4c266475e1f645"], "node": "c4f04269ecdf85f0971d25a6f5225cc22f67b2bc", "parents": ["e49e349979ddabe98218f133d79b2467b81916c1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Greg Stoll \u003cgreg@gregstoll.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2036153 part 1 - add bluetooth service class ID information to WebSerial interfaces r=cmartin,webidl,smaug\n\nThis is the non-platform-specific parts of this change to allow filtering\nbased on bluetooth service class ID.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D303425\n", "files": ["dom/webidl/Serial.webidl", "dom/webserial/PSerialManager.ipdl", "dom/webserial/Serial.cpp", "dom/webserial/Serial.h", "dom/webserial/SerialManagerParent.cpp", "dom/webserial/SerialManagerParent.h", "dom/webserial/TestSerialPlatformService.cpp", "dom/webserial/TestSerialPlatformService.h"], "git_node": "d6c462e584c335332c8727adaaf7c826aaf0aa57", "git_parents": ["64c500f9b5c1282fc136ff3591539540b9ba3e5c"], "node": "46418477a12542deb1653433dfc0d28b04664014", "parents": ["c4f04269ecdf85f0971d25a6f5225cc22f67b2bc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Greg Stoll \u003cgreg@gregstoll.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2036153 part 2 - Windows bluetooth service class ID implementation for WebSerial r=win-reviewers,handyman\n\nVerified on my machine that ExtractBluetoothServiceClassId() works with\nreal hardware.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D303426\n", "files": ["dom/webserial/Win32SerialPlatformService.cpp"], "git_node": "0db5ae3bf9be9d406b25afa41712ead780fde117", "git_parents": ["d6c462e584c335332c8727adaaf7c826aaf0aa57"], "node": "630b9cc5c4da45850e1457984a18d8ea73435b2c", "parents": ["46418477a12542deb1653433dfc0d28b04664014"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Greg Stoll \u003cgreg@gregstoll.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2036153 part 3 - Mac/Linux bluetooth service class ID implementation for WebSerial r=mac-reviewers,spohl\n\nVerified on my Mac that LookupMacBluetoothServiceClassId() works with\nreal hardware. Supporting this on Linux would require (I think) adding\nthe bluez library, which I don't think is worth it right now.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D303427\n", "files": ["dom/webserial/MacBluetoothServiceClassId.h", "dom/webserial/MacBluetoothServiceClassId.mm", "dom/webserial/PosixSerialPlatformService.cpp", "dom/webserial/moz.build"], "git_node": "f6bb09e99a3c76d8640dc4a3ed8ce1651150eeb2", "git_parents": ["0db5ae3bf9be9d406b25afa41712ead780fde117"], "node": "7d2569d2077794883420abbbb7ed0bdc366aeaff", "parents": ["630b9cc5c4da45850e1457984a18d8ea73435b2c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Greg Stoll \u003cgreg@gregstoll.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2036153 part 4 - Bluetooth WebSerial tests r=cmartin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D303428\n", "files": ["dom/webserial/tests/mochitest/mochitest.toml", "dom/webserial/tests/mochitest/serial_test_utils.js", "dom/webserial/tests/mochitest/test_serial_bluetooth_allowlist.html", "dom/webserial/tests/mochitest/test_serial_port_info.html"], "git_node": "7ec54bd2dd1fe98c8d624c988c52783849a85817", "git_parents": ["f6bb09e99a3c76d8640dc4a3ed8ce1651150eeb2"], "node": "04f886ce6b1c0b34e3901ec2fedb4647f8f2b8c0", "parents": ["7d2569d2077794883420abbbb7ed0bdc366aeaff"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Matthew Tighe \u003cmatthewdtighe@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062980 - allow for extraction of simple, human-readable text from PageExtractor r=ai-platform-reviewers,thasan\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319269\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/pageextractor/DOMExtractor.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/pageextractor/PageExtractor.d.ts", "toolkit/components/pageextractor/tests/browser/browser_dom_extractor.js"], "git_node": "7a8016c94ae32fa1bcdf2c065f94aa9a639c6594", "git_parents": ["7ec54bd2dd1fe98c8d624c988c52783849a85817"], "node": "f1aed44af981bf88cf7e24b12713987866e7d4f8", "parents": ["04f886ce6b1c0b34e3901ec2fedb4647f8f2b8c0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Matthew Tighe \u003cmatthewdtighe@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062980 - wire simple text option through Android stack r=geckoview-reviewers,android-reviewers,fmasalha,kaya,bclark\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319270\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/engine-gecko/src/main/java/mozilla/components/browser/engine/gecko/GeckoEngineSession.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/engine-gecko/src/test/java/mozilla/components/browser/engine/gecko/GeckoEngineSessionPageExtractionTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/concept/engine/src/main/java/mozilla/components/concept/engine/pageextraction/ContentParams.kt", "mobile/android/geckoview/api.txt", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/test/PageExtractionTest.kt", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/PageExtractionController.java", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/doc-files/CHANGELOG.md"], "git_node": "a9f54ac9cb285f586d590dadab5b7657c0ba42f9", "git_parents": ["7a8016c94ae32fa1bcdf2c065f94aa9a639c6594"], "node": "a2ec6e0303f0030381d18dd7922b6d116257b11d", "parents": ["f1aed44af981bf88cf7e24b12713987866e7d4f8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Matthew Tighe \u003cmatthewdtighe@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2051605 - add metadata to page extractor to check for paywalled content r=ai-platform-reviewers,thasan\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319271\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/pageextractor/PageExtractor.d.ts", "toolkit/components/pageextractor/PageExtractorChild.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/pageextractor/tests/browser/browser_page_metadata.js"], "git_node": "a7fd05236f354954cf7a84c2c724ffff2a81b2b8", "git_parents": ["a9f54ac9cb285f586d590dadab5b7657c0ba42f9"], "node": "5c4ebeb1dff561c046f693b208234eddd2cf8d94", "parents": ["a2ec6e0303f0030381d18dd7922b6d116257b11d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Matthew Tighe \u003cmatthewdtighe@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2051605 - display error when summarizing paywalled content r=geckoview-reviewers,android-reviewers,android-l10n-reviewers,parker,fmasalha,kaya,bclark\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319272\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/engine-gecko/src/main/java/mozilla/components/browser/engine/gecko/GeckoEngineSession.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/engine-gecko/src/test/java/mozilla/components/browser/engine/gecko/GeckoEngineSessionPageExtractionTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/concept/engine/src/main/java/mozilla/components/concept/engine/pageextraction/PageMetadata.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/summarize/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/summarize/SummarizationScreen.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/summarize/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/summarize/content/ContentProvider.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/summarize/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/summarize/content/PageMetadata.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/summarize/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/summarize/ui/PaywalledContentError.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/summarize/src/main/res/values/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/summarize/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/summarize/SummarizationStoreTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/summarization/SummarizationStoreViewModel.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/summarization/SummarizationTelemetryMiddlewareTest.kt", "mobile/android/geckoview/api.txt", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/PageExtractionController.java", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/doc-files/CHANGELOG.md", "mobile/shared/modules/geckoview/GeckoViewPageExtractor.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "0d7ab3290dd34653d8dd39db147f4f0f2e8ddae0", "git_parents": ["a7fd05236f354954cf7a84c2c724ffff2a81b2b8"], "node": "f4aaa1a7af06880a50e6a2cbeab9b6371c8c4850", "parents": ["5c4ebeb1dff561c046f693b208234eddd2cf8d94"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Serban Stanca \u003csstanca@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2065236 - Remove EmbedderInnerWindowId field from BrowsingContext, r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug\" for causing mochitests failures in browser_multiselect_tabs_unload.js.\n\nThis reverts commit b1c11649010b66c9157551332c5dd3c182a3c404.\n", "files": ["docshell/base/BrowsingContext.cpp", "docshell/base/BrowsingContext.h", "docshell/base/CanonicalBrowsingContext.cpp", "docshell/base/CanonicalBrowsingContext.h", "docshell/base/WindowContext.cpp", "dom/ipc/WindowGlobalChild.cpp", "dom/ipc/WindowGlobalParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/WindowGlobalParent.h"], "git_node": "633327a1873bc0dbde089b28f9c17e9cb2fe803e", "git_parents": ["0d7ab3290dd34653d8dd39db147f4f0f2e8ddae0"], "node": "2a470f5a78bf0c0fae728627d636bb6a9c2abd3d", "parents": ["f4aaa1a7af06880a50e6a2cbeab9b6371c8c4850"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Serban Stanca \u003csstanca@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2048382 \u2014 update tab mute and close buttons for Nova r=desktop-theme-reviewers,tabbrowser-reviewers,niklas,dao\" for causing mochitests failures in browser_delay_autoplay_silentAudioTrack_media.js.\n\nThis reverts commit 75f04a72c569348fad273f816ce016c2d12f9729.\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/tabbrowser/tabs.css"], "git_node": "f8c395c128c2e15d0aa3b5dc8a24369f4cb18a23", "git_parents": ["633327a1873bc0dbde089b28f9c17e9cb2fe803e"], "node": "31ad1892c2cd472bb8d7adffdf6d5f32cb91b03e", "parents": ["2a470f5a78bf0c0fae728627d636bb6a9c2abd3d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Shin \u003cdshin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063854: Don't try to add anchor frame by the same name multiple times. r=emilio\n\nPull request: https://github.com/mozilla-firefox/firefox/pull/339\n", "files": ["layout/base/PresShell.cpp", "layout/base/PresShell.h", "layout/generic/nsIFrame.cpp", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-anchor-position/anchor-name-crash.html"], "git_node": "ebcc08224f296e224ee63074b92405ba45a09f7a", "git_parents": ["f8c395c128c2e15d0aa3b5dc8a24369f4cb18a23"], "node": "1e4fc8691a19c751d3dc5ce851ae6bb1114cf41f", "parents": ["31ad1892c2cd472bb8d7adffdf6d5f32cb91b03e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "yazan \u003cyalmacki@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064652 - Scope the Start Menu shortcut to custom icons, and disable them when the taskbar icon can't be overridden. r=mconley,hsohaney,mossop\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320408\n", "files": ["browser/components/profiles/SelectableProfileService.sys.mjs", "browser/components/shell/CustomIconManager.sys.mjs", "browser/components/shell/StartupOSIntegration.sys.mjs", "browser/components/shell/test/unit/test_customIconManager.js"], "git_node": "a6c98d48309072962bc3db5ed96359c1173cb4bd", "git_parents": ["ebcc08224f296e224ee63074b92405ba45a09f7a"], "node": "73b4392df7e3a085646eaf086f6d4be7335db325", "parents": ["1e4fc8691a19c751d3dc5ce851ae6bb1114cf41f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kalen Lu \u003ckalenblu@icloud.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063246 - Restore autocomplete default scrollbar width and trim inline padding. r=desktop-theme-reviewers,jules\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318520\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/autocomplete.css"], "git_node": "22631af3000c6bd25351c92ae8a8c6c9b80cf7e8", "git_parents": ["a6c98d48309072962bc3db5ed96359c1173cb4bd"], "node": "a8004239ebcc544b046c9932261be024175d730f", "parents": ["73b4392df7e3a085646eaf086f6d4be7335db325"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gela \u003cgmalekpour@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053320 - Part 1: Don't tie Nimbus tooling to `HomeActivity` UI r=android-reviewers,nalexander,Roger\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319628\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/HomeActivity.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/experiments/QANimbusToolingReceiver.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/experiments/QANimbusToolingReceiverTest.kt"], "git_node": "b216958be2dc9076b38001223a24efd6ad0544c4", "git_parents": ["22631af3000c6bd25351c92ae8a8c6c9b80cf7e8"], "node": "244425ac5d6ac7c461e7248fb7632be666c169de", "parents": ["a8004239ebcc544b046c9932261be024175d730f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gela \u003cgmalekpour@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053320 - Part 2: Remove nimbus tooling initialization from Focus r=android-reviewers,Roger\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319634\n", "files": ["mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/focus/activity/MainActivity.kt"], "git_node": "b32d33cd05db02f2add42a560109adc0c0a33467", "git_parents": ["b216958be2dc9076b38001223a24efd6ad0544c4"], "node": "b0e45ebc284c3cccc7deff57efd57e15ba85bdc4", "parents": ["244425ac5d6ac7c461e7248fb7632be666c169de"], "tags": []}, {"author": "nickgrato \u003cngrato@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064522 - [Monitor Agent][FE] Make read url pills clickable ond page title instead of url in monitor cards r=echa\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319924\n", "files": ["browser/components/DesktopActorRegistry.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/actors/SmartWindowTasksChild.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/actors/SmartWindowTasksParent.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/agent-monitor-item/agent-monitor-item.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/agent-monitor-item/agent-monitor-item.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-tasks/ai-tasks.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/monitors-display/monitors-display.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/AgentUI.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/MonitorUIUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_agent_monitor_chat.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_agent_monitor_item.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_smartwindow_tasks_actors.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/xpcshell/test_MonitorUIUtils.js"], "git_node": "20dfd8c624c63123d39b31e17efbe165559a5399", "git_parents": ["b32d33cd05db02f2add42a560109adc0c0a33467"], "node": "396fac2a4e883cc4cb5b0fd03721f78c87501040", "parents": ["b0e45ebc284c3cccc7deff57efd57e15ba85bdc4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tom Ritter \u003ctom@ritter.vg\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1737207: Add documentation describing concerns surrounding global callbacks r=shravanrn\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317627\n", "files": ["docs/config.yml", "extensions/spellcheck/hunspell/glue/mozHunspellRLBoxSandbox.cpp", "moz.build", "security/rlbox/docs/index.md"], "git_node": "f6ed93e5c457391c247801abc8acbafa31e5c780", "git_parents": ["20dfd8c624c63123d39b31e17efbe165559a5399"], "node": "c67f5a50adb0d78c3afa316aba3aab5959ace1d9", "parents": ["396fac2a4e883cc4cb5b0fd03721f78c87501040"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Vincent Tunru \u003cgit@vincenttunru.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062876, Bug 2060155 - Update tracker count on page load panel opens. r=desktop-theme-reviewers,dao,daleharvey\n\nApparently `onContentBlockingEvent` only gets called when a new category of trackers (e.g. fingerprinters) gets blocked, so if multiple trackers in the same category get blocked, the tracker count in the address bar doesn't get updated anymore.\n\nTo compensate, this patch also manually recomputes the number of blocked trackers on navigation complete, and when the trust panel gets opened, to ensure the two are always aligned.\n\nAlso update browser_trust_panel.js for the new count semantics: test_update now counts the tracker already blocked on page load (1/2/3 instead of 0/1/2), and test_blocker_count_no_stale_overwrite is removed since its single-blocker stubbing no longer matches the new compute (to be re-implemented in a follow-up).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319818\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser-trustPanel.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-trustPanel/browser_trust_panel.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-trustPanel/browser_trust_panel_icon.js", "browser/themes/shared/identity-block/identity-block.css"], "git_node": "63e0f328ae1ede50785e1e3bf9e5f7d7d2bf76cb", "git_parents": ["f6ed93e5c457391c247801abc8acbafa31e5c780"], "node": "8668979848b1059cbd58640f9066123d229ca911", "parents": ["c67f5a50adb0d78c3afa316aba3aab5959ace1d9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "ahanot \u003cahanot@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065281 - Use the ads-client's SQLite HTTP cache for New Tab ads r=mconley\n\nPass a MozAdsCacheConfig when building the MozAdsClient so the component's\nSQLite HTTP response cache is actually used on desktop. The database lives at\nads-client.sqlite in the profile directory; TTL and max size are left to the\ncomponent's own defaults, keeping freshness driven by Cache-Control on the\nMARS response.\n\nNew Tab already caches the same MARS payloads a layer up in PersistentCache,\nand that layer is the outer one that decides whether the ads-client is called\nat all. Stop writing those entries while the ads-client is active. Since a\nmissing entry is already treated as expired, that also stops them being read,\nleaving the ads-client cache as the only cache on this path.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320272\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/lib/AdsClient.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/AdsFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/DiscoveryStreamFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/xpcshell/test_AdsClient.js"], "git_node": "2cce7bd157bf2927c0df2c712ec70f0e1c59aee0", "git_parents": ["63e0f328ae1ede50785e1e3bf9e5f7d7d2bf76cb"], "node": "36e5eb43ba5fe50d579fe6d22fda6d7a72214c69", "parents": ["8668979848b1059cbd58640f9066123d229ca911"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Keith Cirkel \u003ckeithamus@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065539 - Force scoped registries flag for sanitizer custom elements tests r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320537\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/sanitizer-api/sanitizer-custom-elements-constructor.html.ini"], "git_node": "948b661f33f39fbbceb8b4355ec3506d17ef9629", "git_parents": ["2cce7bd157bf2927c0df2c712ec70f0e1c59aee0"], "node": "3699dd3b8a2c025d3bb1a3d1a9623557d25988dc", "parents": ["36e5eb43ba5fe50d579fe6d22fda6d7a72214c69"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Exploding Joysticks \u003cExplodingJoysticks@proton.me\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061541 - Remove IO_SERVICE_CONTRACTID in layout/tools/reftest/reftest-content.js r=layout-reviewers,dholbert\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320533\n", "files": ["layout/tools/reftest/reftest-content.js"], "git_node": "c3f61e6ea05da96bb83cfdb38e521c523ce858a0", "git_parents": ["948b661f33f39fbbceb8b4355ec3506d17ef9629"], "node": "20a5be7739975d953f6f0a1306454ebcedc7a041", "parents": ["3699dd3b8a2c025d3bb1a3d1a9623557d25988dc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Rubino \u003cdrubino@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065360 - Record which infobar button was clicked in messaging-system telemetry. r=omc-reviewers,aminomancer\n\nInfobar button clicks report CLICK_PRIMARY_BUTTON or CLICK_SECONDARY_BUTTON,\nchosen by whether the clicked element carries the `primary` class, and the ping\nitself carries only message_id and event. When a message defines two buttons and\nneither sets `primary`, both clicks produce identical pings and the buttons\ncannot be distinguished in analysis.\n\nSpotlight already sends event_context.source, and\nAboutWelcomeTelemetry.submitGleanPingForPing echoes that key into the existing\nmessaging_system.event_source metric for every messaging-system ping regardless\nof surface, so no new Glean metric and no ping change are needed here.\n\nButton clicks now report event_context.source, using a new optional `id` on the\nbutton config and falling back to button_\u003cindex\u003e so existing messages gain the\ndistinction without recipe changes.\n\nThe DISMISSED event reports the originating event type, so the X button reports\ndismiss_button while a teardown the user did not ask for (a \"disconnected\"\nnotification, e.g. the tab or window closing) is no longer conflated with a\ndeliberate dismissal.\n\nMessagingExperiment.schema.json is regenerated from the template schemas with\nmake-schemas.py to pick up the new button `id` property.\n\nTest coverage:\n- browser_asrouter_infobar.js exercises a message with two non-primary buttons,\n  asserting the index fallback for one and an explicit `id` for the other, plus\n  cases for the dismiss-button and disconnected sources.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320313\n", "files": ["browser/components/asrouter/content-src/schemas/MessagingExperiment.schema.json", "browser/components/asrouter/content-src/templates/CFR/templates/InfoBar.schema.json", "browser/components/asrouter/modules/InfoBar.sys.mjs", "browser/components/asrouter/tests/browser/browser_asrouter_infobar.js"], "git_node": "cbec583ed64a8e0aa392e52b0c1f3be1adc0390c", "git_parents": ["c3f61e6ea05da96bb83cfdb38e521c523ce858a0"], "node": "6c8e7d4a3ccbff07cd56d322cdb476675f4118f5", "parents": ["20a5be7739975d953f6f0a1306454ebcedc7a041"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Luca Greco \u003clgreco@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055613 - Prepare telemetry/addons tests for legacy environment addons removal r=chutten,robwu\n\nRemoves activeAddons/theme/GMPlugins test coverage from TelemetryEnvironment and\nAddonManager tests, ahead of removing the environment addons properties as part\nof the child revision.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317632\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/telemetry/tests/unit/TelemetryEnvironmentTesting.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/telemetry/tests/unit/test_TelemetryEnvironment.js", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/test/xpcshell/test_EnvironmentAddonBuilder_telemetry.js", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/test/xpcshell/test_amo_stats_telemetry.js"], "git_node": "654092cd49be56678404397fb1ea77b86e60f360", "git_parents": ["cbec583ed64a8e0aa392e52b0c1f3be1adc0390c"], "node": "32445af6209f63c9ef2d99582cc90d4785a954cd", "parents": ["6c8e7d4a3ccbff07cd56d322cdb476675f4118f5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Luca Greco \u003clgreco@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055613 - Remove activeAddons/theme/activeGMPlugins from the legacy Telemetry environment r=chutten,robwu,urlbar-reviewers,jteow\n\nRemoves environment.addons along with cleaning up about:telemetry and EnvironmentAddonBuilder from\nlogic that was mainly needed due to the legacy telemetry environment.\n\nAlso updates the docs and and decrements the arewegleanyet Legacy/Glean counters.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317633\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/tests/unit/test_exposure.js", "mobile/android/app/geckoview-prefs.js", "toolkit/components/telemetry/app/TelemetryEnvironment.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/telemetry/docs/data/environment.md", "toolkit/components/telemetry/docs/data/main-ping.md", "toolkit/components/telemetry/tests/marionette/tests/client/test_subsession_management.py", "toolkit/components/telemetry/tests/unit/test_CoveragePing.js", "toolkit/components/telemetry/tests/unit/test_EventPing.js", "toolkit/components/telemetry/tests/unit/test_HealthPing.js", "toolkit/components/telemetry/tests/unit/test_MainPingDisablement.js", "toolkit/components/telemetry/tests/unit/test_MigratePendingPings.js", "toolkit/components/telemetry/tests/unit/test_PingAPI.js", "toolkit/components/telemetry/tests/unit/test_TelemetryClientID_reset.js", "toolkit/components/telemetry/tests/unit/test_TelemetryController_idle.js", "toolkit/components/telemetry/tests/unit/test_TelemetryEnvironment.js", "toolkit/components/telemetry/tests/unit/test_TelemetrySession_activeTicks.js", "toolkit/components/telemetry/tests/unit/test_UsageReporting.js", "toolkit/content/aboutTelemetry.js", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/AddonManager.sys.mjs", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/test/xpcshell/test_EnvironmentAddonBuilder_telemetry.js", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/test/xpcshell/test_addons_glean_ping.js", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/test/xpcshell/test_shutdown_early.js", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/test/xpcshell/test_types.js", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/test/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "a00651a7905c9bc6c799c82353cc5ca8e49b283c", "git_parents": ["654092cd49be56678404397fb1ea77b86e60f360"], "node": "172729ec14a1620bf0dc0086ca674ef6d051fb99", "parents": ["32445af6209f63c9ef2d99582cc90d4785a954cd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Pollet \u003cvpollet@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062422 - Use best-onnx to replace MLSuggest handrolled fallback mechanism r=nordzilla,urlbar-reviewers,ai-platform-reviewers,Standard8\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318108\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/private/MLSuggest.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ml/tests/browser/browser_ml_suggest_feature_perf.js", "toolkit/components/ml/tests/browser/browser_ml_suggest_inference.js"], "git_node": "c2fb3b6e9ead2507f9a0df65