gs": []}, {"author": "rperta \u003crperta@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2063064, Bug 2056051: Restructure ImageDecoderReadRequest teardown to remove its CAN_RUN_SCRIPT_BOUNDARY r=media-playback-reviewers,aosmond,jolin\" for causing codecs failures\n\nThis reverts commit 4abd4a22c56c3945bc5d0d3aab969a05cf5564f0.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2056051: Don't cancel the ImageDecoder read request from cycle-collection unlink r=dom-core-reviewers,media-playback-reviewers,smaug,aosmond\"\n\nThis reverts commit 976bbc9aef179896a65ec7c96007fc36c547d662.\n", "files": ["dom/base/NodeIterator.cpp", "dom/media/webcodecs/ImageDecoder.cpp", "dom/media/webcodecs/ImageDecoder.h", "dom/media/webcodecs/ImageDecoderReadRequest.cpp", "dom/media/webcodecs/ImageDecoderReadRequest.h", "dom/media/webcodecs/ImageTrack.cpp", "dom/media/webcodecs/ImageTrack.h", "dom/media/webcodecs/ImageTrackList.h"], "git_node": "daecb98911c58fe0ad22d0c70e4c91f960172ea1", "git_parents": ["147b9012622f05973c6e77baf60b0e6b56705dca"], "node": "6dd703d710dc29e31a2ac688c796126776588a4f", "parents": ["ae303403ed5524d5b2935b886c5396677497a73e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063757 - Make `PresShell::CompleteMove` ignore native anonymous subtrees r=emilio,layout-reviewers\n\nThe content nodes in a UA shadow is not accessible via Selection API\neven though they are selectable by user's operation (e.g., dragging\ntext of the default `\u003csummary\u003e`). Therefore, `Selection::Modify` should\nnot move caret into UA shadow.\n\nWhen `Selection::Modify` cannot find next or previous line when the\namount is \"line\", it falls back to `PresShell::CompleteMove`. However,\n`PresShell::CompleteMove` allows to move selection into native anonymous\nsubtree even though the selection in them may not be managed by the\ndocument level selection.\n\nSo, `PresShell::CompleteMove` should call\n`nsIFrame::GetExtremeCaretPosition` with\n`nsIFrame::IGNORE_NATIVE_ANONYMOUS_SUBTREE`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320083\n", "files": ["dom/base/Selection.cpp", "layout/base/PresShell.cpp", "layout/generic/nsFrameSelection.cpp", "layout/generic/nsFrameSelection.h", "layout/generic/nsIFrame.cpp", "layout/generic/nsIFrame.h", "testing/web-platform/tests/selection/crashtests/selection-modify-line-from-optgroup-in-video-to-details-without-summary.html"], "git_node": "84192a505ed266582d75b83acbbc557e21ced43f", "git_parents": ["daecb98911c58fe0ad22d0c70e4c91f960172ea1"], "node": "2e2c06850c7a3469d88c11c729a0fce244434ec9", "parents": ["6dd703d710dc29e31a2ac688c796126776588a4f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Keith Cirkel \u003ckeithamus@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065649 - Build option list by deeply traversing select subtree r=emilio,firefox-style-system-reviewers,layout-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320588\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/test/forms/browser.toml", "browser/base/content/test/forms/browser_selectpopup_option_in_div.js", "layout/forms/nsListControlFrame.cpp", "layout/reftests/forms/select/option-in-div-multiple-ref.html", "layout/reftests/forms/select/option-in-div-multiple.html", "layout/reftests/forms/select/option-in-div-notref.html", "layout/reftests/forms/select/option-in-div-ref.html", "layout/reftests/forms/select/option-in-div.html", "layout/reftests/forms/select/reftest.list", "layout/style/res/forms.css", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-size-multiple-new-content.html.ini", "toolkit/actors/SelectChild.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "e58cc33eaf2db0fb8f57c1d147d07ce0e7812f86", "git_parents": ["84192a505ed266582d75b83acbbc557e21ced43f"], "node": "a107ee633b811bf93498a0b24498745eeb477c5d", "parents": ["2e2c06850c7a3469d88c11c729a0fce244434ec9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sebastian Hengst \u003caryx.github@gmx-topmail.de\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065722 - do not schedule clang-tidy-full task automatically.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320632\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/source-test/clang-tidy.yml"], "git_node": "3c4d9b9b14c7315c479cca4a92a9d44911d13489", "git_parents": ["e58cc33eaf2db0fb8f57c1d147d07ce0e7812f86"], "node": "3f4d8189023d3d116bebbcbe6b71ab32f25525ec", "parents": ["a107ee633b811bf93498a0b24498745eeb477c5d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064194 part 6 - Say what an underscore means in the tabbrowser. r=tabbrowser-reviewers,jsudiaman\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320072\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/Tabbrowser.sys.mjs", "browser/components/tabbrowser/docs/api.md"], "git_node": "b7f439d2bccb834506e93c4fe26ecbb0bb967377", "git_parents": ["3c4d9b9b14c7315c479cca4a92a9d44911d13489"], "node": "2be95d7e79071bd8486cfc43be21f1e458671dd2", "parents": ["3f4d8189023d3d116bebbcbe6b71ab32f25525ec"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064194 part 7 - Keep the tabbrowser's module getters off the instance. r=tabbrowser-reviewers,jsudiaman\n\nOnly `TabMetrics` has consumers reaching it through `gBrowser`; the rest move to the module's `lazy` object, and the two sibling modules that reached for one import it themselves. Two of the getters were read nowhere at all, one of them shadowed by an identically named entry on `lazy`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320073\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/Tabbrowser.sys.mjs", "browser/components/tabbrowser/content/drag-and-drop.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tab-context-menu.js"], "git_node": "77325a575b0a70bab17bb290c6d1b26f8d799c81", "git_parents": ["b7f439d2bccb834506e93c4fe26ecbb0bb967377"], "node": "60e32c9b0e3aa953e831ae8b967f48b759e91140", "parents": ["2be95d7e79071bd8486cfc43be21f1e458671dd2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062896 - Gate panel-list's click-on-mouseup on an explicit attribute instead of the anchor's role. r=jules\n\nBehavior-neutral: the new attribute is set on the two panel-lists whose anchors carry role=\"combobox\" today, the search mode switcher's and moz-select's.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319167\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/SmartbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInputBase.mjs", "toolkit/content/tests/widgets/test_panel_item_mouseup_click.html", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-select/moz-select.mjs", "toolkit/content/widgets/panel-list/panel-list.mjs"], "git_node": "b76836d1ddffbd90b4499c934dab09bab5f9f315", "git_parents": ["77325a575b0a70bab17bb290c6d1b26f8d799c81"], "node": "ba2f5ef09cf65c95d7ef255d2a2cee684630c60c", "parents": ["60e32c9b0e3aa953e831ae8b967f48b759e91140"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062896 - Stop exposing the search mode switcher as a combobox wrapping a button. r=Jamie,daleharvey\n\nRemoving the role outright, as suggested in bug 2009628 comment 18, leaves the host exposing an unnamed container: every moz-button host produces one, which bug 2064122 tracks.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319168\n", "files": ["accessible/tests/browser/tree/browser_searchbar_new.js", "browser/components/urlbar/content/SmartbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInputBase.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-UrlbarInput/browser_a11y.js"], "git_node": "05d609cbcb212fc730d521592751fcd1418b707f", "git_parents": ["b76836d1ddffbd90b4499c934dab09bab5f9f315"], "node": "6b7cc75bdcca89cfbc7b19c2a601dd70938480b7", "parents": ["ba2f5ef09cf65c95d7ef255d2a2cee684630c60c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065472 - Give SessionStore a helper for the active history entry index. r=sfoster\n\nConsolidation and a readability fix, not a correctness fix: every site already reads the right value. On saved tab data `index` is the history entry, while on a tab element it is the tab strip position that bug 1837253 makes public; `SessionStore.sys.mjs` handles both kinds of objects, and one of these sites reads it off a variable named `tab` that holds saved data.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320414\n", "files": ["browser/components/sessionstore/RecentlyClosedTabsAndWindowsMenuUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStore.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "01df6235ff1b33b660755bbcde29d1ad1b05072b", "git_parents": ["05d609cbcb212fc730d521592751fcd1418b707f"], "node": "94b26a6fde38ebf51abf7b6aefeb34962802eb89", "parents": ["6b7cc75bdcca89cfbc7b19c2a601dd70938480b7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jens Manuel Stutte \u003cjstutte@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065409 - Avoid unnecessary per-handle work in CacheFileIOManager::ShutdownInternal(). r=necko-reviewers,valentin\n\nTwo changes to cut the cost of ShutdownInternal()'s per-handle loop:\n\n1. CacheFileHandle::Log() called nsIFile::GetNativeLeafName() before the LOG()\n   macro, so the string work ran for every handle even when the cache2 log\n   module is disabled. One sampled shutdownhang crash sits exactly there\n   (ShutdownEvent::Run \u003e ShutdownInternal \u003e CacheFileHandle::Log \u003e\n   nsLocalFile::GetNativeLeafName). Bail out early on !LOG_ENABLED(). Fixing it\n   inside Log() rather than at the shutdown call site also covers the other\n   unconditional callers (CloseHandleInternal, DoomFileInternal,\n   DoomFileByKeyInternal). The two other Log() implementations in cache2\n   (CacheIndexEntry, CacheIndexStats) pass everything as LOG() arguments and\n   are already free when the module is off.\n\n2. Once we are past the shutdown I/O lag, MaybeReleaseNSPRHandleInternal()\n   stops closing files, and no index mutation made from here on can reach the\n   disk: WriteIndexToDiskIfNeeded() is already a no-op because mShuttingDown is\n   set, and CacheIndex::Shutdown() - which runs after ShutdownInternal() and is\n   the only caller of WriteLogToDisk() - bails out up front when past the lag.\n   So the CacheIndex::RemoveEntry() calls from this loop are pure waste at that\n   point; skip them for the remaining handles. RemoveEntry() is not just\n   in-memory hashtable work, it also does a DictionaryCache::RemoveDictionaryOMT()\n   main-thread dispatch per call, which the skip avoids too.\n\n   The condition is latched rather than re-tested: sShutdownDemandedTime is set\n   once per session and never reset, so it is monotonic, and latching means we\n   stop reading the clock entirely once it has fired.\n\nHandle bookkeeping is deliberately unchanged - mClosed, MaybeReleaseNSPRHandleInternal()\n(which past the lag only drops our mFD reference and keeps mHandlesByLastUsed\nconsistent) and the mHandles/mSpecialHandles removal all still run, so the\nMOZ_ASSERT(mHandles.HandleCount() == 0) invariant holds.\n\nSkipping RemoveEntry() is safe for the next session: past the lag neither the\nindex nor the journal is written, so the on-disk index stays dirty. The next\nstartup therefore rescans the entries directory and RemoveNonFreshEntries()\ndrops entries with no file on disk - the same cleanup RemoveEntry() would have\ndone. Stale entries encountered before that update completes are handled too\n(OpenFileInternal returns NS_ERROR_NOT_AVAILABLE for OPEN, AddEntry\nreinitializes for CREATE).\n\nNote this does not address the cases where the IO thread is blocked in an\nunrelated cache operation, nor the NtClose() hang inside CloseHandle described\nin comment 0 - CancelSynchronousIo() cannot cancel NtClose.\n\nTesting: no new test. The skip only exists in non-DEBUG builds\n(CacheObserver::IsPastShutdownIOLag() is hardcoded to false under DEBUG) and\nrequires the real shutdown observers to have fired, which the\nshutdownCacheForTesting() harness does not do, so it is not reachable from\nxpcshell. Verified instead on a local opt build: all 64 netwerk/test/unit\ntest_cache2-*.js tests pass, including 39/40/41 which drive a real\nShutdownInternal() and then assert the index recovers across a simulated\nrestart. Re-ran that same suite with the new branch forced permanently on to\nactually exercise the skip - still 64/64. Also confirmed with MOZ_LOG=cache2:5\nthat CacheFileHandle::Log() output is unchanged when the module is enabled\n(leafName still populated).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320371\n", "files": ["netwerk/cache2/CacheFileIOManager.cpp"], "git_node": "07b1a28c89142e671160d4360083b2172de01d03", "git_parents": ["01df6235ff1b33b660755bbcde29d1ad1b05072b"], "node": "45fbccc8cbbee084bf6ffd4f2e4a15afea5da8eb", "parents": ["94b26a6fde38ebf51abf7b6aefeb34962802eb89"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kenneth Langga \u003cklangga@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059329 - Give notifications a process-unique countId. r=saschanaz\n\nA notification's name identifies its replacement chain, and its id\nrepeats across shows of a same-named notification, so backends cannot\ntell two show requests of the same notification apart. The new countId\nis unique per notification instance within the process, letting\nbackends route asynchronous events correctly after a same-name\nreplacement; the Android double-show case in NotificationParent could\nuse it the same way in the future.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320507\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/alerts/AlertNotification.cpp", "toolkit/components/alerts/AlertNotification.h", "toolkit/components/alerts/nsIAlertsService.idl", "toolkit/components/alerts/test/chrome/chrome.toml", "toolkit/components/alerts/test/chrome/test_count_id.html"], "git_node": "53aae7910a5ab199f5496fb75fec91ce26512e7b", "git_parents": ["07b1a28c89142e671160d4360083b2172de01d03"], "node": "9ace7ad8d6808d85371249d8df161876a0bf7f82", "parents": ["45fbccc8cbbee084bf6ffd4f2e4a15afea5da8eb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tiaan Louw \u003ctlouw@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065111 - Remove the layout.css.gradient-color-interpolation-method.enabled pref r=layout-reviewers,firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320374\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "servo/components/style/values/specified/image.rs", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-images/__dir__.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/svg/pservers/reftests/gradient-color-interpolation.svg.ini"], "git_node": "1b1d5fcd40121c4c00877e34c6bcf87541160bb7", "git_parents": ["53aae7910a5ab199f5496fb75fec91ce26512e7b"], "node": "ac98abba8fcfac9564cc4d47d1106057632eeb4a", "parents": ["9ace7ad8d6808d85371249d8df161876a0bf7f82"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lando \u003clando@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Merge firefox-main to firefox-autoland\n", "files": [], "git_node": "f18381a3a2c3198cbc1b0392551afb6d67f73749", "git_parents": ["1b1d5fcd40121c4c00877e34c6bcf87541160bb7", "5b17b585c394a469267f65da3f9794162dd9c5a5"], "node": "edfda439ba6c4d16efe047057f56cf0908b6420e", "parents": ["ac98abba8fcfac9564cc4d47d1106057632eeb4a", "b894f2ca55098e840f7dda1762212fb6129d3a1a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "rperta \u003crperta@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2065649 - Build option list by deeply traversing select subtree r=emilio,firefox-style-system-reviewers,layout-reviewers\" for causing wpt failures\n\nThis reverts commit e58cc33eaf2db0fb8f57c1d147d07ce0e7812f86.\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/test/forms/browser.toml", "browser/base/content/test/forms/browser_selectpopup_option_in_div.js", "layout/forms/nsListControlFrame.cpp", "layout/reftests/forms/select/option-in-div-multiple-ref.html", "layout/reftests/forms/select/option-in-div-multiple.html", "layout/reftests/forms/select/option-in-div-notref.html", "layout/reftests/forms/select/option-in-div-ref.html", "layout/reftests/forms/select/option-in-div.html", "layout/reftests/forms/select/reftest.list", "layout/style/res/forms.css", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-size-multiple-new-content.html.ini", "toolkit/actors/SelectChild.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "2cf08bc2fb025b884e71a4a3c81985479efdded9", "git_parents": ["f18381a3a2c3198cbc1b0392551afb6d67f73749"], "node": "e7d432aaa2b898e141d97727373cf6338a52e0d1", "parents": ["edfda439ba6c4d16efe047057f56cf0908b6420e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "iain holmes \u003ciholmes@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065022: Fix incorrect platform check in LaunchOnLogin code. r=hsohaney,firefox-desktop-core-reviewers ,mconley\n\nCorrect the platform gate around the check for LaunchOnLogin to support any supported platform, not just Windows. Correct the typo inverting the subsequent check in StartupOSIntegration.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320582\n", "files": ["browser/components/BrowserGlue.sys.mjs", "browser/components/shell/StartupOSIntegration.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "8d06e19717ccb451a4ec25f07a951b8afbe716ab", "git_parents": ["2cf08bc2fb025b884e71a4a3c81985479efdded9"], "node": "ebdfd13646b0af35141549bceacac1e8852ac280", "parents": ["e7d432aaa2b898e141d97727373cf6338a52e0d1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064135 - Include more attributes in the offscreen-canvas FontGroupCache key. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nThis means we don't need to throw away the cache when any of these attributes changes.\nAlso fixes the missing fields in the ContextState copy-constructor, so that save()\ndoesn't implicitly clear them.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320434\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/CanvasRenderingContext2D.cpp", "dom/canvas/CanvasRenderingContext2D.h"], "git_node": "c7977d99fefd74022dd5714ceac2780cc599e965", "git_parents": ["8d06e19717ccb451a4ec25f07a951b8afbe716ab"], "node": "9a80a33e912c6069aa00e29fa94e2ea82c75a253", "parents": ["ebdfd13646b0af35141549bceacac1e8852ac280"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1837253 - Give tabs a public index property. r=jsudiaman,tabbrowser-reviewers\n\nNot `tabIndex` as the bug's summary suggested originally: every element inherits a native `tabIndex` property from `Element`.\n\nThe underscored `_index` stays as the write path, since the tabbrowser sets it from outside the tab's own class. SessionStore's check for a tab that never got a position becomes a read of the getter.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320411\n", "files": ["browser/components/extensions/parent/ext-browser.js", "browser/components/extensions/parent/ext-tabGroups.js", "browser/components/extensions/parent/ext-tabs.js", "browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStore.sys.mjs", "browser/components/tabbrowser/AsyncTabSwitcher.sys.mjs", "browser/components/tabbrowser/Tabbrowser.sys.mjs", "browser/components/tabbrowser/content/drag-and-drop.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tab-context-menu.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tab.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tabgroup.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tabs.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tabsplitview.js"], "git_node": "2bb2aff2f3d0c25f729e8ba5683bf4dfe4ad4ecd", "git_parents": ["c7977d99fefd74022dd5714ceac2780cc599e965"], "node": "2472454448e468ccf965655d3175b7bccbdc7349", "parents": ["9a80a33e912c6069aa00e29fa94e2ea82c75a253"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1837253 - Use the tab's index property in tests. r=jsudiaman,tabbrowser-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320413\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/xpcshell/test_TabManagementService.js", "browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_ext_tabGroups_move_onMoved.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/dragdrop/browser_drag_multiselected_splitview.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser_addAdjacentNewTab.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser_addTab_index.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser_multiselect_tabs_duplicate.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser_multiselect_tabs_move.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser_multiselect_tabs_pin_unpin.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser_multiselect_tabs_reopen_in_container.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser_multiselect_tabs_reorder.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser_new_tab_insert_position.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser_pinned_and_hidden_tabs.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser_tabReorder.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser_tab_groups.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser_tab_groups_tabContextMenu.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser_tab_interaction_telemetry.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser_tab_move_active_tab.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser_tab_preview.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser_tab_splitview.js", "devtools/client/webconsole/test/browser/browser_webconsole_clickable_urls.js", "devtools/client/webconsole/test/browser/browser_webconsole_context_menu_open_url.js", "uriloader/exthandler/tests/mochitest/browser_download_open_with_internal_handler.js"], "git_node": "2e063ee8f9b558a76a1c3d54eca1f9181afcb9cc", "git_parents": ["2bb2aff2f3d0c25f729e8ba5683bf4dfe4ad4ecd"], "node": "2a60e54ede11d22bf9c925b6e839b842781bc8fa", "parents": ["2472454448e468ccf965655d3175b7bccbdc7349"], "tags": []}, {"author": "rperta \u003crperta@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2065022: Fix incorrect platform check in LaunchOnLogin code. r=hsohaney,firefox-desktop-core-reviewers ,mconley\" for causing bc failures at browser_startup.js\n\nThis reverts commit 8d06e19717ccb451a4ec25f07a951b8afbe716ab.\n", "files": ["browser/components/BrowserGlue.sys.mjs", "browser/components/shell/StartupOSIntegration.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "756ec13a42375920c345a97b2f5bf2d743b8e2a3", "git_parents": ["2e063ee8f9b558a76a1c3d54eca1f9181afcb9cc"], "node": "3a342112bedb9e660d7e374ed50c80faa1f1c32a", "parents": ["2a60e54ede11d22bf9c925b6e839b842781bc8fa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065199 - Remove declaration that didn't use to apply. r=desktop-theme-reviewers,dao\n\nThis declaration, introduced in bug 1313751, didn't use to apply because\nthe ::before pseudo-element was a block formatting context itself (with\noverflow: hidden), and unicode-bidi is not inherited.\n\nAfter the changes to label rendering in bug 2049182 it applies, but it\napplies to the whole block rather than just the text, causing this\nissue.\n\nThis restores the behavior that we used to ship in 153. Another patch\nincoming with what I think is the desired behavior.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320641\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/toolbarbuttons.css"], "git_node": "62ca14648d63c80ad45657ffcbe1c619dcd84d54", "git_parents": ["756ec13a42375920c345a97b2f5bf2d743b8e2a3"], "node": "f65fe54fe8d81b15c057ace817c77ac7e085fbf8", "parents": ["3a342112bedb9e660d7e374ed50c80faa1f1c32a"], 