ng `bionic` memory with `mozjemalloc` r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\n`libmegazord.so` is loaded through JNA rather than linked into `libxul`.\nLinking it against `mozglue` makes Rust's `free` resolve to `mozjemalloc`,\nwhile `bionic` APIs such as `realpath` return allocations owned by `libc`,\ncausing Fenix to crash during startup. Depending on `nss` preserves the build\norder, so Cargo still cannot run before `libmozglue.so` exists.\n\nFolded NSS continues to use `mozjemalloc`. Rust never takes ownership of NSS\nallocations and releases NSS objects through NSS APIs. The `check_binary` guard\nruns only in automation and prevents a direct `libmozglue.so` dependency from\nreturning.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320332\n", "files": ["python/mozbuild/mozbuild/action/check_binary.py", "third_party/application-services/megazords/full/moz.build"], "git_node": "a7fa9999fd9d0f0ccb2ea408268bcc8dc385d1da", "git_parents": ["b75b470623576120c2a113fc359fb8466bb1767f"], "node": "c70faaf77543f046a74883c70c293447a26f440a", "parents": ["f0f5e6d22380504671b25046551126c015350684"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2033123 - Improve `./mach uniffi generate` output r=nalexander,firefox-build-system-reviewers\n\nWe now also report:\n- What Android bindings were generated.\n- That the command finished successfully.\n\nAnd `--no-completion-messages` is now passed to the\nnested `./mach build`, so it no longer reports\nsuccess before the whole command has finished.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318373\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/mach_commands.py"], "git_node": "f697c9cc63e5bff3fa90c97b7150646849ce757f", "git_parents": ["a7fa9999fd9d0f0ccb2ea408268bcc8dc385d1da"], "node": "4725fd90323c4c391050af3de9c92ccf525428bc", "parents": ["c70faaf77543f046a74883c70c293447a26f440a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2035575 - Package `libmegazord.so` as an extra archive for downstream consumers r=nalexander,firefox-build-system-reviewers\n\nThe desktop `libsForTests` JAR needs `libmegazord.so` for JVM unit tests to\nrun. Produce a `target.libmegazord_so_artifacts.zip` from the built\n`libmegazord.so` at package time and upload it for downstream consumers.\n\nOn desktop the megazord is a non-default `uniffi-target`, so a normal build\nnever produces it. Add a `MOZ_LIBMEGAZORD_ARTIFACTS` option that builds the\nmegazord as part of the default build, so `libmegazord.so `exists by the\ntime package runs and the package step archives it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D292601\n", "files": ["third_party/application-services/megazords/fenix-dylib/moz.build", "third_party/application-services/megazords/full/moz.build", "toolkit/moz.configure", "toolkit/mozapps/installer/package-name.mk", "toolkit/mozapps/installer/packager.mk", "toolkit/mozapps/installer/upload-files.mk"], "git_node": "bc856ca9c0aed1f1bea8ed2275fb6be5ece0c3e5", "git_parents": ["f697c9cc63e5bff3fa90c97b7150646849ce757f"], "node": "e47ef1193b10c08f0c32e16dd73ec51243f48969", "parents": ["4725fd90323c4c391050af3de9c92ccf525428bc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2035575 - Stage `libmegazord.so` under appservices destdir for `libsForTests` gradle tasks r=nalexander,firefox-build-system-reviewers,geckoview-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\nlibmegazord.so was being staged into the geckoview output dir, which\nforced it into the GeckoView AAR even when consumers don't want a-s.\nStage it under an appservices destdir instead, so the megazord gradle\nproject picks it up there for its own AAR.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D298761\n", "files": ["mobile/android/installer/package-manifest.in"], "git_node": "b18ed3f1370a3078ca6240a82a45a2e591da6167", "git_parents": ["bc856ca9c0aed1f1bea8ed2275fb6be5ece0c3e5"], "node": "3c117c53449ffdbce6be6206d8d291c53ba4361b", "parents": ["e47ef1193b10c08f0c32e16dd73ec51243f48969"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2035575 - Integrate megazord AAR into fat AAR pipeline alongside geckoview r=nalexander,geckoview-reviewers\n\nThe fat AAR build needs the full-megazord AAR alongside geckoview's. The\nmegazord output lands under `appservices/`, and artifact builds fetch\n`target.maven.zip` so they pick up both AARs.\n\nThe geckoview archive build also publishes every app-services component\n(via `:publishAppServicesAndroid`), not just the megazord, so the\nstandalone android-components and fenix builds can resolve them as Maven\nAARs from `target.maven.zip`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D306610\n", "files": ["mobile/android/gradle.configure", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/action/fat_aar.py"], "git_node": "0b3478add5d2a216763c4f93a6c4a9faa15d25e5", "git_parents": ["b18ed3f1370a3078ca6240a82a45a2e591da6167"], "node": "4be64d93d1b2f68230ea2fc049a1b044d09a6816", "parents": ["3c117c53449ffdbce6be6206d8d291c53ba4361b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2035575 - Normalize app-services groupId and gate subproject inclusion on dependency-download context r=nalexander,android-reviewers\n\nWhen `MOZ_APPSERVICES_IN_TREE` is set, every gradle consumer that\ndepends on `org.mozilla.appservices:*` should pick up the local\nsubprojects instead of fetching from maven.mozilla.org.\n`ComponentsDependencies` now switches groupId on access based on a flag\nthe settings plugin passes in. The a-s subprojects only load when\n`DOWNLOAD_ALL_GRADLE_DEPENDENCIES` is also set, since standalone\nfenix/focus builds consume a-s as Maven AARs from `target.maven.zip`\ninstead.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D292607\n", "files": ["build/sparse-profiles/taskgraph", "gradle/libs.versions.toml", "mobile/android/android-components/plugins/dependencies/src/main/java/DependenciesPlugin.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/settings.gradle", "mobile/android/fenix/settings.gradle", "mobile/android/focus-android/settings.gradle", "taskcluster/kinds/toolchain/android.yml"], "git_node": "9147aab02684fbeee6f55a4a9569fd32be1ed3e6", "git_parents": ["0b3478add5d2a216763c4f93a6c4a9faa15d25e5"], "node": "c62854db67625dba2ff18a04de662c958aad6a72", "parents": ["4be64d93d1b2f68230ea2fc049a1b044d09a6816"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2035575 - Include NSS runtime dependencies in megazord extra archive for desktop `libsForTests` r=nalexander,firefox-build-system-reviewers\n\nlibmegazord.so depends on NSS shared libs at runtime. Extend the\narchive to also include them (`nss3`, `freebl3`, `softokn3`, etc.),\ngated on the same flags as `services/app-services/nss_libs.mozbuild`.\n\nLink libmegazord.so with an `$ORIGIN` (Linux) or `@loader_path` (macOS)\nrpath so those bundled libraries load from its own directory wherever the\narchive is unpacked. Windows has no rpath and finds them through the\nloader search path.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D292609\n", "files": ["python/mozbuild/mozbuild/action/package_libmegazord_artifacts.py", "third_party/application-services/megazords/fenix-dylib/moz.build", "toolkit/mozapps/installer/packager.mk"], "git_node": "e801d566be03ad73c8830c6dc306743f1c2dbb15", "git_parents": ["9147aab02684fbeee6f55a4a9569fd32be1ed3e6"], "node": "8c4d422c2b82f2e4d9efac59cd27bd9419f37dfd", "parents": ["c62854db67625dba2ff18a04de662c958aad6a72"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2035575 - Extract `libsForTests` native libraries for JVM unit tests r=nalexander,geckoview-reviewers\n\nJVM unit tests load the megazord and NSS libraries through JNA, which\nneeds `jna.library.path` and friends pointing at where those libraries\nlive. Add a Gradle convention that unpacks the `libsForTests` JAR's native\nlibraries through an artifact transform and passes the extracted directory\nto each test task through `jna.library.path` and `java.library.path`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D292611\n", "files": ["mobile/android/gradle/plugins/conventions/src/main/java/org/mozilla/conventions/ProjectPlugin.kt"], "git_node": "8de196ab6b58adbe31781e661d18654cb5b0b76b", "git_parents": ["e801d566be03ad73c8830c6dc306743f1c2dbb15"], "node": "693f59d5be8f3e82050fefee8505d3e565e9fa0c", "parents": ["8c4d422c2b82f2e4d9efac59cd27bd9419f37dfd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lando \u003clando@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Merge firefox-autoland to firefox-main\n", "files": ["js/src/tests/test262/language/expressions/assignment/dstr/array-rest-elision-invalid.js", "js/src/tests/test262/language/statements/for-in/dstr/array-rest-elision-invalid.js", "js/src/tests/test262/language/statements/for-of/dstr/array-rest-elision-invalid.js", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ipprotection/ui/Modifier.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/perf/Performance.kt", "taskcluster/kinds/static-analysis-autotest/kind.yml", "tools/clang-tidy/test/bugprone-argument-comment.cpp", "tools/clang-tidy/test/bugprone-argument-comment.json", "tools/clang-tidy/test/bugprone-assert-side-effect.json", "tools/clang-tidy/test/bugprone-bitwise-pointer-cast.cpp", "tools/clang-tidy/test/bugprone-bool-pointer-implicit-conversion.cpp", "tools/clang-tidy/test/bugprone-bool-pointer-implicit-conversion.json", "tools/clang-tidy/test/bugprone-forward-declaration-namespace.cpp", "tools/clang-tidy/test/bugprone-forward-declaration-namespac