or the findbar textbox and drop the :root[lwtheme] color override.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313812\n", "files": ["toolkit/themes/shared/findbar.css"], "git_node": "42771c647101e19b9875f4efa2189805eda8da10", "git_parents": ["f917bf70fd761fafca75083e545418eeaa916493"], "node": "fc49a71dc39b488e1b38fa942de1ae99cbdd4730", "parents": ["0df5c611d046c33d6ed86d86e03be46dbfbd6de1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jack Brown \u003cjbrown@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060343 - Add newtab.scroll100 and newtab.scroll250 boolean metrics to the newtab ping - r=fchasen\n\nThe newtab page already recorded a single boolean saying \"the user scrolled more than 50px during this session\" (see bug [[ https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2049897 | 2049897 ]]).\n\nThis patch adds two more, for 100px and 250px.\n\nThe page now tells the parent process when the user crosses one of those distances, the parent remembers the deepest one reached per newtab session, and it writes all three booleans into the newtab ping just before that ping is submitted at session end.\n\nMoving the recording to session end has two consequences worth knowing when reviewing: the metrics now report an explicit false when a threshold wasn't reached instead of just being absent, and a scroll is credited to the tab it actually happened in rather than to whichever tab's ping happened to be submitted next.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316410\n", "files": ["browser/components/newtab/metrics.yaml", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Base/Base.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/TelemetryFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Base.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/xpcshell/test_TelemetryFeed.js"], "git_node": "cc8991aeb0e4a6e455959c69d1b295bda497a2e0", "git_parents": ["42771c647101e19b9875f4efa2189805eda8da10"], "node": "6bde3877779217bea26d5840a73189ae0280b50a", "parents": ["fc49a71dc39b488e1b38fa942de1ae99cbdd4730"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066031 - Re-enable the about:processes tests on ASan and TSan, only skipping the profiler start on TSan. r=canova\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320849\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/tests/browser/browser.toml", "toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/tests/browser/browser_aboutprocesses_actionicons.js"], "git_node": "ebb9c3e41054b3e4c870cda416b383b922d4c8b8", "git_parents": ["cc8991aeb0e4a6e455959c69d1b295bda497a2e0"], "node": "26fdbd370814c6d56d14be5a78637194399bb708", "parents": ["6bde3877779217bea26d5840a73189ae0280b50a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "SaaSha Pina \u003csaasha@heysparkbox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053124 - Map title onto inner controls in MozBaseInputElement subclasses. r=akulyk,Mardak\n\nForward the mapped title property to the inner focusable input/button so tooltips and accessible descriptions reach the control, matching moz-button.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315609\n", "files": ["browser/components/genai/content/page-assist.mjs", "browser/components/passwordmgr/content/login-doorhanger-username-field.mjs", "toolkit/content/tests/widgets/lit-test-helpers.js", "toolkit/content/tests/widgets/test_moz_base_input_element.html", "toolkit/content/widgets/lit-utils.mjs", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-checkbox/moz-checkbox.mjs", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-checkbox/moz-checkbox.stories.mjs", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-input-email/moz-input-email.mjs", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-input-email/moz-input-email.stories.mjs", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-input-folder/moz-input-folder.mjs", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-input-folder/moz-input-folder.stories.mjs", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-input-number/moz-input-number.mjs", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-input-number/moz-input-number.stories.mjs", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-input-password/moz-input-password.mjs", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-input-password/moz-input-password.stories.mjs", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-input-search/moz-input-search.mjs", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-input-search/moz-input-search.stories.mjs", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-input-tel/moz-input-tel.mjs", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-input-tel/moz-input-tel.stories.mjs", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-input-text/moz-input-text.mjs", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-input-text/moz-input-text.stories.mjs", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-input-url/moz-input-url.mjs", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-input-url/moz-input-url.stories.mjs", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-radio-group/moz-radio-group.mjs", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-radio-group/moz-radio-group.stories.mjs", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-select/moz-select.mjs", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-select/moz-select.stories.mjs", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-textarea/moz-textarea.mjs", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-textarea/moz-textarea.stories.mjs", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-toggle/moz-toggle.mjs", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-toggle/moz-toggle.stories.mjs"], "git_node": "f5bc0ed7a240755066a5834a3f0be2d1cb3da7d5", "git_parents": ["ebb9c3e41054b3e4c870cda416b383b922d4c8b8"], "node": "02a83d33d6c011e1e55d91b7a96f31ab2d958e2f", "parents": ["26fdbd370814c6d56d14be5a78637194399bb708"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sam Foster \u003csfoster@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2052424 - Fix sidebar animation by removing no-longer-needed nova animation branch. r=jsudiaman\n\n- Turns out the chrome gaps was what broke this. Removing that whole branch for nova fixes it\n- Add a test to assert on animation behavior\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318855\n", "files": ["browser/components/sidebar/browser-sidebar.js", "browser/components/sidebar/tests/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/sidebar/tests/browser/browser_sidebar_animation.js"], "git_node": "0148e1873fe6e9df962316cf1504117a343264a1", "git_parents": ["f5bc0ed7a240755066a5834a3f0be2d1cb3da7d5"], "node": "abc7b1ffdf7761e97972764d1430b79ca0d4df15", "parents": ["02a83d33d6c011e1e55d91b7a96f31ab2d958e2f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicholas Poon \u003cnpoon@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055510 - Preload all popular sites before opening add shortcut bottom sheet r=android-reviewers,skhan\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317075\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/ui/Homepage.kt"], "git_node": "b1eb45b5e54f27ee4e0857a914856bfc5877336c", "git_parents": ["0148e1873fe6e9df962316cf1504117a343264a1"], "node": "7834479edcdfb53c271a1306f7c22cc34c30af76", "parents": ["abc7b1ffdf7761e97972764d1430b79ca0d4df15"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Leo Tenenbaum \u003cltenenbaum@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063871 - r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320925\n", "files": ["parser/html/nsHtml5TreeOperation.cpp"], "git_node": "b99c8922aea8a5c61bf55b096758691bb553beef", "git_parents": ["b1eb45b5e54f27ee4e0857a914856bfc5877336c"], "node": "b6796ce17c9c9a229f0713ec250cb5af690b765b", "parents": ["7834479edcdfb53c271a1306f7c22cc34c30af76"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065629 - Stop rounding a device-space text run's clips out to the device grid r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nBug 2055145 made a text run round its clips out to the device grid, and\nbug 2056856 extended that to both axes for ancestor clips. An overflow clip sits\nflush with the inner edge of its container's painted border box, so rounding it\noutward spills a whole device row or column of scrolled content over that border.\n\nExact is correct: a text clip is applied by clamping the glyph quad's geometry,\nwith no coverage term, so it resolves at the pixel centre - the same grid the\ncontainer's snapped geometry landed on. Round-out moves it a whole pixel off that\ngrid, always in the spilling direction.\n\nSo leave a device-space prim's clips exact, as before bug 2055145. ClipSnap\ncollapses to Nearest / Exact and SnapRounding::RoundOutNonSubpx goes away; the\nbounding rect still rounds out.\n\nReplaces the bug 2055145 wrench test with one for this bug, drops the eight mac\nfuzzy annotations it added, and restores the four expectations bug 2056856\nremoved.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320774\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/clip.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/space.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/visibility.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/text/2056856-bitmap-clip.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/text/bug2055145-ref.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/text/bug2055145.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/text/bug2065629-ref.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/text/bug2065629.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/text/reftest.list", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-backgrounds/border-radius-clip-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-cascade/revert-layer-006.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-cascade/revert-val-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-cascade/revert-val-002.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/text-overflow-scroll-vertical-lr-rtl-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/text-overflow-scroll-vertical-rl-rtl-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-text/white-space/text-wrap-balance-line-clamp-005.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-ui/text-overflow-016.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-ui/text-overflow-028.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-ui/text-overflow-string-005.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-ui/text-overflow-with-selection.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/rendering/replaced-elements/the-textarea-element/textare