490e432e677"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex G \u003cagain@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062352 - [Monitor Agent][Models] Record specific error codes on failed monitor runs r=ai-security-reviewers,tetchart,thasan\n\nFailed runs currently store only the raw error message, so the UI can't\ntell a page that was never fetched apart from a genuine no-match. Failures\nare now tagged with a code at the point where they happen (timeout,\ncanceled, interrupted, content_extraction_error, prompt_load_error,\nmodel/auth/rate limit/network from the inference call) and the code is\nstored on the history entry as errorCode, validated by the store, and\nreused as the telemetry error_code instead of re-deriving it from the\nmessage. Inference failures that carry an HTTP status (MLPA reports\nbudget, QPS, and upstream limits all as 429, often with only \"NNN status\ncode\" in the message) are mapped by status before any message sniffing.\n\ngetPageContent gains a structured variant that reports per-URL success so\nthe monitor can fail a run with content_extraction_error when none of the\nwatched pages could be read, instead of asking the model about error text.\nReads that mechanically succeed but yield no text count as failed reads.\nPartial failures still run the check with the pages that loaded. Mid-run\nteardown is split by intent: deleting the monitor records canceled, while\nshutdown and stale running entries reconciled at load time record\ninterrupted.\n\nMonitor tests that extract more than once per run (snapshot capture\nplus the run-time read) now serve pages with the persistent head.js\nserver, since the one-shot MLTestUtils fixtures can't be read twice and\nfailed reads now fail the run instead of reaching the model.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318768\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/models/Tools.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/agents/Monitor.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/agents/MonitorAgent.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/agents/MonitorStore.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_monitor_agent.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_monitor_errors.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/xpcshell/test_Tools_GetPageContent.js"], "git_node": "abc5dc9ac96695bc97749fe4aab0e92c4ef5d3c8", "git_parents": ["159227ee6106e171045bfd889e99dd03a436919a"], "node": "583a7c259057b3c78efd2a08f5d10ba5cc68ba20", "parents": ["2682c813492c80717344062f53824f30b1657a73"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jeff Muizelaar \u003cjmuizelaar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1972620. Re-enable perfstats for twitch-animation test. r=aglavic\n\nIt doesn't seem to fail anymore.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320610\n", "files": ["testing/perfdocs/generated/raptor.md", "testing/raptor/raptor/tests/benchmarks/twitch-animation.toml"], "git_node": "f0a9f69879fe2fe6721ab2db0d7b6f67d7074efe", "git_parents": ["abc5dc9ac96695bc97749fe4aab0e92c4ef5d3c8"], "node": "c4ed983d2cd19a5914f31ebf8c11419efb3c3e65", "parents": ["583a7c259057b3c78efd2a08f5d10ba5cc68ba20"], "tags": []}, {"author": "unifolia \u003cjlewis@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058311 - SW Auto Tab Grouping Styling, Menu Button Placement, Nova Tweaks r=fluent-reviewers,desktop-theme-reviewers,Mardak,dao,flod,kcochrane\n\nCleans up some spacing and styling in the ATG menu, and moves the button to appear beside the window switcher\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316575\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/navigator-toolbox.inc.xhtml", "browser/base/content/navigator-toolbox.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/smartwindow-group-tabs/smartwindow-group-tabs.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/AIWindow.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/AutoTabGrouping.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_group_tabs_button.js", "browser/components/customizableui/CustomizableUI.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sidebar/tests/browser/browser_verticalTabs_widget_placements.js", "browser/locales-preview/autoTabGrouping.ftl", "browser/themes/shared/smartwindowGroupTabs.css", "browser/themes/shared/toolbarbutton-icons.css", "browser/themes/shared/toolbarbuttons.css"], "git_node": "a3ce1e049826c603cd0934aa97e8cb729ded2855", "git_parents": ["f0a9f69879fe2fe6721ab2db0d7b6f67d7074efe"], "node": "1c0818ef5b9d6cd800add4fe9e513dd30712cc98", "parents": ["c4ed983d2cd19a5914f31ebf8c11419efb3c3e65"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065770 - Correct addTab's inBackground docs: it does select the tab. r=kcochrane\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321254\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/Tabbrowser.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "a82a735f4690bf499142b2fc0f877086cfa04b86", "git_parents": ["a3ce1e049826c603cd0934aa97e8cb729ded2855"], "node": "8346a5128aa10e4926bd28bf233960c67baacf1d", "parents": ["1c0818ef5b9d6cd800add4fe9e513dd30712cc98"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065770 - Fix up URILoadingHelper's JSDoc for rendering. r=nsharpley\n\nsphinx-js collapses every @param description to a single paragraph, so the section headers that grouped openLinkIn's params were rendering as the tail of whichever param preceded them, and the where table came out as one run-on line. Both move into the leading description, which keeps its structure. The missing window and url params are why the rendered signature would have named the wrong arguments, and |where| was being parsed as an RST substitution.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321255\n", "files": ["browser/modules/URILoadingHelper.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "bf2492a050c761c1a1365eb2b36c44af56bce2b4", "git_parents": ["a82a735f4690bf499142b2fc0f877086cfa04b86"], "node": "8c87b5ac080d03ddcc096f9504d805b4c88b160d", "parents": ["8346a5128aa10e4926bd28bf233960c67baacf1d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065770 - Make URILoadingHelper.sys.mjs a documentation source. r=frontend-codestyle-reviewers,nsharpley,Standard8\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321256\n", "files": ["docs/config.yml", "eslint-rollouts.config.mjs"], "git_node": "0ece59eab924221a37c84ce6e8ce40862015bf87", "git_parents": ["bf2492a050c761c1a1365eb2b36c44af56bce2b4"], "node": "b68f8e950b5e0bf3522e32b5ed2b8063f37912b7", "parents": ["8c87b5ac080d03ddcc096f9504d805b4c88b160d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicholas Poon \u003cnpoon@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066192 - When trending / recent searches is enabled on homepage, make new tab button on homepage tab strip navigate home with keyboard down r=android-reviewers,skhan\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321052\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/HomeFragment.kt"], "git_node": "fc64f3a1a985a9bce875c07d587c5d6e20e91029", "git_parents": ["0ece59eab924221a37c84ce6e8ce40862015bf87"], "node": "305fd0c6092b5390fcf547ca766d5df3b6c583be", "parents": ["b68f8e950b5e0bf3522e32b5ed2b8063f37912b7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Martin Stransky \u003cstransky@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063979 [Linux] Disable HW video decoding if dmabuf is not available r=emilio,gtk-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320061\n", "files": ["gfx/thebes/gfxPlatformGtk.cpp"], "git_node": "0f5aadb4e6ddf43b8afda7d3e39eb9d8c6a7e99a", "git_parents": ["fc64f3a1a985a9bce875c07d587c5d6e20e91029"], "node": "683c2e3a667a9bc3a9174b5d9088c26f6e5667f9", "parents": ["305fd0c6092