ranch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2066528: Fix crashes when destroying a DocAccessibleParent for a WindowGlobalParent which is also being destroyed. r=accessibility-platform-reviewers,eeejay\" for causing junit failures.\n\nThis reverts commit b9da3fcbcb3280419d66cd50beeb938978c76eca.\n", "files": ["accessible/ipc/RemoteAccessible.cpp", "dom/ipc/WindowGlobalParent.cpp"], "git_node": "549872202eb07e20ed01aa06ac8d6bdaaa7e2a36", "git_parents": ["786df994607ee7beca8ae8cb2bcc281dd1b40fc8"], "node": "e40f77223ee3d622fdcd19f60a3bd9b6b8394335", "parents": ["ea2171d6d745748c1aca8d6677883b59db15a230"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Matthew Gregan \u003ckinetik@flim.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1991957 - Remove dead audio decoder types from AgnosticDecoderModule. r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nNoticed while fixing the Vorbis channel order in this bug.\n\nBug 1873663 removed the Vorbis, Opus and PCM decoders this module used to\ncreate, but left their DecoderType entries and availability checks behind.\nCreateAudioDecoder() has returned nullptr unconditionally ever since, and\nSupports() only ever tests AV1 and VPX, so none of it is reachable.\n\nIsAvailableInUtility() becomes an unconditional false: it only ever answered\nfor the three audio types, and already fell through to false for AV1 and VPX.\nThe __MINGW32__ workaround for bug 1597408 goes with the Vorbis case.\n\nThe media.rdd-opus.enabled, media.rdd-vorbis.enabled and media.rdd-wav.enabled\nprefs are left alone; PDMFactory still reads all three.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321390\n", "files": ["dom/media/platforms/agnostic/AgnosticDecoderModule.cpp"], "git_node": "53c53883a5130072e8273b7489de799459b6d2f8", "git_parents": ["549872202eb07e20ed01aa06ac8d6bdaaa7e2a36"], "node": "0ab1c7a882d8a896455030ed119afe27557e9e10", "parents": ["e40f77223ee3d622fdcd19f60a3bd9b6b8394335"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Updatebot \u003cupdatebot@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066954 - Update nestegg to d6ec55624d8187a2699ac890b83460b973331400 r=kinetik\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321746\n", "files": ["media/libnestegg/moz.yaml", "media/libnestegg/src/nestegg.c"], "git_node": "207834c8deeb8867cba6388fc77d6a0e058e2554", "git_parents": ["53c53883a5130072e8273b7489de799459b6d2f8"], "node": "09bc0fb42532aed44ca396bf89ad272c66b545a0", "parents": ["0ab1c7a882d8a896455030ed119afe27557e9e10"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jeff Muizelaar \u003cjmuizelaar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066120 - Use declareLazy to set lazy in sessionstore.\n\nThis makes go to definition and find uses work in\nVS code.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320924\n", "files": ["browser/components/sessionstore/SessionFile.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sessionstore/SessionSaver.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStartup.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStore.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sessionstore/SessionWriter.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sessionstore/TabState.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "0912ab0324dc0e5bda70b79af2039b21837a2c1f", "git_parents": ["207834c8deeb8867cba6388fc77d6a0e058e2554"], "node": "4602aa0d3d2133571529df3cfd280431a3c8587c", "parents": ["09bc0fb42532aed44ca396bf89ad272c66b545a0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066528: Fix crashes when destroying a DocAccessibleParent for a WindowGlobalParent which is also being destroyed. r=accessibility-platform-reviewers,eeejay\n\n1. In WindowGlobalParent::RecvDestroy, call DocAccessibleParent::Destroy before starting to tear down the WindowGlobalParent and its descendants.\n  Once Send__delete__ is called, the WindowGlobalParent is starting to tear down and it's no longer possible to get its BrowserParent.\n  Send__delete__ will indirectly end up calling DocAccessibleParent::Destroy again, but that's okay because DocAccessibleParent ignores subsequent Destroy calls.\n2. In OuterDocOfRemoteAccessible, null check GetBrowserParent.\n  (1) should mean that we don't hit this situation in the crash covered by this bug.\n  However, it's still possible that other code paths could hit it due to destruction edge cases, either now or in future.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321478\n", "files": ["accessible/ipc/RemoteAccessible.cpp", "dom/ipc/WindowGlobalParent.cpp"], "git_node": "ced1be2d0b9968f4d913e3ea91cf084e8e1d420b", "git_parents": ["0912ab0324dc0e5bda70b79af2039b21837a2c1f"], "node": "b61d7cb990e7490914030caf12d7c12a0b1dc21c", "parents": ["4602aa0d3d2133571529df3cfd280431a3c8587c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Reem H \u003c42309026+reemhamz@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063525 - Add ETP off state for privacy widget. r=fluent-reviewers,nina-py,bolsson\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319984\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/common/Reducers.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Privacy/Privacy.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Privacy/_Privacy.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/data/content/assets/widget-privacy-etp-off.svg", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/Widgets/PrivacyFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Widgets/Privacy.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/xpcshell/test_PrivacyFeed.js", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/newtab/newtab.ftl"], "git_node": "236231dec232af8e3cc6599522ae2d2d4bef9af4", "git_parents": ["ced1be2d0b9968f4d913e3ea91cf084e8e1d420b"], "node": "b31752a567b373b43a2a57fa277e4933e7650340", "parents": ["b61d7cb990e7490914030caf12d7c12a0b1dc21c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jed Davis \u003cjld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2043092 - Remove Linux content process access to `$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/dconf`. r=Thinker,sandbox-reviewers\n\nThis shouldn't be needed anymore as of the GSettings changes in bug 1980822.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319985\n", "files": ["security/sandbox/linux/broker/SandboxBrokerPolicyFactory.cpp"], "git_node": "41e50fe890d5ffdf984dfe05a899e124ce74419f", "git_parents": ["236231dec232af8e3cc6599522ae2d2d4bef9af4"], "node": "897203c8f045a75f17b85e6bc5a3e3faccd2b282", "parents": ["b31752a567b373b43a2a57fa277e4933e7650340"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Watt \u003cjwatt@jwatt.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2018678 p1. Add WPTs for view timelines with relatively and absolutely positioned subjects. r=layout-scroll-driven-animation-reviewers,dshin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317567\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/scroll-animations/view-timelines/view-timeline-abspos-containing-block-outside-scroller.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/scroll-animations/view-timelines/view-timeline-abspos-outside-scroll-range.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/scroll-animations/view-timelines/view-timeline-abspos-subject.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/scroll-animations/view-timelines/view-timeline-relative-ancestor.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/scroll-animations/view-timelines/view-timeline-relative-subject.html"], "git_node": "be42ef3b0ee869dec5be9a6a3453d033b2d1de96", "git_parents": ["41e50fe890d5ffdf984dfe05a899e124ce74419f"], "node": "48e5cbe1b4c4ea8b154345a133e359678d1f9910", "parents": ["897203c8f045a75f17b85e6bc5a3e3faccd2b282"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Watt \u003cjwatt@jwatt.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2018678 p2. Expose per-axis sticky scroll ranges from StickyScrollContainer. r=layout-scroll-driven-animation-reviewers,layout-reviewers,dholbert,boris\n\nThis adds a read-only GetForFrame() accessor and a GetStickyScrollRangesForAxis() method that re-expresses the stick and containment rectangles of ComputeStickyLimits() as, for each physical side of the given axis, the scroll offset at which sticking to that side begins or ends and the maximum displacement it can produce. ComputeStickyLimits() gains a StickyLimitSpace parameter so that these thresholds can be computed independently of the current scroll position. This information is needed to model how sticky positioning displaces a view timeline subject as a function of the scroll offset.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317568\n", "files": ["layout/generic/StickyScrollContainer.cpp", "layout/generic/StickyScrollContainer.h"], "git_node": "aed0747badc8779a3b9d29ac9cfdb8e3c3736660", "git_parents": ["be42ef3b0ee869dec5be9a6a3453d033b2d1de96"], "node": "3e93e24dd77ab39355666b79036e41f39ea34a22", "parents": ["48e5cbe1b4c4ea8b154345a133e359678d1f9910"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Watt \u003cjwatt@jwatt.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2018678 p3. Make ViewTimeline ranges account for sticky positioning. r=layout-scroll-driven-animation-reviewers,boris\n\nSticky positioning displaces a view timeline subject by a piecewise-linear function d(s) of the scroll offset s, which StickyDisplacement models using the per-axis sticky scroll ranges added in p2. UpdateCachedCurrentTime() now removes the current displacement from the cached subject position so that it is scroll-invariant, and caches the displacement model alongside it. Timeline range boundaries are then computed by solving s - d(s) == offset for the earliest or latest scroll offset, as appropriate for each boundary, matching the earliest/latest wording in the spec. If more than one sticky ancestor affects the subject we fall back to treating the current displacement as permanent.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317569\n", "files": ["dom/animation/ViewTimeline.cpp", "dom/animation/ViewTimeline.h", "testing/web-platform/meta/scroll-animations/view-timelines/sticky/view-timeline-sticky-offscreen-1.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/scroll-animations/view-timelines/sticky/view-timeline-sticky-offscreen-2.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/scroll-animations/view-timelines/sticky/view-timeline-sticky-offscreen-3.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/scroll-animations/view-timelines/sticky/view-timeline-sticky-offscreen-6.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/scroll-animations/view-timelines/sticky/view-timeline-sticky-offscreen-7.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/scroll-animations/view-timelines/view-timeline-sticky-block.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/scroll-animations/view-timelines/view-timeline-sticky-inline.html.ini"], "git_node": "c4c237cb2976c1e661f88d85c3ddb753886aea40", "git_parents": ["aed0747badc8779a3b9d29ac9cfdb8e3c3736660"], "node": "d60ca297f1cbd2f8a8489049550561857f0e83b5", "parents": ["3e93e24dd77ab39355666b79036e41f39ea34a22"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Watt \u003cjwatt@jwatt.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2018678 p4. Add WPTs for view timelines with sticky-positioned subjects. r=layout-scroll-driven-animation-reviewers,boris\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317570\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/scroll-animations/view-timelines/sticky/view-timeline-sticky-containing-block-clamp.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/scroll-animations/view-timelines/sticky/view-timeline-sticky-orthogonal-axis-only.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/scroll-animations/view-timelines/sticky/view-timeline-sticky-zero-size-subject.tentative.html"], "git_node": "0b3cf2f8f38f2bc9728836050acab2b8df4f295e", "git_parents": ["c4c237cb2976c1e661f88d85c3ddb753886aea40"], "node": "10a28649970bd7f48ce6635e51c0541e6e1ea12b", "parents": ["d60ca297f1cbd2f8a8489049550561857f0e83b5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2018678 p4. Add WPTs for view timelines with sticky-positioned subjects. r=layout-scroll-driven-animation-reviewers,boris\" for causing wpt failures at sticky-subpixel-adjustment.html\n\nThis reverts commit 0b3cf2f8f38f2bc9728836050acab2b8df4f295e.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2018678 p3. Make ViewTimeline ranges account for sticky positioning. r=layout-scroll-driven-animation-reviewers,boris\"\n\nThis reverts commit c4c237cb2976c1e661f88d85c3ddb753886aea40.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2018678 p2. Expose per-axis sticky scroll ranges from StickyScrollContainer. r=layout-scroll-driven-animation-reviewers,layout-reviewers,dholbert,boris\"\n\nThis reverts commit aed0747badc8779a3b9d29ac9cfdb8e3c3736660.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2018678 p1. Add WPTs for view timelines with relatively and absolutely positioned subjects. r=layout-scroll-driven-animation-reviewers,dshin\"\n\nThis reverts commit be42ef3b0ee869dec5be9a6a3453d033b2d1de96.\n", "files": ["dom/animation/ViewTimeline.cpp", "dom/animation/ViewTimeline.h", "layout/generic/StickyScrollContainer.cpp", "layout/generic/StickyScrollContainer.h", "testing/web-platform/meta/scroll-animations/view-timelines/sticky/view-timeline-sticky-offscreen-1.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/scroll-animations/view-timelines/sticky/view-timeline-sticky-offscreen-2.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/scroll-animations/view-timelines/sticky/view-timeline-sticky-offscreen-3.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/scroll-animations/view-timelines/sticky/view-timeline-sticky-offscreen-6.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/scroll-animations/view-timelines/sticky/view-timeline-sticky-offscreen-7.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/scroll-animations/view-timelines/view-timeline-sticky-block.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/scroll-animations/view-timelines/view-timeline-sticky-inline.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/scroll-animations/view-timelines/sticky/view-timeline-sticky-containing-block-clamp.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/scroll-animations/view-timelines/sticky/view-timeline-sticky-orthogonal-axis-only.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/scroll-animations/view-timelines/sticky/view-timeline-sticky-zero-size-subject.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/scroll-animations/view-timelines/view-timeline-abspos-containing-block-outside-scroller.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/scroll-animations/view-timelines/view-timeline-abspos-outside-scroll-range.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/scroll-animations/view-timelines/view-timeline-abspos-subject.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/scroll-animations/view-timelines/view-timeline-relative-ancestor.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/scroll-animations/view-timelines/view-timeline-relative-subject.html"], "git_node": "4ab9706d7facb19ed5841258db08bbe30844859c", "git_parents": ["0b3cf2f8f38f2bc9728836050acab2b8df4f295e"], "node": "85eea8498cd0f7ded4380b83bebe0f442fe71ab3", "parents": ["10a28649970bd7f48ce6635e51c0541e6e1ea12b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2062795 - tweak checkbox and radio styles for Nova r=emilio,layout-reviewers\" for causing reftest failures at /checkbox-clamp-01.html\n\nThis reverts commit 368606ece14862c0c24bdef602db6c50168c1221.\n", "files": ["layout/reftests/box-shadow/1212823-2-ref.html", "layout/reftests/box-shadow/reftest.list", "layout/reftests/forms/input/checkbox/reftest.list", "layout/reftests/image-element/reftest.list", "widget/Theme.cpp"], "git_node": "aa6479632cc3aa5f5b10ae4ac9b40914e67a65cf", "git_parents": ["4ab9706d7facb19ed5841258db08bbe30844859c"], "node": "dca14595438c971eb8807e1169c4eda48bf619fd", "parents": ["85eea8498cd0f7ded4380b83bebe0f442fe71ab3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Reem H \u003c42309026+reemhamz@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063963 - Fix tracker count refresh issue in Privacy widget. r=nina-py\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321442\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/common/Actions.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Privacy/Privacy.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/Widgets/PrivacyFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Widgets/Privacy.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/xpcshell/test_PrivacyFeed.js"], "git_node": "2a770946653f30826b73178769b055706fd17cfa", "git_parents": ["aa6479632cc3aa5f5b10ae4ac9b40914e67a65cf"], "node": "a359803f87199c9b3a104c981552f7f3aa0813b3", "parents": ["dca14595438c971eb8807e1169c4eda48bf619fd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jari Jalkanen \u003cjjalkanen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049342: Use thread safe manager for prefix sets. r=asuth,mccr8,timhuang\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318398\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/url-classifier/VariableLengthPrefixSet.cpp", "toolkit/components/url-classifier/VariableLengthPrefixSet.h", "toolkit/components/url-classifier/tests/gtest/TestUrlClassifierPrefixSetReporter.cpp", "toolkit/components/url-classifier/tests/gtest/moz.build"], "git_node": "4e06be5543c28c25440b6fb66094ff3410340cc1", "git_parents": ["2a770946653f30826b73178769b055706fd17cfa"], "node": "3189cc6bec7b30c482e0b46915e41e4772c4a95f", "parents": ["a359803f87199c9b3a104c981552f7f3aa0813b3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Eden Chuang \u003cechuang@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2048545 - P1 Android clipboard ContentProvider plumbing. r=edgar,geckoview-reviewers,m_kato\n\nJava side of Bug 2048545. Mirrors the macOS/Linux/Windows implementations\nfrom Bug 1956304 for Android (GeckoView).\n\nThe initial consumer is the W3C Async Clipboard API web custom format\nprotocol (Appendix A of the spec: Android shares the Linux/ChromeOS\nconvention where the JSON essence -\u003e slot map lives under\n\"application/web;type=\\\"custom/formatmap\\\"\" and each essence's bytes\nlive under \"application/web;type=\\\"custom/formatN\\\"\"). However the\nplumbing added here is MIME-agnostic \u2014 any future clipboard consumer\nthat needs to publish a multi-item ClipData backed by URIs can reuse\nthe same session/provider/commit flow.\n\nGeckoClipboardContentProvider is a new ContentProvider that serves the\nbytes for Firefox-authored clips via content:// URIs of the shape\ncontent://AUTHORITY/\u003csessionId\u003e/\u003citemIndex\u003e. It uses a Pipe so bytes\nnever hit disk. The authority is derived per applicationId\n(\"${applicationId}.clipboard\") so Fenix, GVE, and any other GeckoView-\nbased package can coexist on the same device without hitting Android's\none-authority-per-name restriction (INSTALL_FAILED_CONFLICTING_PROVIDER).\n\nClipboard.java gets a MIME-agnostic session-based write API\n(openWriteSession / addPayload / commitWriteSession / cancelWriteSession)\nso the C++ side can push payloads one at a time without a byte[][] JNI\nhop. Payload order matters: the first added payload's URI is bundled\nonto ClipData.Item[0] together with the standard text/HTML flavors,\nsubsequent payloads become items 1..N.\n\nThe web-custom-format read API (getWebCustomFormatMapJson /\ngetWebCustomFormatPayload / hasWebCustomFormatMap) walks the primary\nclip's items and resolves each Uri's MIME via\nContentResolver.getStreamTypes().\n\nAndroidManifest_overlay.jinja registers GeckoClipboardContentProvider\nwith authority \"${applicationId}.clipboard\", exported=\"true\", and\ngrantUriPermissions so other apps can resolve the URIs cross-app.\n\nDepends on Bug 1956304.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D307753\n", "files": ["mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/AndroidManifest_overlay.jinja", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/gecko/Clipboard.java", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/gecko/GeckoClipboardContentProvider.java"], "git_node": "20780d9bb9f3116b5d2208bf5ab7de7571b4753c", "git_parents": ["4e06be5543c28c25440b6fb66094ff3410340cc1"], "node": "c72861f14a48eceb1093c55f0ddc579043ff0dd4", "parents": ["3189cc6bec7b30c482e0b46915e41e4772c4a95f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Eden Chuang \u003cechuang@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2048545 - P2 Android Gecko clipboard support for web custom format. r=edgar,m_kato\n\nGecko (C++) side of Bug 2048545. Wires widget/android/nsClipboard.cpp\ninto the Java session/read APIs added in P1.\n\nSetNativeClipboardData handles \"web foo/bar\" flavors by building a\nWebCustomFormatMap, serialising to JSON, and pushing the payloads\nthrough Clipboard.openWriteSession /\naddPayload / commitWriteSession. The\nstandard text/HTML flavors in the same transferable are co-published\non the same ClipData so callers asking for text/plain after a mixed\nwrite still find them.\n\nGetNativeClipboardData adds two branches before the legacy text/raw\npath:\n  - kWebCustomFormatMapType fetches the map JSON from the primary clip,\n    parses it, and returns the per-essence \"web foo/bar\" flavors as an\n    nsIMutableArray.\n  - \"web foo/bar\" fetches the map, looks up the matching per-essence\n    MIME, and reads its bytes via the ContentProvider URI.\n\nHasNativeClipboardDataMatchingFlavors recognises both shapes and\nlazy-loads the map JSON on the first \"web \" query.\n\nDepends on Bug 1956304.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D307803\n", "files": ["widget/android/nsClipboard.cpp"], "git_node": "ca947f8992e08ce16be852fd0a1b80e7678cdf3e", "git_parents": ["20780d9bb9f3116b5d2208bf5ab7de7571b4753c"], "node": "cd82ba21b67f4d43609dff2492c174ac003da153", "parents": ["c72861f14a48eceb1093c55f0ddc579043ff0dd4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Eden Chuang \u003cechuang@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2048545 - P3 Enable web custom format tests on Android. r=edgar\n\nNow that Bug 2048545 P1/P2 land the Android-side support for the W3C\nAsync Clipboard API web custom formats, lift the Android skips and\nexpected-failure annotations:\n\n  - Drop the Android FAIL/CRASH expectations from the four\n    clipboard-apis web-platform test .ini files.\n  - Remove the navigator.userAgent.includes(\"Android\") early-returns\n    from widget mochitest tasks that exercise web custom formats\n    (test_web_custom_format, test_read_custom_formats_from_clipboard_pref,\n    test_web_custom_format_data).\n\nDepends on Bug 1956304.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D307804\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/clipboard-apis/async-custom-formats-write-read-web-prefix.tentative.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/clipboard-apis/async-custom-formats-write-read-without-web-prefix.tentative.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/clipboard-apis/async-custom-formats-write-read.tentative.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/clipboard-apis/async-unsanitized-plaintext-formats-write-read.tentative.https.html.ini", "widget/tests/file_test_clipboard.js", "widget/tests/file_test_clipboard_getDataSnapshotSync.js"], "git_node": "f1bab812e9d0c6e83ed4f0ecbdd38e12d6aea76e", "git_parents": ["ca947f8992e08ce16be852fd0a1b80e7678cdf3e"], "node": "6c5502c5632d0ddd04efc550e5ca21631c39d6ee", "parents": ["cd82ba21b67f4d43609dff2492c174ac003da153"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sotaro Ikeda \u003csotaro.ikeda.g@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066982 - Remove unused GLBlitHelper::BlitImageToFramebuffer() r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321770\n", "files": ["gfx/gl/GLBlitHelper.cpp", "gfx/gl/GLBlitHelper.h", "gfx/gl/GLBlitHelperD3D.cpp", "gfx/layers/GLImages.cpp"], "git_node": "c1b4318c71c2d1213acee137eab6449cc2cc0d46", "git_parents": ["f1bab812e9d0c6e83ed4f0ecbdd38e12d6aea76e"], "node": "720b71c001e4c0185bb668e26931c5b704d9e4fe", "parents": ["6c5502c5632d0ddd04efc550e5ca21631c39d6ee"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2066982 - Remove unused GLBlitHelper::BlitImageToFramebuffer() r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\" for causing build bustages at /GLBlitHelper.cpp\n\nThis reverts commit c1b4318c71c2d1213acee137eab6449cc2cc0d46.\n", "files": ["gfx/gl/GLBlitHelper.cpp", "gfx/gl/GLBlitHelper.h", "gfx/gl/GLBlitHelperD3D.cpp", "gfx/layers/GLImages.cpp"], "git_node": "72cf5f090ae41fa75c1aaea129f7e5548a708ef4", "git_parents": ["c1b4318c71c2d1213acee137eab6449cc2cc0d46"], "node": "8922249c6e3fd187d763e495fdcf5046225e4f0b", "parents": ["720b71c001e4c0185bb668e26931c5b704d9e4fe"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Release Engineering Landoscript \u003crelease+landoscript@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug - Bumping Firefox l10n changesets r=release a=l10n-bump DONTBUILD CLOSED TREE\n\nach -\u003e c0299aa65c653ffc826cc228727db0ca0f8641ad\naf -\u003e c0299aa65c653ffc826cc228727db0ca0f8641ad\nan -\u003e c0299aa65c653ffc826cc228727db0ca0f8641ad\nar -\u003e c0299aa65c653ffc826cc228727db0ca0f8641ad\nast -\u003e c0299aa65c653ffc826cc228727db0ca0f8641ad\naz -\u003e c0299aa65c653ffc826cc228727db0ca0f8641ad\nbe -\u003e c0299aa65c653ffc826cc228727db0ca0f8641ad\nbg -\u003e c0299aa65c653ffc826cc228727db0ca0f8641ad\nbn -\u003e c0299aa65c653ffc826cc228727db0ca0f8641ad\nbo -\u003e c0299aa65c653ffc826cc228727db0ca0f8641ad\nbqi -\u003e c0299aa65c653ffc826cc228727db0ca0f8641ad\nbr -\u003e c0299aa65c653ffc826cc228727db0ca0f8641ad\nbrx -\u003e c0299aa65c653ffc826cc228727db0ca0f8641ad\nbs -\u003e c0299aa65c653ffc826cc228727db0ca0f8641ad\nca -\u003e c0299aa65c653ffc826cc228727db0ca0f8641ad\nca-valencia -\u003e c0299aa65c653ffc826cc228727db0ca0f8641ad\ncak -\u003e c0299aa65c653ffc826cc228727db0ca0f8641ad\nckb -\u003e c0299aa65c653ffc826cc228727db0ca0f8641ad\ncs -\u003e c0299aa65c653ffc826cc228727db0ca0f8641ad\ncy -\u003e c0299aa65c653ffc826cc228727db0ca0f8641ad\nda -\u003e c0299aa65c653ffc826cc228727db0ca0f8641ad\nde -\u003e c0299aa65c653ffc826cc228727db0ca0f8641ad\ndsb -\u003e c0299aa65c653ffc826cc228727db0ca0f8641ad\nel -\u003e c0299aa65c653ffc826cc228727db0ca0f8641ad\nen-CA -\u003e c0299aa65c653ffc826cc228727db0ca0f8641ad\nen-GB -\u00